e":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T15:00:41-08:00","id":7055,"title":"","content":"Saw <b>Thor</b> today.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The whole of it played out well enough. But I guess I was hoping they'd put the &quot;God&quot; back in Thunder-God. The closest we saw in that was Thor making it stop raining on Darcy.<br /> And this leads to the problem I'm having with how they're presenting Thor and Asgard in general. It's like the whole of it are a technologically advance race rather than a pantheon of gods that were there at the beginning of all.<br /> Pretty much agree with what was said in <a href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/movies/thor-the-dark-world-brings-back-marvels-alien-superhero.html?_r=0\" target=\"_blank\">this review</a><br /> <i><br /> But repackaging a Norse god as an alien superhero takes chutzpah, not humor (unless you count the Viking ship that serves as his spacecraft), and movie studios have yet to lose money by assuming that their audiences have the intellectual discernment of newborns. So if the multiple idiocies on view strike you as neither here nor there, it\u2019s probably because your eyeballs are too busy recoiling from the onslaught of disorienting 3-D effects, or else too distracted by the title character\u2019s Popeye arms and really big mallet. </i><br /> <br /> The screen seems to take on life when either Loki or Darcy come into it. And I think Loki pretty much steals the show.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T16:35:40-08:00","id":7092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Thor\u00a9\u00ae\u2122 Marvel Entertainment Group LLC, a Disney Studios company <b>is</b> a member of a technologically advanced alien race, which happens to also be a pantheon of gods with origins that predate the current universe. They were a sort of raw creative force, given form and purpose by the beliefs of humans (a largely chance encounter). Because of the type of force involved, their definition as incarnations of Asgardian mythical figures was complete... including making it so that they are what they are even before they became what they are, in a fun bit of time-ignoring predetermination.<br /> <br /> Which was kind of added on a bit later. At the core of it, Jack Kirby drew them with a certain aesthetic and Stan Lee (and Gerry Conway) wrote them as interacting with alien invaders more often than they interacted with modern humans... so that is what <i>Marvel Comics</i> Thor is and has been. If you don't like the sort of ray-gun aesthetic, or want something more closely modeled on Norse myth/legend/religious belief, then you need to find another product.<br /> <br /> Complaining that Thor\u00a9\u00ae\u2122 is not following the Prose Edda is much like complaining that Vampire: the Requiem isn't word for word identical to the works of Bram Stoker. The failing isn't in the product, but in your rigid expectations.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Said best here: <a href=\"http://arousinggrammar.com/2012/07/01/thor-vs-iron-man/\" target=\"_blank\">Thor Versus Iron Man</a> Before Thor became &quot;Disneyfied.&quot;<br /> <i>&quot;Do not let them forget what a god of thunder is and what that means.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T17:49:17-08:00","id":7117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=7055#post7055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saw <b>Thor</b> today.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> But repackaging a Norse god as an alien superhero takes chutzpah, not humor (unless you count the Viking ship that serves as his spacecraft), and movie studios have yet to lose money by assuming that their audiences have the intellectual discernment of newborns. So if the multiple idiocies on view strike you as neither here nor there, it\u2019s probably because your eyeballs are too busy recoiling from the onslaught of disorienting 3-D effects, or else too distracted by the title character\u2019s Popeye arms and really big mallet. [/I]<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> oh then you gonna love this guy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span><br /> <img src=\"http://images4.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20081224185741/marveldatabase/images/9/98/Beta_Ray_Bill_(Earth-616).png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Beta Ray Bill.<br /> <br /> I personally dont mind the alien angle in Thor and its ok for the movies as mixing magic + technology for mainstream audiences would have been trickier. On the comics thought you also have the other pantheons who are depending on earth worship to survive and the line get murky there.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T20:49:45-08:00","id":7166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Would you like me to provide you with some panels of him piloting an open-topped longship through space, or pushing blinking buttons on an Asgardian control panel from comic books published in the early sixties?</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Why would I care to see that?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your contention that it has been Disneyfied is frankly one that leads me to believe that you have a very narrow understanding of the subject matter, and that in your ignorance you are parroting something you read online by someone else who had no idea what they were saying, but still wished to complain.<br /> This aesthetic and the departure from Norse mythology has absolutely nothing to do with Disney purchasing Marvel. It has everything to do with the specific interpretation of the character of Thor as published by Marvel comics for fifty years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh And what did you think it was when he became the Rune King and decided to end the cycle of Ragnarok? And then became reborn because of <i>belief</i> that he and Asgard was needed?<br /> It seems to me you're very quick to throw labels around whenever someone has an opinion that departs from your own.<br /> Perhaps it's because of your own intolerance and thin skin. I suggest you grow some thicker skin and learn to accept that others' opinions may differ from your own.<br /> <br /> They're departure going from the mysticism to science based is idiotic. There were only three superheroes prepped to challenge Warlock when he kept the Infinity Gauntlet; Thor, Silver Surfer, and Doctor Strange. And I get the feeling that they aren't going to create a Dr. Strange movie anytime soon.<br /> <br /> <br /> And Beta Ray Bill is awesome!<br /> From <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beta_Ray_Bill\" target=\"_blank\">Walt Simonson</a>: [I]&quot;<i>One of the cool things about Thor was the enchantment around Mjolnir and the original inscription on it. So I thought, well that means someone else can pick up this hammer and get this power, if they're worthy! This is the most powerful weapon of the Norse gods. This hammer is a killing weapon. It's used to kill Frost Giants and others. So I created Bill because he's noble, and he's designed to kill. He's got a great purpose as a warrior, and also the noble ability. That makes him &quot;worthy&quot; whatever that may be.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T21:03:34-08:00","id":7171,"title":"","content":"<b>Thor: the Dark World</b> is fun, but one thing I noticed as we were leaving the theater was that the instant it was over, my friend and I stopped talking or thinking about it. I feel bad about that. Loyalty is pretty deep in my nature, and not caring enough about Chris Hemsworth and Tom Hiddleston to be fascinated by their movie feels like a betrayal to me. In the end, though, that's just how I feel: good but not great; fun but not super-interesting. As such, my ability to give an in-depth review is pretty difficult for me to offer, particularly in light of everything Loxosceles has already said.<br /> <br /> Idris Elba is the king of all badasses. He sits on a throne made of gold mined from meteorites that he personally caught in his fists as they fell to the Earth, and the throne is also a motorcycle. His crown is made of equal parts fire and electric guitar riffs.<br /> <br /> There are two stingers. The first one is awesome and reminds me of why Benicio del Toro is one of the best actors I know of. The second is wet your pants funny.<br /> <br /> There are at least two areas where I feel like subplots were cut in editing. One involves Sif and Thor, the other involves Erik Selvig. I won't go into more because of my no spoilers policy, but I just feel like more was filmed than was shown to us.<br /> <br /> The final action sequence of the movie is almost perfect. There is only one place it missteps, and that is which direction Mjolnir approaches Thor from. It should have approached him from the front.<br /> <br /> ...Yeah, that's pretty much all I have to add.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T22:20:45-08:00","id":7192,"title":"","content":"Anyone else going to see the Doctor Who 50th Anniversary Special in theaters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T03:13:02-08:00","id":7268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=7171#post7171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idris Elba is the king of all badasses. He sits on a throne made of gold mined from meteorites that he personally caught in his fists as they fell to the Earth, and the throne is also a motorcycle. His crown is made of equal parts fire and electric guitar riffs.</div> </div> </div> </div>A while ago, it occurred to me that Idris Elba's big climactic speech in Pacific Rim is being given mostly to people who are going to wind up staying back at the base and awaiting the results of the final mission, so it's less of a &quot;inspire you all to give 110% before we go into battle&quot; moment and more of &quot;I'm going off to die now; here's something to remember how awesome I was&quot;.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T11:19:34-08:00","id":7519,"title":"","content":"For me, while greater plot coherency and character investment would be nice, I was primarily looking to Thor: The Dark World for scope and mythology, which it had in droves. And maybe a bit of giving some of the side characters more to do, which it did well enough (even if one of them got something cool to do right before some complete bullshit, but whatever). I am satisfied by it to the degree that I would greatly enjoy watching it again, though taking on the criticisms of others shall give me heightened standards for the next one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T11:27:11-08:00","id":7523,"title":"","content":"Did anyone think that Jaime Alexander (Sif) had this &quot;Wonder Woman&quot; vibe going for her?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T12:31:59-08:00","id":7568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=7523#post7523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did anyone think that Jaime Alexander (Sif) had this &quot;Wonder Woman&quot; vibe going for her?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would totally support her as Wonder Woman, though the costume might need to be adjusted to include sleeves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T13:51:54-08:00","id":7649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you think that the Marvel Comics science fiction spin on Asgardians is stupid, the people to take it up with are Stan Lee and Jack Kirby.<br /> <br /> Just hop onto your non-science-fiction time machine, head back to 1962 and let them know how dumb they are before they sit down to produce Journey Into Mystery #83, when he fights aliens. Definitely get to them before Journey Into Mystery #85, when Loki appears and Thor gets really irresponsible by using Mjolnir to produce anti-matter on the streets of Manhattan.<br /> <br /> The point being; the departure from the mysticism is inherent in the character, as written by Marvel comics. The times when it has returned fully to the mysticism, and actually cut out the science fiction (rather than combining the two) are the rare events. It is a naive criticism to say, &quot;Thor the movie should not have sci-fi, it should be more like the comics.&quot; because those sci-fi elements are inherent in those comic books.</div> </div> </div> </div>thor was always science fiction? In his origins i mean. i always thought that he was a mystic hero in a world with both mystic and science fiction and that the mix of the two as a integral of thor have come recently. Meaning that in the old comic his powers were magic based exclusively and that the notion of asgardians being a advance scientific civilization was something new.<br /> <br /> However it is in the comics, it pretty ambigous now. Fear itself went with the movie angle a lot but mysticism is a core part of the character. And while i could buy later revision of the character to go more in accordance with the movie it still leaves the issue of the other gods who are all magic based (the greek ones, with hercules)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","user":"kaho","date":". 11-10-2013, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T15:01:11-08:00","id":7675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=7649#post7649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> thor was always science fiction? In his origins i mean. i always thought that he was a mystic hero in a world with both mystic and science fiction and that the mix of the two as a integral of thor have come recently. Meaning that in the old comic his powers were magic based exclusively and that the notion of asgardians being a advance scientific civilization was something new.<br /> <br /> However it is in the comics, it pretty ambigous now. Fear itself went with the movie angle a lot but mysticism is a core part of the character. And while i could buy later revision of the character to go more in accordance with the movie it still leaves the issue of the other gods who are all magic based (the greek ones, with hercules)</div> </div> </div> </div>The consensus from the convention I was at last year was that the movies are going with the Superman idea of a alien superhero, while the comics remain strictly mystic. (There's this enchantment on that hammer see?) When Captain America had been assassinated Thor summoned his ghost to ask if he wanted to be avenged. And then in the Ultimates during an alien invasion, that version of Thor summons the einherjar (dead heroes)...initially the Avengers thought him a madman...after doing that, there was a crisis of faith.<br /> Which segues nicely into the reason that was explained to me why Disney doesn't want the God in Thunder-God; <b>controversy</b>. They don't want to see such characters as the <a href=\"http://marvel.wikia.com/Arthur_Blackwood_(Earth-616)\" target=\"_blank\">Crusader</a> which attacked Thor because of his religious beliefs. They don't want to see Thor <a href=\"http://i138.photobucket.com/albums/q265/rychehitman/thor/REBIRTH/Issue%203/page_14.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">threaten the nation with a biblical deluge</a> as he once did when he became pissed at Iron Man and SHIELD. It's a whole lot safer (and profitable) if the movie version of Thor gets nice and neutered and plays nice with everyone else. Especially the federal government.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 11-10-2013, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T15:57:16-08:00","id":7712,"title":"","content":"I just watched a movie called Glengarry Glen Ross, adapted from a play by David Mamet.<br /> <br /> It's... wow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8kZg_ALxEz0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8kZg_ALxEz0\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8kZg_ALxEz0\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8kZg_ALxEz0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The scene is the opening of the movie, and... all I can think of is that I should check out more stuff from Mamet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T17:03:29-08:00","id":7735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=7712#post7712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just watched a movie called Glengarry Glen Ross, adapted from a play by David Mamet.<br /> <br /> It's... wow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8kZg_ALxEz0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8kZg_ALxEz0\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8kZg_ALxEz0\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8kZg_ALxEz0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The scene is the opening of the movie, and... all I can think of is that I should check out more stuff from Mamet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty impressive, yeah? IMO, the movie definitely deserves its acclaim. There is one thing that bothers me about the movie, though - or more accurately, about its reception. See, Alec Baldwin's speech at the beginning is definitely the most memorable moment in the film...but I don't think many people take it into account that his character is <b>emphatically not a good guy.</b> <br /> <br /> You're not supposed to listen to that speech and come away thinking that yeah, that was awesome, just the kick-in-the-ass those guys needed to really make some sales. But I can't tell you how many people I've talked to who accepted it at face value. Sorta like how so many people watch Fight Club and come away with the idea that Tyler Durden was a generally awesome dude instead of a nihilistic psychopath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T17:06:15-08:00","id":7736,"title":"","content":"I've never really understood the difference between magic and science as aesthetics in fiction anyway. I mean, honestly, what's the difference between a ray gun and a wand that shoots beams of fire? Between riding a dragon and flying an X-wing? Between a magic ring of power that's linked to an evil wizard's soul or a doomsday weapon that emits EM radiation the evil scientist can track with his equipment? Or, to borrow an example from the movie itself, between a soulforge and a quantum mechanic whatsit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T17:14:41-08:00","id":7743,"title":"","content":"I think it's what I call the &quot;drill sergeant&quot; effect. The drill sergeant is hurling abuse at you, sure, but he lets you know right off the bat that real combat is a thousand times worse than anything he can throw at you, and he genuinely wants you to improve, to be prepared for what is to come. His job is to make you better, so you take the abuse as the challenge it is rather than an insult.<br /> <br /> Mitchell &amp; Murray obviously wanted Baldwin's character to do the drill sergeant deal, but the character made no bones about the fact that he thought the salesmen were a complete waste of space, so the other characters took his &quot;pep talk&quot; for the insulting abuse it was.<br /> <br /> So yeah. Corporate America. Not that Communist Russia was any better.<br /> <br /> (PS: Have you noticed how things involving money usually gradually turn into nightmarish garbage in one way or another? That's what I've taken away from my understanding of economic history.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T17:40:12-08:00","id":7762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=7743#post7743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's what I call the &quot;drill sergeant&quot; effect. The drill sergeant is hurling abuse at you, sure, but he lets you know right off the bat that real combat is a thousand times worse than anything he can throw at you, and he genuinely wants you to improve, to be prepared for what is to come. His job is to make you better, so you take the abuse as the challenge it is rather than an insult.<br /> <br /> Mitchell &amp; Murray obviously wanted Baldwin's character to do the drill sergeant deal, but the character made no bones about the fact that he thought the salesmen were a complete waste of space, so the other characters took his &quot;pep talk&quot; for the insulting abuse it was.<br /> <br /> So yeah. Corporate America. Not that Communist Russia was any better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mhm, I think the drill-sergeant precedent is why Baldwin's speech caught on with people as much as it did. It's just surprising within the context of the film - i.e., the illegal and unethical acts the characters commit in desperation - that people can <i>still</i> look at the story and think that yes, the harsh always-be-closing mindset is absolutely the right one.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit biased, though. Always hated dealing with that kind of authority figure in real life. Accordingly, that scene in <i>Full Metal Jacket </i>where Private Pyle takes revenge on Hartman is one of my favorites in cinema. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T18:06:08-08:00","id":7776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=7675#post7675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The consensus from the convention I was at last year was that the movies are going with the Superman idea of a alien superhero, while the comics remain strictly mystic. (There's this enchantment on that hammer see?) When Captain America had been assassinated Thor summoned his ghost to ask if he wanted to be avenged. And then in the Ultimates during an alien invasion, that version of Thor summons the einherjar (dead heroes)...initially the Avengers thought him a madman...after doing that, there was a crisis of faith.<br /> Which segues nicely into the reason that was explained to me why Disney doesn't want the God in Thunder-God; <b>controversy</b>. They don't want to see such characters as the <a href=\"http://marvel.wikia.com/Arthur_Blackwood_(Earth-616)\" target=\"_blank\">Crusader</a> which attacked Thor because of his religious beliefs. They don't want to see Thor <a href=\"http://i138.photobucket.com/albums/q265/rychehitman/thor/REBIRTH/Issue%203/page_14.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">threaten the nation with a biblical deluge</a> as he once did when he became pissed at Iron Man and SHIELD. It's a whole lot safer (and profitable) if the movie version of Thor gets nice and neutered and plays nice with everyone else. Especially the federal government.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are looking at a few isolated events, the exceptions to the rule, and then saying, &quot;Yeah, that is how it is.&quot; However, when one looks at Marvel's Thor as a whole it is immediately evident how the comics approach the topic. The exceptions you highlight do not amount to enough evidence to overturn the fifty years of evidence for the other side of the question. Obviously, you don't like that approach, but that doesn't change the fact that is how Marvel has approached it since the beginning.<br /> <br /> Next weekend is looking like a bust for me for movies. I might go see <b>About Time</b>. Has anyone seen that one yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T19:45:36-08:00","id":7828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=7192#post7192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else going to see the Doctor Who 50th Anniversary Special in theaters?</div> </div> </div> </div> Im still debating that one. They only show it in the capital in my country so that would mean 150 dollars just taking the bus there and if i dont get some place to crash it would mean 50 more in a hotel. But on the other hand while it may seems like to much people do the same for a concert and i never care enough of going to one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T20:36:24-08:00","id":7851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=7776#post7776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are looking at a few isolated events, the exceptions to the rule, and then saying, &quot;Yeah, that is how it is.&quot; However, when one looks at Marvel's Thor as a whole it is immediately evident how the comics approach the topic. The exceptions you highlight do not amount to enough evidence to overturn the fifty years of evidence for the other side of the question. Obviously, you don't like that approach, but that doesn't change the fact that is how Marvel has approached it since the beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I see this in reverse.<br /> The few isolated stuff is in favor of the science crap.<br /> Fifty years of evidence is hyperbole for not reading the original stuff...or reading the material after Simonson, who recreated Mjolnir for Beta Ray Bill with all the enchantments built into &quot;Stormbreaker.&quot;<br /> And when Mjolnir was damaged, it took Dr. Strange to fix it.<br /> Marvel approached <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thor_(Marvel_Comics)\" target=\"_blank\">Thor</a> from the beginning as a desire to top the Hulk:<br /> <i><br /> Lee in 2002 described Thor's genesis early in the Marvel pantheon, following the creation of the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hulk_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\">Hulk</a>:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> [H]ow do you make someone stronger than the strongest person? It finally came to me: Don't make him human \u2014 make him a god. I decided readers were already pretty familiar with the Greek and Roman gods. It might be fun to delve into the old Norse legends...</div></i><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <br /> <br /> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T02:38:31-08:00","id":7942,"title":"","content":"Pure, no mystical stuff doesn't seem particularly evident in the movie either, when Odin does stuff like cast an enchantment over Mjolnir or Loki is referred to as a master of sorcery, but I guess that's not worth paying attention to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T02:44:01-08:00","id":7944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=7736#post7736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never really understood the difference between magic and science as aesthetics in fiction anyway. I mean, honestly, what's the difference between a ray gun and a wand that shoots beams of fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the time there isn't. When it's good fantasy, well...<br /> <br /> Look at the Wikipedia article &quot;magical thinking&quot;; that basically describes the premises I apply to what goes on in good fantasy.<br /> <br /> Science fiction often deviates heavily from what is actually possible or practical, but when it's decent, it's at least vaguely guided by principles of determining the mechanistic responses of physical and chemical phenomena and levering those into desired results.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T07:09:54-08:00","id":8034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thor has appeared in just shy of 4,900 comic books. I have read about 3,500 of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sure. And how you interpret them is up to you. (When Thor was transformed into a frog, I'm sure you had to stretch your mind on that one)<br /> I've already cited instances and given pages that have proven my point.<br /> If you want Superman to have long blonde hair and swings a mean hammer, I'm not going to change your opinion that the comic books have a Norse God of Thunder, fighting for a planet where he was once worshipped.<br /> <br /> And since this isn't going anywhere, how about a couple more pics?<br /> Skurge, the Executioner <a href=\"http://wac.450f.edgecastcdn.net/80450F/comicsalliance.com/files/2011/04/thor16.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">handed an M16 assault rifle</a>, and looking <a href=\"http://i345.photobucket.com/albums/p388/proteus_lives/Scan11816.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">awesome</a>.<br /> And here he is <a href=\"http://wac.450f.edgecastcdn.net/80450F/comicsalliance.com/files/2011/04/thor17.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">holding the bridge at Gjallerbru</a> and dying a noble death.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T09:41:11-08:00","id":8154,"title":"","content":"Is the Thor in the movie somebody who <i>wasn't</i> once worshipped? Did I hallucinate Selvig's familiarity with everything Thor was talking about in the first movie? Or how Odin transformed Thor into a mortal by shouting at him and then told Mjolnir that it would bestow its power on somebody who was worthy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T10:11:31-08:00","id":8178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=8034#post8034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've already cited instances and given pages that have proven my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just going to say one last thing, and then leave it alone. I am sure in your mind you have &quot;proven your point&quot; but as several of us are trying to point out, you haven't. Compared to the mountain of evidence representing the other side of the discussion, you have yet to put a dent in it. As you said though, you have a right to your own interpretation. Just don't take it personal when the meager references you have provided aren't enough to change anyone else's minds on the topic.<br /> <br /> Thor 3 predictions anyone? I am hoping for a movie interpretation of Marvel's take on Ragnarok. A lot of that depends on how the other Marvel movies play out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T11:56:18-08:00","id":8278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing that the mini-scene in the credits of Thor 2 was more a set-up for Guardians of the Galaxy or Avengers 3 than it was for Thor 3; though obviously that's pure speculation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guardians, yeah. Benicio del Toro is the villain in that one.<br /> <br /> As to what the third movie will be about...well, the final reveal before the credits pretty well indicates whom the villain will be, but as to plot, I've no idea. Maybe they'll dip into the current run of Thor comics to do the whole &quot;Thor of the future&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T12:43:09-08:00","id":8304,"title":"","content":"They are <a href=\"http://www.inquisitr.com/1025872/thor-3-ragnarok-desired-by-chris-hemsworth-for-thor-the-dark-world-sequel/\" target=\"_blank\">talking about Thor 3</a> <img src=\"http://cdn.inquisitr.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/Thor-3-Ragnarok-Desired-By-Chris-Hemsworth-For-Thor-The-Dark-World-Sequel-665x385.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> Apparently Hemsworth wants Thor to face off against Surtr. But it's just talk for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T14:21:27-08:00","id":17304,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.aintitcool.com/node/65196\" target=\"_blank\">This review</a> has it pegged for me:<br /> <i>&quot;THE HUNGER GAMES: CATCHING FIRE exceeds expectations so much that I'm legitimately worried that the MOCKINGJAY films won't be able to deliver on the promise of this movie. I'm definitely steering clear of the book this time; at the end of CATCHING FIRE, I was full of anticipation the likes that I hadn't felt since I was a kid, wondering just how in the hell Luke Skywalker was going to get Han Solo away from the clutches of Jabba the Hutt.<br /> ....CATCHING FIRE is a great sequel that exceeds the original in almost every way, a rare enough creature these days that deserves to be celebrated. This franchise has its EMPIRE STRIKES BACK, and now the real question is whether or not they can live up to the gauntlet thrown down here. It's going to be fun to see them try. </i><br /> ----------------<br /> I have to admit, it was fantastic.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T13:17:16-08:00","id":17889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=17304#post17304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.aintitcool.com/node/65196\" target=\"_blank\">This review</a> has it pegged for me:<br /> <i>&quot;THE HUNGER GAMES: CATCHING FIRE exceeds expectations so much that I'm legitimately worried that the MOCKINGJAY films won't be able to deliver on the promise of this movie. I'm definitely steering clear of the book this time; at the end of CATCHING FIRE, I was full of anticipation the likes that I hadn't felt since I was a kid, wondering just how in the hell Luke Skywalker was going to get Han Solo away from the clutches of Jabba the Hutt.<br /> ....CATCHING FIRE is a great sequel that exceeds the original in almost every way, a rare enough creature these days that deserves to be celebrated. This franchise has its EMPIRE STRIKES BACK, and now the real question is whether or not they can live up to the gauntlet thrown down here. It's going to be fun to see them try. </i><br /> ----------------<br /> I have to admit, it was fantastic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was actually disappointed by Mockingjay, but the screen adaptations have actually improved the first two books (I particularly like the expanded scenes in the Capital as a means of plot exposition). I'm more than a tad worried about the fact that they've split Mockingjay into two movies, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T10:21:59-08:00","id":19247,"title":"","content":"I'll just leave this one here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Jr5rzSMNmRM\" target=\"_blank\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Jr5rzSMNmRM\" data-code=\"Jr5rzSMNmRM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Jr5rzSMNmRM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ultron is one of my favourite Avengers villains, so I'm pretty excited. Judging from this teaser, it seems Tony Stark will be Ultron's creator in the cinematic universe. It's too soon to be sure, though.</div></div> </div> </div></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T17:09:50-08:00","id":19441,"title":"","content":"So, I watched Thor: the Dark World over the weekend. It was pretty cool, like all the Marvel movies. I just had one thought on a particular scene:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Just after Thor has released Loki, Loki is taking the opportunity to test his limits by heckling his savior with various illusions. Thor takes these juvenile antics in stride, until Loki pulls out a disguise of Captain America, mocking the Captain's patriotism and devotion to justice. It's only at this point that Thor shows true anger, shoving Loki into a pillar and covering his mouth. Now, the obvious reason for this would be that Asgardian guards happen to be walking past at that moment, but I think Thor would have done that anyway.<br /> <br /> The Avengers bonded during their first outing together, becoming friends forged in the fire of battle. But of all the various personalities on display, Thor and Steve Rogers have the most in common: Both are honorable, noble warriors, dedicated to a righteous path, and totally and utterly loyal to their people. It would not surprise me to learn that Thor respects Steve more than any other human, and that impugning the Captain's purity would be a serious berserk button.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I'm just reading to much in to it, I don't know.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T19:37:11-08:00","id":20941,"title":"","content":"Breaking news say Paul Walker, co-star of the Fast &amp; Furious franchise, died in a car crash today in California. I know they are still filming F&amp;F7, but I don't know what has and hasn't been done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T22:52:23-08:00","id":21009,"title":"","content":"Paul Walker and another person, yeah. My sympathies to their loved ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T19:43:25-08:00","id":30215,"title":"","content":"<b><u>The Hobbit: The Desolation of Smaug</u></b><br /> <br /> The movie may have its flaws, but I wasn't seeing any. Ok I admit, Laketown annoyed me. But I thought the history given was good.<br /> And for me, most of the additions done by Jackson not only worked, they worked well. Especially Tauriel. Her character and the small story arc with her added some nice moments that gave a bit of warmth that I felt was needed.<br /> I shall be seeing this again.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T10:49:21-08:00","id":30486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=30215#post30215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>The Hobbit: The Desolation of Smaug</u></b><br /> <br /> The movie may have its flaws, but I wasn't seeing any. Ok I admit, Laketown annoyed me. But I thought the history given was good.<br /> And for me, most of the additions done by Jackson not only worked, they worked well. Especially Tauriel. Her character and the small story arc with her added some nice moments that gave a bit of warmth that I felt was needed.<br /> I shall be seeing this again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am reposting this from my Facebook:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#37404E\"><span style=\"font-family:lucida grande\">The Hobbit: The Desolation of Smaug is very good. Excluding a few technical issues (that I won't go into to avoid spoilers), the movie was exciting and entertaining. If you enjoyed the first one, you should enjoy this one as well and probab</span></span><span style=\"color:#37404E\"><span style=\"font-family:lucida grande\">ly a little bit more.<br /> <br /> That said, as a life long fan of the source material, I do not like a lot of the changes Peter Jackson made to this portion of the story. While the first movie featured some small changes to Tolkien's tale, I felt Jackson was still working within the realm of what I would consider Tolkien's work. This film features major changes to the narrative, as well as the creation of completely new characters and story lines. At this point, Peter Jackson's The Hobbit is only loosely based on the narrative penned by Tolkien. While the movie buff in me enjoyed the movie, the literature buff in me did not.<br /> <br /> Anyone who knows me, knows I am an advocate for, &quot;The movie is not the book, the book is not the movie.&quot; That said, I am still disappointed because The Hobbit had everything it needed to be a great movie. Jackson's influence does not make the story any better, just different.<br /> <br /> All that aside, Smaug is... absolutely amazing. Jackson did an absolutely brilliant job in capturing everything that is great and terrifying about the dragon. Jackson's Smaug is the new high bar when it comes to this mythical creature in film.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T15:33:31-08:00","id":51110,"title":"","content":"So I just saw 12 Years a Slave. Quite good, including in several ways I wouldn't have expected (the soundtrack was effectively punchy), and appropriately unsettling, but... also kind of unsettling in weird, uncomfortable ways.<br /> <br /> Like, it's weird that I think the character I might have the most... not quite sympathy, not quite identification, but something within that band, towards Michael Fassbender's character, right? I don't know, something about how crazy and violent he is, but also kind of pathetic and figuratively (and possibly literally) impotent he is, he keeps sticking out in my mind.<br /> <br /> Like, at the end, where he's <i>really</i> adamant against letting Northup go and complaining about the money he paid for him and such, I almost feel kind of perversely sorry for him, like thinking &quot;hey, at least maybe he'll get some kind of state compensation to recoup his loss&quot;, and I feel awfully dirty.<br /> <br /> It's probably the strangest response I've ever had to a film.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T12:25:35-08:00","id":51776,"title":"","content":"I know I'm really late to the party on these, but I finally got to watch <b>The Dark Knight Rises</b> and <b>The Man of Steel</b>.<br /> <br /> For The Dark Knight Rises, using spoiler in case there's anyone who's not been able to see it even longer than me:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I thought it was a good finish to the series, and I like how it could be taken into a new series with &quot;Robin&quot;. I'm probably too aware of the mythology for Talia to have been a surprise, so I had her pegged early on. Making Bane less super-solider and more devoted nut-case from the League of Shadows was a nice way to make him fit the established mythology. I'm still waffling on the part about Bruce fixing the auto-pilot: on one hand, it's a classic Batman move; on the other hand, this Batman always seemed more willing to die executing the crazy-ass moves. It may have been just a tad over hyped by the people I know who'd seen it in theatres, but I'm in Colorado, so there was that fun, extra level of &quot;I might die seeing this&quot; tension over the movie. All in all, not a bad movie.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> For The Man of Steel, same as above, spoilers:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Now I see why the had Russell Crowe as Jor-El. This is not the gentle Marlon Brando style Jor-El. This is a Jor-El who's seen war and needs to be believable kicking ass and taking names. Kevin Costner as Jonathan Kent also made more sense as the movie went on, especially once he let the tornado take him to show Clark he meant what he said. Henry Cavill had a good look for the character and pulled off the performance pretty well. It's not easy to be that sincere and upstanding without being cheesy. Christopher Reeve had a harder time of it with each sequel. Henry Cavill did good this time, we'll see if he has the stamina to stay that way. The way Krypton was shown I think worked very well for it's early sci-fi pulp roots, somewhat over the top, but just enough to make it &quot;not just humans in space&quot;. Zach Snyder was also a good choice because this movie needs to be kind of over the top, it's friggin' Superman, after all. I didn't like how quickly he had a costume, though. I know it's just a red &amp; blue suit in the established Kryptonian style, but still....too quick and easy. My favorite part has to be how they made sure Lois Lane is not a blind idiot. She already knows who he really is and she has to PRETEND SHE DOESN'T (which would have made the whole &quot;romantic comedy&quot; style of Lois &amp; Clark about 50 times funnier, I think). Makes about 10,000 times more sense than this smart reporter being fooled by a pair of glasses. Again, all in all, not a bad movie.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T23:42:57-08:00","id":52188,"title":"","content":"Well said on Man of Steel, Papa Bear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T09:00:54-08:00","id":52451,"title":"","content":"Saw Wolf of Wall Street last night. It was an excellent film. Not the best work for Scorsese or Leo but very funny. In fact, while it may have had its rather serious moments it was still funny in them. The only thingg that got me was with all the drugs they were doing, I was expecting to hear The Rolling Stones song he plays every time people are doing drugs. Don't want to ggo into gratuitous details and spoil anything.<br /> <br /> when I saw it though I also saw some of the new movie PVs. I'm really excited to see Monument Men. It looks excellent and has an all star cast. I'm also looking forward to Noah. Not because I'm a fan of the bible, bible stories or all of that. Its got an excellent cast and its Darron Aronofsky film and looks excellent. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T09:41:25-08:00","id":55511,"title":"","content":"Yeah, having just recently watch The Dark Knight Rises and The Man of Steel and Green Lantern, there does seem to be just a bit too much focus on blowing stuff up and action scenes and not quiet enough on &quot;reasons to give a crap about these people&quot;.<br /> <br /> Related rant: I think they're too afraid of making people feel something, because (according to the executives) that doesn't belong in the big summer superhero movies.....y'know, despite the fact that both the Christopher Reeve Superman and Michael Keaton Batman did exactly that......idjits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T09:58:10-08:00","id":55529,"title":"","content":"Can someone with the power of Superman fight others like himself without any collateral damage? Kind of reminiscent of the Hulk going to war and banging away at the San Andreas Fault. He won't be stopped without a lot of banging...anyway.<br /> I thought that the director shot for a sense of &quot;realism&quot; in that..well when giants fight it out people (and buildings) will get stepped on regardless of how super-careful one is.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of how silly it is to catch someone in mid-air while flying fast. How can that happen without any harm to the person caught, when an adult running as fast as he can into anyone can seriously hurt the person being run into?<br /> <br /> Sorry, I ramble a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T07:09:44-08:00","id":56101,"title":"","content":"They must not have had the Timm/Dini team working on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T07:48:51-08:00","id":56126,"title":"","content":"I've said this before, but I really get the impression that DC is trying to bring back the nineties, when style was more important than substance and the audience was teenaged pocket-miners who just wanted to see big dudes punch things and hot chicks strut around in poses. I guess I can't blame them for that if that's what the market wants, but the hell of it is, I don't know anyone who wants that. I never see those seemingly hypothetical rabid fans of Nehru collars in the only comic shop in town; it's all middle-aged guys like me who are weary of this sort of thing (or at least that's how everyone says they feel; maybe they're putting on airs to cover for their guilty pleasures) who like good stories like you can find at Marvel and Image, guys who keep saying things like, &quot;Well, DC just canceled the last book of theirs I actually liked reading.&quot;<br /> <br /> I suppose there must be an audience for Nu52. It's been going on too long for this to be a charade of denial and self-delusion, of creators insisting that if they keep pretending they're making the stuff we in the audience want then it will become true that we want it. I just don't know where those people <i>are</i>, though.<br /> <br /> Maybe they're the people who like <b>Man of Steel</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T08:43:52-08:00","id":56163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=56126#post56126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said this before, but I really get the impression that DC is trying to bring back the nineties, when style was more important than substance and the audience was teenaged pocket-miners who just wanted to see big dudes punch things and hot chicks strut around in poses. I guess I can't blame them for that if that's what the market wants, but the hell of it is, I don't know anyone who wants that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they are under the impression that is what the market wants because most of the people working on the books and making the decisions are <i>guys who grew up reading those comics in the 90s</i>. Problem is, most of those guys either quit reading the books or they don't have the money to spare on comic books or (like me) haven't been able to keep up over the years and now have attempted to get back into it <i>only to find the very things that made me walk away in the first place.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T08:45:08-08:00","id":56164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=56126#post56126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe they're the people who like <b>Man of Steel</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey come on, by most accounts Man of Steel was an awesome movie.<br /> <br /> I just wish that they had used a different name, since Man of Steel might imply it was a superman movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T11:46:47-08:00","id":56258,"title":"","content":"As far as DC animation goes, the recently released JLA Adventures: Trapped in Time seems a lot better. The characters are the new 52 versions, but the characterization and the storytelling are closer to what made the DC animated movies so good in the first place. Not to mention stuff like the classic Legion of Doom headquarters and a cameo by a certain pair of people and their dog... It is not the best ( and like most stories involving time travel and mysterious foes, it is has plot holes) but it is miles away from Justice League: War.<br /> <br /> That said, it seems to be available only in a single store chain and I think only in the US, which sort of smells like DC sabotaging itself, though I'm not business savvy enough to know what can be going on behind that decision. I just hope they don't use the lower sales that will likely come out of this approach to justify doing more EXTREEEEEME! 90s revival stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T14:48:24-08:00","id":56370,"title":"","content":"Sadly I finally watched Oblivion. I want the money back i didn't pay to see it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T17:57:13-08:00","id":56476,"title":"","content":"I just saw two films at the local dollar theater, and I'm glad I didn't pay more for either.<br /> <br /> <b>Thor: the Dark World</b> was sadly kind of forgettable. Usually I leave one of these films wanting to talk about some part of it, but most of it just sort of slid out of my mind as soon as the house lights came up. It criminally under-used the acting talent assembled. The best parts of it were Loki and Thor verbally sparring. The worst parts were... well... the entire behavior pattern of the Dark Elves, who are bad guys <i>just because</i>. What exactly would &quot;returning the universe to darkness&quot; do? They didn't actually seem particularly uncomfortable in the world as it was, so what was so great about the old setup that they felt it worth wrecking everything else to reproduce? Also, Thor and Jane's &quot;romance&quot; is at the &quot;do you like me? check yes/no&quot; note-passing Jr. High phase, not the Swearing-Devotion-Across-the-Cosmos-and-Eternities phase. But that hasn't exactly changed from the first movie.<br /> <br /> The other movie was <b>Ender's Game</b>. My initial prediction was correct - way too much of that book happened inside of its protagonist's head for an easy screen translation. But even the stuff that wasn't Ender's internal struggles was pretty under-developed<i>. </i>I can forgive the drop in emphasis on Peter and Valentine, who only got their sequel-establishing sub-plot when the short story became a novel. But the other kids at Battle School and the Battle School Game itself were practically footnotes. Everyone seemed to be trying very hard, but it was just a bad script to start with. It was nice to see Harrison Ford actually giving a crap about his part, as a lot of his recent movies have felt pretty phoned-in. I liked the visuals a lot, but wish they'd used them to tell more actual story, instead of just kind of shuffling us from one set piece to the next as quickly as possible while the kid playing Ender looks like he's going to cry because the writers haven't provided him anything more interesting to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T09:52:18-08:00","id":56833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=55511#post55511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Michael Keaton Batman</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is one that has aged terribly.<br /> <br /> Not in a special effects sense, just that with more than twenty years of perspective, the shimmer has faded a lot.<br /> <br /> It still <i>looks</i> pretty good, but the character of Batman himself is a weird cipher (and not just because of his cavalier attitude towards human life; despite comics purism, you can theoretically get away with a Batman willing to kill people, assuming you don't opt from the outset to include the &quot;no killing&quot; part of the mythology), and the plot meanders aimlessly for ages before stumbling towards a conclusion.<br /> <br /> Even Jack Nicholson's Joker... the performance itself is good, but his actual presence in the story is undermined by inconsistencies and vagaries, although some of the specific scenes have enough audacity to almost save it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isat