yxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T06:38:54-08:00","id":61507,"title":"","content":"I did not know Macfarlane is making a new movie right now. It's something about a farmer trying to win back his girlfriend in the old west, or something. I don't know. All I know is, <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/media/rm858445568/rg1528338944?ref_=hm_snp_i1\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> is a poster for it, and I'm pretty much in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T11:45:07-08:00","id":63523,"title":"","content":"I heard about Jesse Eisenberg being cast as Lex Luthor in <b>Batman of Steel</b> or whatever they're actually calling it, and I had no reaction because I don't care. The original movie did not sell me on a sequel. Let them cast whomever they want for whatever role they want.<br /> <br /> Yesterday, though, a thought struck me.<br /> <br /> Lex Luthor is an evil man whose superpower is having lots of money and controlling the media...and they hired a Jew to play him.<br /> <br /> I hope the movie is very, very careful about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T13:32:29-08:00","id":63577,"title":"","content":"Well, I had some doubts about them making &quot;The Dark Knight Returns.&quot; And I was somewhat accepting of Affleck in the Batman role since this is set in a potential future and Bruce Wayne will look aged anyway. But...Eisenberg? I like the actor in other movies well enough. But this seems very miscast to me. *sigh* But then I had doubts about Heath Ledger too...<br /> <img src=\"http://i7.photobucket.com/albums/y297/neios/meanwhile_zps67c3f4e1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T18:37:58-08:00","id":63680,"title":"","content":"Oh...my...God... You mean it's true...<br /> <br /> When I saw this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gIntDen7fv0\" data-code=\"gIntDen7fv0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/gIntDen7fv0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I thought it was a joke. You know them making fun of how progressively stupid they're handling the next Superman film. Ben Affleck as Batman? I'm fine with that. Affleck's a talented actor and he could do it quite well. Batman being Man of Steel 2? ...What? No he shouldn't be there. Maybe Wayne could show up in a bit role to build things up for his movie and the Justice League movie but <i>not </i>Batman! Wonder Woman in there as well? WHAT?! Is this the Justice League movie or Man of Steel 2? These guys are way too desperate to catch up to Marvel.<br /> <br /> But Eisenberg as Lex Luthor...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *Sighs* I love DC, more than I love Marvel, so when I see WB doing such bonehead moves it frustrates me. Why is Batman the only DC character they seem to be able to do right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T04:31:19-08:00","id":63873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=63523#post63523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lex Luthor is an evil man whose superpower is having lots of money and controlling the media...and they hired a Jew to play him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mark Zuckerberg is a real life evil person whose superpower is having lots of money and controlling social media, and he's a Jew...ish person.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Lex Luthor as a 21st century digital media type self-made billionaire is not the worst take a modern movie could have; at the very least, it would manage to be distinct, since Luthor as supervillain and corporate overlord has already been done and done well repeatedly.<br /> <br /> I mean, just having Jesse Eisenberg outright play Lex Luthor as Mark Zuckerberg wouldn't be very good, but I don't think casting him intrinsically portends to bad things. I mean, the guy <i>is</i> an Academy Award nominated actor (in a capacity that more broadly means something than it does for, say, Nicholas Cage).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T05:11:32-08:00","id":63889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=63873#post63873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, just having Jesse Eisenberg outright play Lex Luthor as Mark Zuckerberg wouldn't be very good, but I don't think casting him intrinsically portends to bad things.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not intrinsically. Like I said, I just hope they're careful with what they're doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T07:27:42-08:00","id":63962,"title":"","content":"When I was at a patient's house the other day, some old movie was on; I looked up the title but have since forgotten it. Not really the point. The scene I saw (and to judge from Wikipedia's synopsis, this scene was not representative of the movie as a whole, which it bills as a comedy) was Jimmy Stewart working as a salesperson in a boutique owned by the Wizard of Oz. Oz was having marital troubles--his wife was spending was too much money, and Oz didn't have the guts to cut her off--that were distracting him at work, which meant he wasn't complimenting Jimmy Stewart every time Jimmy managed to not trip over his own dick on the way to the toilet, which Jimmy took as a sign that the boss had it out for him. Jimmy confronted Oz about it, but Oz didn't want to discuss his marital problems with an employee and was stressed out to boot, so they got into an argument and Jimmy Stewart had to decide whether he'd stay or leave.<br /> <br /> I was fascinated. It was a scene--and as far as I knew at the time, a movie--about misunderstandings and miscommunications brought on by dueling senses of pride, and what's more, it was...how can I put this? It made me realize I can't remember the last time I watched a movie about things that could actually happen in the real world. I want to see more of that. God-aliens beating up elves is fun and all, but I feel like I imagine an old-time sailor feels when he gets to shore after a month and can finally have something to eat other than pickled meat. I feel starved for something I didn't realize I was missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T09:32:14-08:00","id":64068,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this is one of the reasons I love the older movies. Seems only the British are still making movies that are just about shit that happens to people. TV has pretty much taken over the &quot;stuff that happens to people&quot; drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T11:39:48-08:00","id":64157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er... yeah, you should watch more of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I miss when there were video rental stores in town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T11:50:44-08:00","id":64171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>The Little Shop Around the Corner</i>.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing about classic films...<br /> <br /> Storytelling styles have changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that <i>Shop Around the Corner</i> basically wrote the formula for every romantic comedy ever written and is being copied to this day, sometimes almost literally in the case of <i>You've Got Mail</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T12:20:20-08:00","id":64202,"title":"","content":"I passed on The Dark Knight of Steel so I really couldn't care less about Daredevil vs Superman with Wonder Woman the scrawny amazon. Don't get me wrong I think Gal Gadot is a beautiful woman, but she shouldn't be playing Wonder Woman.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T13:46:10-08:00","id":64285,"title":"","content":"Just in general I've seen actors that everyone said would be terrible for a role do fantastic at it. I've seen actors that everyone said would be perfect for a role do terrible at it. I've seen movies that have all the right actors in all the right roles that turned out to be complete crap, and I've seen movies where it was nothing but bit-actors that turned out fantastic.<br /> <br /> Good actors are just that. Hold off on saying someone can't hold a role down until you see them do that role. If you want an example, there was a time when Leslie Nielsen could only ever be cast in dramatic movie roles because nobody in the industry could possibly see him working out as anything but a dramatic actor.<br /> <br /> <br /> Getting down on a movie in the early stages... eh I'll do it, but mostly for writing and directing, because you can at least know the general tendencies of the director and the writers, and you can at least argue that the direction they want to go in is one that you don't think fits the established character or style of previous media... Making superman a dark and gritty character for example, or Michael Bay doing a remake of Anne of Green Gables... While it might be fully possible that he could do a lovely job on the latter, given his fondness for explosions I'd expect he'd try to put them in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T13:49:17-08:00","id":64290,"title":"","content":"It recently occurred to me that <i>The Lego Movie</i> is probably the closest thing we'll ever get to a Justice League movie. I don't know how this makes me feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T14:03:54-08:00","id":64300,"title":"","content":"hmm..I recall reading that Warner Bros wanted Joss Whedon to make a Wonder Woman movie, but he eventually turned it down. He just couldn't find the right way to present the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T14:23:27-08:00","id":64309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not as though most male super-heroes have been cast exclusively from a pool of actors who have an appropriate physical build.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't Christopher Reeve have to put on thirty or fifty pounds before they'd let him wear the tights? I used to have a book about the making of the Superman movies, and there's a story of how the first day of his physical training (with David Prowse, the guy who wore the Darth Vader suit), he threw up and passed out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=64300#post64300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall reading that Warner Bros. wanted Joss Whedon to make a Wonder Woman movie, but he eventually turned it down. He just couldn't find the right way to present the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that how it went? I heard they passed on his scripts, more or less firing him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T14:44:27-08:00","id":64321,"title":"","content":"Ah! <a href=\"https://&#91;url=http://insidetv.ew.com/2013/09/24/joss-whedon-interview/3/\" target=\"_blank\">]I stand corrected</a>...<i>It is hard. She\u2019s a tough nut to crack. I know she\u2019s famous as a television show, but I don\u2019t think she lends herself to television. I think she only works on an epic scale. I saw a bit of the David E. Kelley [NBC pilot]. That was not a good marriage.</i> It was <a href=\"http://www.complex.com/pop-culture/2013/07/comic-book-movies-that-almost-happened-but-didnt/joss-whedon-wonder-woman\" target=\"_blank\">Warner Bros</a> that did him in...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T18:50:56-08:00","id":64491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=61507#post61507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not know Macfarlane is making a new movie right now. It's something about a farmer trying to win back his girlfriend in the old west, or something. I don't know. All I know is, <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/media/rm858445568/rg1528338944?ref_=hm_snp_i1\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> is a poster for it, and I'm pretty much in.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... ugh. I'm conflicted. On the one hand, hooray NHP in <i>anything</i>. On the other hand, Seth Macfarlane is a <i>disease</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T19:00:34-08:00","id":64495,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/BHKb8cU.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T19:36:07-08:00","id":64514,"title":"","content":"I don't hate Eisenberg's casting, but funny is funny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T20:00:33-08:00","id":64529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not once have I heard anyone say anything negative about her acting ability, or personality </div> </div> </div>I have. I can't comment myself, because I never had any interest in watching any of the Fast &amp; Furious movies, but I've seem/heard a <i>lot</i> of people complain that Gadot's acting in that was pretty poor (sometimes alongside comments on her being too skinny, sometimes not - in which case it usually took the form of &quot;she can bulk up for the movie, but she would need a lot more time to become a good actress&quot;).<br /> <br /> It is my main worry for sure, especially after being informed she was training to get a more appropriate physique for the role. Though not <i>that </i>big a worry, since I have pretty low expectations for the movie anyway =P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T22:39:48-08:00","id":64614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, if someone can't take something as nuanced and sophisticated as a Fast and Furious script and deliver a performance worthy of an Oscar, they must be a shit actor.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the first movie is any indication, it is not like Wonder Bat of Steel is gonna be all that sophisticated either XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T03:07:44-08:00","id":64712,"title":"","content":"Huh, Jonah Hill is only thirty. Somehow I expect him to be older.<br /> <br /> Actually, Jonah Hill as the Penguin seems like it would be inspired casting...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T03:18:08-08:00","id":64718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That Heath Ledger kid was too pretty and effeminate to pull off the Joker, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know it's funny, for all the &quot;Christopher Nolan stripping out comic book-isms&quot; stuff, looking at the one shot we get of the Joker without any of the makeup, I almost feel like he'd have actually come across as more off-putting and sinister if he'd spent the whole movie looking like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T05:53:10-08:00","id":64773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That Heath Ledger kid was too pretty and effeminate to pull off the Joker, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's at least possible Heath Ledger got very lucky with that role in that he had access to Gary Oldman, who is one of the very best portrayers of terrifying psychopaths currently living. That isn't intended to take away from Mr. Ledger's performance, though; no matter who coached him or what advice he got, he did well with the role. I only bring it up because I don't know Gal Gadot has access to those same resources in terms of someone who can give her good advice, learned from years of experience, on how to play Wonder Woman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T07:04:46-08:00","id":64813,"title":"","content":"A hot chick filling out a teddy fighting crime...and that's not sexist at all?<br /> <br /> ...hmm...don't know about that.<br /> <br /> My personal favorite pic of WW:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i1174.photobucket.com/albums/r610/wonelson/WonderWoman_zpsdfbf1629.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Good muscle tone, strong facial features...and yeah, she fills out that teddy. Which means boobs as well as...everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 02-04-2014, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T08:05:15-08:00","id":64843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=64813#post64813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A hot chick filling out a teddy fighting crime...and that's not sexist at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, for women in comic books, a teddy is downright Victorian...but no, no, that's the wrong tack to take. It comes off like I'm making excuses. The real answer is, I don't know if Wonder Woman's costume is sexist. It's about as revealing as a man's spandex is in comics, and it seems to have been designed in the same thought process as male costumes (&quot;be bright and shiny and attract attention to the logo&quot;), but at the same time, a woman in underwear just doesn't come across the same as a man in underwear generally does. I guess I'm going to say it's not inherently sexist until the artist starts drawing her in poses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=64813#post64813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good muscle tone, strong facial features...and yeah, she fills out that teddy. Which means boobs as well as...everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>...What's your point?<br /> <br /> EDIT: As long as we're off on image-based tangents, here's a costume design I wouldn't mind seeing in a movie (though personally, I'd have added more armor, like at least greaves):<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://img.gawkerassets.com/img/18jedx2pw5o35png/ku-xlarge.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I personally don't see what's not sexy about a woman in pants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 02-04-2014, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T09:30:52-08:00","id":64918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=64843#post64843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's about as revealing as a man's spandex is in comics, and it seems to have been designed in the same thought process as male costumes (&quot;be bright and shiny and attract attention to the logo&quot;), but at the same time, a woman in underwear just doesn't come across the same as a man in underwear generally does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the biggest giveaway is the fact that the costume stops just above her breast line. Clothing on women that doesn't reach the neck or shoulders is generally meant to draw emphasis in a manner that is attractive.<br /> <br /> There's that whole discussion on whether attractive clothing is empowering for women or not, which... is a bit beyond me at the moment, but at the most basic I'll say that at least that plays into the intent of Wonder Woman.<br /> <br /> Of course, the intent of that for Wonder Woman in her initial conception is actually something I see as a lot less ambiguous in terms of intent (and, in my view, success) of empowerment, since being portrayed as a sexually secure and powerful woman was part of the original point of her, at a time when you didn't see much of that kind of thing from any portrayal of women. It really was pretty good for its time, and I can even see an argument for maintenance for legacy purposes, although I personally would prefer something of an update.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: As long as we're off on image-based tangents, here's a costume design I wouldn't mind seeing in a movie (though personally, I'd have added more armor, like at least greaves):<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://img.gawkerassets.com/img/18jedx2pw5o35png/ku-xlarge.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome.<br /> <br /> As for the casting of Wonder Woman, while I don't really feel in a position to prejudge the actor, and while the degree to which Wonder Woman's superhuman strength is reflected in her physique varies between portrayals, I would have at least preferred it if there had been cast somebody with less of a conventionally attractive body shape that could also serve as a visual signifier for physical prowess, just because that's a subject of neglect in Hollywood blockbusters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T09:35:14-08:00","id":64921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=64843#post64843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...What's your point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sex sells. The comic book readership has always been dominated by the hetero-sexual male. Yeah, I know no one wants to hear that.<br /> A good example was the joke that some made of an Avengers' poster for the movie earlier:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://24.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m3smyafagW1rs4ljfo1_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> WW's costume underwent several changes and even added legging a few years ago. (I believe) And it always went back to the teddy.<br /> If Wonder Woman is too skinny...I'm pretty sure that will be seen as a negative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T10:11:59-08:00","id":64946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=64921#post64921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sex sells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, maybe it's the shit mood I'm in right now, and maybe I'll feel bad about this later, but I am supremely fucking tired of the suggestion that I ought to base not only my personal tastes in artistic expression but also my sense of right and wrong on some appeal to capitalist success. So sex sells; so the fuck what? Apple products sell too, so should I suddenly be okay with the fact that they're manufactured by indentured Chinese servants who hate their working conditions so much the factories have to imprison them behind barred windows with safety netting installed on every floor in order to keep them from committing suicide by jumping out of the windows? Diamonds sell, so should I be okay with the way African warlords wipe out thousands of innocent people in pursuit of shiny rocks to sell to diamond conglomerates who artificially boost the price of diamonds by hoarding them to create scarcity where none exists? Walmart sells, so should I be okay with the fact that they deliberately pay their workers a subsistence wage and encourage them to apply for government assistance just to survive, such that the taxpayer is ultimately footing the bill for Walmart's salary plans?<br /> <br /> The almighty fucking dollar is not God, and it does not have some divine right to determine what I am okay with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=64921#post64921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The comic book readership has always been dominated by the heterosexual male.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>I'm</i> a heterosexual man, and personally, I'd prefer it if the industry would quit treating me like a pathetic pocket-miner who will only read about a woman if I can jack off to her. Hell, never mind if that's disrespectful to women,* and never mind if it's deliberately short-sighted to try to appeal to one demographic to the exclusion of a provable minority who want to be part of the fandom but feel unwelcome,* it's disrespectful to <i>me</i> and my intelligence. How about the industry does me the courtesy of thinking I want a good story about Wonder Woman and not drawings of round titties to stare at?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=64921#post64921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Wonder Woman is too skinny, then I'm pretty sure that will be seen as a negative.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if that's what people decide to bitch about, then I will continue to believe that such complaints are sexist bullshit.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Which it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T10:43:29-08:00","id":64972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=64946#post64946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, maybe it's the shit mood I'm in right now, and maybe I'll feel bad about this later, but I am supremely fucking tired of the suggestion that I ought to base not only my personal tastes in artistic expression but also my sense of right and wrong on some appeal to capitalist success. So sex sells; so the fuck what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Capitalism will get the movie made. Not your personal sense of artistic expression. (Unless you have a good deal of money. But then that would appeal to capitalism, so I guess not.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=64946#post64946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>I'm</i> a heterosexual man, and personally, I'd prefer it if the industry would quit treating me like a pathetic pocket-miner who will only read about a woman if I can jack off to her. Hell, never mind if that's disrespectful to women,* and never mind if it's deliberately short-sighted to try to appeal to one demographic to the exclusion of a provable minority who want to be part of the fandom but feel unwelcome,* it's disrespectful to <i>me</i> and my intelligence. How about the industry does me the courtesy of thinking I want a good story about Wonder Woman and not drawings of round titties to stare at?</div> </div> </div> </div>Write the producers. I'm sure they will be more than happy to cater to your personal sensibilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=64946#post64946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if that's what people decide to bitch about, then I will continue to believe that such complaints are sexist bullshit.<br /> *Which it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrugs* It's what most of the US public wants. If your leads (most of the time a sexy female is among them if not more of them) aren't appealing in any way, then that movie likely (not always) won't rake it in at the box office. Comedies seem to be the exception.<br /> On the theme, Superhero movies are pretty much always that way. &quot;She&quot; has to be appealing. It's part of the character. It's that connection between strong, independent, smart, and powerful. And it's always sexy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T10:59:46-08:00","id":64984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=64946#post64946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The almighty fucking dollar is not God, and it does not have some divine right to determine what I am okay with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll grant you the second, but I'm fairly certain the first is considered unamerican... after all it's stamped on the money to ensure that people trust god just as much as the almighty dollar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T11:24:30-08:00","id":65004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=64972#post64972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Capitalism will get the movie made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, so the fuck what? Capitalism got <b>the Room</b> made. That it has been or is being made does not mean I have to fucking agree with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=64972#post64972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Write the producers. I'm sure they will be more than happy to cater to your personal sensibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>And for a third time, so the fuck what? If the producers disagree with me, I am required to agree with them? My beliefs have to be validated by the current creative team?*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=64972#post64972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's what most of the US public wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the US public wants McDonald's and Nascar.<br /> <br /> <br /> *where the word &quot;creative&quot; is encased in fingerquotes so sarcastic they produce visible waves of light in a new, sarcastic band of the EM spectrum","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T12:32:13-08:00","id":65066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">First point: she's been quoted as saying that she has started an exercise and diet routine specifically intended to add muscle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will not say she can't do it, but she doesn't seem to have the frame for it so I will be surprised if she looks the part.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second point: I'm getting pretty irritated with how often this is being brought up as being the objection to the casting choice. It's not as though most male super-heroes have been cast exclusively from a pool of actors who have an appropriate physical build. The ones which are reasonably analogous in this regard are comparatively few; <b>especially at the time of casting.</b> Although more recently a number of them have gone out of their way to work towards Body by Jim Lee. Not once have I heard anyone say anything negative about her acting ability, or personality. It's exclusively been that she's too skinny, with about a 50/50 split between not having enough muscles and not having large enough breasts. </div> </div> </div>.[/quote]No, but at the same time it has often been done in the past and a good actor can't nessecarilly pull off every role. Looking the part can be very important. I personally am not talking about breasts. If that was a consideration that is something that could be faked just like Superman's or Batman's package if that was a worry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Third point: that tendency doesn't say anything good about Wonder Woman as a character... or more specifically, the audience reception towards Wonder Woman as a character. With the usual caveats that get tacked on when discussing a character that has had literally hundreds of different writers involved, Wonder Woman at her best is defined by an unfailing tenacity and toughness of character. Her best stories are about her agency, as she defines herself <b>by</b> herself, in defiance of her mother, the greek pantheon, societal expectations or the whims of super villains. </div> </div> </div>Look adds a lot fo the feel of a character. There are also quirks and inflections that can work against some actors/actresses. That is one big problem I have with the Duck as Batman. I think he is a perfectly good actor, but he can't seem to leave enough of himself behind and it colors every role he plays.<br /> <br /> Clooney is the same way.there is too much of him in every role. Honestly I hated Clooney as Batman, but though he was perfect for Bruce Wayne. Sam as I hated Brandon Routh as Clark Kent, but could have made a good Superman if the script didn't suck so bad. Both were roles that actually could have worked if they used to actors. Still that wouldn't have fixed the movies because they had bad scripts.<br /> <br /> And while I had some things I didn't like some of the new Batman I liked Christian Bale as Batman/Bruce Way because he is a method actor that can leave himself out of a role. Some of why so many Superhero movies fail is because they don't bother getting the right actors for a part. Either find an actor that fits the part or one that can become the part.<br /> <br /> Skipped the forth and fifth.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T13:14:45-08:00","id":65092,"title":"","content":"Bale worked for me. And despite misgivings Ledger worked for me. Especially after seeing a released pic of him in full makeup, which I thought was scary as hell. But I believe Nolan kept to the spirit of the characters, as well as retaining the general appearance. I have misgivings with Gadot as WW. Everything has to be near perfect if they don't want to stick with the iconic figure. And I mean that literally. Her figure was the iconic woman figure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T13:47:06-08:00","id":65107,"title":"","content":"I honestly have to kind of wonder what went on behind the scenes in this casting.<br /> <br /> Not in a negative way, mind, more... like, if it's just stunt casting, you'd expect somebody more well known.<br /> <br /> I suppose it could be agent business maneuvering, but I'd wonder at what somebody had to do to get this kind of pull.<br /> <br /> Could it be that she actually gave a good audition?<br /> <br /> I will, however, admit that Zack Snyder gives me a level of trepidation concerning the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T13:49:17-08:00","id"