div> </div>I'm not sure you understood the point of that joke.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T13:54:35-08:00","id":65115,"title":"","content":"Hey Shadowflame, I stand by my underlying points and everything, but I want to publicly apologize to you for being such a dick about it, with all the cursing and whatnot. I'm mad about some stuff going on, and I took it out on you. That's not okay, and I'm sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T14:28:33-08:00","id":65143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=64843#post64843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: As long as we're off on image-based tangents, here's a costume design I wouldn't mind seeing in a movie (though personally, I'd have added more armor, like at least greaves):<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://img.gawkerassets.com/img/18jedx2pw5o35png/ku-xlarge.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I personally don't see what's not sexy about a woman in pants.</div> </div> </div> </div>1)That's sexier than the normal getup, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> 2)Good Lord, if the comics had adopted that, I probably would have read them at some point.<br /> <br /> ...Shit, this is going to get me into the conversation, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T14:31:24-08:00","id":65147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure you understood the point of that joke</div> </div> </div> </div> I saw it as poking fun at the inherent sexism of the original poster. But then that's the point in casting a smoking hot redhead, which in turn is how the comic-book character is typically seen. JimB: I agree with you on some of those points. But those relate more to current social issues. A production that wants to sell a comic-book movie? Well...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T14:58:05-08:00","id":65163,"title":"","content":"Well, two bits: The bigger problem is that, if the general populace is anything like me on this instance, and for once I think they might, Wonder Woman becomes a very weird thing to take seriously at face value, which means it needs to not just be a good movie, it needs to be <i>very</i> good. When the Justice League animated series was on TV, I remember watching a few of the episodes and being blown away by what an amazing character Wonder Woman was. Before in my life I was never able to take her seriously-she looked like a cheap knock-off of Superman designed to appeal to the female demographic but still had a design to draw in the guys. Learning about the Greek background just made it weirder for me(And I <i>like </i>Greek mythology). I imagine for the ignorant populace, Wonder Woman sits in this same weird place that begs the question &quot;Why should we take her seriously?&quot;.<br /> <br /> The problem, then, can't begin with the actor*-the potential for problems exists much higher up the line. You need a production company, writers, and directors who are willing to take the character seriously, understand her extremely well, and work to make her as awesome as she can be, a role-model of sorts**, someone <i>everyone</i>(or a vast majority) can look up to.<br /> <br /> Nolan? Good start. Zack &quot;I dedicated <i>Sucker Punch</i> to my mom&quot; Snyder? And the ball has already been dropped. Particularly if it follows the lead of Man of Steel.<br /> <br /> So....on the one hand, they can cast whoever for Wonder Woman because, as it stands, I have little hope. On the other hand...Man, if any movie deserved to be a good movie, it should have been Wonder Woman. She's someone I think lots of people could use in their personal mythology.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Of course, all of this is naysaying before I've even seen anything about it. If the trailers and reviews are good enough, I will gladly watch it.<br /> <br /> *because actress makes me want to grind my teeth.<br /> **That's a loaded term filled with nasty expectations, but it stands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T01:23:25-08:00","id":65495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=65163#post65163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nolan? Good start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Mister Madonna-Whore complex himself?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T01:25:44-08:00","id":65497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=65147#post65147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I saw it as poking fun at the inherent sexism of the original poster. But then that's the point in casting a smoking hot redhead, which in turn is how the comic-book character is typically seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, somebody appropriating criticism of a thing in order to illustrate and reinforce the presence of that thing is a new experience to be sure.<br /> <br /> Excuse me, I need to make an appointment with an icepick.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T07:30:26-08:00","id":65680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=65495#post65495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? Mister Madonna-Whore complex himself?</div> </div> </div> </div>...granted, but at least the man has a better sense of storytelling in general.<br /> <br /> (I hadn't really thought about it until you pointed it out, but yeah, that is a hell of trend there Nolan.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: And it's<i> still</i> a better choice than Zak &quot;I dedicated <i>Sucker Punch</i> to my mom&quot; Snyder as director.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T16:26:28-08:00","id":66046,"title":"","content":"Speaking of superhero casting, I have just read an article about the new Fantastic Four movie and, while I don't have any problems with a black Johnny Storm, the idea of a female Doctor Doom (which, apparently, is being discussed) leaves me highly dubious. Right now, for reasons I don't think I'm able to describe properly yet, it simply does not work for me.<br /> <br /> As a side note, Arc, would you mind explaining the whole &quot;Zack &quot;I dedicated <i>Sucker Punch</i> to my mom&quot; Snyder &quot; thing to me? I haven't watched Sucker Punch (well, I've watched ten minutes of it, but I had to leave) and I feel like I'm missing a part of the discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-05-2014, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T16:44:53-08:00","id":66063,"title":"","content":"<b>Sucker Punch</b> is supposed to be a movie about feminism. Snyder's apparent intent was to make a shit-ton of cheesecake, of women dressed up in fetish outfits for the men in the audience to wank to, and pepper that with reminders that all of this is in the head of a mentally damaged girl imprisoned falsely who is ultimately lobotomized to protect the secrets of the man who imprisoned her. The sucker punch in the movie's title is directed at the audience, to make them feel bad for being aroused at all the objectified women Snyder portrayed.<br /> <br /> If I had to guess, Arc's problem is that no matter what his intentions, Zack Snyder still put a lot of women in fetish outfits and objectified them for men to wank to, then at the end threw up his jazz hands and cried, &quot;Feminism! Because it's okay to fetishize and objectify women if it's ironic! This one's for you, Ma!&quot; It would be like me walking up to a black person with a bucket of fried chicken and some watermelon to draw attention to how horrible of a thing I'm doing, and then dedicating the act to Rosa Parks. I'd get my ass kicked and I'd deserve it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 02-05-2014, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T17:10:10-08:00","id":66091,"title":"","content":"<i>Sucker Punch</i> is a really bad movie. All of its's scenes are boring, the characters aren't flat so much as non-existant, the connections of the layers of the main characters psychosis are blurry and value-less, its' sub-theme of sacrifice was absent until the end, at which point it was....kind of just done, and on top of that the entire thing is surprisingly sexist, horribly inverting the hoped-for-female-empowerment theme with sheer incompetence and (ironically) terrible self-subversion. Which, in and of itself, is bad enough.<br /> <br /> Zak Snyder dedicated it to his mom out of the deep love and respect he had for her.<br /> <br /> What. The. Fuck.<br /> <br /> It's been stuck in my mind as his defining mark ever since.<br /> <br /> EDIT: You know, I had a thing here about how I guiltily liked it after walking out despite knowing how bad it was because of low expectations, but you know what? That was then, this is now. Sucker Punch is a terrible movie, and you just might be a bad person if you still enjoy it.<br /> <br /> EDIT:It's also so bad I forgot that feminism was supposed to be the point, not just a subtextual thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":".  WHY DO I KEEP FINDING UNNECESSARY WORDS? 02-05-2014, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T10:23:24-08:00","id":66558,"title":"","content":"Emily Browning looks like a girl I had a HUGE crush on in high school, so I have blinders on when it comes to that movie. The 16 year old in me is watching the movie, and he has no taste, so he thinks it's AWESOME!!!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T10:42:10-08:00","id":6657