wed to make in a given post. I really don't think it's a revelation to point out there is a lot of fetishization going on here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 02-06-2014, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T13:46:23-08:00","id":66699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=66570#post66570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrugs*<br /> I found it entertaining. The girls wore more clothing than most do at high school proms, so I really didn't see much in the way of fetishes.</div> </div> </div> </div>One man's fetish is another man's fashion choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T14:31:30-08:00","id":66735,"title":"","content":"All in the name of feminism.<br /> <br /> I hate to make it seem like <i>Sucker Punch</i> has a point, but since we're on it, I seem to remember one person found some interesting things to consider in the imagery. Each girl in the fantasy seems to take on one particular fetish as an image, but likewise also takes on a warrior class from certain cultures. Baby Doll, as an example, is easy-she taps into the otaku culture by being both the sexualized schoolgirl but also drawing on samurai iconography(the Katana being the big one, but the guy made notes of several other small things). Sweet Pea taps into knight imagery, one of them was a viking, etc. On top of that, the settings they worked in on the hyper fantasy psychosis trips were ones where women are often portray sexily for no good reason beyond fan pandering, from high fantasy to steampunk and dystopian cyberpunk(I'm not sure how valid that is, but it was interesting to hear the guy talk about it), so the conquest of those places was also vaguely conquering the sexism. I don't remember all of it, and at this point and time I'm not sure how valid it was, but it was an interesting discussion.<br /> <br /> Interesting, but horribly flawed. Even acknowledged by that one guy's ramblings, it just doesn't hold up from the transition of a conceptual design to the execution, particularly when you account for the first two layers of Babydoll's psychosis. The scenes are boring and really don't tie into what's going on and make no real statements beyond some visual metaphor with zero exposition even implied. If the idea was to take the sexualizing objectification of these fetishes and subvert it into being self-reigned icons of female empowerment, then somewhere along the way Zak Snyder got so decidedly distracted by Emily Browning's thigh line that he forgot that idea.<br /> <br /> And it's not like the idea can't be executed. Going to my otaku side here, I found it surprising in my later years that Sailor Moon was considered quite a feminist piece, but after having read the manga and rewatched the (Dic/Saban American serialized version of, aka the worst version of) the anime, I was pleasantly surprised to find out they were right. One of the ways it was unexpectedly so was how it subverted the idea behind several traditonally feminine ideas and icons by just flat out making them powerful and respectable, from the sailor fuku to the idea of the more traditionally regarded feminine emotions being the ones that take down the bad guys(and not in a &quot;Oh, I'll redeem it&quot; way most of the time, more in a &quot;Now you burn, now you bleed, now you die&quot; sense, which is weird). I'm not versed enough to talk heavily on the subject, but here's a springboard I picked up from last year: <a href=\"http://henshinjustice.com/2013/08/07/nostalgia-critic-takes-a-stab-at-sailor-moon/\" target=\"_blank\">http://henshinjustice.com/2013/08/07...t-sailor-moon/</a><br /> <br /> Sucker Punch never really gets around to the respect part, or even really the powerful aspect. It has violence to feed guys want of action and fetishized women to feed guys want of arousal. THe girls kicking ass never means anything, it's all mindless showcasing, with no significance to the struggle or stakes beyond the basic one to give it impact, and thus it's violence and not power. The fetishization is never given any implication of self-reign or determination(in comparison again to the Sailor Moon fuku), it's mindless titillation, with none of the girls owning it and giving us a reason to respect them regardless of what they're wearing, thus it's arousal, no empowerment.<br /> <br /> I'm rambling, and heaven forbid I be the one to turn this into a feminism discussion thread-while I support and try and be mindful of the subject, I am woefully ignorant of the many intricate details beyond the basic idea of &quot;treat people like people, not vaginas and certainly not as dolls&quot;-but it must be said that if all you want is mindless action and titillation, Sucker Punch is...well, not even good there, because the action is boring and the eye candy disturbing, but passable. But for what it was intended to do? Ugh. Man, Zak, I don't know how you can aim so high and end up shooting the ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T14:46:07-08:00","id":66746,"title":"","content":"Hell, I'll admit it. Some times I'm just not that evolved. Where's the hot women thread again? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T14:47:57-08:00","id":66749,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm hardly evolved either-the reason I went to Sucker Punch was I figured that if I got nothing else, at least I'd get cute girls kicking ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T14:51:20-08:00","id":66751,"title":"","content":"If I knew it wouldn't be in bad taste, I'd post some recent prom pictures. Considering that some of them are underage and wearing as little as they did, it's probably as close to child porn as it can get. Heck, today's bikinis are just a couple of strips of cloth that cover far less than what was seen in Suckerpunch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T15:03:10-08:00","id":66766,"title":"","content":"I hope it doesn't seem like a reflection on anyone involved in the discussion when I say I think it's best I bow out until the topic changes. This seems like one of those conversations where I get all self-righteous and end up saying things that drives people away from the community, and I don't want another repeat of that on my track record. Let it just be said that though I think <b>Sucker Punch</b> is one of the worst-handled attempts at feminism I've ever seen, and though I think judging it on a comparative scale is nothing more than an attempt to excuse it for its sins, at the end of the day it's just a fucking movie, so I can't consider anyone a bad person for liking it.<br /> <br /> Right. Have fun, everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T15:08:32-08:00","id":66772,"title":"","content":"No no, it's cool. I don't even really want to be in this conversation, myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T04:16:15-08:00","id":67101,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, that awful looking Robocop movie is coming out in a few days.<br /> <br /> My, how mine brother and I had 