le":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=68106#post68106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, is 47 Ronin any good? I have heard zip about that movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>It exceeded my expectations by quite a bit, but my expectations were <i>very low</i>. As such, I have a hard time parsing how I actually feel about it.<br /> <br /> I went expecting a stupid action movie with some entertaining swordplay choreography. The actual film is a little more thoughtful than that. It's important to note, Keanu Reeves isn't actually the main character. He's sort of the Merlin to the actual protagonist's King Arthur. His whole sub-plot is kind of shoehorned in unnecessarily, but the resulting film <i>isn't</i> the most heavily embellished version of that story by a long shot. There are a couple parts of the story that I'll bet they had to fight the studio for, that were refreshingly true to the original, but risks to put in front of Western audiences. Even so, I recommend waiting for the Dollar Theater or Netflix or something. But this far after it came out, that was probably your plan in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T19:37:44-08:00","id":69566,"title":"","content":"Oh no...47 Ronin? oh god no...I really wanted the time I wasted refunded. There just wasn't anything to this movie. I wanted to like this movie. But there wasn't anything to like. Even the fight scenes were stilted and boring. I was shocked at how bad it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T21:32:38-08:00","id":69617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=68392#post68392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm seeing the Lego movie today. Unless Robocop is just mind blowing, I don't think I care to see it..</div> </div> </div> </div>I just got back from an advanced screening of RoboCop.<br /> <br /> *MIND BLOWN*<br /> <br /> Most remakes will continue to suck, but this one stands as a fine example of a remake done right. I will be seeing it again this weekend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T10:04:05-08:00","id":69892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=69617#post69617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just got back from an advanced screening of RoboCop.<br /> <br /> *MIND BLOWN*<br /> <br /> Most remakes will continue to suck, but this one stands as a fine example of a remake done right. I will be seeing it again this weekend.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dunno, this is the Robocop remake I really want to see: <a href=\"http://www.ourrobocopremake.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.ourrobocopremake.com/</a><br /> <br /> I've heard mixed reviews on the one in theaters, so I dunno. Just seems unnecessary to me I guess. I wish they'd made a new movie about a robot cop and not called it Robocop....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T10:59:35-08:00","id":69913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=69892#post69892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard mixed reviews on the one in theaters, so I dunno. Just seems unnecessary to me I guess. I wish they'd made a new movie about a robot cop and not called it Robocop....</div> </div> </div> </div>But then they'd be accused of stealing the idea or it being too derivative of Robocop.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's a catch 22.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T11:04:39-08:00","id":69916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=69913#post69913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then they'd be accused of stealing the idea or it being too derivative of Robocop.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's a catch 22.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just call it RoboCop: The Next Generation move the timeline ahead 10 years and highlight that things have changed dramatically. You get continuity for the elements you want, a reason for everything else being different and telling a new story, and the nerds can have a fight about how KirkRoboCop could beat up PicardRoboCop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T14:18:45-08:00","id":70037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cyborg Picard is Locutus... and no, Kirk couldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather see that movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T17:44:10-08:00","id":70173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=69913#post69913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then they'd be accused of stealing the idea or it being too derivative of Robocop.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's a catch 22.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear ya. I just find it funny in this day and age, when everyone has easy access to almost every movie, we still have to remake everything...<br /> <br /> Why not just re-release the original? Then you spend almost no money(well, not as much) on something thats already made, rather than millions of dollars on remaking it, not knowing if it'll make back any of the money you spent on it.<br /> <br /> It's crazy to me...or I'm just crazy. I get remakes have happened since movies were first made, but up until the mid 80's, not every had easy access to movies, so they only way they'd see something was if it came out in theaters. So, they'd remake thing, or remake foreign movies American audiences wouldn't get a chance to see otherwise.<br /> <br /> We don't live in that world anymore, yet damn near every movie is just a remake of the same shit we've all already seen. Mostly...<br /> <br /> As much as I love movies, I really hate them sometimes. :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=69916#post69916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just call it RoboCop: The Next Generation move the timeline ahead 10 years and highlight that things have changed dramatically. You get continuity for the elements you want, a reason for everything else being different and telling a new story, and the nerds can have a fight about how KirkRoboCop could beat up PicardRoboCop.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be perfectly fine with me...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T03:05:02-08:00","id":70456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=69916#post69916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the nerds can have a fight about how KirkRoboCop could beat up PicardRoboCop.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never really understood this one. I mean, sure, Kirk could probably beat up Picard, but then Picard would initiate a conversation about how their role as Starfleet officers means they're supposed to exemplify a stance that demonstrates that superior physical force is no indication of moral or qualitative superiority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T03:08:34-08:00","id":70457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=69913#post69913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then they'd be accused of stealing the idea or it being too derivative of Robocop.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would probably help to also have their own, but different plot, setting and character beats that would present a different central thesis statement to the idea of a police officer being made into a cyborg than Robocop. That would actually require them to have a central thesis statement, mind.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T04:16:27-08:00","id":70474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=70457#post70457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would probably help to also have their own, but different plot, setting and character beats that would present a different central thesis statement to the idea of a police officer being made into a cyborg than Robocop. That would actually require them to have a central thesis statement, mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly my thought..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T08:26:09-08:00","id":70620,"title":"","content":"I mean, obviously following Robocop there were all kinds of derivative, mindless cyborg cop vs 80s criminal or corporate bigwigs films.<br /> <br /> Like the Robocop sequels.<br /> <br /> That's just the way with big hit genre properties; half of it trying to recapture that bottled lightning, the others just churning it out to for people who have caught the bug for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T08:50:34-08:00","id":70628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=70457#post70457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would probably help to also have their own, but different plot, setting and character beats that would present a different central thesis statement to the idea of a police officer being made into a cyborg than Robocop. That would actually require them to have a central thesis statement, mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the central thesis of most of these movies was &quot;show off cool special effects while killing extras and blowing shit up&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T16:06:58-08:00","id":70900,"title":"","content":"Robocop has that, but it also has themes of corporatism and urban decay and the struggle for humanity and individuality in the face of extreme urban violence and the attempts of corporations to reduce one down to just a cog in their machine. That's part of what helps it stand out and makes it enduring. That and the satire of contemporary media, with the news provided in stock reinforcement of the status quo by photogenic people, and the pervasiveness of trashy, lowest common denominator entertainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T16:30:45-08:00","id":70909,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.escapistmagazine.com/videos/view/the-big-picture/8777-Why-Robocop-Still-Rules\" target=\"_blank\">Here is a video</a> about old <b>RoboCop</b> and why it is a good movie. It agrees with Isator's take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T19:28:51-08:00","id":70978,"title":"","content":"So I watched old <i>RoboCop </i>awhile back and... I hated it. (Can I say that? Is that blaspheme?) I don't really care about new <i>RoboCop</i>. I'll probably see it some day, but not soon.<br /> <br /> In other news <i>Monuments Men</i> was... not good. Wasn't terrible either, but mostly I just didn't care. And this is about a subject that I actually care about. The movie just fails to deliver any meaningful emotion. I don't care about the characters at all. Additionally, it struck me as having the same problems as a silly historical fiction where the main characters met everyone important. I doubt the real people made as many important discoveries as the characters in the movie did. And finally, I feel the movie creates artificial tension where it isn't needed. It annoys me when movies do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T02:20:34-08:00","id":71117,"title":"","content":"I want to see Vampire Academy, and I don't know why. I don't expect it to be good. I <i>have</i> read the books and they were nothing special (the thin