Pompeii tonight. I'm not expecting much.</div> </div> </div> </div>When Arc and I saw that previewed, he said, facetiously, &quot;Pompeii 2?&quot; and the guy sitting behind us said, &quot;Is this a sequel? I didn't know there was a first one&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T02:26:54-08:00","id":75491,"title":"","content":"So... seen the RoboCop remake.<br /> <br /> Is a very, very different movie. At first it seemed like an somewhat edulcorated version of the old (some characters I expected to be bastards almost seemed sympathetic) but it made a progressive turn to something more akin to the source material. Still, quite more hopeful and clean (in a bad way) than the original.<br /> <br /> <b>Things I liked:</b><br /> -The character played by Samuel L &quot;<i>moterfakar</i>&quot; Jackson. It represents the manipulation in media (the part of the &quot;debate&quot; is priceless, as is the cheesy American flag background). Also worth mentioning the tipical &quot;If you vote this law, you are voting to have the terrorists on the street&quot; demagogic crap so usual among certain political sectors.<br /> -Gary Oldman, of course.<br /> <br /> <b>Things I didn't like:</b><br /> -There's no the same feeling of loss regarding Murphy's family as in the first and that takes away from the character.<br /> -The fact that the dystopian future of the first movies is basically our present with robots in Afganistan (also, they could have done more with that, it seemed like too tack on and in your face)<br /> -The themes of corruption were better executed in the first movie.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T02:44:18-08:00","id":75493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=75427#post75427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah.<br /> <br /> I haven't read the books, but the movie gave me the impression the setting had some interesting things going on. As a reader of the series, what are your thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>The books aren't as deep and complex as something like Dune, buts it's not a children's book. Towards the end (book 6) it gets more political, dealing with weird Moiroi rules over who can ascend to the throne. The movie seemed to hit all the points very rapid fire (one thing I hated was the words being written on screen when someone said them), but honestly if the movie would have taken longer to set everything up I'd have gotten bored.<br /> EDIT: Also the breeding's weird. Dhampirs protect Moroi because they need them to breed, sex with humans results in human children (I believe, been about 2-3 years since I've read them).<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The only differences I noticed from the book was the first Strigoi attack didn't happen (but this was better, I think the movie needed to show off the villains) and I don't remember Lissa being able to manipulate fire and water. I think it was Spirit only in the book.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that a mark against its favor, though? Like, not only is it a story you already have in a book at home and didn't need to pay more money for, it's also a <i>worse</i> version of the story you already have?</div> </div> </div> </div>The movie itself wasn't worth the money, the book was better. But I took my girl out, had a good time with her, and that was worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":57,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","user":"solomon birch","date":". 02-20-2014, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T05:19:35-08:00","id":75537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=75491#post75491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... seen the RoboCop remake.<br /> <br /> Is a very, very different movie. At first it seemed like an somewhat edulcorated version of the old (some characters I expected to be bastards almost seemed sympathetic) but it made a progressive turn to something more akin to the source material. Still, quite more hopeful and clean (in a bad way) than the original.<br /> <br /> <b>Things I liked:</b><br /> -The character played by Samuel L &quot;<i>moterfakar</i>&quot; Jackson. It represents the manipulation in media (the part of the &quot;debate&quot; is priceless, as is the cheesy American flag background). Also worth mentioning the tipical &quot;If you vote this law, you are voting to have the terrorists on the street&quot; demagogic crap so usual among certain political sectors.<br /> -Gary Oldman, of course.<br /> <br /> <b>Things I didn't like:</b><br /> -There's no the same feeling of loss regarding Murphy's family as in the first and that takes away from the character.<br /> -The fact that the dystopian future of the first movies is basically our present with robots in Afganistan (also, they could have done more with that, it seemed like too tack on and in your face)<br /> -The themes of corruption were better executed in the first movie.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've heard if you don't compare it to the original, it's a passable movie. Not great, but not too bad.<br /> <br /> Sounds like a Netflix viewing to me...<br /> <br /> <br /> Now a movie I really want to see but haven't got to yet is Her. Been hearing good things about it and I wish I'd made it to the theater to support it..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T09:53:38-08:00","id":75707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=72265#post72265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get it, but okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a simple stupid interjection to make people pause. It seemed like a good WTF moment. Or like Cereal Killer's scream &quot;Tension breaker, had to be done&quot;. Seemed kind of a like it was building to this really heavy side thing. And no, I had no clue where JimB was going with the SC comment other than it might have been similar but more on the satire talk so &quot;pie&quot; worked there to. When all else fails, pie.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=73764#post73764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I watched 'Empire Records' this weekend. Had seen it in a few years. I forgot how much I loved that movie. I used to watch it over and over.<br /> <br /> Showed it to my son, and he loved it too! So much so that we watched both versions of the movie within two days. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I love that movie. Didn't know there were two versions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=75432#post75432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that a mark against its favor, though? Like, not only is it a story you already have in a book at home and didn't need to pay more money for, it's also a <i>worse</i> version of the story you already have?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't say on it since I haven't read the books, but it was a big reason why I didn't like the latter Harry Potter movies. While the first where not exactly like the books the changes didn't take away. The latter movies made changes for changes sake. They didn't make it more understandable or in some other way help the story along when things had to be removed, but more like they missed the point of what was being said in the books.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-