e":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T00:39:01-08:00","id":77513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=77419#post77419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THe Lego Movie is one of the most intelligent films to have come out recently and everyone needs to see it.<br /> <br /> I mean it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw it this evening, and I agree. Excellent movie all around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T06:21:34-08:00","id":77623,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=77477#post77477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny, yes, but inferior.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrugs*<br /> <br /> Far more entertaining, and I didn't have to spend any money or waste two hours.<br /> <br /> Sorry, maybe it was the headache I had when watching it, but Lego movie was very overrated to me. More than likely I am jaded by what constitutes an &quot;intelligent&quot; movie versus an entertaining movie. I didn't find a whole lot subtlety, just the opposite. The message was about a subtle as a brick to the face. It was a cute movie. That was all it was to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T09:51:38-08:00","id":77699,"title":"","content":"I would like to discuss <b>the Lego Movie</b>, but I can't think of any meaningful way to do so without spoiling the plot. I know I was very underwhelmed by the commercials and previews, but for all that the commercials make the jokes seem like random wackiness hurled with desperate panic in a hope to make someone, anyone think the shtick they're seeing is funny, the movie itself in genuinely hilarious. I laughed at damned near everything I saw, whether out of appreciation for a good joke or simple delight at the imagination behind the set pieces and the skill of the animation, and I have not left a movie feeling so emotionally satisfied as I did yesterday in a very long time. The humor and plot are a bit meta, which may or may not be against its favor in your eyes, but I loved it. I also feel like the charges of the movie being unsubtle have to be answered: there's some truth to them, but at the same time, I have to give the movie mad props for making a villain who isn't actually a bad person, but one who has a caring and nuanced relationship with the hero and whose conflict with him is ultimately a differing ideology.<br /> <br /> I have made a solemn vow not to go to any toy store or toy aisle for the next six months, though, because I want to own everything I saw on that screen, and I'm sure Lego is happily selling it all. If you saw Metalbeard, then you know what I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T10:23:35-08:00","id":77711,"title":"","content":"I don't need to <i>try </i>to look cool. I simply refuse to pretend to be some artsy-fartsy critic.<br /> <br /> Rather pretentious to psycho-analyze a person you don't know posting on the 'net. (But if it entertains you, go ahead and insult my intelligence..yet again.)<br /> <br /> Quite frankly there seem to be a few that can't understand why others dislike things that they like for... &lt;insert reason&gt;.<br /> <br /> And it seems that if someone has a criticism against something...some people will conjure up anything to dislike that person. (I wasn't entertained by the movie, but I was entertained by a YT clip....so I'm just a contrarian..or too stupid. Pick one)<br /> <br /> <br /> The YT vid was created by the same folks that created them all...and helped produces <a href=\"http://news.cnet.com/8301-17938_105-9901653-1.html\" target=\"_blank\">all sorts of toy weapons</a> for Lego products; BrickArms.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T15:27:27-08:00","id":77846,"title":"","content":"I'll grant you, I didn't go into length about why I think Lego was a &quot;OHMAHGAWD MINDBLOWINGLY GOOD!&quot; yesterday, but I am nursing a sore throat that causes a massive headache every time I cough that is kicked into high gear every time I suck in cold air, and I did have to walk about a mile or so in an Idaho town in winter, so it was inconvenient.<br /> <br /> That said, Shadow, it really does seem like you go out of your way to shit on just about every opinion. You're the one who's been doing most of the fighting on the past few pages, and I'm not really sure <i>why</i>. A lot of the time, you seem like you just want to piss people off. Quite frankly, if you had just said the last paragraph of this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=77623#post77623\">part</a> and kept out Dumbass America and some of the other shit, I wouldn't care. Instead, You come across as pretentious as the artsy-fartsy critics you seem to disdain, and cruder to boot.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not like you have to like everything everyone else does-I know I hate 300 and a lot of people here like it-but I've never had any issue over it because I just talk about the movie.<br /> <br /> As for artsy-fartsy critics...eh, I'm gonna leave that one alone aside from mentioning I'm a storyteller and I want to tell good stories. Anything more at this point and I'd probably have to use the words &quot;jangling keys&quot;, which is not something I want to just arbitrarily throw at people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-23-2014, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T16:39:37-08:00","id":77875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=77699#post77699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to discuss <b>the Lego Movie</b>, but I can't think of any meaningful way to do so without spoiling the plot. I know I was very underwhelmed by the commercials and previews, but for all that the commercials make the jokes seem like random wackiness hurled with desperate panic in a hope to make someone, anyone think the shtick they're seeing is funny, the movie itself in genuinely hilarious. I laughed at damned near everything I saw, whether out of appreciation for a good joke or simple delight at the imagination behind the set pieces and the skill of the animation, and I have not left a movie feeling so emotionally satisfied as I did yesterday in a very long time. The humor and plot are a bit meta, which may or may not be against its favor in your eyes, but I loved it. I also feel like the charges of the movie being unsubtle have to be answered: there's some truth to them, but at the same time, I have to give the movie mad props for making a villain who isn't actually a bad person, but one who has a caring and nuanced relationship with the hero and whose conflict with him is ultimately a differing ideology.<br /> <br /> I have made a solemn vow not to go to any toy store or toy aisle for the next six months, though, because I want to own everything I saw on that screen, and I'm sure Lego is happily selling it all. If you saw Metalbeard, then you know what I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm totally with you. I grinned and laughed the whole movie. I loved it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T18:11:15-08:00","id":77948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_posted