t for that because it does a lot of things right. The characters are well-developed, and I cried like three or four times at the plights of the sisters and their inability to figure out ways to overcome their heartbreaking loneliness and the prison of sheer inertia their relationship is trapped inside. The jokes are pretty good, and the snowman--his name is Olaf, right?--looked cringe-worthy from the trailers and commercials, but the sincerity and earnestness of his portrayal, both in the actor and the animators, had me cheering for him the whole time.<br /> <br /> Honestly, my biggest problem with the movie is the musical numbers. There are too many, they felt too crammed in, and the one in the middle with the trolls dragged on for<i>ever</i>. If that's the biggest annoyance I have with a Disney movie, then I think I'm doing pretty well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T21:25:01-08:00","id":80789,"title":"","content":"The troll song was one of two points I almost went &quot;Really Disney?&quot; and almost slotted it off as a standard production. THen they just almost casually drop the theme/solution right there at the end and all I could say was &quot;You clever bastards&quot;.<br /> <br /> The other point was Olaf's Song, and that was redeemed by &quot;I'm gonna tell him&quot;.<br /> <br /> Frozen was easily the third best movie of the year for me last year, and easily the most accessible of those three for everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T14:23:58-08:00","id":81770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=80216#post80216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then, dammit, Cthulhu needs his own movie series.....and comic book series.....and animated Saturday morning show............................wait, maybe this isn't such a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>He got a game on Steam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T21:00:41-08:00","id":82934,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I might be alone in thinking this, but this year's crop of movies for the Oscars were a little on the we