e.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Yea, theres no way he didn't make a copy of himself. So I suspect he'll show up later on.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=110612#post110612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really wish <b>Agents of SHIELD</b> would quit reminding me it's attached to the movie, though. As I've said elsewhere, a show with a budget of like two million bucks and a runtime of forty-one minutes is not doing itself any favors by comparing itself to a blockbuster that lasts two and a half hours and has a budget of like South America's gross national product.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like what they've done with the tv show and how it weaves in and out of the movies. It's a nice little tie in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's not perfect mind you, but I'm ok with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":24,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","user":"Mr Gone","date":". 04-11-2014, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T20:39:05-07:00","id":111212,"title":"","content":"Omw to see Oculus. I really want this movie to scare the crap out of me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T07:35:33-07:00","id":111465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=111212#post111212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Omw to see Oculus. I really want this movie to scare the crap out of me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let us know how it is. That's a movie that I want to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T12:07:21-07:00","id":111664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=111465#post111465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let us know how it is. That's a movie that I want to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was a little disappointed. Clever writing, although it needed some polishing as it becomes convoluted at times. Exactly half of the major cast was excellent, while the other half was horrible (and played by otherwise phenomenal talents, so I am not sure what happened there). There were a couple decent scares, far fewer than I wanted to experience.<br /> <br /> I guess my recommendation is to proceed with caution. There are some things worth seeing in this film, but in other ways it was very much a let down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":8,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","user":"Storyteller","date":". 04-24-2014, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T18:58:01-07:00","id":118207,"title":"","content":"Well, I just saw a wonderful movie called &quot;Saving Mr. Banks,&quot; and let me tell you, it made me cry in all the right ways. I won't say anything else that might spoil the film, but If you need some good old fashioned heartwarming for grown-ups, I would not hesitate to recommend it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T17:22:10-07:00","id":120623,"title":"","content":"I just watched <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt1767354/?ref_=fn_al_tt_1\" target=\"_blank\">Off Thomas</a>, and that is a great flick. I haven't read any of the books, but I will be checking them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T00:45:12-07:00","id":120815,"title":"","content":"Well, Hell. I didn't even know that there was an Odd Thomas movie.<br /> <br /> I can heavily recommend the books though. Dean Koontz's best work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T18:58:05-07:00","id":122138,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about the upcoming Dr. Strange movie the other day. Dr. Strange is a confounding character to me, but one I've always <i>wanted</i> to be interested in, so that's what got me thinking about his movie: I wanted to figure out what it could be that would make me interested in it.<br /> <br /> The first thing to pop to mind was magic. It is fairly important to me that magic be a completely irrational process. It bugs me when magic is treated like an observable and repeatable process, because that makes it just another form of science and Dr. Strange becomes just a reskinned version of Iron Man, with pink zaps instead of white repulsors and a cape instead of rocket boots but both ultimately doing the same things the same ways.<br /> <br /> <i>No,</i> I thought to myself, <i>if I had my druthers, magic would be based entirely upon the needs of the moment and how they intersect with the magician's ability to believe in the irrational, so that the effectiveness of any spell will be based on the purity of the magician's focus, with stray emotions and distracting thoughts detracting from the magic's effectiveness and/or altering the spell in ways the magician didn't intend.. Each spell--I don't know how you'd do this, I'm not a cinematographer, but in the movie I'd like to see, each spell would be like a snapshot of Dr. Strange's frame of mind at the instant he cast the spell. In fact, the primary conflict would probably not be between him and Dormammu, but rather, that would be more like a metaphor or a backdrop for the real conflict, which is his journey to regain some measure of faith after years of practiced cynicism from his trade and the bitterness of absorbing his injuries.</i><br /> <br /> Then I realized that you just need to cram the Technocracy in there somewhere and I'd have done a pretty good job of describing a <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> movie.<br /> <br /> Still not sure how I feel about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T20:45:24-07:00","id":122176,"title":"","content":"This isn't the first time someone attempted to adapt a live action Dr. Strange to the screen.<br /> <br /> It... didn't go well...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://atopfourthwall.blogspot.com/2014/03/doctor-strange.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://atopfourthwall.blogspot.com/2014/03/doctor-strange.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://atopfourthwall.blogspot.com/2014/03/doctor-strange.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://atopfourthwall.blogspot.com/2014/03/doctor-strange.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T11:20:08-07:00","id":122508,"title":"","content":"I just watched <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0RhwyPrUWx8\" target=\"_blank\">Die Farbe</a>, a German indie film based on Lovecraft's <i>The Colour Out of Space</i>. They're raising money for a new movie so it's free to watch on Youtube till Sunday. I loved it, but I also love Lovecraft, so I am biased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T11:29:54-07:00","id":122515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=122138#post122138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each spell--I don't know how you'd do this, I'm not a cinematographer, but in the movie I'd like to see, each spell would be like a snapshot of Dr. Strange's frame of mind at the instant he cast the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same way they showed RDJ's version of Sherlock Holmes going thru the process.<br /> <br /> &quot;By focusing my mind upon the Enochian name of Micha-El, on his aspect as a warrior, in full thunderous glory, I shall bring about a lightning bolt to slaughter my enemy in a flashing cacophony.&quot;<br /> <br /> Y'know, or something like that..... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> BTW, there's a direct-to-video <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0910865/?ref_=nv_sr_2\" target=\"_blank\">Doctor Strange</a> animated movie, I think they did a good job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T12:09:34-07:00","id":122560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=122515#post122515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a direct-to-video <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0910865/?ref_=nv_sr_2\" target=\"_blank\">Doctor Strange</a> animated movie, I think they did a good job.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw it once. I don't remember it being <i>bad</i>, but I don't remember liking it much either. &quot;Oh look, it's the same origin story they always do, except Strange whines at his mentor all throughout his training period like Daniel whined at Mr. Miyagi,&quot; is about all I remember of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T12:52:20-07:00","id":122594,"title":"","content":"There was too much, I'm a mystic now so I will make a magic sword (reeked of lightsaber-envy to me) and practicing kung-fu, instead of being mystics doing mystical things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T06:52:39-07:00","id":123116,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that was a major downside to it, kung-fu &quot;magic&quot; versus spell-casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T09:42:15-07:00","id":123231,"title":"","content":"I get turning magic into kung fu. It adds a level of visual (or maybe a better word is &quot;visceral&quot;) imagery to a conflict than two dudes gesticulating like they're both having grand mal seizures and spouting poetry involving made-up words like &quot;Hoggoth.&quot; That might not be what you're wanting in a movie about magicians and sorcerers, but I do get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0