Future Wolverine or more properly Wolverine 5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfAsh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=124744#post124744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im not surprised to hear the negative feedback for spidey. It looks like they packed too much into it and to be honest I fear they might be doing the same with days of future past - I wish they had stuck with xmen first class instead of mashing the casts from both movie series together.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it would be a grand idea if Fox actually gave a rats ass about the IP. As has been said the only thing seems to be to keep it from going back to Marvel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T15:31:56-07:00","id":129307,"title":"","content":"Has anyone seen <i>Neighbors</i> yet? I am thinking about seeing it this weekend, and I am hoping someone I know has an opinion on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T13:41:54-07:00","id":130125,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.escapistmagazine.com/videos/view/escape-to-the-movies/9177-Neighbors-Genuinely-Funny?utm_source=latest&amp;utm_medium=index_carousel&amp;utm_campaign=all\" target=\"_blank\">Movie Bob liked it.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T18:51:30-07:00","id":141138,"title":"","content":"So, Godzilla was done rather well, for what it is.<br /> Because of the focus, which is well, the monsters, it loses out whenever it goes to the human point of view.<br /> Essentially, Godzilla is indifferent to the humans...ants scurrying about. But he certainly takes a dim view of any other gaiju roaming about. (I'm pretty sure his roar translates to &quot;There can only be one!&quot;) And this is where the movie kinda shines. This reboot is fairly faithful to the old movies. I won't be surprised to hear of a sequel in the works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T19:36:59-07:00","id":141172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=126958#post126958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem is this last I heard the script was totally completed before they got Singer. And what did Singer prove of Superman Returns? No matter how good the director nor how much money you throw at it you can't fix a crappy script. I'm not saying the movie has to be crap, but Fox has already proven they don't care about the IP. This feels like nothing more than a setup for someone's further attempt to write their name to a franchise which is the only thing that 90% of movies using pre-established IP are. I'm not looking forward to Days of Future Wolverine or more properly Wolverine 5.<br /> <br /> I think it would be a grand idea if Fox actually gave a rats ass about the IP. As has been said the only thing seems to be to keep it from going back to Marvel.</div> </div> </div> </div>The script for this X-Men comes from issues 141-142 of the Uncanny X-Men, so the script was pretty much written for them a while ago. The major change being Wolverine is the one whose consciousness is sent back rather than Sprite/Kate Pryde, I wouldn't go so far as to call it Wolverine 5. Because of the differences between the movie universe and comics it wouldn't make much sense to use Kitty Pryde, as she hasn't been born yet at the point in time the divergence between timelines occur in the movie universe. I'm hoping that they retcon the so-so second and painfully bad third movies out of existence (X-Men Origins Wolverine was pretty shitty too), The Wolverine was a significant improvement and I thought First Class was pretty good even if I disagreed with the characters they chose for the students. I'd still prefer that Marvel got the movie rights back though, I'd like to see a series of setup movies leading to an AvX type story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 05-17-2014, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T09:20:13-07:00","id":141633,"title":"","content":"There are six reasons you go watch Godzilla.<br /> <br /> Two of them are Godzilla breathing nuclear fire.<br /> <br /> Four of them are that god-amazing roar.<br /> <br /> Those and the final monster fight more than make up for the rest of the movie. See it once in theaters.(Seriously)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T10:51:51-07:00","id":141712,"title":"","content":"I enjoyed Godzilla. My only gripes were...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I wish there was more Godzilla in it, and more monster battles. Those were amazing. Then there were a few little things, but I can forgive anything as long as there is awesome monster fighting. Not that I didn't enjoy the human element. I wouldn't want them to drop any of that. I just wanted them to add another 20 to 30 minutes of Godzilla on M.U.T.O.(s) combat fury. I would have happily sat through the whole thing.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T12:07:25-07:00","id":141728,"title":"","content":"GOJIRA! Spoiler contains a wee bit more specifics and is also me griping.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Seriously. Every time a city was going to get wrecked, they cut straight to the aftermath.<br /> <br /> I actually didn't enjoy the human element, and I question the sanity of these people, but it is needed to give Godzilla and the MUTO's the stage. I just wish it had been more engaging.<br /> <br /> Also, this movie has ridiculously bad understanding of radiation and other general physics an even basic surveillance. It's impossible to suspend your disbelief until Godzilla shows up and makes you forget reality is even there.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> THAT SAID, again, what the movie delivers when it delivers is really good, and makes up for all the problems, if not enough so to warrant a second theater viewing.<br /> <br /> And seriously, see it in theaters. I don't care how good you or your friend's sound system is, it's not enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"