nature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T07:46:29-07:00","id":151289,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=151238#post151238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmf...I rank this movie tie for 3rd in X-Men movies that were good...to ok.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whats your ranking of the X-Men movies then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=151238#post151238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was just too oriented towards the kid crowd.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was? I thought it was pretty mature. How was it too kiddie?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T10:34:31-07:00","id":151446,"title":"","content":"The first two X-Men movies was the breakout and top of the list and I'll probably keep viewing them that way.<br /> X-Men First Class undid the amazingly shitty &quot;Last Stand.&quot; And after that Wolverine Origin movie I thought the whole franchise should have been tossed in the trash.<br /> First Class and Days of Future Past are tied to me for 3rd place. &quot;Future Past&quot; would likely rank higher if this wasn't just another Wolverine movie. (as I see it)<br /> <br /> As for maturity, this is why I made an unfair comparison to Captain America; the Winter Soldier. Winter Soldier had themes that were pretty adult, as epitomized in the character of Alexander Pierce. And not just adult, but those themes were pretty much alive today and very current. (I'm looking at Drone attacks, Snowden, NSA surveillance, etc...) Whip out a newspaper headline today and no one would be surprised at the &quot;putting a gun to everyone's head and calling it protection.&quot; It was thought-provoking.<br /> <br /> &quot;Future Past&quot; didn't really require much thought, despite the space-time quandary. And it was made to fix the crap that went on earlier with the prior movies. We pretty much knew what was going to happen, and in that it was kinda tame. I had a bit of fun with the movie but that was all. Had they stuck with the comic-book stuff, such as scenes like <a href=\"http://biffbampop.files.wordpress.com/2012/11/uxm142-13.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this one</a> which shows Wolverine's ambiguous ethics or scenes as shown <a href=\"http://www.comicsblend.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/06/UXM142.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">on this cover</a> where Wolverine gets <a href=\"http://ifanboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/07/Uncanny-X-Men-Vol.-1-142-1981.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">blasted down to his bones</a>. Or scenes such <a href=\"http://amocat.net/kiotr/KIOTR-Gallery/albums/UncannyX-Men141and142-DaysofFuturePast,andMindOutofTime/Uncanny_141_DoFP_1.sized.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">as this one</a> which evokes the level of desperation that I genuinely felt reading it, but didn't feel it from the movie.<br /> Had they simply put the comic-books in movie form it would have been better in my opinion. But I understand that they had to fix the prior mistakes, and they wanted to throw a few nods towards characters that became popular later on in the series that reflects the younger fanbase. I get it, but to me it made a lesser movie than it could have been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T06:35:27-07:00","id":152453,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=151446#post151446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first two X-Men movies was the breakout and top of the list and I'll probably keep viewing them that way.<br /> X-Men First Class undid the amazingly shitty &quot;Last Stand.&quot; And after that Wolverine Origin movie I thought the whole franchise should have been tossed in the trash.<br /> First Class and Days of Future Past are tied to me for 3rd place. &quot;Future Past&quot; would likely rank higher if this wasn't just another Wolverine movie. (as I see it)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, with X-Men 3 and X-Men Origins the franchise was going down the tubes. Luckily First Class was way better than expected. I love the first two X-Men movies, but looking back at it, there are a few things in that first movie that are rough to watch. So, I'm glad DoFP reset things abit, and now we can move forward and do whatever and not be beholden to those earlier movies. I like DoFP included a lot of the original cast though, and it was a nice tie-in to the original movies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=151446#post151446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for maturity, this is why I made an unfair comparison to Captain America; the Winter Soldier. Winter Soldier had themes that were pretty adult, as epitomized in the character of Alexander Pierce. And not just adult, but those themes were pretty much alive today and very current. (I'm looking at Drone attacks, Snowden, NSA surveillance, etc...) Whip out a newspaper headline today and no one would be surprised at the &quot;putting a gun to everyone's head and calling it protection.&quot; It was thought-provoking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I can understand that. And yea, it was alittle more mature in that regard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=151446#post151446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Future Past&quot; didn't really require much thought, despite the space-time quandary. And it was made to fix the crap that went on earlier with the prior movies. We pretty much knew what was going to happen, and in that it was kinda tame. I had a bit of fun with the movie but that was all. Had they stuck with the comic-book stuff, such as scenes like <a href=\"http://biffbampop.files.wordpress.com/2012/11/uxm142-13.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this one</a> which shows Wolverine's ambiguous ethics or scenes as shown <a href=\"http://www.comicsblend.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/06/UXM142.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">on this cover</a> where Wolverine gets <a href=\"http://ifanboy.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/07/Uncanny-X-Men-Vol.-1-142-1981.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">blasted down to his bones</a>. Or scenes such <a href=\"http://amocat.net/kiotr/KIOTR-Gallery/albums/UncannyX-Men141and142-DaysofFuturePast,andMindOutofTime/Uncanny_141_DoFP_1.sized.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">as this one</a> which evokes the level of desperation that I genuinely felt reading it, but didn't feel it from the movie.<br /> Had they simply put the comic-books in movie form it would have been better in my opinion. But I understand that they had to fix the prior mistakes, and they wanted to throw a few nods towards characters that became popular later on in the series that reflects the younger fanbase. I get it, but to me it made a lesser movie than it could have been.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that. I would have loved if they could made the comic as-is into a movie. But, with all the changes they'd made in the movies themselves, they basically just had to use the story as a spring board to use with the characters they'd already used in the movie. But, I thought they stayed pretty true to the spirit of the original story, even though they changed it up.<br /> <br /> But I agree, it'd have been awesome if they could have done of the death scenes like they did in the comic, or having Storm challenge Wolverine like that...it'd have been amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T07:17:44-07:00","id":152481,"title":"","content":"One thing that did strike me about DoFP was that despite Wolverine once again being the main character for the most part it really wasn't about him. You could have replaced him with any of the other future X-Men and there wouldn't have been much difference. It was more like First Class, revolving around Charles, Eric and Raven. Most of the time, especially after he finally got Xavier going, Logan was more like a passenger in the film than an active part of it. Really about the only two major things he brought to the story was the linchpin of the Past-Future connection and getting young Xavier going, both which could be done by anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T12:18:26-07:00","id":152780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=152481#post152481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that did strike me about DoFP was that despite Wolverine once again being the main character for the most part it really wasn't about him. You could have replaced him with any of the other future X-Men and there wouldn't have been much difference. It was more like First Class, revolving around Charles, Eric and Raven. Most of the time, especially after he finally got Xavier going, Logan was more like a passenger in the film than an active part of it. Really about the only two major things he brought to the story was the linchpin of the Past-Future connection and getting young Xavier going, both which could be done by anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, that's a good point, and one of the things I liked about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Wolverine wasn't overused...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T12:34:21-07:00","id":152798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=152780#post152780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, that's a good point, and one of the things I liked about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <b>Wolverine wasn't overused</b>...</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, wait, wait.......that can't be right! It's an X-MEN MOVIE, right?<br /> <br /> Next you're gonna tell me TVTropes is going to have to rename <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/WolverinePublicity\" target=\"_blank\">Wolverine Publicity</a> to something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T05:36:46-07:00","id":153720,"title":"","content":"I know...I was shocked too. <img src=\"https: