ginally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=154112#post154112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. I'll end up watching it, naturally, but I do want to say good for Marvel if it ends up being an action movie. More thirty-year-old women in general need to be cast in action movies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and I have no doubt Scarlett Johansson will be able to hold an action movie. Plus, I think she's awesome. I have thought so ever since I saw her in Ghost World.<br /> <br /> I can't wait to see what they do!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T15:27:53-07:00","id":154223,"title":"","content":"The Lucy movie she is doing seems cool. Curious that she has to do a non-super hero movie to get Super Powers XD<br /> <br /> That said, I probably won't watch it, because the &quot;I use a higher percentage of my brain when normal people only use 10%&quot; reasoning for super powers is a huge pet peeve of mine and one of the things that utterly crushes my ability to suspend disbelief.<br /> <br /> Edit: as for her leading an action movie, I've read that, of all the stars in the Avengers, she was the most dedicated to the physical training and to doing as much of her own stuntwork as possible. This excerpt from an interview also points in that direction:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well first of all, my stunt girlfriend \u2026 is a wonderful stunt woman by the name of Heidi Moneymaker \u2014 that\u2019s her real name. And yeah, she\u2019s awesome. And this is our third [together], she\u2019s played the widow every time along with me. So we have really worked together from the beginning to develop this fighting style that you see. We want to keep the consistency of it, it\u2019s such a fun and playful kind of fighting style.<br /> <br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> And you know, it actually made it a lot easier for me because first of all the crazy acrobatic stuff that you see I start and finish, and then Heidi does ridiculous things with her body that I could never do. Even if it was my job. She\u2019s amazing and deserves all, a lot, most of the credit. A very brave and very inspiring person. You know, I just basically wound myself trying to emulate whatever she does.<br /> And, you know, hopefully they can use as much of my face as possible. I like to, I wanna be as, involved as I can. And, the stunt guys are, they let me do it \u2019cause they\u2019re nuts. So \u2026 there\u2019s a big insurance policy on the film. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 05-31-2014, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T17:46:07-07:00","id":154387,"title":"","content":"I just watched Cloud Atlas.<br /> <br /> It was a very strange movie. Because I really, really suck at facial recognition, it took me forever to notice that there were more recurring actors than Hugo Weaving throughout the various storylines.<br /> <br /> It was really good, though. <br /> <br /> Also, throughout all of time and space, Hugo Weaving remains terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T18:36:34-07:00","id":154419,"title":"","content":"I am watching the J.J. Abrams <b>Star Trek</b> on TV, and I gotta say, the plot could have really used a rewrite. The bad guy wants revenge for his planet exploding because of human error, so he goes back in time to get his revenge...but why does it never occur to him that maybe a better use of his time travel technology would be to go back in time <i>and stop his planet from blowing up</i>? It just really makes the villain's stated motives seem suspect when he has the ability to prevent the extinction of his species (and every other species native to his planet, but never mind) and he'd rather let them all die so he can be pissed off. And sure, maybe he's a lunatic who'd rather get revenge for a slight he could erase from history, but the dude has a whole goddamned crew following him. Not one of them thought of maybe just fixing the problem either?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yeah, I know he said he needed to kill the Federation to keep his planet safe. It's still stupid to antagonize everyone in the galaxy and just hope no one takes you out before you fix the actual problem and save your species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 05-30-2014, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T18:44:38-07:00","id":154424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=154387#post154387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I really, really suck at facial recognition, it took me forever to notice that there were more recurring actors than Hugo Weaving throughout the various storylines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell me about it. I honestly, every time I see the image, think <a href=\"http://cdn.escapistmagazine.com/media/global/images/library/deriv/426/426583.png\" target=\"_blank\">this guy is me</a>. You might think I'd know what I look like, but nope, every single time I think, &quot;That's me!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T19:31:07-07:00","id":154456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=154387#post154387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just watched Cloud Atlas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like <i>Cloud Atlas</i>. Sixsmith and Frobisher are the cutest couple! The book is on my (constantly lengthening) list of books to read.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was a very strange movie. </div> </div> </div>Very strange. I didn't really have any idea what was going on the first time I watched it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T19:42:24-07:00","id":154468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=154419#post154419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am watching the J.J. Abrams <b>Star Trek</b> on TV, and I gotta say, the plot could have really used a rewrite. The bad guy wants revenge for his planet exploding because of human error, so he goes back in time to get his revenge...but why does it never occur to him that maybe a better use of his time travel technology would be to go back in time <i>and stop his planet from blowing up</i>? It just really makes the villain's stated motives seem suspect when he has the ability to prevent the extinction of his species (and every other species native to his planet, but never mind) and he'd rather let them all die so he can be pissed off. And sure, maybe he's a lunatic who'd rather get revenge for a slight he could erase from history, but the dude has a whole goddamned crew following him. Not one of them thought of maybe just fixing the problem either?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yeah, I know he said he needed to kill the Federation to keep his planet safe. It's still stupid to antagonize everyone in the galaxy and just hope no one takes you out before you fix the actual problem and save your species.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Star Trek Into Darkness is even worse. Basically they took Star Trek 2: The Wrath of Khan and Star Trek 6: The Undiscovered Country, mashed them together and cut out most of the intelligent ideas within said films, threw in far too many lens flares* and cooked up a stupid, and at times non-nonsensical, plot.<br /> <br /> And this guy is doing the next Star Wars film.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyone else think we mind come to long for the Prequel Trilogy?<br /> <br /> *I honestly think there are even more in Into Darkness than the previous film.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T20:33:48-07:00","id":154492,"title":"","content":"Are you kidding? The man's trying to write Star Trek as Star Wars. Of course the Trek movies are bad, he was in the wrong sandbox. Give him the right toys and it should be better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T06:10:11-07:00","id":154737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=154492#post154492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you kidding? The man's trying to write Star Trek as Star Wars. Of course the Trek movies are bad, he was in the wrong sandbox. Give him the right toys and it should be better.</div> </div> </div> </div>So again anyone else think we mind come to long for the Prequel Trilogy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T07:42:29-07:00","id":154823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=154737#post154737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So again, anyone else think we mind come to long for the Prequel Trilogy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand what that sentence is supposed to mean. I'm guessing you mean &quot;might&quot; rather than &quot;mind?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T09:39:00-07:00","id":154923,"title":"","content":"He's thinking that the rather vilified prequels may come to look a lot better after seeing what's JJ Abrams does with the series.<br /> I'll wait and see myself. Since I'm not a trekkie neither of the Star Trek movies bothered me much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T13:22:41-07:00","id":155150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=154823#post154823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand what that sentence is supposed to mean. I'm guessing you mean &quot;might&quot; rather than &quot;mind?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it's supposed to be might. And that's what happens when you reply to a thread shortly after waking up in the morning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T13:43:43-07:00","id":155191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=154419#post154419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am watching the J.J. Abrams <b>Star Trek</b> on TV, and I gotta say, the plot could have really used a rewrite. The bad guy wants revenge for his planet exploding because of human error, so he goes back in time to get his revenge...but why does it never occur to him that maybe a better use of his time travel technology would be to go back in time <i>and stop his planet from blowing up</i>? It just really makes the villain's stated motives seem suspect when he has the ability to prevent the extinction of his species (and every other species native to his planet, but never mind) and he'd rather let them all die so he can be pissed off. And sure, maybe he's a lunatic who'd rather get revenge for a slight he could erase from history, but the dude has a whole goddamned crew following him. Not one of them thought of maybe just fixing the problem either?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yeah, I know he said he needed to kill the Federation to keep his planet safe. It's still stupid to antagonize everyone in the galaxy and just hope no one takes you out before you fix the actual problem and save your species.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be noted that the Romulans who went back in time didn't do it purposefully, they got caught up in Spocks Red Matter blackhole/worm hole. And though it isn't spelled out very well in the movie(it's there, but you really have to be paying attention) they were imprisoned for several years and while there cooked their revenge plan. They then broke out of prison and started with the plan.<br /> <br /> Not trying to defend their plan or anything, it is pretty stupid. But they didn't go back in time on their own, they just got caught up in an accident. If I remember correctly...<br /> <br /> <br /> And just to say, Into Darkness could have been better. I just wished they'd dropped the whole Khan thing and done something new.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=154456#post154456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like <i>Cloud Atlas</i>. Sixsmith and Frobisher are the cutest couple! The book is on my (constantly lengthening) list of books to read.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really liked it too! I really need to read it one of these days.. But yea, I too loved the movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T18:30:36-07:00","id":155344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=154737#post154737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So again anyone else think we mind come to long for the Prequel Trilogy?</div> </div> </div> </div>1)I feel dismissed, and that makes me frown.<br /> 2)I think you're probably the only one who might worry about that.<br /> <br /> Seriously, the amount of worry for Episode 7-sorry, VII in general is kind of ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T09:30:56-07:00","id":155699,"title":"","content":"I've got a question. Fox owns the rights to X-Men, and Sony's got Spidey. But Marvel gets to use Quicksilver and Scarlet Witch as long as they don't mention that they're mutants, because they were also Avengers. Once upon a time Wolverine <i>and</i> Spiderman were Avengers (Beast too I believe). If they wanted, could they show up in Avengers 3? (Not that I want them to, I'm just curious as to how the legalities would work)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T15:17:55-07:00","id":156008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=155344#post155344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, the amount of worry for Episode 7-sorry, VII in general is kind of ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Alot people who love the OT and were disappointed in the PT might have some worries and reservations about the new ones. I know I do, alittle bit. But, with Lucas not directing and only being loosely involved, the new movies have a much better chance of being better than the Prequels,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solomon birch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=155699#post155699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a question. Fox owns the rights to X-Men, and Sony's got Spidey. But Marvel gets to use Quicksilver and Scarlet Witch as long as they don't mention that they're mutants, because they were also Avengers. Once upon a time Wolverine <i>and</i> Spiderman were Avengers (Beast too I believe). If they wanted, could they show up in Avengers 3? (Not that I want them to, I'm just curious as to how the legalities would work)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. It's a weird legal mess I'd suspect. Since Quicksilver and Scarlet Witch aren't 1st tier characters, and haven't been in the movies before, maybe they were easier to strike a deal for, than A listers like Wolvy and Spidey?<br /> <br /> I'd much rather Marvel just strike a deal with Fox and Sony and reclaim their characters and just give them a cut of the money made from the movies. Then integrate them all into the Marvel Cinematic Universe.<br /> <br /> Though I will admit that maybe the X-men should just remain in their own universe. I mean, in the Marvel Universe people hate Mutants for being born with their powers, but then love some of the other superhero because they got their powers in an accident?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T18:04:03-07:00","id":156113,"title":"","content":"I saw <b>Godzilla</b> last weekend. It was okay. I have nothing to say that Omicron and and Arc didn't say already.<br /> <br /> I saw <b>a Million Ways to Die in the West</b> yesterday. It was also okay. I remember laughing at various points in the movie, but a day later I can't remember any of the jokes. Like, seriously, not one joke. I am sitting here in my chair muttering to myself, &quot;Oh, shit, what was that funny thing Charlize Theron said,&quot; and I got nothing. It seems to be a very disposable movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T18:43:55-07:00","id":156126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solomon birch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=155699#post155699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a question. Fox owns the rights to X-Men, and Sony's got Spidey. But Marvel gets to use Quicksilver and Scarlet Witch as long as they don't mention that they're mutants, because they were also Avengers. Once upon a time Wolverine <i>and</i> Spiderman were Avengers (Beast too I believe). If they wanted, could they show up in Avengers 3? (Not that I want them to, I'm just curious as to how the legalities would work)</div> </div> </div> </div>There are several issues that make me think that the &quot;Marvel Cinematic Universe&quot; will eventually implode. Re: As previously &lt;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=125878#post125878\">posted</a>;&gt;<br /> Mentioning Dr. Strange in Winter Soldier is hopeful, but: <i>&quot;Up until this point, the Marvel Cinematic Universe has consisted of a \u201csuperhero\u201d team membered by a science-created super soldier (Captain America); a science-created super-soldier failure (Hulk); a tech genius (Iron Man); a \u201cgodlien\u201d (Thor); and some highly trained operatives (the agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.). That doesn\u2019t leave a lot of room to explain the wide array of Marvel Comics superpowers, like flight, super-speed, energy projection, psychic abilities, invulnerability, etc.&quot;</i><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T22:35:51-07:00","id":156269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=156008#post156008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I will admit that maybe the X-men should just remain in their own universe. I mean, in the Marvel Universe people hate Mutants for being born with their powers, but then love some of the other superhero because they got their powers in an accident?</div> </div> </div> </div>That part has always made perfect sense to me, you are coming at it from the wrong angle. It's not the fact they received powers or how they got them, it is what they represent. Mutants are the next step in evolution, due to wipe humanity out of existence. A human who somehow gained powers is still a human. They don't represent the end of everything you are. They represent a lot of things, but that is not one of them. It doesn't help there are a lot of mutants running around claiming they are better than humans, and they can do whatever they please.<br /> <br /> On a different note, I saw Maleficent tonight. Interesting film with some nice elements, but I was a little underwhelmed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T22:45:55-07:00","id":156273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=156008#post156008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? Alot people who love the OT and were disappointed in the PT might have some worries and reservations about the new ones. I know I do, alittle bit. But, with Lucas not directing and only being loosely involved, the new movies have a much better chance of being better than the Prequels,</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why I find the amount of worry over the new Star Wars movies silly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T00:03:27-07:00","id":156291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=156269#post156269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That part has always made perfect sense to me, you are coming at it from the wrong angle. It's not the fact they received powers or how they got them, it is what they represent. Mutants are the next step in evolution, due to wipe humanity out of existence. A human who somehow gained powers is still a human. They don't represent the end of everything you are. They represent a lot of things, but that is not one of them. It doesn't help there are a lot of mutants running around claiming they are better than humans, and they can do whatever they please.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing the Marvel Universe is soon to be seeing religious nuts protesting &quot;God hates the Terrigen mist&quot; XD<br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">If it has not already. I have not read any books dealing with this yet</span>.<br /> <br /> Inhuman is a terrible thing to carry as your &quot;classification&quot; already, but nuhuman as Medusa puts it seems even worse than mutant in drawing that sort of ire. I mean, a bunch of people with super-powers calling themselves &quot;new humans&quot;? Magneto must be kicking himself for not thinking that appellation first...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T17:57:51-07:00","id":161288,"title":"","content":"Well after over a decade the guys at <a href=\"http://roosterteeth.com/home.php\" target=\"_blank\">Roosterteeth Productions</a> are finally getting a chance to make a full length feature film, something they've dreamed to do for years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iB4g23Bdvqo\" data-code=\"iB4g23Bdvqo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/iB4g23Bdvqo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RfRPq5VHugc\" data-code=\"RfRPq5VHugc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/RfRPq5VHugc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> If you wish to donate to the cause, you can do so <a href=\"https://www.indiegogo.com/projects/lazer-team-by-rooster-teeth\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. They given us Red vs Blue, RWBY, Achievement Hunter and so many other great web-videos so let's give them some support on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T07:08:27-07:00","id":161682,"title":"","content":"It sounds like the &quot;Edge of Tomorrow&quot; is going to be an awesome movie. Which confounds my expectation that it'll be Groundhog Day with power armor and aliens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T09:14:26-07:00","id":161794,"title":"","content":"Considering that a majority of stories can be summarized as &quot;It's like [this story], but with [genre piece] and [possibly a quirk but most likely another genre piece]&quot;, I expect some people get confounded a lot.<br /> <br /> But that said, yeah, I had zero expectations for Edge of Tomorrow and it's getting a lot of glowing praise. I'm interested now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T09:59:16-07:00","id":161817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=156269#post156269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That part has always made perfect sense to me, you are coming at it from the wrong angle. It's not the fact they received powers or how they got them, it is what they represent. Mutants are the next step in evolution, due to wipe humanity out of existence. A human who somehow gained powers is still a human. They don't represent the end of everything you are. They represent a lot of things, but that is not one of them. It doesn't help there are a lot of mutants running around claiming they are better than humans, and they can do whatever they please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats a good point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T12:11:51-07:00","id":161910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=156008#post156008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I will admit that maybe the X-men should just remain in their own universe. I mean, in the Marvel Universe people hate Mutants for being born with their powers, but then love some of the other superhero because they got their powers in an accident?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bigots aren't known for their critical thinking skills. And tons of Superheroes are unfairly hated in the Marvel Universe, it's pretty much Spider-Man's entire schtick.<br /> <br /> The way the X-Men operate, getting into fights with the Brotherhood, causing massive property damage and then running off when the smoke clears, doesn't exactly endear them to the public. Of course, since sticking around means they're gonna get mobbed, its not much of an option either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T13:06:03-07:00","id":161948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=161682#post161682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like the &quot;Edge of Tomorrow&quot; is going to be an awesome movie. Which confounds my expectation that it'll be Groundhog Day with power armor and aliens.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I saw it.<br /> <br /> I also expected it to be <i>Groundhog Day</i> with power armor and aliens, and that is exactly what it was. It was awesome!<br /> <br /> Time looping in movies was around long before <i>Groundhog Day</i>, but that movie was so great it came to represent all the films that used it. It is a great film, and it deserves the pedestal it sits on. So when the trailers showed us the basic premise of <i>Edge of Tomorrow</i> (EoT) I, like many others, compared the two. However, the end result does not suffer from being similar to <i>Groundhog Day</i>. Note: I say similar because we do get an explanation for the time looping in EoT that helps to drive the plot, while in <i>Groundhog Day</i> Phil never really understands why he is trapped in the same day until the great conclusion of the film.<br /> <br /> On its own, EoT has a great story, excellent characters, interesting special effects (nothing original, deriving a lot of the effects from other films, but all well used), and all in all, it is a great piece of work. It will never get away from being called '<i>Groundhog Day</i> in Power Armor with Aliens' but in this case that is not a bad thing as both are excellent films.<br /> <br /> Rotten Tomato is giving EoT a 89% critic rating and a 92% fan rating, and imho, that is pretty accurate. EoT is a great film and I look forward to watching it again (which I will probably be doing this evening).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T18:41:05-07:00","id":162064,"title":"","content":"I didn't see it as &quot;Groundhog Day&quot; as much as I saw it as a video game; learn it bit more and get only so far into the game then dying, rinse, repeat. And like many a good video game there's a decent storyline. Add in Tom Cruise and Emily Blunt, and you have something pretty damn good. Cruise shows us all why he's still at the top of his game. And he's not even the badass in this. (at first he's pretty much a dick.) He has plenty of moments where he drops back a bit and lets Blunt shine, and that chemistry shows. And she comes across as pretty hardcore. (I think I would have liked to have heard the conversation they had at the end)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T22:32:03-07:00","id":162219,"title":"","content":"Very pleasantly surprised with how much I enjoyed the <i>Edge</i>. Mostly Flame and Storyteller hit on the things I like, although the editing and framing is <i>fantastic</i> for the story mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T12:53:40-07:00","id":162621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=161910#post161910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bigots aren't known for their critical thinking skills. And tons of Superheroes are unfairly hated in the Marvel Universe, it's pretty much Spider-Man's entire schtick.<br /> <br /> The way the X-Men operate, getting into fights with the Brotherhood, causing massive property damage and then running off when the smoke clears, doesn't exactly endear them to the public. Of course, since sticking around means they're gonna get mobbed, its not much of an option either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats a good point as well. I forget sometimes that Spider-man is hated, well, by the papers anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But yea, the X-Men can't exactly stick around after some of their big fights...<br /> <br /> <br /> BTW, I just saw Edge of Tomorrow with my son and we both loved it!! So yea, I totally agree with ST and Flame. I can't wait to watch it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T19:26:20-07:00","id":163063,"title":"","content":"Quite a few moments that were very funny...and even a couple that were kinda moving...<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The training scenes...I lost track of how many times she shot him dead. That became a funny punchline after that.<br /> As in the farm:<br /> <i>&quot;10 minutes and then I'm killing you.&quot;<br /> &quot;Fine.&quot;</i><br /> Then that scene where he tries to sneak away under an APC but gets crushed by it instead. Shocking but damn I laughed.<br /> Rather poignant however at the end when you realize that he knows everything about her, including that she's the true hero. Whereas she knows nothing about him. That's why I would have liked to have heard that conversation.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T04:19:48-07:00","id":163382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=163063#post163063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite a few moments that were very funny...and even a couple that were kinda moving...<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The training scenes...I lost track of how many times she shot him dead. That became a funny punchline after that.<br /> As in the farm:<br /> <i>&quot;10 minutes and then I'm killing you.&quot;<br /> &quot;Fine.&quot;</i><br /> Then that scene where he tries to sneak away under an APC but gets crushed by it instead. Shocking but damn I laughed.<br /> Rather poignant however at the end when you realize that he knows everything about her, including that she's the true hero. Whereas she knows nothing about him. That's why I would have liked to have heard that conversation.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Oh yea, I couldn't help but laugh when he got crushed trying to roll under that truck. And yea, him getting shot all the time during training was great.<br /> <br /> And yea, there was some very moving stuff. Like the one cycle where he just can't watch her die again, and so he just takes off on his own.<br /> <br /> And I loved that ending. At first I wasn't sure where they were going with it, but where they stopped was perfect.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:52:08-07:00","id":163706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hanged Man</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't bother to see Abrams Trek 2: It's NOT the Wrath of Kahn (Psych! It's actually the Wrath of Kahn).</div> </div> </div> </div>Star Trek: Into Darkness was also not very good, but at least it was a morality play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T10:28:06-07:00","id":163792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hanged Man</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that appealed to me about Star Trek: TOS is the moral, ethical and philosophical questions it tackled (on TV at least). It was a very thoughtful show, and actually relatively light on action for how much we joke about Kirk solving problems with punching. Abrams Trek had none of that. It was a big dumb action movie, with an ensemble cast of cardboard cutouts, and a plot that held up as well as cotton candy in a hurricane.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original series was, despite its camp and its piss-poor effects, ultimately a show about what it means to be human. It took a while for the creators to figure that out, but that's why the dynamic of Kirk, Spock, and McCoy eventually became so central: they form a single person between them. Spock is logic, McCoy is emotion, and Kirk is the balance between the two of them that make a complete and well-balanced person. J.J. Abrams either does not understand that or does not care, and while I don't need or necessarily want a remake to be exactly the same as the original, I do not understand what Abrams had to say about Star Trek as a property that made a remake necessary. I think it was someone in this thread who suggested the whole movie is just his demo reel for Star Wars, and that makes sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T10:47:04-07:00","id":163804,"title":"","content":"Sadly, this has been an on-going trend in sci-fi for decades now - getting more and more away from the foundations, which was exploration of the human condition and how we would react to non-human situations (planets, life-forms, etc). Original and Next Gen Star Trek did this well. Stargate (more the show than the movie, but even the movie had it's moments) did this well for quite some time. X-Files and Quantum Leap barely had any FX at all (no ships, few massive make-up effects, mostly done with trick photography and dim-lighting).<br /> <br /> Early on (print-only and radio shows early), sci-fi was only differentiated from drama (or, sometimes, comedy) by the unlikely/impossible/far into the future situations the characters found themselves in. People stuck on a distant planet facing their fondest desires as an alien trap <i>were still people reacting like people</i>. It was a new way to explore how people <i>really </i>are.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, as long as they have some nice looking CGI shit, it's sci-fi. For a lot of people watching these movies, you could skip the people altogether and just show shit blowing up for 2 hours.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT - Seriously, if they can make a &quot;Sharknado <i>2</i>&quot;, then it's clearly <i><b>not </b></i>about the story or the performances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 06-09-2014, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T05:44:07-07:00","id":164748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=163792#post163792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original series was, despite its camp and its piss-poor effects, ultimately a show about what it means to be human. It took a while for the creators to figure that out, but that's why the dynamic of Kirk, Spock, and McCoy eventually became so central: they form a single person between them. Spock is logic, McCoy is emotion, and Kirk is the balance between the two of them that make a complete and well-balanced person. J.J. Abrams either does not understand that or does not care, and while I don't need or necessarily want a remake to be exactly the same as the original, I do not understand what Abrams had to say about Star Trek as a property that made a remake necessary. I think it was someone in this thread who suggested the whole movie is just his demo reel for Star Wars, and that makes sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really think Abrams wanted to make a Star Wars movie, but settled for Star Trek. Look at the 2009 reboot. It's a much better Star Wars movie than a Star Trek. I love it, but admittedly it's pretty far from what the Original Series is. Though, after Wrath of Khan, nearly every Star Trek movie had be an action movie...and that's all the 2009 Star Trek is.<br /> <br /> I really wish with Into Darkness they'd have done something completely different and not included Khan at all. Or if they just had to, have it where they have to work with him, only to be betrayed by him at the end, with him escaping so they can set up a logical rivalry of some sort.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=163804#post163804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, this has been an on-going trend in sci-fi for decades now - getting more and more away from the foundations, which was exploration of the human condition and how we would react to non-human situations (planets, life-forms, etc). Original and Next Gen Star Trek did this well. Stargate (more the show than the movie, but even the movie had it's moments) did this well for quite some time. X-Files and Quantum Leap barely had any FX at all (no ships, few massive make-up effects, mostly done with trick photography and dim-lighting).<br /> <br /> Early on (print-only and radio shows early), sci-fi was only differentiated from drama (or, sometimes, comedy) by the unlikely/impossible/far into the future situations the characters found themselves in. People stuck on a distant planet facing their fondest desires as an alien trap <i>were still people reacting like people</i>. It was a new way to explore how people <i>really </i>are.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, as long as they have some nice looking CGI shit, it's sci-fi. For a lot of people watching these movies, you could skip the people altogether and just show shit blowing up for 2 hours.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT - Seriously, if they can make a &quot;Sharknado <i>2</i>&quot;, then it's clearly <i><b>not </b></i>about the story or the performances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell me about it, it's pretty sad. Plus, a lot of Sci-Fi stuff are remakes as of late, so they're just rehashing the same shit. Or, like you said, pumping out the shittiest movies with shit CGI....look at nearly anything the Sci-Fi channel does(I refuse to call them syfy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T07:43:33-07:00","id":164825,"title":"","content":"sci fi should be rly deep. agreed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T08:54:17-07:00","id":164854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=164748#post164748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really think Abrams wanted to make a Star Wars movie, but settled for Star Trek. Look at the 2009 reboot. It's a much better Star Wars movie than a Star Trek.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what I think as well. As a Star Trek movie it misses the whole point of Star Trek, but it would have fit in Star Wars fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":787,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","user":"Sorwen","date":". 06-11-2014, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T09:05:48-07:00","id":164858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=164854#post164854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is what I think as well. As a Star Trek movie it misses the whold point of Star Trek, but it would have fit in Star Wars fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a huge Star Wars fan and I don't see where it would have been a good movie for that franchise, either.<br /> <br /> All I remember from the new Star Trek movie was a lot of snippets of unnecessary CGI.....which, despite what was used in the Prequel Trilogy, is <b>not </b>what that franchise is about, either!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">((Dammit, George, why didn't you listen to Professor Campbell's lectures about the Fallen Hero path before you made those!!??!!))</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T09:47:36-07:00","id":164888,"title":"","content":"Not really the movie as whole, but more the tone and pace of it. Least for me.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yd0j97RhZUQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yd0j97RhZUQ\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yd0j97RhZUQ\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yd0j97RhZUQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":24,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","user":"Mr Gone","date":". 06-10-2014, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T10:23:19-07:00","id":164920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=164748#post164748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really think Abrams wanted to make a Star Wars movie, but settled for Star Trek. Look at the 2009 reboot. It's a much better Star Wars movie than a Star Trek. I love it, but admittedly it's pretty far from what the Original Series is. Though, after Wrath of Khan, nearly every Star Trek movie had be an action movie...and that's all the 2009 Star Trek is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the good Star Trek, and some of the not so good ones, have had smart ideas beneath the action. Star Trek 2 was just as much about Kirk grappling with old age and the inevitability of death as it was about Khan's vengeance. And when it comes to that it also is a commentary on vengeance and obsession. Star Trek 6 was very much a commentary on the ending Cold War and old warriors reacting to the end of those hostilities and their old enemies no longer being their enemies. In fact of the original ten films just about all of them had some underlying ideas beneath all the actions, something to chew on in-between space battles and fight scenes.<br /> <br /> The reboot could have been handled better but prior to Into Darkness I gave it a pass simply because I was hopeful for the new universe they were setting up. Now I see it as a pretty bland, typical Hollywood sci-fi junk food, pretty lights and effects but low on substance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=164748#post164748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really wish with Into Darkness they'd have done something completely different and not included Khan at all. Or if they just had to, have it where they have to work with him, only to be betrayed by him at the end, with him escaping so they can set up a logical rivalry of some sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if he was just John Morrison, Star Fleet officer turned terrorist they could have done it much better and smarter. Or they had just decided to do a reboot of the Space Seed story, without Old Spock which was a whole other problem I had with the reboot series, it could have been pretty good. But no they couldn't resist the fanservice. So they went about taking as much as they could from Wrath of Khan without taking in of the intelligent plot and ideas behind all the big moments.<br /> <br /> Oh, and that whole rip off of Spock's sacrifice from Wrath of Khan was nothing more than one big middle finger at all the old Star Trek fans.<br /> <br /> MovieBob has best summed up my overall opinion on Abrams getting Star Wars and Star Trek.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jAg68T1N_9A\" data-code=\"jAg68T1N_9A\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/jAg68T1N_9A/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I agree that Abrams is a decent filmmaker and that's fine, there's wrong with that. So why, oh why, has he gotten the two greatest sci-fi universes out there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T12:12:52-07:00","id":165011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=164920#post164920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually the good Star Trek, and some of the not so good ones, have had smart ideas beneath the action. Star Trek 2 was just as much about Kirk grappling with old age and the inevitability of death as it was about Khan's vengeance. And when it comes to that it also is a commentary on vengeance and obsession. Star Trek 6 was very much a commentary on the ending Cold War and old warriors reacting to the end of those hostilities and their old enemies no longer being their enemies. In fact of the original ten films just about all of them had some underlying ideas beneath all the actions, something to chew on in-between space battles and fight scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say original six, rather than 10. The Next Gen movies are cool on the surface(at least the first), but that's about all they are. Hell, the one with the clone Picard is again just another attempt at Wrath of Khan.<br /> <br /> But yea, I'll go with on the original six...mostly. Even the bad ones had a good under current.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=164920#post164920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, if he was just John Morrison, Star Fleet officer turned terrorist they could have done it much better and smarter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally! Plus, it'd have been a much more original story, which would have been a lot better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=164920#post164920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or they had just decided to do a reboot of the Space Seed story, without Old Spock which was a whole other problem I had with the reboot series, it could have been pretty good. But no they couldn't resist the fanservice. So they went about taking as much as they could from Wrath of Khan without taking in of the intelligent plot and ideas behind all the big moments.<br /> <br /> Oh, and that whole rip off of Spock's sacrifice from Wrath of Khan was nothing more than one big middle finger at all the old Star Trek fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally with you. They got bogged down in trying to cram in as much fanservice as they could, which really hurt the story. It wasn't a terrible movie, but not nearly as good as I'd hoped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T07:51:53-07:00","id":165905,"title":"","content":"I've always hated Search for Spock. And my favorite has always been Voyage Home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T09:42:25-07:00","id":166042,"title":"","content":"I can imagine someone hating <b>Star Trek III: the Search for Spock</b>. After all, it undid a powerful moment in the universe's history for no other reason than to continue the franchise while explaining how Spock can continue to age in time with the rest of the cast. Still, I like that movie just because it underlines the whole ego-superego-id relationship Kirk, McCoy, and Spock have by destroying Kirk's career, ship, and child when one component of that hive-psyche is removed from the equation. Also, it updated Klingons to look like a different species rather than just brown humans with Russian accents, so there's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T10:55:13-07:00","id":166100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=166042#post166042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it updated Klingons to look like a different species rather than just brown humans with Russian accents, so there's that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, they did that in Star Trek: The Motion Picture, but nobody can stay awake during that film long enough to notice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T11:24:45-07:00","id":166115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=148948#post148948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also saw Godzilla. When Godzilla was on-screen, it was amazing. But, it was over an hour before he appears, and for the longest time they kept cutting away from him, which was alittle irritating. But, when he was on screen, it was pretty bad ass...just wish they're been more of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was prepared for &quot;Twenty Minutes with Jerks&quot;, so I was actually pleasantly surprised that it didn't take so long for things to get rolling. Also, current filmmaking theory is that &quot;less is more&quot; which is ironic in this age of special effects...Just look at the first Transformers movie. So, we have to sit through hollywoods' attempts to make us connect to the human POV characters, when we're really just there for the Fantastic Element of the story...<br /> <br /> And, yeah, the constant cutaways practically had me yelling at the screen...was that some sort of cruel joke? Or were there producers somewhere thinking &quot;What, you mean people are actually paying to see the giant monsters fight each other? I don't think so! Throw in some scenes of military action, and endanger the guys' wife and kid some more!&quot; Ugh.<br /> <br /> The firebreathing sequence was incredibly cool, yes, as was everyone's reaction to him by the end...but the whole thing was kinda spoiled for me by the film's insistence on trying to be so &quot;realistic&quot;...much like Man of Steel, in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T13:01:00-07:00","id":166184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=166100#post166100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, they did that in <b>Star Trek: the Motion Picture</b>, but nobody can stay awake during that film long enough to notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I've seen that maybe half a dozen times, and I don't remember ever seeing a Klingon anywhere. When did they show Klingons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T13:06:19-07:00","id":166190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=166115#post166115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was prepared for &quot;Twenty Minutes with Jerks&quot;, so I was actually pleasantly surprised that it didn't take so long for things to get rolling. Also, current filmmaking theory is that &quot;less is more&quot; which is ironic in this age of special effects...Just look at the first Transformers movie. So, we have to sit through hollywoods' attempts to make us connect to the human POV characters, when we're really just there for the Fantastic Element of the story...<br /> <br /> And, yeah, the constant cutaways practically had me yelling at the screen...was that some sort of cruel joke? Or were there producers somewhere thinking &quot;What, you mean people are actually paying to see the giant monsters fight each other? I don't think so! Throw in some scenes of military action, and endanger the guys' wife and kid some more!&quot; Ugh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it would have been different if most of said characters were interesting but of the only two I found interesting... well they killed one of them at the end of the first third while the other was largely pushed to the side for more of Generic McBland and his wife and kid who were just as bland and generic as him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T13:32:47-07:00","id":166203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=166184#post166184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I've seen that maybe half a dozen times, and I don't remember ever seeing a Klingon anywhere. When did they show Klingons?</div> </div> </div> </div>I be