le":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T10:38:39-07:00","id":190474,"title":"","content":"The first Transformers moive was a good take on updating the franchise. All of the others after that were about as Transformers as the two GI Joe movies where GI Joe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T11:19:59-07:00","id":190494,"title":"","content":"That first movie was impressive. There were moments that seemed almost scary. Especially the opening sequence when Blackout took out that military base.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T21:12:14-07:00","id":203465,"title":"","content":"Welp, I finally saw the new Transformers...and was pleasantly surprised!<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Pros:<ul><li>All the silly, stupid, juvenile &quot;humor&quot; that I so detested throughout the series...pretty much gone. There is humor in it, but it doesn't overshadow a much darker, more serious film. It may be telling that the one obvious comedy-relief character dies a horrible death early on...</li> <li>Frank Welker, baby! His &quot;Galvatron&quot; didn't get as much screentime as I'd have liked, but at least he wasn't a criminal waste of a character, like Shockwave was in the last film.</li> <li>Much more focus on the Autobots, esp Prime, as opposed to Bumblebee, who's more of a minor figure this time.</li> <li>Fewer, less annoying human characters. Mark Wahlberg really carried this part pretty well, and it was refreshing to see an adult interacting with the Autos rather than a kid. Kelsey Grammar pretty much OWNED this movie! And Bingbing Li was pretty sweet and cool, and definitely nice to look at...</li> <li>Transformer designs that (gasp) are actually clear and comprehensible, more like the designs from Transformers Prime, tho still with the innards hanging out somewhat. I just wish Prime had kept his G1 cabover look...</li> <li>Instead of making each movie more or less separate, they are clearly going for a more connected myth arc this time. Something about the Transformers' creators (who we briefly glimpse) wanting them back...</li> <li>Lockdown: One of the cooler original characters from more recent franchises, very interesting to see how they portray him here. Something of the &quot;Boba Fett&quot; of Transformers, he may well be a breakout character!</li> <li>The action was pretty over the top and exciting, but that was never a problem with the series...</li> <li>Optimus Prime, brandishing his golden sword while riding Grimlock into battle? Hell yeah!!</li> <li>Rainbow Dash cameo! Nice...</li> </ul>Cons:<ul><li>Cursing Autobots. To be fair, this can make sense...They've been around soldiers most of their time adapting to Earth life, and soldiers cuss. Still rubs me the wrong way, though.</li> <li>It's looong! I'm normally for character development, but there's a lot of scenes that could have been trimmed. Esp some of the chase scenes involving the humans.</li> <li>Human action scenes. There actually was a good reason for some of them, but...I'm just here for the bots, man.</li> <li>Flag City. Here's a drinking game that'll have you wasted before the first hour is done: Take a swig every time an American flag is waving in the shot! Seriously, what was up with that?</li> <li>Product placement: Pretty blatant at times. Interestingly, one of them seems to be for a Chinese drink...</li> <li>The man-made Transformers' transforming sequences...just, ugh.</li> <li>Explosions! Well, I knew what I was getting into...At least one scene is so damn bombastic, it borders on self-parody!</li> <li>...Wasn't this the exact same ending for Prometheus?</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>So, on the whole, there was more to like in it than to dislike, at least for me. It seems that someone, if not Bay himself, is listening to fan complaints and addressing them. If a creator/studio makes an honest effort to improve their product, I see nothing wrong with supporting it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T22:20:35-07:00","id":203514,"title":"","content":"Hand, I'm going to have to disown you. I'm sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T05:30:23-07:00","id":203752,"title":"","content":"I agree with most of what Hand covered.<br /> And even though it's not really shown, the bots took the kid gloves off when dealing with humans. The exception being Wahlberg's character and by extension his daughter and her bf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T10:30:59-07:00","id":203945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=203514#post203514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hand, I'm going to have to disown you. I'm sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Heh. You must do what you feel is right, of course...[/Obi-Wan]<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, I have no vested interest in hating on creators/companies/franchises/whatever...When they go wrong, I call them on it. When they go right, or make an actual effort to correct their mistakes, I give them credit for it. I calls `em like I sees `em, no more, no less. <br /> <br /> I actually WANT good movies, whether they be Transformers, Star Wars, whatever. If Bay continues with the changes he's shown in this movie, maybe we'll actually get some good, even great, TF films in the future! I see nothing wrong with hoping for the best...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T10:34:12-07:00","id":203948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=203752#post203752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with most of what Hand covered.<br /> And even though it's not really shown, the bots took the kid gloves off when dealing with humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it was definitely shown! <br /> <br /> A friend of mine had a problem with Optimus' behavior and actions, as too OOC. I can see that, but I allowed for it, given that, in such *extreme* circumstances, even the best of us can bend, if not break. And Optimus is more appealing, to me at least, if he can be plausibly tested, rather than just being relentlessly perfect and stoic, at all times...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T17:11:09-07:00","id":204372,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm just too cynical or something, but I just can't bring myself to watch that new Transformers. After the last one, I refuse to subject myself to them. That 3rd one was horrible, and while I can suspend my disbelief for somethings, I can only suspend it so far.<br /> <br /> If you open a portal to bring another planet to a planet, neither of them will survive. Also, if half way through the transit of said planet through a portal, if the portal gets turned off, you've just cut that planet in half. It's not just going to hang there and then resume when you turn the portal back on.<br /> <br /> So yea....<br /> <br /> Might be nitpicky, but thats only the tip of the iceberg of my issues with those movies. I really wanted to like them, but I can't...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T21:46:10-07:00","id":205645,"title":"","content":"I could say something snarky about criticizing the &quot;science&quot; of a movie about living, alien robots, but honestly...I feel your pain. Normally, I can handwave these things pretty easily, but, getting back to Abrams' Star Trek, the very notion that a single supernova can *somehow* destroy an entire galaxy is so...ugh!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> At least there was nothing quite that abysmally stupid in the sequel...although the fact that someone in the story process apparently thinks that &quot;cold fusion&quot; literally involves freezing temperatures is pretty damn close. Fortunately, that bit of stupidity was a tiny part of the plot and easily ignored/explained (maybe in the future, they call superfreezing devices &quot;cold fusion&quot; ironically!)...<br /> <br /> In the last TF movie, I was just amused that the &quot;teleporting Cybertron&quot; plot was lifted straight from the classic cartoon, along with the bit about the Autobots' rep getting so bad, they're asked to leave the planet (no Laserbeak dancing with hot chicks in a nightclub, tho!). I dunno, maybe the super scientific alien device has fail safes we can't understand that prevent the very disaster you're talking about?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T21:47:55-07:00","id":205646,"title":"","content":"Also saw Dawn of the Planet of the Apes. Pretty good, tho I don't think it's quite &quot;the movie of the year&quot; like everyone's saying. It's funny to think that Andy Serkis is now basically the King of Mo-Cap Acting, and I don't think I've ever actually seen his face!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T00:53:20-07:00","id":205799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=205646#post205646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's funny to think that Andy Serkis is now basically the King of Mo-Cap Acting, and I don't think I've ever actually seen his face!</div> </div> </div> </div>You have, actually, if you've ever seen Return of the King. He played Smeagol directly in the beginning scene of the film.<br /> <br /> *-*-The More You Know-*-*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T04:28:08-07:00","id":205938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=205645#post205645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could say something snarky about criticizing the &quot;science&quot; of a movie about living, alien robots, but honestly...I feel your pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I can suspend my disbelief enough for transforming alien robots, but that 3rd movie really pushed it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=205645#post205645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normally, I can handwave these things pretty easily, but, getting back to Abrams' Star Trek, the very notion that a single supernova can *somehow* destroy an entire galaxy is so...ugh!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm just defending it, and I don't have the exact quote, but I always took that as the supernova event was threatening to destroy the galaxy as in the Romulans were causing problems and maybe war would break out. Or that because of the time vortex, the galaxy was &quot;destroyed&quot;. I dunno...but yea, saying a supernova would destory a galaxy is pretty dumb.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=205645#post205645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the last TF movie, I was just amused that the &quot;teleporting Cybertron&quot; plot was lifted straight from the classic cartoon, along with the bit about the Autobots' rep getting so bad, they're asked to leave the planet (no Laserbeak dancing with hot chicks in a nightclub, tho!). I dunno, maybe the super scientific alien device has fail safes we can't understand that prevent the very disaster you're talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd hope so. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But yea, I guess it was from the cartoon...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T06:10:31-07:00","id":205983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=205799#post205799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have, actually, if you've ever seen Return of the King. He played Smeagol directly in the beginning scene of the film.<br /> <br /> *-*-The More You Know-*-*</div> </div> </div> </div>He can also be seen, looking actually rather adorable in his blue business suit, in Jennifer Garner's (pre-Affleck) rom-com, 13 Going On 30.<br /> <br /> <br /> ....I mean, I've never seen that before and the ending NEVER makes me cry happy little tears! &lt;_&lt; .... ... &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;_&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T14:02:59-07:00","id":206513,"title":"","content":"So my wife and I saw Snowpiercer a couple weeks ago, and while it didn't get a huge release I'm gonna recommend it to everyone who gets the chance. It's dark and strange, with a vein of black humor that surfaces now and again. While I know some people who just aren't going to be able to get past the core setting of the movie (a train circling a frozen Earth once a year, containing all that remains of humanity), it makes for an interesting concept in the execution.<br /> <br /> Also, I went to see it out of some small spite--there was some attempted-but-failed executive meddling on this one (specifically, one of the Weinsteins wanted to cut out about half an hour of character development and replace it with some narration), and so seeing it in theaters as the director wanted made me kind of happy.<br /> <br /> FWIW, consider it highly endorsed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T17:13:00-07:00","id":206695,"title":"","content":"Oh yea, Snowpiercer was awesome! I really liked it alot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T17:13:48-07:00","id":206696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_poste