id":208407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=208121#post208121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mine too! I just wish Lucas would have for me as an adult too. He made such great movies back in the day....wonder what happened?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>He argued with the union too much and prevented Steven Spielberg from directing <b>Return of the Jedi</b>, thus preventing any and all input he would have from then forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T09:42:33-07:00","id":208415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=206819#post206819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So one thing that's been bugging me for a while is that Indy doesn't actually seem all that important to the resolution of the plot.<br /> I mean sure, he's there, he does heroic things and romances the girl, but in Raiders and Last Crusade, the villains are all done in not by Indy's actions,<br /> but by the very macguffin they've been seeking.<br /> <br /> If Indy hadn't been there, the Nazis still would have obtained the ark and opened it, getting fried in the process.<br /> All the baddies would have either died to the traps in the canyon of the Crescent Moon, Chosen Poorly, or been swallowed by the earth for going beyond the great seal.<br /> Indy didn't need to interact with the plot at all - it would have ended the exact same way.<br /> <br /> And then I realized it WOULD NOT have ended the same way, in fact in a very BAD way, because of one factor - People.<br /> <br /> If Indiana had not found Marion and rescued her in Raiders, she would have been tortured and killed by the Gestapo for the medallion. The Nazis had already captured Indy's dad<br /> in Crusade; indeed, that was the whole reason he embarked on the whole adventure - to rescue his dad. Jones Sr. certainly couldn't have survived all that on his own; he would<br /> have been just as dead as Marion.<br /> <br /> And that is the true measure of Indiana Jones' accomplishments. He doesn't save Things, he saves People. He was only mildly interested in the Grail until his dad disappeared, and he would have<br /> let the Nazis have the Ark if they let Marion go.<br /> <br /> Indiana brought the people he loved safely through the darkest part of their lives, and in the end, that is the true measure of a Hero.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>They used that one on Big Bang Theory recently. I had another counter-argument to yours (but yours is also an excellent point).<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Nazis would NOT have found the Staff of Ra without Indy. They had no clue where to even begin looking. They were trying to find Abner Ravenwood. How many people were going to look for a respected archaeologist with a rare Egyptian artifact <b><i>in a bar in Tibet</i></b>? By the time they tracked down Marion, the war probably would have been over. Indy, however, being still totally in love with and obsessed with her, knew exactly where to go. Oh, and did anyone else notice Herr Toht (the guy in the glasses and black hat) was on the same plane as Indy? THE NAZIS LET THE ALLIES GET THAT MESSAGE!!! They <i>knew </i>Indy would know where to find Abner and Marion and planned to follow him all along. If he hadn't picked up and left, they would have been running their little fascist asses off trying to track down the daughter of a dead man<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MtntTvuv8Aw\" target=\"_blank\"><i><b> IN A BAR IN TIBET!!!</b></i></a></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T12:08:24-07:00","id":208538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=208399#post208399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/blog/6-common-movie-arguments-that-are-always-wrong/\" target=\"_blank\">6 Common movie arguments that are always wrong!</a><br /> <br /> Agree or disagree?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just from the titles, those do sound like rather flimsy arguments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=208415#post208415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had another counter-argument to yours</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. The argument seems to presume that Indy was the ONLY one who knew where the Ravenwoods were, which I find a little bit unlikely. Indy was the ONLY person Abner and Marion were close to that was still alive and could be found?<br /> They probably just followed Indy because he both had a personal history with the Ravenwoods AND would have wanted to find the Ark, so he would have traveled there as fast as he could. But that's just my reaction; it could be true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=208415#post208415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(but yours is also an excellent point)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay! x2","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 07-25-2014, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T14:20:19-07:00","id":208677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=208121#post208121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mine too! I just wish Lucas would have for me as an adult too. He made such great movies back in the day....wonder what happened?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>When you finally realize that the reason you always try to play a sword wielding magic user in games is because of Star Wars you realize just how fucked up a kids influence can be and how long they last. Even now knowing this I cant stop myself from doing it.<br /> <br /> Now excuse me while I go kill a great white shark with a lightsaber to the score from Harry Potter while a glowing finger alien is swayed by a Jamaican sounding alien with a speech impediment to turn control of the galaxy over to a despot.<br /> <br /> Maybe aliens will find my remains in 50 thousand years and turn me into a real boy too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T17:37:28-07:00","id":208904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=208677#post208677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you finally realize that the reason you always try to play a sword wielding magic user in games is because of Star Wars you realize just how fucked up a kids influence can be and how long they last. Even now knowing this I cant stop myself from doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! Whenever I boot up a game with character creation, I almost always go for a melee-magic user with strong morality and a code of honor, and now I know why!<br /> <br /> And if there's any kind of rogue on my team, they better act more like Robin Hood than Dick Turpin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T20:06:26-07:00","id":208978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=208407#post208407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He argued with the union too much and prevented Steven Spielberg from directing <b>Return of the Jedi</b>, thus preventing any and all input he would have from then forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew that Spielberg was set to direct RotJ (and I'm still working on my Parallel World Machine so that I can get to the timeline where that DID happen!), and that he couldn't because he was a member of the Director's Guild, for whatever reason that blocked him from doing so. But I never heard that Lucas was the cause of that problem...<br /> <br /> (They should have just done what Robert Rodriguez did when the Guild told him he couldn't direct a scene in his best bud Tarantino's film: Quit! Why should those guys get to dictate what contributions to movie history they get to make? Well, it was a different time I guess...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorwen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now excuse me while I go kill a great white shark with a lightsaber to the score from Harry Potter while a glowing finger alien <b>is swayed by a Jamaican sounding alien with a speech impediment to turn control of the galaxy over to a despot.</b><br /> <br /> Maybe aliens will find my remains in 50 thousand years and turn me into a real boy too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got all those references except for the bolded part...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T20:18:50-07:00","id":208983,"title":"","content":"Jar Jar Binks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T21:16:27-07:00","id":209014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=208983#post208983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jar Jar Binks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where?! [spins around]<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, nevermind, I get it.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T12:59:09-07:00","id":209480,"title":"","content":"I have seen <b><u>Lucy</u></b>. And it didn't suck.<br /> Less violent than I thought it'd be. And more...preachy, or philosophical if you will.<br /> And all Johansson.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T14:08:15-07:00","id":209517,"title":"","content":"So, Wonder Woman:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://postimage.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://s30.postimg.org/cqv11lzrl/image.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> Overall I think she looks pretty well for the role. My personal vision of a &quot;real life&quot; WW would be more muscular, but that is not a big deal. The armor looks good in my opinion, more complex and ornate than I would do it, but such detailed designs tend to work fairly well in film. A nit to pick: I don't like the boot soles, would prefer if they were flat or nearly flat.<br /> <br /> Now, what I would really like is for the armor in the actual movie to have much more vivid colors than in this poster. Get some real red and gold in there. Superman's outfit in Man of Steel was very muted, though, so I shouldn't expect much.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T14:34:22-07:00","id":209532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=209480#post209480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have seen <b><u>Lucy</u></b>. And it didn't suck.<br /> Less violent than I thought it'd be. And more...preachy, or philosophical if you will.<br /> And all Johansson.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to see Lucy.<br /> <br /> Rexburg doesn't show any R-rated movies at its theaters. :-(","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T14:44:43-07:00","id":209536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=209517#post209517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Wonder Woman:</div> </div> </div> </div>Something about that image bugs me...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T18:59:57-07:00","id":209676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=209536#post209536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something about that image bugs me...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... something about it doesn't sit right with me either. Not sure what it is but its there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T19:20:53-07:00","id":209702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=209676#post209676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... something about it doesn't sit right with me either. Not sure what it is but it's there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only colors are shades of brown; the obviously greenscreened background gives her an aura that, when combined with the brownness, makes her look like a character in <b>300</b>; her sword has no tip and is sized wrong, looking like something you find in a bin of accessories at a Halloween store; the combination of wedge heels and camera perspective make her feet look like they were drawn by that dude who does all the artwork for Pathfinder books and gives everyone clubfoot; there's no indication of what those straps on her chest and hips are for; the vaguely skeletal haze behind her brings to mind images of a plane's cargo hold if that hold was split down the middle and spread open, which, given that she has a sword, makes me wonder if she didn't cause that flaming wreckage behind her.<br /> <br /> I am very disappointed, but--and I say this in all seriousness--not nearly as disappointed as I was prepared to be. Of course, it's hard to get too invested when I have no interest in seeing the end product anyway.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh! And another thing that doesn't sit right with you is you thought we had moved beyond leather armor on superheroes in like 2004.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T19:36:09-07:00","id":209716,"title":"","content":"Well...after staring at it for a while...I'm leaning towards that the appearance is more promising. (However needs more muscle tone. (This is my <a href=\"http://th00.deviantart.net/fs71/PRE/i/2013/118/8/4/wonder_woman_by_jeffach-d59egpa.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">choice pic</a> for WW. And I'd be happy with the armor shown above replacing the Old Glory teddy)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T20:49:35-07:00","id":209784,"title":"","content":"AH Xena warrior princess in high heels. <br /> <br /> You know, I'm kinda prefering the reboot they did on her recently because it put her in an outfit that largely makes sense for an amazon warrior that came to america in the current day... It was basically biker leathers over a decent outfit.<br /> <br /> But hey, it's good to see that in a dark and gritty reboot process in which they have no problem making batman's gear look military, his outfit look like real armor they're still perfectly willing to embrace the hilarity of making wonderwoman a glamazon in high heels, thong, boob plate (complete with what looks like it could be a subtle nipple projection, hard to tell on the photo but it looks like it's there on her right).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T06:44:25-07:00","id":210096,"title":"","content":"It's actually not bad, at least it's waaay better than I was expected, but...are those the actual colors? Maybe I'm being hopeful that they're not, but the photo looks like it might be taken under some weird kind of lighting or something...I *really* hope those are the actual colors, because WW needs to be &quot;darkened&quot; even less than Superman does! <br /> <br /> It just really pains how much Warners/DC keeps tragically *missing the point* with their own characters, how they've been misled into thinking that &quot;going dark&quot; is what's popular! The funny thing about that is that they mostly believe that because &quot;that's what made Marvel successful&quot;, but if they would just LOOK at the actual movies Marvel is putting out, they would see Bright, Colorful Costumes! Fun, Light-Hearted Adventure! Boundless Hope and Optimism! In short, all the things that DC originally brought to the table in the first place, and that world-weary audiences are starved for now! <br /> <br /> And DC has the original characters, who are literally custom-made for this...and they choose to ignore all that and go the exact other way off a cliff, because *someone* told them &quot;Hey, The Dark Knight and Watchmen are the sort of things people really want to see!&quot; (yeah, back in the 90s...)<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ugh, these movies could be so great, so easily, and yet...gah, it just makes me sad...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T07:06:35-07:00","id":210126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=210096#post210096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are those the actual colors? Maybe I'm being hopeful that they're not, but the photo looks like it might be taken under some weird kind of lighting or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's obviously shot through some kind of sepia-tone filter, but I personally can't glean much hope that you'll see the actual colors later. I mean, this is <i>Zach Snyder</i>. He shot his entire first big movie under a sepia filter, and all his films I'm personally aware of seem to have been shot under various kinds of color filters. What I'm saying is, I doubt brown is the only color she wears, but since it's Snyder, I can't make myself assume he will allow us to <i>see</i> those colors, so the real colors don't actually matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:04:35-07:00","id":210257,"title":"","content":"I'll watch it, but I really don't have a lot of faith in it. DC Animated movies are fantastic. Live action? Not so much. Marvel is so far ahead of them right now it's a joke. Guardians of the Galaxy moves the needle even further along. It's THAT good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:10:06-07:00","id":210262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=210257#post210257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll watch it, but I really don't have a lot of faith in it. DC Animated movies are fantastic. Live action? Not so much. Marvel is so far ahead of them right now it's a joke. Guardians of the Galaxy moves the needle even further along. It's THAT good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do you live that you've already seen Guardians of the Galaxy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:30:57-07:00","id":210293,"title":"","content":"I'm going to have to avoid a lot of threads like this for the next week or so. The people who've seen it seem so enthused they want to post reviews without spoiler tags, and I want to go into this movie fresh, so yeah. Not that I'm saying Dude of Legend plans to do what I just described; I'm just saying, it's happened enough already that I'm taking precautions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T09:41:51-07:00","id":210309,"title":"","content":"From some early reviews Guardians of 