<br /> Or, they could still do it, if they went with animation! So long as it was better animation than that awful Xena cartoon from back in the day...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T10:08:26-07:00","id":211390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=211315#post211315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, she's showing up on Agents of SHIELD, so someone must feel she still has some pull...<br /> <br /> Or, they could still do it, if they went with animation! So long as it was better animation than that awful Xena cartoon from back in the day...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0902272/?ref_=nv_sr_6\" target=\"_blank\">She already did do the voice.</a> Still not as satisfying as seeing her kicking ass in the name of Zeus on the big screen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T18:47:05-07:00","id":216332,"title":"","content":"<b>Guardians of the Galaxy</b> is a funny movie and a good time. You should go see it, but you already know that, don't you? I'll be editing this post to discuss it more in depth.<br /> <br /> First off, almost everything I have to say will be put in spoilers. Second, almost everything I have to say will be negative, which I think I need to take a moment to clarify: I <i>like</i> <b>Guardians of the Galaxy</b>. It is not a great movie, but it is a very good one that I think anyone can enjoy, and if you don't enjoy it, then I want to you to show me your reflection in a silver-backed mirror because I'm pretty sure you're a goddamned vampire or something. It's just that I can't really talk about the positive stuff because the positive stuff is the jokes, and what kind of dick would I have to be to spoil the jokes for you by transcribing them into a text format where they'd lose most of their charm?<br /> <br /> I recommend <b>Guardians of the Galaxy</b>. Never doubt it. It's just the nature of comedies is I can only talk about the bad stuff.<br /> <br /> Right. Here we go.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The movie falls short of being great, in my estimation, because it's just a little bit too light. The pacing feels very rushed to me, about as rushed and forced as the opening &quot;You're in a tavern and you see some adventurers&quot; opening every newbie GM has done. I'd love it if the movie would have slowed down to give us more time to spend with the characters, but it was too busy being funny for me to ever really get interested in their drama or development.<br /> <br /> The weakest link is Zoe Saldana's Gamora. I'm not sure what to make of the character. On the one hand, she's an assassin everyone in the universe can identify by sight, but on the other, she gets slapped around easier than any other character, and her characterization seems inconsistent, at one moment battle-hardened and at another jumping like the scream queen in a slasher flick because someone slapped a window.<br /> <br /> At times, when I'm being snarky to myself, I think this isn't a movie at all, but just a collection of Easter eggs arranged in a three-act format. That's unfair, though. I don't think the Easter eggs actually do anything to detract from the movie, and in fact, I think they serve a very important purpose in the narrative: they demonstrate how <i>weird</i> this galaxy is. It's <i>weird</i>, man, and what's more, you'll probably notice that every time someone stops to be stumped by its weirdness, that character is punished for it. I counted at least fifteen people who died because they stopped to say, &quot;Wait, what?&quot; instead of just rolling with it like the Guardians did. I'm not sure if that is intended more as a statement about the universe or the nature of this particular movie--i.e., a warning to the audience to not get hung up on it and just let the movie be the movie--but either way, I like the effect.<br /> <br /> I'm not a big fan of Bradley Cooper's voice for Rocket. I also feel like this should have been an R-rated movie, because I think even people who aren't fans of the comics will pick up on Rocket being intended as a foul, brusque character, but the PG-13 rating really restricts him, so his scenes come off to me like the edited-for-network reruns of <b>South Park</b>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'd read someone saying this movie would be the <b>Star Wars</b> of this generation, so I went in with high hopes that were somewhat let down. I don't think the movie is epic enough for that. It is, however, a hell of a good time, funny and weirdly honest about its humor in ways that I think are better than, say, <b>the Avengers</b>; compare the artificial snark of Tony's one-liners to the way the prisoner whines at Drax and I think you'll see where I'm coming from. You should go see this movie, but only if you like having fun watching good movies. If not, then this probably isn't the flick for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 08-05-2014, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T13:21:10-07:00","id":216847,"title":"","content":"I just saw it Jim and I loved it!! Might have been rushed a tad, but it was just plain fun! And thats what I was looking for in a movie like this, something that is fun.<br /> <br /> I can't wait to see where they go from here!<br /> <br /> BTW<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I loved the Howard the Duck cameo! That was so awesome!!</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T13:37:56-07:00","id":216867,"title":"","content":"Good to know I won't be wasting my money, though I was going to see GOG anyway despite good or bad reviews. It was one my favourite comics when I was young and I've wanted to see it on silver screen for ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T16:51:08-07:00","id":217059,"title":"","content":"Guardians of the Galaxy was entertaining.<br /> Had some issues though...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">On the whole there seems to be a de-leveling of power in just about every way.<br /> The Nova Corps is shown to be this pathetic force that can barely hold back a single Kree warship...really? And yet they had the just signed some peace treaty with the Kree...yeah..sure.<br /> <br /> Drax's monomania isn't focused on Thanos, it's focused on Ronan. Only at the end does that get fixed because...Ronan gets killed?<br /> <br /> There's this &quot;humanizing&quot; or perhaps better to say &quot;terranizing&quot; element. No one seems neither more than or less than capable than a normal Terran. It's no wonder that Groot is the &quot;big gun&quot; here. And the &quot;Collector is no powerful &quot;Elder&quot; either as we see at the end credits. Nor is Gamora feared for her tie to Thanos.<br /> But then this is the nice and fluffy Disney Cinematic Universe so I suppose that's to be expected.<br /> <br /> The one scene where Ronan meets Thanos was well done. Ronan is no Loki to treat only with a Servant of Thanos. Indeed Ronan rather unceremoniously kills said Servant and talks directly to Thanos.<br /> That pointed out, this is the very two dimensional Ronan of the earlier comic-book years.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The movie was good on it's own. But any connection to the comic-books is pretty much in name only.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T08:20:30-07:00","id":217414,"title":"","content":"Saw guardians last night in imax. I'd say it's a good film but I expected better. The opening scene is brilliantly done but the rest of the movie is not as funny as I expected. The cineworld staff showing us to our seats were all kitted out in guardians dress up including a really cute girl spray tanned green which was oddly ....really attractive (latent ST:OS childhood memory coming back?!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T11:09:38-07:00","id":217529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=216847#post216847\" rel=\