lineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T20:36:35-08:00","id":300692,"title":"","content":"Just glad they went with Cumberbatch for Strange instead of someone like Joaquin Phoenix or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T18:22:32-08:00","id":306300,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Interstellar</b></u><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The movie is superficial when it comes to science. Of the big three sciences only physics was represented..kinda sorta well enough. Astronomy not so much. Biology was non-existent (I kept wondering when decontamination was supposed to kick in after visiting a potential planet, but I got nothing.)<br /> The tech seems represented in the form of two &quot;robots&quot; primarily AI programmed with human emotive responses. (TARS was the main with Honesty factored in at 90%. Diplomacy prevented it from being too honest. Sense of humor factored in at 90% as well, but turned down to 75% because the sarcasm was just a bit much.)<br /> As it is, humanity is pretty much hopeless and needs a bit of help...from &quot;others&quot; to get out of the galaxy. Those others seem to play out that they may be &quot;us.&quot; Not too sure... Surprise cameo by Matt Damon who isn't exactly a good guy.<br /> This movie isn't for the science guru. It's more a philosophical exercise. There's talk in the movie about fuel and supplies, but it doesn't get specific. Nor does it go into psychological issues that can potentially happen. (I recall reading an indepth plan NASA had for a Mars mission. This movie had none of the things mentioned that should have been.)<br /> The connection between father and daughter was the main motivation here. And this is the emotional issue that kicks in.<br /> I could have easily forgiven the slipshod science for the sake of presenting a story, but I wasn't too entertained by the story. (The one guy stuck in the ship in orbit near a black hole. One hour <i>roughly</i> on the planet nearby equaled 7 years on that ship. They got stuck on the planet a little longer and that guy hung in there for 23 years. Really? Yeah, I got that he &quot;hibernated&quot; in and out, but I needed more)<br /> So, a science movie was a miss. An entertaining story was also a miss.<br /> I wanted to like this movie but I found little to like. (Hathaway in space and not one person suggested repopulating a planet with her? Well, I was thinking it)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T12:54:01-08:00","id":306864,"title":"","content":"The last movie I saw theatrically was when I took my parents out to see the recent rerelease of Gone With The Wind...unfortunately, I made a mistake and didn't choose the theater that was showing it in IMAX! Oh, well...<br /> <br /> I'm kinda wanting to see Big Hero Six, but I'm torn: Unfortunately, due to the climate of theatrical animation in this country, the trailers are really playing up the silly/slapstick comedy, which is understandable, as they think they have to to get kids in the seats, but *I can't stand that*! Still, trailers are not always representative; the trailers for Rise of the Guardians made it look like Santa's Helper Elves dominated the movie (appealing to all those kids who loooved the Minions, no doubt), when they were actually barely in it. To be clear, I don't mind humor, I just don't like &quot;stupid&quot; humor, esp arising from &quot;stupid&quot; characters...<br /> <br /> So, the one question I have about BH6 is: What is the ratio of comedy to action/drama? Are there action scenes on par with RotG, The Incredibles, and Megamind (those last two, btw, are great examples of how to have fun and funny animation that aren't exactly &quot;kid's films&quot;)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T19:40:59-08:00","id":307099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=300692#post300692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just glad they went with Cumberbatch for Strange instead of someone like Joaquin Phoenix or the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope they change it. Ralph Fiennes is perfect for it and has the right age and everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T19:40:59-08:00","id":307100,"title":"","content":"Big Hero 6 is awesome as hell. I laughed, I cheered, I cried-and for a second, I was scared in a way that Terminator always failed to deliver on. Go see it. The balance is neatly handed, and easily on par with Incredibles and Megamind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T10:28:16-08:00","id":308341,"title":"","content":"Consider me sold, then! I'll probably see it (or Interstellar) on my day off tomorrow. Incidentally, I'd also add the Kung Fu Panda movies to the list of animated films with a great blend of action/comedy/drama!<br /> <br /> Anyone seen Birdman yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T13:15:35-08:00","id":311608,"title":"","content":"Just saw Big Hero 6, very much recommended.<br /> <br /> I won't spoil the plot, but it did have more complexity and pathos than I expected from a kid's movie. I grew up watching Batman: the Animated Series and Animaniacs, so I always appreciate it when media folks don't treat children like fragile-souled imbeciles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T15:35:29-08:00","id":313326,"title":"","content":"Went to see interstellar - very disappointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T16:30:00-08:00","id":314902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfAsh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=313326#post313326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Went to see interstellar - very disappointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>What didn't you like about it?<br /> <br /> Anyway...<br /> <br /> I saw Big Hero 6 yesterday and loved it!! Such a good movie!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T16:34:32-08:00","id":314926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=306300#post306300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Interstellar</b></u><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The movie is superficial when it comes to science. Of the big three sciences only physics was represented..kinda sorta well enough. Astronomy not so much. Biology was non-existent (I kept wondering when decontamination was supposed to kick in after visiting a potential planet, but I got nothing.)<br /> The tech seems represented in the form of two &quot;robots&quot; primarily AI programmed with human emotive responses. (TARS was the main with Honesty factored in at 90%. Diplomacy prevented it from being too honest. Sense of humor factored in at 90% as well, but turned down to 75% because the sarcasm was just a bit much.)<br /> As it is, humanity is pretty much hopeless and needs a bit of help...from &quot;others&quot; to get out of the galaxy. Those others seem to play out that they may be &quot;us.&quot; Not too sure... Surprise cameo by Matt Damon who isn't exactly a good guy.<br /> This movie isn't for the science guru. It's more a philosophical exercise. There's talk in the movie about fuel and supplies, but it doesn't get specific. Nor does it go into psychological issues that can potentially happen. (I recall reading an indepth plan NASA had for a Mars mission. This movie had none of the things mentioned that should have been.)<br /> The connection between father and daughter was the main motivation here. And this is the emotional issue that kicks in.<br /> I could have easily forgiven the slipshod science for the sake of presenting a story, but I wasn't too entertained by the story. (The one guy stuck in the ship in orbit near a black hole. One hour <i>roughly</i> on the planet nearby equaled 7 years on that ship. They got stuck on the planet a little longer and that guy hung in there for 23 years. Really? Yeah, I got that he &quot;hibernated&quot; in and out, but I needed more)<br /> So, a science movie was a miss. An entertaining story was also a miss.<br /> I wanted to like this movie but I found little to like. (Hathaway in space and not one person suggested repopulating a planet with her? Well, I was thinking it)</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>While it wasn't perfect, I still enjoyed. The science was enough to keep me interested. I loved the Robots! They were great, and pretty original in form.<br /> <br /> I was more just glad this movie wasn't a remake or sequel, and it was nice to see something original, if a little derivative of some similar space movies...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T16:46:38-08:00","id":314930,"title":"","content":"I thought the robots were the best part of the movie. They were indeed quite original and even though I might have been disappointed in the film there's this thinking from Nolan that shows in his movies that makes me look forward to his next project, whatever it may be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T11:11:51-08:00","id":315532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=314902#post314902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What didn't you like about it?<br /> <br /> Anyway...<br /> <br /> I saw Big Hero 6 yesterday and loved it!! Such a good movie!</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadowflames post pretty much covered it. I'll add all that smalshy stuff really put me off. Anne Hathaways so called physicists' whining about love being the 5th dimension killed it for me (she's still gorgeous though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). There they are, the world 'top scientists' trying to save the world and she wants to gamble it all on love. I have a background in science and any scientist I've met, male or female, would never think like that.<br /> One of the things I liked about 2010 was that it didnt need to resort to this type of nonsense - it stuck to the scientific principles a lot more than most movies IMO.<br /> <br /> Where can I find the damn 'spoiler' button so I can go into more detail ? lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1440,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","user":"LordOfAsh","date":". 11-18-2014, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T18:38:13-08:00","id":315814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfAsh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=315532#post315532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadowflames post pretty much covered it. I'll add all that smalshy stuff really put me off. Anne Hathaways so called physicists' whining about love being the 5th dimension killed it for me (she's still gorgeous though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/s