m.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T08:04:46-08:00","id":321832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=320987#post320987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Order of the Phoenix was my least favorite Harry Potter book and my favorite movie because the editing was crap. I think they did an excellent job translating Hunger Games and Catching Fire to the screen and hope the ending of Mockingjay fixes the problems with that book too.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with the movie was it left out/changed some of what was actually good about the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T12:15:07-08:00","id":322050,"title":"","content":"Anyway, there is this talk going on in my other forum, so I will ask here too:<br /> <br /> How do you feel about the way Jackson adapted LOTR?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T12:28:22-08:00","id":322061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=322050#post322050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, there is this talk going on in my other forum, so I will ask here too:<br /> <br /> How do you feel about the way Jackson adapted LOTR?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he mostly missed the point. It was supposed to be about subtle acts of ordinary goodness and kindness and ended up about how Aragorn and Gandalf died for our sins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T12:31:35-08:00","id":322063,"title":"","content":"My opinion is that movies are good enough for casual audience, but it's worth to delve into books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T12:39:05-08:00","id":322068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=322050#post322050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, there is this talk going on in my other forum, so I will ask here too:<br /> <br /> How do you feel about the way Jackson adapted LOTR?</div> </div> </div> </div>With <b>Lord of the Rings</b>, he did great. The entire story is a massive tome with multiple (what should have been) side bars that bog it down. Things were added, things were taken away, but the story, themes, and moods were preserved sufficiently for a screen adaptation.<br /> <br /> With <b>The Hobbit</b>, not so much. 2 movies would have been plenty to cover the whole book. 3 was unnecessary. 1 would have done the trick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T12:45:05-08:00","id":322077,"title":"","content":"Quoting one user on what things were done wrong in the adaptation (this is what happened in the books):<br /> <br /> Gimli is not actually a joke character.<br /> Legolas doesn't do everything.<br /> Aragorn isn't trying to run from his responsibilities and instead has been working for decades to reclaim his throne. There is no love triangle. His sword gets reforged as soon as possible instead of in like the third movie. Also he's honorable and doesn't murder emissaries from behind during parley.<br /> Elrond is friendly with Aragorn and isn't a dick.<br /> Faramir doesn't get seriously tempted by the Ring; he just turns away.<br /> Denethor is a great man who fell into despair instead of just nuts.<br /> In the backstory Sauron actually goes down fighting Gil Galad and Elendil; he doesn't murderstomp everyone and then randomly explodes because his finger got cut off after he slooowlyyy tried to give Isildur a hug or something.<br /> Sauron's final death is actually cool and not a lighthouse looking around and poofing out.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. 