","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=345881#post345881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Hobbit: Battle of Five Armies</u></b>And the purists already hate these movies.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not a purist and I haven't even watched the movies so I don't have an exact opinion. But I will always be suspicious when one book with 300 pages takes the same amount of movies that a book of 1200 pages and especially when it takes a least amount of hours to read the book than to watch the movies. Unless I would be terribly surprised by watching the Hobbit Trilogy, I'd say it's nothing but a publicity stunt and squeezing the tit for the ever last drop of milk.<br /> <br /> It is probably entertaining as a Sunday movie. I'll watch it someday, probably.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T06:44:23-08:00","id":347360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=347282#post347282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not a purist and I haven't even watched the movies so I don't have an exact opinion. But I will always be suspicious when one book with 300 pages takes the same amount of movies that a book of 1200 pages and especially when it takes a least amount of hours to read the book than to watch the movies. Unless I would be terribly surprised by watching the Hobbit Trilogy, I'd say it's nothing but a publicity stunt and squeezing the tit for the ever last drop of milk.<br /> <br /> It is probably entertaining as a Sunday movie. I'll watch it someday, probably.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am a purist and I do hate these movies, but I must clarify one thing: Peter Jackson is attempting to use details from Tolkien's notes and the LOTR backstory to fill in details of what happens in the Hobbit, like the fact that Gandalf just kind of wanders off during the second act for no apparent reason in the novel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T21:19:21-08:00","id":352312,"title":"","content":"Yes, the movies are based on more than just the one novel, and he added a bit of his own story as well.<br /> Part 3 was... okay? It was lacking in many ways and while I was entertained in part, I was mostly bored by the film. This story would have been better served as a pair of movies. Peter Jackson stretched it too far and the whole suffered for it, imho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":