ttp://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T20:52:09-08:00","id":362047,"title":"","content":"So, according to a reporter from Variety, Scarlet Johansson accepted the role of Major Motoko Kusanagi on an adaptation of Ghost in the Shell by Dreamworks.<br /> <br /> I like her, but I wish that the studio was willing to take a change on a Nipponic actress (Rinko Kikuchi already looked a lot like Motoko in Pacific Rim, for instance). Still, if they <i>must</i> have someone with enough star power to get butts on seats (because Ghost in the Shell may be well known among Anime fans, but that is not exactly enough to make Hollywood-grade returns on a movie, I suspect) and who can do well on an action/espionage/sci-fi movie, I'm sure she can do it. Still, the movie will likely get some bad press for the whitewashing, so they better hope Scarlet Johansson's and whoever else is in the main roles can bring enough people to compensate for that.<br /> <br /> It is a vicious circle of not having sufficiently famous Asian actors for leading movies (Jet Li, Jackie Chan, Ming-Na Wen, Lucy Liu and so on are getting pretty old for action movies) and not having Asian actors in movies making them never sufficiently famous to lead movies, though.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I wonder which version of Ghost in the Shell continuity they will ruin, I mean, <i>adapt </i>for the movie ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T05:45:22-08:00","id":362359,"title":"","content":"I'll say here what I've said elsewhere: I think there's potential in this casting. In a manga that explores the idea of what sex, gender, and sexual orientation mean when the body containing those traits is artificial, there's room to explore what race means as well as a Japanese woman picks an Anglo body for purposes of fashion of whatever (assuming the live-action movie is still about Japan and Japanese characters, which it may not be); what makes a person Japanese, once the body is removed from the equation?<br /> <br /> Of course, the guy set to direct is the one who churned out <b>Snow White and the Huntsman</b>, so I have no reason to believe he intends to pursue such a topic with his casting choice. I'm just saying it's a way the movie could go. It's still pretty whitewash-y, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T10:13:57-08:00","id":362594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=362359#post362359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll say here what I've said elsewhere: I think there's potential in this casting. In a manga that explores the idea of what sex, gender, and sexual orientation mean when the body containing those traits is artificial, there's room to explore what race means as well as a Japanese woman picks an Anglo body for purposes of fashion of whatever (assuming the live-action movie is still about Japan and Japanese characters, which it may not be); what makes a person Japanese, once the body is removed from the equation?<br /> <br /> Of course, the guy set to direct is the one who churned out <b>Snow White and the Huntsman</b>, so I have no reason to believe he intends to pursue such a topic with his casting choice. I'm just saying it's a way the movie could go. It's still pretty whitewash-y, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually Snow White and the Huntsman was a deliciously deep film saddled with an unfortunate star whose only talents were looking waiflike and sad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T12:32:31-08:00","id":362806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=362047#post362047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, according to a reporter from Variety, Scarlet Johansson accepted the role of Major Motoko Kusanagi on an adaptation of Ghost in the Shell by Dreamworks.<br /> <br /> I like her, but I wish that the studio was willing to take a change on a Nipponic actress (Rinko Kikuchi already looked a lot like Motoko in Pacific Rim, for instance). Still, if they <i>must</i> have someone with enough star power to get butts on seats (because Ghost in the Shell may be well known among Anime fans, but that is not exactly enough to make Hollywood-grade returns on a movie, I suspect) and who can do well on an action/espionage/sci-fi movie, I'm sure she can do it. Still, the movie will likely get some bad press for the whitewashing, so they better hope Scarlet Johansson's and whoever else is in the main roles can bring enough people to compensate for that.<br /> <br /> It is a vicious circle of not having sufficiently famous Asian actors for leading movies (Jet Li, Jackie Chan, Ming-Na Wen, Lucy Liu and so on are getting pretty old for action movies) and not having Asian actors in movies making them never sufficiently famous to lead movies, though.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I wonder which version of Ghost in the Shell continuity they will ruin, I mean, <i>adapt </i>for the movie ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div> I dropped it before it even came out. Not gonna watch this garbage. I like Scarllet but come the HELL on. They should've just gotten Megumi Hayashibara or Rinko Kikuchi and actually, I don't know, set it in Japan. Its kind of important to plot. Like really important to plot. TBH I don't give a fuck about them getting buts in the seats. No reason to sacrifice the integrity of the piece for that. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T10:49:04-08:00","id":369867,"title":"","content":"I know I'm WAY behind on this one, and maybe it was just me who felt like this while watching it, but did anyone else expect Spike Jonze's <b>Where the Wild Things Are</b> to be that uncomfortable to watch?<br /> <br /> Not because it's a badly made/acted/written film. Just the opposite. It is <i><b>so </b></i>damn accurate to how a lonely boy from a broken home would feel and react it was making me squirm while watching it. The monster were so nonchalant about eating him and tearing down everything as to be way scarier than they seemed in the book. And their personalities: the reflections of the angry little boy who acts out, the insecure little boy who isn't sure what to do and the other one who never gets listened to, the abusive female (his sister? his mother?) who berates him and tears apart everything he tries to build, the other one who's trying to be nice to him but makes no sense to the others and just seems to agitate everything, the single voice of reason in the middle of everything else trying to keep peace and quite the angry one.<br /> <br /> I'm glad I watched it before letting the Baby Bears see it. I don't know if I'd want to let them watch it until they're older and can understand some of what's going on better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T18:45:59-08:00","id":370559,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">That moment when Max was acting out when he stood on top of the table and demanded of his mother; <i>&quot;Woman, feed me!&quot;</i> I kinda laughed. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T19:16:10-08:00","id":373221,"title":"","content":"John Wick is a treasure of a movie. If you don't hate action movies, you should see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T09:28:50-08:00","id":373544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=373221#post373221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View