e.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Are they... trying to make Batman a villain? Yeah, he's an anti-hero in his darker depictions, but if this is the first major motion picture where he's an out-and-out villain...<br /> <br /> GOOD.<br /> <br /> At least they're not trying to ride Marvel's coattails with the &quot;heroes who sometimes fight each other&quot; schtick. This way, they're trying to do something new, something audiences probably haven't seen before. They're mixing it up, playing with expectations. Heck, it looked like Bruce was using GUNS at one point! GUNS!<br /> <br /> If they were actually smart enough to realize they need to throw a real curveball with this one to compete with Marvel and Disney, I might actually go see it. Maybe.<br /> <br /> ...Oh who are we kidding, it doesn't look very good anyway.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Edit: I do have to give them credit for Batman's voice modulator, a lot more convincing and intimidating than growling real low and hoping nobody laughs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 04-20-2015, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","ti