attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T09:33:05-07:00","id":518203,"title":"","content":"I was just gonna ask if anyone had seen MM yet. I also never really &quot;got&quot; that whole post-apocalyptic thing (other than Fist of the North Star, which was cool for other reasons). But the reviews have been good, and if you say it's more than past depictions, then maybe I'll give it a shot...<br /> <br /> This thread has been curiously silent, recently. Did any of those who hadn't seen Avengers yet get around to doing so?Anyone looking forward to Tomorrowland?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T10:40:14-07:00","id":518292,"title":"","content":"All the mentioned movies I'm waiting for them to hit DVD before I watch them, but I am curious about Tomorrowland, but that's mostly because I'm a sucker for the puply retro-futuretech of the 30's and 50's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:17:35-07:00","id":518502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=518203#post518203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone looking forward to Tomorrowland?</div> </div> </div> </div>*raises hand* Won't be seeing it right away, as I am poor. But when it hits the cheap theater, probably. See the strange Canadian's reasons above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T19:40:36-07:00","id":518691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=518203#post518203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did any of those who hadn't seen Avengers yet get around to doing so?Anyone looking forward to Tomorrowland?</div> </div> </div> </div>Saw Age of Ultron about a week or so ago; I liked it quite a bit, but I suspect I'm Marvel's target audience for the MCU because I find even their weakest offerings entertaining in some fashion. So, mileage may vary.<br /> <br /> As for Tomorrowland... meh, will wait for positive reviews before seeing it, if I do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T12:09:09-07:00","id":519832,"title":"","content":"It's been a while but here's two standouts. One has just made it onto Netflix.<br /> <br /> Zombeavers. The name gives a glimpse into the depths of the movie, but the boundlessness can only be truly appreciated by watching it in its entirety.<br /> <br /> But not really. It's a B Movie. Not a 'So bad it's good,' type, but an overall okay movie on its own. It probably won't be remembered as fondly as other, more noteworthy zomcoms like Sean of the Dead, but you'll probably see a scene or two you'll keep with you long after the movie's over.<br /> <br /> Put simply, a few college girls decide to take a trip to a cabin by a lake. For bonding. One's been having trouble with her boyfriend, her best friend doesn't know what she sees in him, another pines for her boyfriend to the point that she arranged for him to come so they can hook up, and the other boyfriends tag along.<br /> <br /> Also, toxic waste is turning beavers into zombeavers. This quickly becomes a problem. Especially considering what the bite of a zombeaver does to a human.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I think Cortney Palm did really well in it, I was fully expecting her to be the trashy friend who died first but she sort of stole the show. All the writing and characterization was well done, though, considering the effort usually put into movies like these.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Horsehead. This movie hearkens back to the thriller flicks of the 70s and giallo that didn't necessarily involve a monster beyond the ones in a character's own mind.<br /> <br /> Jessica, who seems to be around college age, comes back to her family's home in, I think, the English country to attend a wake for her grandmother. She has a history of night terrors and sleep paralysis and, lately, has started learning about lucid dreaming in order to try and deal with it after a few particularly enigmatic dreams in her bedroom, next to the one where her grandmother's body lays.<br /> <br /> Her dreams center around her grandmother's life and the titular horsehead, a thing in the robes of a bishop with a menacing-looking horse's head. I think there's some similarities with It Follows, here, but I took the Following Thing to be a sort of manifestation of sexual guilt passed down from one's parents, but your own theory may be different and there's a lot of it open to interpretation.<br /> <br /> Throughout the experience she's also dealing with her awkward relationship with her mother and, I think, her stepfather and a sickness that hinders her attempts to discern reality from dream. An issue she may already be having enough trouble with.<br /> <br /> It's not the best movie out there. But it is interesting, which is the biggest draw for me when it comes to movies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-19-2015, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T20:57:23-07:00","id":523945,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, I never got into the whole Jurassic Park thing. Saw the first one when it came out, and enjoyed it, but haven't seen it in years, and never bothered with any of the sequels.<br /> <br /> The trailer for the new one plays at my job, and I only think two things when I see it again and again:<br /> <br /> WHY are they still building these parks?! Doesn't the *same damn thing* happen every time?? The dinos get loose, attack and eat a bunch of people. No insurance company *in the world* would cover this operation!<br /> <br /> BUT, having said that...it looks like they've finally perfected it, to the point where the park is now as well-known and popular as Sea World, and just as safe. So what do they do? &quot;These dinos are too tame and safe, let's genetically engineer *an even stronger, smarter original dino that's waaay more dangerous than anything nature ever produced! There's just no way this can possibly bite us in the ass!&quot; Well, guess what happens...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> At this point, I give up and just start rooting for the dinosaurs to win, since obviously humans are so suicidally idiotic that we may as well be wiped out by our own dino-creations, who should be smart enough not to make our dumbass mistakes...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Should have cool effects, tho!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 05-22-2015, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T21:53:05-07:00","id":523980,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you didn't miss much from the next two sequels. They weren't as good as the original.<br /> <br /> To the human's credit, however, the sequels didn't involve building any new parks (the humans in the Jurassic Park universe are not that stupid), but rather dealing with the fallout of the Park's failure; specifically, revolving around the facilities where the dinosaurs were cloned.<br /> <br /> So yes, the humans learned their lesson (mostly) and didn't try the Park idea again until they knew for a fact it was safe.<br /> <br /> As for creating the super-dinosaur... look. It's just one of those things you have to do. You may know exactly what's going to happen, but it's just too awesome an idea not to go through with. /joke","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 05-22-2015, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T22:07:11-07:00","id":523984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=523980#post523980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for creating the super-dinosaur... look. It's just one of those things you have to do. You may know exactly what's going to happen, but it's just too awesome and idea not to go through with. /joke</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://25.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_mdf8c4FWNb1qiikpjo1_500.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T07:02:17-07:00","id":524388,"title":"","content":"Between simple greed and man's curiosity is where you'll find Jurassic Park.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T20:35:17-07:00","id":525046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=524388#post524388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between simple greed and man's curiosity is where you'll find Jurassic Park.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Funnily enough, that works both in-universe and in RL (the studio's greed and the audience's curiousity)!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T10:42:28-07:00","id":525588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=519832#post519832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been a while but here's two standouts. One has just made it onto Netflix.<br /> <br /> Zombeavers. The name gives a glimpse into the depths of the movie, but the boundlessness can only be truly appreciated by watching it in its entirety.<br /> <br /> But not really. It's a B Movie. Not a 'So bad it's good,' type, but an overall okay movie on its own. It probably won't be remembered as fondly as other, more noteworthy zomcoms like Sean of the Dead, but you'll probably see a scene or two you'll keep with you long after the movie's over.<br /> <br /> Put simply, a few college girls decide to take a trip to a cabin by a lake. For bonding. One's been having trouble with her boyfriend, her best friend doesn't know what she sees in him, another pines for her boyfriend to the point that she arranged for him to come so they can hook up, and the other boyfriends tag along.<br /> <br /> Also, toxic waste is turning beavers into zombeavers. This quickly becomes a problem. Especially considering what the bite of a zombeaver does to a human.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I think Cortney Palm did really well in it, I was fully expecting her to be the trashy friend who died first but she sort of stole the show. All the writing and characterization was well done, though, considering the effort usually put into movies like these.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I watched this last night. It was about what I expected to be. Courtney Palm was great though!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T10:43:38-07:00","id":525589,"title":"","content":"Oh! There is a movie in Netflix I'm pretty excited about called 'Before I Disappear'. It was based on an Oscar winning short film called Curfew, which I loved. So, I'm pretty excited to see it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"htt