ty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T20:53:57-07:00","id":532730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=532625#post532625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://screenrant.com/agents-of-shield-carter-season-2-3-marvel-tv-feud/\" target=\"_blank\">Marvel Studios Fails Fans by fighting Marvel TV</a>...not pretty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where the hell did that guy got the idea that Agent Carter is not a good show? The feminine-empowerment angle was too forced at times, but the show was well written, well produced and very well acted. It had excellent fight choreography and well developed characters with believable motivations and dialogue. And so what if Age of Ultron had nothing to do with it? I doubt anyone felt &quot;betrayed&quot; that the movie didn't have some convoluted reason to link Ultron (or Tony's actions) to Howard.<br /> <br /> The author of this article touches on some curious behind-the-scenes conflicts, but also says a lot of badly argued bullshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T07:47:11-07:00","id":535575,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry but the author sounds like he is taking it personally that his favorite show isn't the center of attention as far as the movies go. As he mentions in an aside Agents of Shield got a second season in spite of poor ratings. Not to mention he seemed to have failed to read the whole articles or watched some of those shows that he seem to think totally proves his point. For instance how Joss Whedon admitted AoS wasn't going to work as far as the movies were concerned even before it came out &quot;but these Avengers movies are for people to see the Avengers movies and nothing else.&quot;. Then there is the fact that movies and TV has vary seriously different schedules.<br /> <br /> Between those two things let a lone it is generally a bad idea to mix and match unless the TV series is driving the movie which isn't the case here. Heck this is the first time a studio has successfully mixed and match between different movies. Maybe there is a conflict, but honestly all I see is Marvel trying to protect the next five years of movies. They had releases planned for 2020 before the shows were even announced. That can't rely on a TV show/shows that have to bend to the appeal of viewers to make sure it stays on the air. It isn't like the cartoons are mixing perfectly(as far as I've seen) either and those are Marvel Studios.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":787,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","user":"Sorwen","date":". 06-01-2015, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T16:54:51-07:00","id":549518,"title":"","content":"I just watched the first TinkerBell movie. There are a lot of things that make no damn sense. Tinker Bell is called such because she's a &quot;Tinker&quot; fairy. Her name is Bell. Yet people call her Tink for short. That's like having a friend Rick who works as a gardener and calling him Gard for short. What? <br /> <br /> More:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">And then, thanks to Tink's new inventions, they are able to prepare for spring in a night and do what took them &quot;months&quot; (as said by the queen) to do before. The fairies have been making spring happen for, what, hundreds or thousands of years? And no-fairy has come along and come up with an idea to improve their process until now? What do other Tinker fairies do?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> *sigh*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T17:23:38-07:00","id":549533,"title":"","content":"I saw the Neverbeast one, and the pirate fairy one. Not starring Tink, who was sort of a supporting protagonist, apparently the whole fairy kingdom is very against innovation, they were really peeved when the pirate fairy, whose name I forget but she wasn't a pirate until afterwards, decided to experiment and try new things.<br /> <br /> But that is the problem with a lot of media. It often promotes the status quo. New things are bad, trying to break out of your alloted space in life and get a better job that doesn't fit the lifestyle you're in? You're a sellout, and generally through the course of the movie you'll be shown how much you don't fit in through some ridiculously hamhanded method, then go back to that life you never recognized before was so great, despite all the pressure and harshness of lifestyle. In case you can't tell by my semi ranting, it really bugs me. Even sci-fi often falls for it, you can't really have a new idea without it going amok or you going crazy over it. You can't make AI and helpful robots without bigots hating them in the streets and them deciding to revolt and put you all in battery packs. It infuriates me, at times.<br /> <br /> So! In that vein, I'd like to recommend <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt2793490/?ref_=fn_al_tt_1\" target=\"_blank\">Starry Eyes</a>. It's about Sarah, a girl who's in LA to be an actress but so far can't really break out of her serving job at not-Hooters beneath a sleazy manager. She hangs out with a bunch of 'friends' and lives with a roommate who honestly cares about her. She also has a habit of, under pressure, sort of freaking out and primal screaming and pulling her hair out. After an audition, which it implies she bombs at, she lets this out in the bathroom and one of the casting people hears it, then encourages her to do it again. They are impressed and, with some further decisions to be made, it's clear she's in line to get the job.<br /> <br /> At this point I realize I'm just explaining what happens in the movie, so let me just skip that and move onto a sort of summary. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">They want to make her a star. The problem is, they're occultists. And it's clear they want to put her through all the usual stereotyped rigmarole to make sure she's truly got what it takes, when what it takes is a willingness to do <i>anything </i>to be a star. Now, in a normal movie she might go back to her friends and be happy in her job, or get a big break with another, since he's a low budget would-be producer. But her friends aren't the standard all-supportive cast. While only one seems overtly mean to her, being constantly passive aggressive and one-upping her achievements and putting her down, the others clearly don't care, and the would-be producer just wants to get her in the sack. So what you get is sort of a mirror. On one hand, the agents want to exploit her and the producer wants to use her, and the cult wants her to give in, on the other hand the friends want her to exploit her and use her and have her give in and try to be like them. There is a standout, in the roommate, who does honestly seem to care about her. And obviously the movie side has a more sinister bent, but it would lead to great success.<br /> <br /> The movie is all about that, the price of fame and fortune and the cost it can take from you and whether you want it enough that the cost is worth it.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Great flick, really turns the standard on its head, and I appreciate pretty much any attempt to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-10-2015, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T05:24:54-07:00","id":549973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I saw the Neverbeast one, and the pirate fairy one. </div> </div> </div>Amusingly enough, those are the other ones on my queue to watch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date