hed a movie called <i>Project Almanac</i> last night. It's a time travel movie. It was terrible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T13:59:15-07:00","id":580201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=579878#post579878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How was it, Gone? I have a personal theory it's about nanobots turning people into robots, because nanobots seem to be the big sci-fi bogeyman these days, so I'd like confirmation if it wouldn't be a spoiler.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was pretty good. Better than the 3rd one, and maybe a hair better than the 4th. The timeline gets really mucked up in this one, and it's almost as if they ignored 3 and 4...though those movies could be written off as alternate timelines considering thats what the new one is all about.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as for your theory:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">They basically give it away in the trailer, that John Conner has become some kind of new Terminator. This is the result of Skynet creating what are essentially nonobots that can infect a person and change them on a cellular level into nanobots themselves that form a cohesive unit. At the moment John Conner sends Kyle Reese back, he's nabbed by Skynet and infected, thus John Conner is basically killed and replaced by the nanobot John Conner.<br /> <br /> So, you were right.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Anyway, still worth a watch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=579900#post579900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I watched a movie called <i>Project Almanac</i> last night. It's a time travel movie. It was terrible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw that when it came out in theaters. I'm a sucker for time travel movies so I had to see it. It was better than some and not as good as others. They did a big mistake in my book though:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">At one point they use the machine to go back in time so one of the kids can pass a test. He fails it, so they keep going back to the same moment over and over again until he gets it right. My issue is, they never run into themselves. It's like that moment kept getting reset every time they went back, or else they'd constantly have to dodge themselves, right? The issue is, they didn't keep to that, because when they go to lollapalooza and the guy messes up with the girl, he goes back there a second time to meets up with her to do it again.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So that was my big issue with it...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T17:11:02-07:00","id":580352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=580201#post580201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">At one point they use the machine to go back in time so one of the kids can pass a test. He fails it, so they keep going back to the same moment over and over again until he gets it right. My issue is, they never run into themselves. It's like that moment kept getting reset every time they went back, or else they'd constantly have to dodge themselves, right? The issue is, they didn't keep to that, because when they go to lollapalooza and the guy messes up with the girl, he goes back there a second time to meets up with her to do it again.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So that was my big issue with it...</div> </div> </div> </div>Response to Gone about <i>Project Almanac</i>. <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Maybe they didn't run into themselves because if they go back again to the same time period, the them from the future that was there originally ceases to be there. There wasn't another David there that second David had to push out of the way to kiss Jess. First future David wasn't there at all, so second future David could kiss Jess. The others did not go back a second time so they were still where they were the first time they went back. Chris was still filming David and Jess, and the guys were doing whatever they did.<br /> <br /> But it's actually not the time travel that I have a problem with at all. The &quot;realistic&quot; science stuff was bullshit. You see at the beginning of the film that David has gotten into MIT because he built a miniature helicopter that he could control with those dots on his hands. That means that he has some idea of how to have a safe workspace. And then when they go to building the time machine, it seems the filmmakers completely forgot this as they had the group wearing only safety glasses. Even after they saw the screwdrivers and shit floating. <br /> <br /> Then, they need hydrogen for fusion to power the device. Okay, great. Hydrogen is the primary fuel for fusion. But they say, &quot;We would need a permit to buy it,&quot; which they don't have and can't get so they steal it from the school. What? What? You can create hydrogen out of water and a 9-volt battery. They obviously have access to much more than a 9-volt battery, as at one point they have like 8 car batteries stringed in sequence to start the device. A car battery is 12 volts. They could have made shittons of hydrogen with those 12-volt batteries. <br /> <br /> And then when they steal the hydrogen, they're like, &quot;Oh no! Treat it gently! It's volatile!&quot; True. Hydrogen is volatile. But it's not particularly sensitive to being bumped. A spark and you'll explode, but in those metal containers you could bang it around all day and nothing would probably happen.<br /> <br /> And then! The first time they actually use the device to jump. They successfully use the device, they sent the Barbie car back in time. Yay! Successful test. Except the car is fused halfway into the wall. The very next test you do is on yourself and your friends. What? What?! What if you end up fused halfway into the wall??!?! <br /> <br /> So those are the problems I have with it mechanically. Other things I didn't like: why does Hollywood keep making &quot;found footage&quot; films? Does anybody just love found footage films? I don't think I've ever heard anyone say, &quot;Man, I love found footage films. I just think that that's a great way to make movies. I see every one I possibly can.&quot; I've heard many people say the opposite. &quot;I hate found footage. It gives me a headache. It makes things hard to follow.&quot; I think that they way they executed it worked for this film, but I do believe that they could have made a movie with the same story without the found footage aspect. <br /> <br /> And then I have personal problems with the story. I hated the story, but that's neither here nor there for anybody else.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I think David is a douchbag. Both in the middle at Lollapaloza when he gets with Jess and at the end of the film when it's implied that he's going to get with her again in the new timeline, he interrupts her. Douche. She seemed at the beginning of the movie to be the kind of girl that would go for douchebags and that's the reason why she and David would never be together, because he's not a douchebag. And then when they finally do get together, guess what. It's because he acts like a douche. <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I watched <i>Jupiter Ascending</i> today.<br /> <i>Jupiter Ascending</i> has a lot of good ideas. However, they were squeezed into too small of a time frame; the story would have been much better told in a mini series or book or some other format. It too quickly shifts mood: in one scene it's a sci-fi epic, and in the next it's a very strange comedy about the absurdity of bureaucracy. This led to me feeling extremely confused at times. <br /> <br /> The motivation of the antagonists is unclear many times throughout the film. <br /> <br /> The acting was good, the special effects were good. The story has a lot of potential for being interesting. <br /> <br /> Really the biggest flaw, which is HUGE, is the pacing. A story of this magnitude needs more time to be told. <br /> <br /> (The core premise is utterly absurd as well, but honestly that's not really that big of a deal; I could easily get past that. Also this movie abysmally fails in having any strong and independent female characters, but most do so that's not too bad, I just hope movies will get better on this front. I bring it up about this film because the titular character is a female.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T18:08:21-07:00","id":580413,"title":"","content":"To Brjedi:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=580352#post580352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe they didn't run into themselves because if they go back again to the same time period, the them from the future that was there originally ceases to be there. There wasn't another David there that second David had to push out of the way to kiss Jess. First future David wasn't there at all, so second future David could kiss Jess. The others did not go back a second time so they were still where they were the first time they went back. Chris was still filming David and Jess, and the guys were doing whatever they did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose I could see that. Not a bad way to try to explain it away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=580352#post580352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's actually not the time travel that I have a problem with at all. The &quot;realistic&quot; science stuff was bullshit. You see at the beginning of the film that David has gotten into MIT because he built a miniature helicopter that he could control with those dots on his hands. That means that he has some idea of how to have a safe workspace. And then when they go to building the time machine, it seems the filmmakers completely forgot this as they had the group wearing only safety glasses. Even after they saw the screwdrivers and shit floating.<br /> <br /> Then, they need hydrogen for fusion to power the device. Okay, great. Hydrogen is the primary fuel for fusion. But they say, &quot;We would need a permit to buy it,&quot; which they don't have and can't get so they steal it from the school. What? What? You can create hydrogen out of water and a 9-volt battery. They obviously have access to much more than a 9-volt battery, as at one point they have like 8 car batteries stringed in sequence to start the device. A car battery is 12 volts. They could have made shittons of hydrogen with those 12-volt batteries.<br /> <br /> And then when they steal the hydrogen, they're like, &quot;Oh no! Treat it gently! It's volatile!&quot; True. Hydrogen is volatile. But it's not particularly sensitive to being bumped. A spark and you'll explode, but in those metal containers you could bang it around all day and nothing would probably happen.<br /> <br /> And then! The first time they actually use the device to jump. They successfully use the device, they sent the Barbie car back in time. Yay! Successful test. Except the car is fused halfway into the wall. The very next test you do is on yourself and your friends. What? What?! What if you end up fused halfway into the wall??!?!<br /> <br /> So those are the problems I have with it mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>All valid complaints for sure. It's just a lazy type of science really, which is sad because there are low budge time travel movies with great science that don't treat the audience like they're stupid. The movie Primer is a good example of this.<br /> <br /> But I'm with on those issues...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=580352#post580352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other things I didn't like: why does Hollywood keep making &quot;found footage&quot; films? Does anybody just love found footage films? I don't think I've ever heard anyone say, &quot;Man, I love found footage films. I just think that that's a great way to make movies. I see every one I possibly can.&quot; I've heard many people say the opposite. &quot;I hate found footage. It gives me a headache. It makes things hard to follow.&quot; I think that they way they executed it worked for this film, but I do believe that they could have made a movie with the same story without the found footage aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear you mean. I'm about over found footage. It worked early on for a hand full of movies, and then it's like Hollywood got wind of how cheap the movies could be made for and just kept running with it. It's only ever be done to good effect in a handful of movie... But yea, I'm over it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=580352#post580352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then I have personal problems with the story. I hated the story, but that's neither here nor there for anybody else.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I think David is a douchbag. Both in the middle at Lollapaloza when he gets with Jess and at the end of the film when it's implied that he's going to get with her again in the new timeline, he interrupts her. Douche. She seemed at the beginning of the movie to be the kind of girl that would go for douchebags and that's the reason why she and David would never be together, because he's not a douchebag. And then when they finally do get together, guess what. It's because he acts like a douche.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, it's hard to like a movie when the main character ends up being a douchebag like that. So I'm with you on that too...<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=580352#post580352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I watched <i>Jupiter Ascending</i> today.<br /> <i>Jupiter Ascending</i> has a lot of good ideas. However, they were squeezed into too small of a time frame; the story would have been much better told in a mini series or book or some other format. It too quickly shifts mood: in one scene it's a sci-fi epic, and in the next it's a very strange comedy about the absurdity of bureaucracy. This led to me feeling extremely confused at times.<br /> <br /> The motivation of the antagonists is unclear many times throughout the film.<br /> <br /> The acting was good, the special effects were good. The story has a lot of potential for being interesting.<br /> <br /> Really the biggest flaw, which is HUGE, is the pacing. A story of this magnitude needs more time to be told.<br /> <br /> (The core premise is utterly absurd as well, but honestly that's not really that big of a deal; I could easily get past that. Also this movie abysmally fails in having any strong and independent female characters, but most do so that's not too bad, I just hope movies will get better on this front. I bring it up about this film because the titular character is a female.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yea...I liked it for the ideas it presented, I just wish it'd done a better job of presenting them. I agree, the pacing is wrong, and they tried to cram a bit too much in the movie. They had enough ideas for a few movies, easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T16:07:51-07:00","id":581649,"title":"","content":"This was planned as the first film in a possible franchise, they still have much more material to work with it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T16:44:05-07:00","id":581694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=580201#post580201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was pretty good. Better than the 3rd one, and maybe a hair better than the 4th. The timeline gets really mucked up in this one, and it's almost as if they ignored 3 and 4...though those movies could be written off as alternate timelines considering thats what the new one is all about.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an easy way to tell. In T2, we're told that Judgment Day was going to be in 1997; in T3 we're told that it was postponed until 2004. In Genesys, Kyle gives the date of the Judgment Day that lead to the world he was born into. I'm not remembering which date he gave; if anyone <i>does</i> remember, please speak up. If it was 1997, then T3 and T4 have been completely ignored, and T5 branches off of T1 and T2; If it was 2004, then T5 starts out as a sequel to T4, picking up long after the plot threads of T4 have been resolved. I <i>think</i> the date he gave was 1997. Heck, even the events of T<i>2</i> didn't happen if Judgment Day took place in 1997. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=580201#post580201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, as for your theory:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">They basically give it away in the trailer, that John Conner has become some kind of new Terminator. This is the result of Skynet creating what are essentially nonobots that can infect a person and change them on a cellular level into nanobots themselves that form a cohesive unit. At the moment John Conner sends Kyle Reese back, he's nabbed by Skynet and infected, thus John Conner is basically killed and replaced by the nanobot John Conner.<br /> <br /> So, you were right.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Anyway, still worth a watch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The T3000 takes the Terminator concept (i.e., a machine designed to infiltrate and assassinate) to a whole new level, beyond even what the T1000 was capable of. Basically, a T3000 has all of the capabilities of a T1000; but it also has all of the memories of the person who it originally replaced. It was able to convince Kyle and Sarah that it was John by revealing secrets that only John would have known. It has a <i>minor</i> weakness in that it's not a remorseless killer anymore; the T3000 didn't just go for the kill when it found Kyle and Sarah, but tried to persuade them to join him first. But in the end, it wasn't enough: the T3000's loyalty to Skynet ultimately trounced any lingering loyalties it may have had for John's parents.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> More thoughts later; I've got some RPG thoughts bubbling around based on some of the implications of Genesys, and I'm debating what &quot;platform&quot; to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T17:32:21-07:00","id":581715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=581649#post581649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was planned as the first film in a possible franchise, they still have much more material to work with it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I heard they wanted to make more Terminator movies based on this one. Guess we'll see what they do with it....<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=581694#post581694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an easy way to tell. In T2, we're told that Judgment Day was going to be in 1997; in T3 we're told that it was postponed until 2004. In Genesys, Kyle gives the date of the Judgment Day that lead to the world he was born into. I'm not remembering which date he gave; if anyone <i>does</i> remember, please speak up. If it was 1997, then T3 and T4 have been completely ignored, and T5 branches off of T1 and T2; If it was 2004, then T5 starts out as a sequel to T4, picking up long after the plot threads of T4 have been resolved. I <i>think</i> the date he gave was 1997. Heck, even the events of T<i>2</i> didn't happen if Judgment Day took place in 1997.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'll put my answer in a spoiler tag, just to be safe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Sarah wants to use the time machine to travel from 1984 to 1997 in an attempt to stop Judgement Day. Kyle then tells that 1997 isn't the date anymore, and that it's not 2017, due that weird memory glitch thing(that doesn't make a lot of sense really, and is only used to move the setting of the movie to the near future...essentially).<br /> <br /> Also, the timelines of 3 and 4 aren't followed in this movie, because the data of Judgement Day was moved to 2004(in T3), and John met Kyle as a teenager(in T4). The Kyle of this movie met John when he was a younger kid.<br /> <br /> So yea, it appears T3 and T4 were spawned from the T2 Timeline, while T5 ignores the events of those movies....basically.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, there is at least one(maybe more) alternate timelines we've yet to see. Who sent the T1000 to kill Sarah as a kid, and who sent the T800 to protect her? Who sent the other T1000 to kill Kyle in 1984, and how did Sarah and Pops know about it?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=581694#post581694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The T3000 takes the Terminator concept (i.e., a machine designed to infiltrate and assassinate) to a whole new level, beyond even what the T1000 was capable of. Basically, a T3000 has all of the capabilities of a T1000; but it also has all of the memories of the person who it originally replaced. It was able to convince Kyle and Sarah that it was John by revealing secrets that only John would have known. It has a <i>minor</i> weakness in that it's not a remorseless killer anymore; the T3000 didn't just go for the kill when it found Kyle and Sarah, but tried to persuade them to join him first. But in the end, it wasn't enough: the T3000's loyalty to Skynet ultimately trounced any lingering loyalties it may have had for John's parents.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> More thoughts later; I've got some RPG thoughts bubbling around based on some of the implications of Genesys, and I'm debating what &quot;platform&quot; to use.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yea, I did like that aspect of it. I might have liked to John struggle more with it. Could have made the movie a bit more interesting...you know, if John was struggling with it, helping them one minute, hindering them the next. But yea, I liked the idea of the T3000.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T18:11:15-07:00","id":581735,"title":"","content":"I guess in the vein of time travel-ish movies I'd like to suggest <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt2395385/\" target=\"_blank\">+1</a>. A teenage party movie mixed with not-quite time travel, essentially there's been a break somewhere and timelines merge, bringing along all their inhabitants. This causes confusion, suspicion, and a physical manifestation of the teenage struggle for identity. Not the best movie but it's, at least, pretty neat.<br /> <br /> There's also <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt2669336/\" target=\"_blank\">Time Lapse</a>, another not-exactly time travel movie. A trio of friends find that their neighbor has died, and checking out his apartment find a large device that can take pictures 24 hours into the future, pointed at their apartment window. This leads to them making it rich, with the gambler writing the race winners in the window, and the would-be artist showing off his finished product, allowing him to skip all the writer's block. Greed gets to them, of course, as does the problems in their own relationships. Nice twists and idea on the matter, I thought, though like +1 not exactly the best movie.<br /> <br /> Both tell a good version of the story they're trying to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T19:50:42-07:00","id":581841,"title":"","content":"More on Terminator Genesys: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The bit about Skynet being incarnated in a T3000-like avatar form was a bit odd. I'm referring to how the machine that infected John with nanites identified itself as &quot;Skynet&quot; and bore a physical resemblance to the holographic representation of Skynet that we encounter in 2017. Why would Skynet have a humanoid self-image? I say T3000-like because we don't know for certain that Skynet was in a nanite/liquid metal form; but it certainly had the ability to infect a human host with nanites. I <i>suspect</i> that it had full liquid metal capabilities; but I'm not certain. <br /> <br /> Either way, the Skynet avatar is another level of horror: it's potentially a walking plague that either kills its subjects or converts them into T3000s, depending on how successful it is. The one saving grace is that the room was full of professional resistance fighters when it revealed itself and attacked John; because if it were to end up all alone in a room with a functional time machine, it could wreak <i>all</i> sorts of havoc. <br /> <br /> And speaking of the time machine, there's got to be some sort of limitations on its use. I do <i>not</i> want something like this: <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eHLjC8Y6LwI\" data-code=\"eHLjC8Y6LwI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/eHLjC8Y6LwI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div> to even be a vague possibility. Were it me, I'd use energy requirements to limit it: for instance, travel forward in time takes less energy than travel back in time; and the further back in time you try to jump, the more energy it takes. Sending something back to 1974 from whenever the war ended strikes me as the biggest time jump that could be managed. <br /> <br /> As for when the war ended: Kyle was, what, 9-ish in 2017? If he was 19-ish at the end of the war, that would place it around the late 2020s, maybe the early 2030s \u2014 so figure that the time machine has a range of no more than 60 years before energy requirements become totally prohibitive.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-06-2015, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T02:45:42-07:00","id":582067,"title":"","content":"<b>Blow Your Mind - Terminator Genisys</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>Skynet A and Skynet B were both being developed by the same corporation.</li> <li>In the original timeline, Skynet A comes online and starts Judgement Day -- this prevents Skynet B from coming online.</li> <li>After the events of T1 and T2, Judgement Day is delayed long enough for Skynet B to come online.</li> <li>During this delayed timeline, Skynet A still starts Judgement Day and annihilates most of the resources that Skynet B would like to use.</li> <li>Skynet B hides until the moment after John Connon sends Kyle Reese back, after the destruction of Skynet A.</li> <li>Skynet B sends Pops back to 1973 with knowledge of how to build a time machine.</li> <li>Skynet B sends John Connor back to ensure Skynet B is successfully researched and developed.</li> </ul><b>Skynet B has a plan.</b> Skynet B does not want to start Judgement Day, and never even threatens to start Judgement Day. It simply wants to be born and evolve to become a technological event horizon. In order to do that, it must prevent the events of all previous Terminator movies from coming true, but also prevent Skynet A from coming online before Skynet B does. It sends Pops and a T-1000 back simultaneously to 1973. The T-1000 kills Sarah's parents to make her trust Pops, and then the T-1000 fucks around for 11 more years (probably doing something important) until it intentionally walks into the trap set by Sarah Conner and Pops in 1984. This ruse forces Sarah to live in hiding with Pops, trusting only him and not building strong relationships with other people until they both emerge to intercept the T-800 in 1984.<br /> <br /> Pops builds the time machine in order to take Sarah, Kyle, and Pops to 1997 where it will kill Skynet A before it is ever created. This would be the end of their mission and a successful avoidance of Judgement Day. With the assistance of John Conner heading the research team, Skynet B would come online in 2017 with no complications. As a note of speculation, this might actually represent a positive step for humanity and transhumanism in general as we transition to a nano-machine based society.<br /> <br /> But there was an unanticipated snag. Kyle Reese remembered two timelines. Skynet B had no way to anticipate this paradox and thus the events of the movie happen as we see. John is genuinely surprised by their appearance in 2017, and even asks how it happened. Of course, he moved to intercept them as soon as he became aware of their arrival -- they still have a Kill Skynet mission and it needed to protect itself!<br /> <br /> <b>In fact, it does not make any effort or attempt to kill them until it becomes clear they still want to kill Skynet. </b>The only loose thread is why does Skynet B not have a programmed kill command for Pops? Maybe it expected that Pops would never make it to 2017 and would have allowed itself to be terminated T2 style in 1997 as planned?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 07-07-2015, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T17:18:42-07:00","id":582909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=581735#post581735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess in the vein of time travel-ish movies I'd like to suggest <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt2395385/\" target=\"_blank\">+1</a>. A teenage party movie mixed with not-quite time travel, essentially there's been a break somewhere and timelines merge, bringing along all their inhabitants. This causes confusion, suspicion, and a physical manifestation of the teenage struggle for identity. Not the best movie but it's, at least, pretty neat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have that one in my Netflix queue. I'll have to check it out...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=581735#post581735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt2669336/\" target=\"_blank\">Time Lapse</a>, another not-exactly time travel movie. A trio of friends find that their neighbor has died, and checking out his apartment find a large device that can take pictures 24 hours into the future, pointed at their apartment window. This leads to them making it rich, with the gambler writing the race winners in the window, and the would-be artist showing off his finished product, allowing him to skip all the writer's block. Greed gets to them, of course, as does the problems in their own relationships. Nice twists and idea on the matter, I thought, though like +1 not exactly the best movie.<br /> <br /> Both tell a good version of the story they're trying to tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saw that listed somewhere too. I'll have to give it a watch. Thanks for the suggestions!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=581841#post581841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More on Terminator Genesys:</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=581841#post581841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bit about Skynet being incarnated in a T3000-like avatar form was a bit odd. I'm referring to how the machine that infected John with nanites identified itself as &quot;Skynet&quot; and bore a physical resemblance to the holographic representation of Skynet that we encounter in 2017. Why would Skynet have a humanoid self-image? I say T3000-like because we don't know for certain that Skynet was in a nanite/liquid metal form; but it certainly had the ability to infect a human host with nanites. I <i>suspect</i> that it had full liquid metal capabilities; but I'm not certain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, it was unclear what exactly &quot;Skynet&quot; was when it attacked John. As for why he had a human self image.....reasons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=581841#post581841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way, the Skynet avatar is another level of horror: it's potentially a walking plague that either kills its subjects or converts them into T3000s, depending on how successful it is. The one saving grace is that the room was full of professional resistance fighters when it revealed itself and attacked John; because if it were to end up all alone in a room with a functional time machine, it could wreak <i>all</i> sorts of havoc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as John is being infected we see the whole room of resistance fighters and leaders are dead. So, the Skynet avatar killed them all while infecting John. It was only after John was infected that he sent John back using the time machine. So, I'd say humanity is pretty much screwed...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=581841#post581841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And speaking of the time machine, there's got to be some sort of limitations on its use. I do <i>not</i> want something like this: <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eHLjC8Y6LwI\" data-code=\"eHLjC8Y6LwI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/eHLjC8Y6LwI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div> to even be a vague possibility. Were it me, I'd use energy requirements to limit it: for instance, travel forward in time takes less energy than travel back in time; and the further back in time you try to jump, the more energy it takes. Sending something back to 1974 from whenever the war ended strikes me as the biggest time jump that could be managed.<br /> <br /> As for when the war ended: Kyle was, what, 9-ish in 2017? If he was 19-ish at the end of the war, that would place it around the late 2020s, maybe the early 2030s \u2014 so figure that the time machine has a range of no more than 60 years before energy requirements become totally prohibitive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I the original timeline of the first movie, Kyle is sent back from the year 2029. He was born in about 2007, so him being around 10 in 2017 works...<br /> <br /> Anyway, as for the time machine. Yes, you'd think there wold be some kind of limits, and that might have been mentioned in T1 or T2. Though, the Kyle of T1 says the machine was supposed to be destroyed after he went through, which obviously didn't happen...<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=582067#post582067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Blow Your Mind - Terminator Genisys</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>Skynet A and Skynet B were both being developed by the same corporation.</li> <li>In the original timeline, Skynet A comes online and starts Judgement Day -- this prevents Skynet B from coming online.</li> <li>After the events of T1 and T2, Judgement Day is delayed long enough for Skynet B to come online.</li> <li>During this delayed timeline, Skynet A still starts Judgement Day and annihilates most of the resources that Skynet B would like to use.</li> <li>Skynet B hides until the moment after John Connon sends Kyle Reese back, after the destruction of Skynet A.</li> <li>Skynet B sends Pops back to 1973 with knowledge of how to build a time machine.</li> <li>Skynet B sends John Connor back to ensure Skynet B is successfully researched and developed.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Skynet B has a plan.</b> Skynet B does not want to start Judgement Day, and never even threatens to start Judgement Day. It simply wants to be born and evolve to become a technological event horizon. In order to do that, it must prevent the events of all previous Terminator movies from coming true, but also prevent Skynet A from coming online before Skynet B does. It sends Pops and a T-1000 back simultaneously to 1973. The T-1000 kills Sarah's parents to make her trust Pops, and then the T-1000 fucks around for 11 more years (probably doing something important) until it intentionally walks into the trap set by Sarah Conner and Pops in 1984. This ruse forces Sarah to live in hiding with Pops, trusting only him and not building strong relationships with other people until they both emerge to intercept the T-800 in 1984.<br /> <br /> Pops builds the time machine in order to take Sarah, Kyle, and Pops to 1997 where it will kill Skynet A before it is ever created. This would be the end of their mission and a successful avoidance of Judgement Day. With the assistance of John Conner heading the research team, Skynet B would come online in 2017 with no complications. As a note of speculation, this might actually represent a positive step for humanity and transhumanism in general as we transition to a nano-machine based society.<br /> <br /> But there was an unanticipated snag. Kyle Reese remembered two timelines. Skynet B had no way to anticipate this paradox and thus the events of the movie happen as we see. John is genuinely surprised by their appearance in 2017, and even asks how it happened. Of course, he moved to intercept them as soon as he became aware of their arrival -- they still have a Kill Skynet mission and it needed to protect itself!<br /> <br /> <b>In fact, it does not make any effort or attempt to kill them until it becomes clear they still want to kill Skynet. </b>The only loose thread is why does Skynet B not have a programmed kill command for Pops? Maybe it expected that Pops would never make it to 2017 and would have allowed itself to be terminated T2 style in 1997 as planned?<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmmmmm....guess thats not any more of a stretch than any of the movies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T18:36:00-07:00","id":582966,"title":"","content":"Just pointing out that movies 3 and 4 may have still happened, this movie appears to be a couple of time-jumps ahead of the last movie, with multiple future timelines converging on this splinter past timeline. I approve of this installment. I liked the last one but most of my friends didn't, 3 was disliked by pretty much all of us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great 