ovie appears to be a couple of time-jumps ahead of the last movie, with multiple future timelines converging on this splinter past timeline. I approve of this installment. I liked the last one but most of my friends didn't, 3 was disliked by pretty much all of us.</div> </div> </div> </div>T3 was just ok, not bad, not good. T4 was pretty good and I enjoyed it.<br /> <br /> But yea, I like the idea of all these multiple futures sending things back in time and mucking things up. :P<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=583122#post583122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, especially since Word of God says...<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>The Skynet we see in this movie is not the same Skynet from the earlier Terminator movies.</li> <li>The T-1000 from 1984 is the same one that killed Sarah's Parents in 1973.<br /> </li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> I had a feeling about Skynet. Seems there have been multiple versions throughout the movies.<br /> <br /> I didn't know about the T-1000 though. I don't remember them specifically saying, so I wasn't sure if that was the same one or if Skynet sent one after Kyle too.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For al