ck Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T20:47:05-07:00","id":680626,"title":"","content":"Anyone see the recent <b>Poltergeist</b> remake? I haven't heard much good about it, but on the other hand, Sam Rockwell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T21:05:51-07:00","id":680632,"title":"","content":"Yeah, he was good in it, it wasn't that good though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T21:25:27-07:00","id":680654,"title":"","content":"Eh. Might be worth a Redbox, then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T15:32:39-07:00","id":681460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=680626#post680626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone see the recent <b>Poltergeist</b> remake? I haven't heard much good about it, but on the other hand, Sam Rockwell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen a lot of horror film remakes, but Poltergeist was the first one I would consider to be disappointing for one major reason: It forgets what type of movie it is and loses control of the all important pacing of a haunting film. Seriously half the movie is the house going from trivial things to full manifestation haunting in the space of about 2 days it seems. The second half clues you into why: The director was dying to get you to see their CGI of the ghost world.<br /> <br /> I had the chance to see Hotel Transylvania 2 this weekend and it too nosedived because of one major flaw: The main theme of the movie that they work so hard to perfectly present and support throughout the movie gets undermined at the very end in the stupidest way possible. The sad thing is that had it not done that it would have at least equaled its predecessor as Tartakovsky once again reined in Adam Sandler and managed to get some relatively great acting out of him and the rest of the cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T16:19:36-07:00","id":681509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nist498</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=681460#post681460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen a lot of horror film remakes, but Poltergeist was the first one I would consider to be disappointing for one major reason: It forgets what type of movie it is and loses control of the all important pacing of a haunting film. Seriously half the movie is the house going from trivial things to full manifestation haunting in the space of about 2 days it seems. The second half clues you into why: The director was dying to get you to see their CGI of the ghost world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like most horror films tend to forgo pacing and slather on the CGI and the like.<br /> <br /> The last one that tickled my fancy was the Babadook and I think that's mostly because it was cheap and as such, they couldn't CGI the monster away and thus had to rely on pacing.<br /> <br /> And plus that popup book in the movie is the freakest thing I've seen in a while.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T18:59:52-07:00","id":681654,"title":"","content":"I managed to get up with the others and see a trio of horror movies a couple weekends ago that were good examples of budget being inversely proportionate to quality.<br /> <br /> The first was Cooties. I've been trying to find budget numbers on it but have failed. I get the feeling the company, Lionsgate, has recognized it for what it is as it only had a limited release before its direct to video and streaming services releases. Still, there's some semi-big names in the cast. Elijah Wood, Rainn Wilson, Jack McBrayer and Nasim Pedrad, Jorge Garcia, and a number of the writers doubled as actors. Long story short, even though I know it's too late for that, a small town has poorly treated chickens, serves them to schools, and apparently has same-day shipping because it infects the entire United States school system throughout the course of the day. Kids who eat this turn into fast zombies. There must be another cause of the outbreak because barely any kids managed to get out of the school before the whole town was overtaken, somehow. There's a lot of bad jokes, including a man with a speech impediment solely for the words 'dual rear wheel,' over the top characters you can't really connect with, and some good special effects. Horrible movie, I don't recommend it to anyone.<br /> <br /> Then there was Hellions, something I've actually been looking forward to. Grainier film, which I equate to less quality, it's about a teenage girl who just found out she's pregnant with the bad boy she fools around with. In what's a common, but not bad, trope nowadays, it tries to tread the boundaries of whether it's all in her head, representative of the turmoil she's in, or whether it's actually happening. What is 'it?' Well, it's Halloween night, and her mom is out with her little brother, leaving her to man the door. Unfortunately the only trick or treaters are strange little kids in strange masks, who make it clear they have designs on her baby. Robert Patrick was in it, as a protective sheriff with a past that shares some parallels to her current situation. Decent movie, good acting all around, nice special effects, there's some poor dialogue and the script is weak in places but it's not bad like Cooties was.<br /> <br /> Finally was Last Shift. A gem and the best movie I saw that night. Officer Jessica Loren has always wanted to be a cop, like her father. And we join her on her first night on the job, unfortunately on the one year anniversary of her father's on-the-job death. She's got an easy first assignment. The old station is shutting down, they still have some 'hazardous materials' to ship out. Act as a security guard until the truck comes to pick it up. Shift ends in the morning. No problem, right? Well you've seen movies before and you can probably figure out there's more to it and probably get some clues as to what just based on what I've briefly said about it. There's good acting all around, the special effects are sparse but well handled. It all takes place in the old station, which you really get a feel for as the movie goes on and pieces start being put together. Like Hellions there was a lot of, 'is this supernatural? or just in her mind?' but unlike Dora, the star of Hellions, Jessica is a trained policewoman and not just a damsel-in-distress. I appreciate not everyone likes the minimalist kind of thing in movies, but I really dig it, and would recommend the movie. It does have its cheesy parts, but it's good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-28-2015, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T15:03:32-07:00","id":682372,"title":"","content":"Just came out of Solace, pretty decent entry for that type of movie. Imdb has it at 6.6 which I'd agree with. There were some cool parts to it with some missed opportunities. Anyone else seen it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T13:02:57-07:00","id":686088,"title":"","content":"The Hive just came out on Steam for an unreasonable $9.99. Still, it's a good movie with a nice meshing of horror and sci-fi told in a unique manner. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Basically the protagonist wakes up with amnesia in a boarded up room with warnings for him all around and a pleading note to, 'REMEMBER.' He tries to remember, and we see the flashback sequence, but it's clearly not any of his memories he's...remembering. Anyways what unfolds is a not-quite zombie outbreak, told from the perspective of the protagonist who is in touch with the hive mind that's taking over things. It was a really nice twist on storytelling, I thought, as he puts together what happened to him through pieces of other peoples memories, as well as his own. The not-zombies were pretty well done. I'm a fan of minimalism and really the most notable feature was a shifting of the eyes that seriously conveys a creepy vibe. As well as black vomit.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T14:55:22-07:00","id":686175,"title":"","content":"I saw The Martian today, and found it to be quite excellent. It had two of the things I love the most; a lone person trying to adapt and endure to survival in isolation in a harsh environment, and groups of people discussing methods to solve technical problems. Then it had the climax revolving around stuff in space, which I found quite involving, as space is terrifying. Pretty great performance from Matt Damon. I would recommend it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T10:27:40-07:00","id":688505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=686175#post686175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw The Martian today, and found it to be quite excellent. It had two of the things I love the most; a lone person trying to adapt and endure to survival in isolation in a harsh environment, and groups of people discussing methods to solve technical problems. Then it had the climax revolving around stuff in space, which I found quite involving, as space is terrifying. Pretty great performance from Matt Damon. I would recommend it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw it yesterday and loved it for all the reasons you stated. It was great!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T11:31:58-07:00","id":688553,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Martian was great. Check out metacritic - slate.com gave it 5/10 and the comments rip into the reviewer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T21:09:17-07:00","id":689255,"title":"","content":"You folks have likely come across this theory before, but it's new to me. I have chosen to believe that it's completely true, because it makes the Matrix Trilogy not only watchable after the first, but downright enjoyable for me as a trilogy.<br /> <br /> Agent Smith: The (unwitting) One and true savior of Zion, the human and digital inhabitants of the Matrix, and possibly all sentient life left on Earth.<br /> It was never Neo. He was just a piece of the puzzle. The anomaly, the One, was actually Agent Smith. <br /> Haven't heard the theory and/or thought that the Matrix Trilogy sucked? Think this is crazy?<br /> Watch this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/VkMU1mKdwPI\" data-code=\"VkMU1mKdwPI\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/VkMU1mKdwPI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Makes sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 10-05-2015, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T14:54:29-07:00","id":705743,"title":"","content":"My brother dragged me off to see Pan. It was... goddawful. So much worse than even my lowest expectations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T04:30:08-07:00","id":706629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=705743#post705743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My brother dragged me off to see Pan. It was... goddawful. So much worse than even my lowest expectations.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's about what I hear. Feel like elaborating, or is it not worth the effort? I personally stopped giving a shit the moment the term &quot;ancient prophecy&quot; appeared in the commercials, because I have never understood the need to frame the events of a narrative as predetermined, with the ending already spoiled by an author-insert prophet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T05:30:41-07:00","id":706674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's about what I hear.</div> </div> </div> </div> I just want to be clear, lest one make the legitimate conclusion of this being a case of a man in his twenties snarking over a film made for children; a lot of what I would criticise about the film are things I would think wind up making it extremely unengaging to children, and going by what I saw in that theater, it would seem to play out. My brother and I were in a packed screening (such that we wound up sitting in different parts of the room), and we both independently observed that the kids seemed widely restless and disinterested. There might be a certain popular wisdom that this is just what you'll get out of asking them to sit down to watch something in a big dark room for ninety minutes, but given how I've seen children in and out of cinemas watch films enraptured (Inside Out is a recent stand out example), I'm given to conclude that that just means you've got a bad children's film. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feel like elaborating, or is it not worth the effort?</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe later; myself and my brother have managed to have hours of conversation out of its innumerable flaws. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally stopped giving a shit the moment the term &quot;ancient prophecy&quot; appeared in the commercials</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, that's a big one. Films for children don't need to talk down to them, but I doubt any child is really being engaged by a bunch of people onerously going on about their super serious war and how they need some generic chosen one to fix it (and then adults will be put off as well by just how lazy destiny driven narratives are). That would be bad enough on its own, but it's Peter Pan; the quintessential aspect of the character, the thing that everybody knows and that all other adaptations are built around is &quot;fun loving boy who never wants to grow up&quot;, and they get none of that in there. I'm not saying there's no room for originality in adaptations, particularly in something so frequently adapted, but when you don't even get the core quality, what is the point of him being Peter Pan in the first place? That's before you get into the issues with replacing &quot;never grows up&quot; with a generic destiny, how the supposed protagonist of the story has extremely thin and vague motivation, and as Chosen Ones go he basically accomplishes <i>nothing</i>. I mean, I was galled enough when people were putting all of their hopes and investment on this child who had yet to actually do anything, but for it to not even have a payoff? For them to not even bother to give him his unearned triumph (while still having him actually win)? That's.. that's just bad screenwriting, people. Just... it seriously fails on every level, every single scene has something wrong with it in at least one of visuals, narrative composition, characterisation, dialogue, acting and action (and often several at once), which are bad enough in any case, but have to lather it up with frequent bizarre, unearned choices for disconnected references to popularly recognised Peter Pan details (one of the more egregious is this actual exchange of dialogue at a point after the kid escapes from a cell and disappears into a jungle: &quot;so you're saying the boy is lost?&quot; &quot;Yes sir, he is a lost boy&quot;). Just... for those of you who have kids, don't see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T10:04:40-07:00","id":707050,"title":"","content":"My biggest issue with Pan was that the stupid movie came across as one spectacle scene after another barely held together with a paper thin plot that made no sense whatsoever. Seriously, you could tell that they were trying to quickly move you from one special effects shot after the next. That motivation was so overriding that they did practically none of the characters justice. Peter isn't Peter Pan, not even a shadow of such. Hook is a wasted character with very little to suggest what he would eventually become. Tiger Lily is your stereotypical empowered action woman that appears all throughout cinema these days. Blackbeard acts like an idiot and yet the writers expect us to see him as a credible threat. Seriously I think this movie wasn't supposed to be about Peter Pan and the studio just slapped the name on for recognition because they knew they had a turd on their hands. In short:<br /> <br /> The characters were stupid<br /> The plot was stupid<br /> The pirates singing &quot;Smells like Teen Spirit&quot; in world war II no less was stupid<br /> The effects were the only thing salvageable and even then many of them were just wonky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T10:36:28-07:00","id":707085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nist498</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hook is a wasted character with very little to suggest what he would eventually become.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not just what he might become (although seriously, there is no way that this character can in any way become a Captain Hook familiar to us, unless there was a plot about him becoming possessed by Blackbeard's ghost), but where he even came from. That was another one of the film's structural problems; it wants to create this elaborate background to the effect of Blackbeard having created some kind of society by having some kind of network of kidnappers and human traffickers for hundreds of years, and all it does is just create weird questions about where any of these people (of whom there have to be <i>thousands</i>, maybe tens of thousands) come from and how that affects them. I mean, is Hook supposed to have been brought there as an orphaned child as well? Or Smee? Are you gonna give any of these people personalities that might be conductive with the idea that they've been working in mines their whole lives? I'm not saying these should be things the movie tells me, just that it should either not be a precept in the first place or else at least not vaguely dance around the issue. Also, you know... why are there no women in their society? Hundreds of years and Blackbeard kidnaps (presumably) one woman, ever? You'd think that at some point he'd think his ridiculous steampunk society could be sustained more easily by having people reproduce, especially around the time his flying pirate ships are doing slave runs through aerial warzones. (seriously, how did three Spitfires not bring that stupid ship down? I wouldn't really walk out of a movie, but if I would that scene would have been the time to do it) <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nist498</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tiger Lily is your stereotypical empowered action woman that appears all throughout cinema these days.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, my brother illustrated a good point on this subject as a thing in general by comparing such characters to Princess Leia, somebody who is an active part in several action scenes without them drawing a direct line around her labeled &quot;action woman&quot;. She's not your super ultimate badass, she's just a person able to take part in violence when violence is necessary, and it gives every time she takes part in a shootout or strangles somebody with a chain more meaning than all the fighting fucktoys in the world. I saw Gremlins for the first time yesterday as well, and one of the most striking things I found about it was how Billy's mother acted in her one big sequence; certainly scared, but she picks up a knife and goes around killing the things to the extent that she's able, because what else are you going to do? It doesn't even matter that she's not entirely successful, what matters is that she is <i>active</i> in a scene, she is thinking and responding. That's the meaning of agency, and it was striking to me because you don't often see that kind of character being given such action. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nist498</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blackbeard acts like an idiot</div> </div> </div> </div> You know during that scene after Peter flies for the first (out of two) times where Blackbeard brings him to his room to talk about mortality and all kinds of shit that really keeps the kids' attention, I thought the film was almost working up to something clever with the idea of somebody trying to subvert a prophecy by winning their destined killer over to their own side (I later recognised that I may have thought this partially because he seems to share several traits with the classic Pan, what with the society of technically kidnapped children and his own variation on the whole living forever thing), but nope. He just elucidates on how he thinks Peter has been prophecized to kill him (and I mean... why? It's not as if he's particularly difficult to kill, or a child being able to fly would give him all that much advantage), and then... sends him back to his cell. It's not as if Blackbeard is supposed to have any compunction with killing children, as we literally saw him do that in the previous scene. It has to be among the most egregious instances of a movie contriving to keep its protagonist alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T14:57:12-07:00","id":707425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=686175#post686175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw The Martian today, and found it to be quite excellent. It had two of the things I love the most; a lone person trying to adapt and endure to survival in isolation in a harsh environment, and groups of people discussing methods to solve technical problems. Then it had the climax revolving around stuff in space, which I found quite involving, as space is terrifying. Pretty great performance from Matt Damon. I would recommend it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Did you see Gravity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T16:16:58-07:00","id":707704,"title":"","content":"What part of &quot;space is terrifying&quot; was unclear?!?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Sure, I'm going to see &quot;A Tiny Nudge Will Send You Carreening into Infinite Nothing until you Suffocate: The Movie&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T17:12:30-07:00","id":707732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=707704#post707704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What part of &quot;space is terrifying&quot; was unclear?!?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Sure, I'm going to see &quot;A Tiny Nudge Will Send You Carreening into Infinite Nothing until you Suffocate: The Movie&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The part where you said The Martian was &quot;quite involving&quot; exactly because of that! Not to mention that everything you described it as fits Gravity equally well (except there's no team of people, that we get to see, anyway). Now I'm scared to ask if you liked Interstellar, which also had those two things... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Appros of nothing, Discovery Family showed the Back to the Future trilogy, which I recorded and am watching now. The 2015 part of Part II takes place just a few days from now, Oct. 21! Good time to rewatch the series, if you're able...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T03:27:23-07:00","id":708474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=707732#post707732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part where you said The Martian was &quot;quite involving&quot; exactly because of that!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, at the end, as a small instance and an action climax.<br /> <br /> I'm okay with a generally terrifying thing when it's there at the end to be a source of final tension, not when you're making a feature length out of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm scared to ask if you liked Interstellar, which also had those two things</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything I hear about Interstellar makes it sound... well, not a nice word. I'm familiar enough with Christopher Nolan to think that he's vastly unsuited to imitating Stephen Spielberg. Actually placing them in space is largely irrelevant to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T04:27:35-07:00","id":708507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=707732#post707732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Appros of nothing, Discovery Family showed the Back to the Future trilogy, which I recorded and am watching now. The 2015 part of Part II takes place just a few days from now, Oct. 21! Good time to rewatch the series, if you're able...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to the Back to the Future triple feature on the 21st! Cannot wait!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T11:33:21-07:00","id":709070,"title":"","content":"So I saw the Green Inferno. I felt like I had to, as I enjoyed much of Eli Roth's work, even though I don't like Italian cinema, or the films the movie is based on. I wouldn't recommend it to just random people on the streets, it wasn't great. But anyone curious about it and interested in those movies would probably like it. Roth's movies have a tendency to delve into the face of evil among us when their characters are faced with evil or danger, and this movie doesn't disappoint in that regard. Some of the acting faltered at points, a fault, I think, of an unbalance in the writing. Some of the characters were written very realistically, others were written with more of a dramatic flare one would expect in this kind of movie and it does stand out. Still, I thought some of the main offenders, notably Sky Ferreira and Daryl Sabara, ended up really killing it, even though Sky had a relatively minor role.<br /> <br /> It was nagging me throughout the movie but I recognized Lars, the character played by Sabara. Afterward I checked and found where I recognized him from. He was in Teen Lust, a sort of coming-of-age story about the protagonists race to lose their virginity, with a twist. The families of the protagonist Neil and his friend, played by Sabara, are members of a Satanic Church. And Neil has been specially groomed by this church to be sacrificed, as a virgin, to empower the forces of Darkness and, when realizing this teenage baptism is going to end in death, make a last moment escape and spend the rest of the night doing what they can to ensure that Neil survives. Since the church is spread throughout the power structure of the town and calling for help is not an option, they decide to lose Neil's virginity. It's a silly premise, and the movie's entire concept is about ten years too late, but overall it is a slightly fun movie and where the writing fails the acting picks up the slack. As a bonus, Cary Elwes plays the hunchbacked High Priest of the Satanic Church.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T14:13:35-08:00","id":763447,"title":"","content":"Just watched 'Afflicted'. Its only got 2 starts on netflix but if you like vampire movies its awesome !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user