le":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T14:51:38-08:00","id":764411,"title":"","content":"I just watched Tucker and Dale Vs Evil a couple of days ago (yeah, I know, I'm super-late to the party). I think I haven't laughed so hard with a movie in years, and it was good because I certainly needed it.<br /> <br /> Any good Werewolf movies? I've seen a bumch of them recently: Wolf, The Wolfman, Ginger Snaps I, II and III, Wolves, Wer (loved this one to pieces, saw it twice in a row), Never Cry Werewolf, and some others, but still didn't scratch the itch. Recomendations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T16:06:17-08:00","id":764472,"title":"","content":"Tucker and Dale vs Evil was great.<br /> <br /> There's actually been a slight surge in werewolf movies but I haven't found any I really liked.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt2393827/?ref_=fn_al_tt_1\" target=\"_blank\">Howl</a> was okay. It had good moments and bad but I wouldn't say it was a great movie, a lot of it was sort of plodding and predictable. The werewolves themselves were pretty cool, they used a lot of practical effects which is always nice. I really want to see <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt2818178/\" target=\"_blank\">When Animals Dream</a>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt2027154/\" target=\"_blank\">Love Bite</a> was cute. The Howling Reborn was pretty lame. A Game of Werewolves was pretty good. There was a Korean movie called the Howling but I got bored and didn't finish so I don't know if there's actually a werewolf in it, the depiction of the woman in the workplace really turned me off, too, it was pretty bad in that regard. I'm not the most PC individual but she was a cop assigned to this department and pretty much everyone just openly treated her like shit for no reason other than her being a woman in the same job as them. Otherwise I have a few on my list. Werewolf: A Beast Among Us, Night Wolf, and Dark Moon Rising. A sequel to Dog Soldiers is on the horizon, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-12-2015, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T16:10:17-08:00","id":764475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=763952#post763952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I didn't like it it's not really fair of me to say that. It was definitely me, I couldn't stand the protagonist and was sick of it five minutes in but other people really liked it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, well, maybe I'll check it out sometime..we'll see. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=764411#post764411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just watched Tucker and Dale Vs Evil a couple of days ago (yeah, I know, I'm super-late to the party). I think I haven't laughed so hard with a movie in years, and it was good because I certainly needed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you liked it! I stood in the rain for 2 hours to see it premiere at SXSW in 2010. Totally worth it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=764411#post764411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any good Werewolf movies? I've seen a bumch of them recently: Wolf, The Wolfman, Ginger Snaps I, II and III, Wolves, Wer (loved this one to pieces, saw it twice in a row), Never Cry Werewolf, and some others, but still didn't scratch the itch. Recomendations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out Wolf Cop(for some camp) and one called Late Phases. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr clas