56-08:00","id":768732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfAsh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=767858#post767858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dog soldiers is great</div> </div> </div> </div>It is indeed!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T15:33:50-08:00","id":768752,"title":"","content":"Saw it again yesterday as per your recomendation, LordOfAsh. It was older that I remebered, but it is great indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T08:13:57-08:00","id":770739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=765595#post765595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, I'd heard the new James Bond movie had some issues....</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm...I've come to think that review is overly harsh. Yes, the Big Reveal could have been handled better, and he's spot-on about JB being the only action hero who *doesn't* need personal reasons to do his damn job! But it's not like the series hasn't gone there before, most notably in License to Kill. In fact, I think this movie rips off the beats of LtK more than it does any Marvel movie. <br /> <br /> The overall plot was suspiciously closer to this years' Mission Impossible: Rogue Nation than anything else (although the influence, if any,could have gone either way), and the whole &quot;secret conspiracy to infiltrate our govt/intel services&quot; plot is surely as old as spy fiction itself. <br /> <br /> (On a similar note, Maybe I need to watch Skyfall again, but why do people keep saying it's the same movie as The Dark Knight? Aside fromthe ONE plot point of the villains arranging their own capture so they can attack the heroes' HQ from within (which also pops up in The Avengers!), I don't see any similiarity.)<br /> <br /> And there are only so many ways to keep action fresh, from the general formulas of Hero chases Baddies, Hero escapes Baddies, Hero fights Baddies in/on moving plane/train/boat/etc, it's frankly amazing we haven't run out of ways to make any of this exciting!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I didn't...and apparently no else did either. Well, a few people did and they totally hated it, so it was pulled out of theaters after like 2 weeks...<br /> <br /> I heard very bad things about it. </div> </div> </div>There were basically two ways they could have gone with Jem: Either embrace the 80s vibe, full-on, or make it a Very Modern thing to appeal more to young people. They went the latter road, which probably makes sense from a business POV, but alienates most of the real fans whose nostalgia could have saved the flick. Who knows, maybe it could even have started an 80s revival! Ah well...at least we have Moonbeam City!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T09:08:54-08:00","id":770772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=770739#post770739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mm...I've come to think that review is overly harsh. Yes, the Big Reveal could have been handled better, and he's spot-on about JB being the only action hero who *doesn't* need personal reasons to do his damn job! But it's not like the series hasn't gone there before, most notably in License to Kill. In fact, I think this movie rips off the beats of LtK more than it does any Marvel movie.<br /> <br /> The overall plot was suspiciously closer to this years' Mission Impossible: Rogue Nation than anything else (although the influence, if any,could have gone either way), and the whole &quot;secret conspiracy to infiltrate our govt/intel services&quot; plot is surely as old as spy fiction itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having not seen the movie, the only I can say is:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I wish they wouldn't have made Blofeld and Bond related(well, sort of related). I just don't think they really needed to do that...</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=770739#post770739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(On a similar note, Maybe I need to watch Skyfall again, but why do people keep saying it's the same movie as The Dark Knight? Aside fromthe ONE plot point of the villains arranging their own capture so they can attack the heroes' HQ from within (which also pops up in The Avengers!), I don't see any similiarity.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, no idea either...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=770739#post770739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were basically two ways they could have gone with Jem: Either embrace the 80s vibe, full-on, or make it a Very Modern thing to appeal more to young people. They went the latter road, which probably makes sense from a business POV, but alienates most of the real fans whose nostalgia could have saved the flick. Who knows, maybe it could even have started an 80s revival! Ah well...at least we have Moonbeam City!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Again, having not seen the movie I heard that while they tried to make it modern, they didn't do a very good job of it. So, while trying to modernize it I guess they completely missed the point of it?<br /> <br /> I dunno...I never really watched the animated series or anything so I can't comment much on it. I just know alot of people really love the original..<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T05:33:47-08:00","id":772997,"title":"","content":"When I first heard about this movie, I thought it was a joke of some sort.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt3672840/\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Blade</a>. Starring Jackie Chan, John Cusack, and Adrien Brody.<br /> <br /> It's not a comedy, Chan does a lot more dramatic roles in China, especially historical stuff, so his presence isn't odd. And I realize Cusack is trying to rebrand himself as an action hero for some reason, but it's still hard to imagine him as anything other than 80s dorkus or 90s-2000s depressed man. And Adrien Brody, who bounces between award-winning roles and horrible stuff like inAPPropriate Comedy. He's been in the occasional action movie too but seems to do better with thrillers and drama.<br /> <br /> Has anyone seen it? It's won some awards in China but seems like a horrible concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T08:57:21-08:00","id":780574,"title":"","content":"I saw <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt3526286/\" target=\"_blank\">#Horror</a> and it was a seriously great movie. It manages to twist a lot of preconceptions and does a fantastic job building up tension while also giving you fragile protagonists to get into. The description of it said it was about a bunch of girls having a sleepover and getting into trouble via social media, implying that they did something online that brought about some sort of maniac seeking vengeance. I think the description's been changed now but the girls were a lot younger than I was expecting. I thought it would be the usual 'in their late teens played by 30 year olds' but they were all around the age of 12 and played by actors near there. Maybe it's not PC to say but the youth really made it easier to worry about them, as they aren't really grown-up enough to handle the kind of dangers I was expecting. And the tension keeps ramping up, with there being a sort of division among the girls as they sort of turn on each other, with the other girls quickly following the majority. The meanness gets pretty bad, but there's usually someone trying to turn things around to a more neutral stance. Then there's rumors of previous murders in the house, rumors of a haunting, the house itself is scary as it's decorated by an art collector with bizarre tastes, the kids find a gun, the mother leaves them to ostensibly get pizza but really to just let them have some time to themselves while she hangs out with her friends. It was surprisingly good acting, from young kids, and I thought a lot of the meanness was a pretty good example of what you'd see going on. Timothy Hutton appears as one of the girls' fathers, barging in to chew out the girls and the scenery while they're alone for their being mean to his daughter and leaving them paralyzed in fear at the only authority figure around.<br /> <br /> All that said there's one thing that keeps it from being a perfect horror flick, and that's the ending. There's a message sown throughout the movie. It's not entirely subtle but it's not hammering you over the head with it, it's background noise and understandable. A few minutes before the end, however, all pretenses are dropped and they ham-handedly shove the message in your face. It really detracted from what was otherwise a great movie.<br /> <br /> I also saw <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt3079380/\" target=\"_blank\">Spy</a>, with Melissa McCarthy, who I've only seen before in her appearances on SNL. This movie was also sort of misrepresented, and I think it did a disservice. The, admittedly few, ads that I saw for it seemed to suggest that the protagonist Susan, played by McCarthy, was going to be a sort of bumbling idiot who stumbles their way through an espionage mission similar to Maxwell Smart or how Mr. Bean might do it. 'Ha ha, look at the fat lady trying to be a spy.' But she's not that way at all in the movie. She's certainly placed her life on hold to assist another man, and she doesn't have in the field <i>experience</i>, but she's a CIA analyst and very good at her job, and she's also prepared for field work. It's something she's long wanted to do before being won over by agent Bradley Fine, who appreciated her skills and sniped her before she could become a field agent, tasking her eternally to be his back-up.<br /> <br /> So, she's not an idiot. The same cannot be said for most of the other characters, and it's hilarious. Jason Statham stands out as a British expat working for the CIA and being a complete jackass as he vows revenge for his fallen comrade. He's done some subtle comedy before under Guy Ritchie, and the Crank movies are more over-the-top than strictly comedy, but he really kills his role here. Everyone else is very good too, basically playing overblown stereotypes of the kinds of characters you might see in an action-espionage flick. There's some minor issues with the special effects that were weird enough to stand out, some of the fight scenes were a bit overthought, the the script seems to think Melissa is Sam Jackson for a bit, and an unnecessary cameo by 50 Cent, but it's truly a funny movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-05-2015, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T07:28:17-08:00","id":781694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=780574#post780574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also saw <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt3079380/\" target=\"_blank\">Spy</a>, with Melissa McCarthy, who I've only seen before in her appearances on SNL.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love all her movies. If you like buddy cop movies, definitely check out <i>The Heat</i>, whose sequel appears to have sadly been put on indefinite hiatus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T15:37:36-08:00","id":783715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=781694#post781694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love all her movies. If you like buddy cop movies, definitely check out <i>The Heat</i>, whose sequel appears to have sadly been put on indefinite hiatus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw it, I liked it. Definitely a good buddy cop flick, I think Spy really succeeded better on the comedy route. Not that the Heat wasn't funny it just wasn't 'always on' the way Spy was. Bummed to hear about the sequel, it would have been nice to have more buddy cop series going on. The Other Guys was great, and Ride Along was okay. Still a strong genre, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Also saw Scouts Guide to the Zombie Apocalypse. I've actually been waiting for it for months because it seemed like a pretty novel idea. Unfortunately aside from pairing two genres they decided to throw novelty to the curb. It's basically got your teenage coming-of-age story, with one teenage scout torn between his two best friends, one of whom has sort of nagged him into leaving the scouts behind so they can get girls their junior year, while the other friend is wholly into the scouts and has no idea his friends are going to abandon him. The 'main' scout also has a crush on the first friends sister that he hasn't gotten the nerve to do anything about. Maybe some stressful scenario that forces him to take charge will change things? The genre is your standard zombie outbreak. Apocalypse is really too strong a word. The zombies were alright, the make-up was great but it didn't keep much consistency between them, so some zombies are smart, some are mindless, some run, some shamble. The acting wasn't bad, the characters could have enunciated better. I can't imagine anyone thinking this is their favorite movie but it's got some laughs and isn't really bad, just unoriginal.<br /> <br /> It does have one of the most memorable strip club scenes I can recall. Second most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  After writing this I remembered the Adventures of Priscilla, Queen of the Desert. 12-10-2015, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T23:38:16-08:00","id":786539,"title":"","content":"Just saw the Spielberg movie JAWS all the way through for the first time.<br /> <br /> <i>Holy cow</i>, people. If you're wondering how Spielberg became a household name, <i>watch this movie</i>. <i>Good Lord.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T21:43:31-08:00","id":788528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=780574#post780574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also saw <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt3079380/\" target=\"_blank\">Spy</a>, with Melissa McCarthy, who I've only seen before in her appearances on SNL. This movie was also sort of misrepresented, and I think it did a disservice. The, admittedly few, ads that I saw for it seemed to suggest that the protagonist Susan, played by McCarthy, was going to be a sort of bumbling idiot who stumbles their way through an espionage mission similar to Maxwell Smart or how Mr. Bean might do it. 'Ha ha, look at the fat lady trying to be a spy.' But she's not that way at all in the movie. She's certainly placed her life on hold to assist another man, and she doesn't have in the field <i>experience</i>, but she's a CIA analyst and very good at her job, and she's also prepared for field work. It's something she's long wanted to do before being won over by agent Bradley Fine, who appreciated her skills and sniped her before she could become a field agent, tasking her eternally to be his back-up.<br /> <br /> So, she's not an idiot.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds pretty much exactly like a gender-flipped version of Steve Carell's Get Smart movie! Not claiming her's is ripped off or anything, just saying that, having loved that one, I might like this one, too...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=786539#post786539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just saw the Spielberg movie JAWS all the way through for the first time.<br /> <br /> <i>Holy cow</i>, people. If you're wondering how Spielberg became a household name, <i>watch this movie</i>. <i>Good Lord.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Just wait till you get to the 3D one!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah, Jaws was pretty much THE original Summer Blockbuster, barely predating Star Wars, which solidified the concept (summer used to be a dumping ground for movies the studios didn't expect much from, with winter/Christmas being reserved for the big hits). The impact of both of those films on pop culture, and how they helped to shape the cinematic landscape of the 80s, cannot be underestimated!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T12:34:47-08:00","id":788918,"title":"","content":"I wish there was a movie coming out this weekend that I thought a lot of people would see so I could see it too and have fun conversations about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T12:39:58-08:00","id":788920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=788918#post788918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish there was a movie coming out this weekend that I thought a lot of people would see so I could see it too and have fun conversations about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this december brings the ONE movie I've been waiting for since my childhood--that's right, Alvin and the Chipmunks 4: The Road Chip!! If this movie season is remembered for *anything*, it'll be that, and I'm sure all internet forums will explode with de