 href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=794152#post794152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, but it was about some hateful people. Thus the title.<br /> <br /> Despite the unsavory views of some of the characters, they were fleshed out enough to appreciate them as more than simple stereotypes. As it took place after a notable and vicious war and more than a few characters were veterans of said war, their animosity towards each other was understandable.<br /> <br /> I suppose if you're just sitting through a movie to get to the violent parts it would be hard to appreciate the rest of the movie, though I think even the type of person who would do that would appreciate the violent parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw this past weekend and really liked it! Of course, all the character are terrible people, but they were certainly interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=812363#post812363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stepdad got a bunch of SAG screeners, going to watch The Big Short, Beasts of No Nation and Straight Out of Compton sometime this week. I really hope he gets a copy of The Force Awakens at some point, but I doubt that'll be on the mailing list.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh cool! I hope you like Straight Outta Compton. I saw it when it came out and really liked it a lot!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">M