teful Eight. The Encounter, which seriously needed some nudity but I wouldn't recommend.<br /> <br /> And Freaks of Nature, which wasn't really good but might be worth watching if you like horror-comedies revolving around some shallow teenage coming-of-age drama. Surprisingly good take on the attitudes of the vampires, except for one thing near the end that seemed forced. Somehow Petra, the 'main' girl who wanted to lose her virginity to darkly handsome vampire Milan Pinache was the most sympathetic character, I found. The whole thing would really have benefited from being a miniseries or something, giving time to flesh things out and not feel so rushed, plus maybe the writers could have learned how to spell Panache.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-30-2016, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T20:19:10-08:00","id":828574,"title":"","content":"Deadpool was perfect. Everything I ever wanted in a Deadpool movie, including stuff I never knew I wanted. I credit Ryan Reynolds for the most part--but hot damn was that film amazing. Definitely going to see it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/