FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T04:31:16-08:00","id":831650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=829877#post829877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember when a $58 million budget wasn't considered all that skimpy.<br /> <br /> \u200bYou know what made me really happy in this movie? The Blackbird, not that stupid fucking X-Jet from the earlier X-Men movies. Better cameo than even Stan Lee's (which was pretty fucking awesome too). Getting to see Colossus for a large part of the movie was great too, especially when Deadpool tries to kick his ass. That was all made of win.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally with you!! Seeing the actual blackbird was so awesome! And Colossus looked great!!<br /> <br /> And yea, I loved the movie! Can't wait to see it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T12:04:03-08:00","id":832643,"title":"","content":"Watching the Matrix hd for the first time in a while.<br /> <br /> Has anybody else encountered problems with the audio? Special effects really loud, dialogue too quiet?<br /> <br /> I've tried watching it on Blu-ray and digital download - problem seems to persist. Is it that the audio is unbalanced? Maybe I need a home theater? Losing my hearing?<br /> <br /> Or do all the characters just talk too softly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T07:34:30-08:00","id":833247,"title":"","content":"I could talk for days about how important a character Superman is to me, and I may yet make such a post, but I want to talk for a second about Batman. <br /> <br /> The creator perhaps most directly responsible for the vision of Batman we will see in the upcoming movie is Frank Miller, a writer and artist heavily influenced by the noir genre. He always struck me as a writer with more style than substance, but his style was entertaining, and since I read to be entertained, that was fine.<br /> <br /> But something changed inside Mr. Miller on 9/11. PTSD has made of him nearly a self-parody whose characters are an author-insert (for they are all the same character) who is an ultra-violent, racist, xenophobic fascist proposing brutal Final Solutions to make the world safe from scary foreigners. A lot of people find his post-9/11 work offensive, and I suppose I do too, but mostly I pity him. He is a wounded man who needs healing. <br /> <br /> I go into a poor fellow's psychiatric history because it occurred to me today that I can say nearly all of that about Batfleck, too: At least judging by the promotional material, Batman seems to be a dark-minded man who was changed by the movie's equivalent of 9/11 into an ultra-violent, racist, xenophobic fascist who want to enact a brutal Final Solution against an alien to keep the world safe from scary foreigners to the point that he becomes self-parodic. <br /> <br /> I tend to suspect this parallel is unintentional just because I do not credit the movie's creators with the savviness to make such allusions, but even so, it seems savagely tone deaf to me to make such a character choice; to make Batman an expy of one of his most famous creators who is now perhaps most famous for being sick. It feels like a bad satire. <br /> <br /> That is not to say there is no room to tell stories about people traumatized by a city being destroyed and thousands of people dying in the tragedy, but...I dunno, man. In this case it just seems super uncool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T09:24:50-08:00","id":833335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=833247#post833247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could talk for days about how important a character Superman is to me, and I may yet make such a post, but I want to talk for a second about Batman.<br /> <br /> The creator perhaps most directly responsible for the vision of Batman we will see in the upcoming movie is Frank Miller, a writer and artist heavily influenced by the noir genre. He always struck me as a writer with more style than substance, but his style was entertaining, and since I read to be entertained, that was fine.<br /> <br /> But something changed inside Mr. Miller on 9/11. PTSD has made of him nearly a self-parody whose characters are an author-insert (for they are all the same character) who is an ultra-violent, racist, xenophobic fascist proposing brutal Final Solutions to make the world safe from scary foreigners. A lot of people find his post-9/11 work offensive, and I suppose I do too, but mostly I pity him. He is a wounded man who needs healing.<br /> <br /> I go into a poor fellow's psychiatric history because it occurred to me today that I can say nearly all of that about Batfleck, too: At least judging by the promotional material, Batman seems to be a dark-minded man who was changed by the movie's equivalent of 9/11 into an ultra-violent, racist, xenophobic fascist who want to enact a brutal Final Solution against an alien to keep the world safe from scary foreigners to the point that he becomes self-parodic.<br /> <br /> I tend to suspect this parallel is unintentional just because I do not credit the movie's creators with the savviness to make such allusions, but even so, it seems savagely tone deaf to me to make such a character choice; to make Batman an expy of one of his most famous creators who is now perhaps most famous for being sick. It feels like a bad satire.<br /> <br /> That is not to say there is no room to tell stories about people traumatized by a city being destroyed and thousands of people dying in the tragedy, but...I dunno, man. In this case it just seems super uncool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, Frank Miller. We joke about him, but seriously, that guy needs some professional help.<br /> <br /> I will give them credit for giving the audience a <i>different</i> version of Batman this time around, instead of just the same Batman over and over. That shows they're actually putting some effort into this project. Too bad it's the &quot;unfortunate implications&quot; version, like you said.<br /> <br /> Hm... I once speculated that it would be interesting to see Batman portrayed as a villain for once, and Miller-Batman seems like the logical choice. Don't know how I feel about that now after you brought it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 02-19-2016, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T11:22:44-08:00","id":833400,"title":"","content":"It does not make me appear particulary bright, but the moment I realized how clearly damaged and bitter Miller is was after reading the tirade he made after the announcement that the second season of Daredevil will feature Elektra.<br /> <br /> Not cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T11:29:33-08:00","id":833406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=833400#post833400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does not make me appear particulary bright, but the moment I realized how clearly damaged and bitter Miller is was after reading the tirade he made after the announcement that the second season of Daredevil will feature Elektra.<br /> <br /> Not cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not aware of that tirade, and suspect I am happier for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T11:44:32-08:00","id":833418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=833247#post833247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I go into a poor fellow's psychiatric history because it occurred to me today that I can say nearly all of that about Batfleck, too: At least judging by the promotional material, Batman seems to be a dark-minded man who was changed by the movie's equivalent of 9/11 into an ultra-violent, racist, xenophobic fascist who want to enact a brutal Final Solution against an alien to keep the world safe from scary foreigners to the point that he becomes self-parodic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see where you got ultra-violent from, but how do you get racist, xenophobic or fascist?<br /> <br /> After the Man of Steel movie came out, and pretty much since then, people have been constantly complaining about how he destroyed an entire city and got a lot of people killed and how 'that's not the Superman I know.'<br /> <br /> Batman's wanting to stop Superman isn't because he's of another race, it's because he has the potential to kill or dominate all of humanity without anyone being able to stop him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-19-2016, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T12:00:15-08:00","id":833430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=833418#post833418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see where you got ultra-violent from, but how do you get racist, xenophobic or fascist?</div> </div> </div> </div>You asking about Miller, Batfleck, or both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T12:05:31-08:00","id":833434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=833430#post833430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You asking about Miller, Batfleck, or both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=833247#post833247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Batman seems to be a dark-minded man who was changed by the movie's equivalent of 9/11 into an ultra-violent, racist, xenophobic fascist who want to enact a brutal Final Solution against an alien to keep the world safe from scary foreigners to the point that he becomes self-parodic.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Though I have to admit if you have any evidence of Frank Miller acting ultraviolent, that would be very interesting to see, considering his fragile state. I'm aware of his work and political beliefs but not of any him inflicting any violence on anyone.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T13:07:25-08:00","id":833463,"title":"","content":"(Too much effort to quote on a phone.)<br /> <br /> First, nofather, you are quite right about Frank Miller never having been physically violent to anyone I know of. I apologize for sloppy wording. I think, based on his invective against Middle Easterners, he <i>would</i> be violent if he could be, but I base the accusations of racism and xenophobia on his statements about Muslims, and the accusations of fascism on his proposed solutions to the &quot;problem&quot; of Muslims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T18:20:52-08:00","id":833626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=833406#post833406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am not aware of that tirade, and suspect I am happier for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you haven't missed anything and it's pretty tame compared to other stuff he said, but for me it was the so-called moment of clarity where I finally saw how much that man has fallen from grace","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-wo