","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T10:49:21-07:00","id":855131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=854048#post854048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyone notice a rise in religious movies of late? My local theater (MJR) is showing two of them, and we're getting more of them in the video section at work (the latest is apparently about a father who's upset that his daughter is learning about *gasp* Evolution at college, and is <i>determined to do something about it!</i>)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, given the tumultuous times, there's an increased call for that sort of thing. It's unfortunate that movies tend to go the route of portraying the other side as the worst possible representation of that side.<br /> <br /> I just saw the Hallow. It's a good horror movie, but really it's a much better horror movie if you're a parent. There's a child involved and it really brings home the fear and dread. It's still neat, though. I actually came back thinking <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">it would be an interesting take on Changeling, as they were arguably the primary antagonist of the film.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-29-2016, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T14:10:56-07:00","id":856710,"title":"","content":"So...are we going to talk about Batman v Superman? Or are there just no words...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T15:50:46-07:00","id":856751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=856710#post856710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...are we going to talk about Batman v Superman? Or are there just no words...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman kills people with a machine gun......<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GTmfnK6XDiA\" data-code=\"GTmfnK6XDiA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/GTmfnK6XDiA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I wanted to like this movie but i left sooo heart broken i had to go home and read my Starman Omnibus just to remind myself there is good DC stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T15:52:29-07:00","id":856752,"title":"","content":"I've seen it. I actually liked it, specially since that &quot;Superman&quot; deserved so much to be punched in the face. Serioulsy, is incredibly anoying and unbearable. I found Ben Afleck's Batman to be quite good, surprisingly. Also, the costume is probably my favourite of all the film/tv adaptations (no the armor one, though that is fine too, just the regular bat-costume)<br /> <br /> EDIT: yeah, well...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 03-31-2016, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T16:25:04-07:00","id":856763,"title":"","content":"It was a good movie. I don't like the way they went with Batman but it isn't the animated series Batman, and I wasn't expecting it to be. Still, it wasn't as if he was the Terminator. Affleck was good, Wonder Woman was good, Superman was good, but they are going with the new 52 version, a man trying to find his place in the world. The movie was very much about fear and how it was keeping the heroes from being heroic.<br /> <br /> The other future Justice League member reveals was poorly placed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-31-2016, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T16:31:05-07:00","id":856765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=856751#post856751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Batman kills people with a machine gun......<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GTmfnK6XDiA\" data-code=\"GTmfnK6XDiA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/GTmfnK6XDiA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I wanted to like this movie but i left sooo heart broken i had to go home and read my Starman Omnibus just to remind myself there is good DC stories.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know what you mean.... I was pretty shocked by it too...even though I thought Affleck played a pretty good Batman, murdering aside...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=856752#post856752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen it. I actually liked it, specially since that &quot;Superman&quot; deserved so much to be punched in the face. Serioulsy, is incredibly anoying and unbearable. I found Ben Afleck's Batman to be quite good, surprisingly. Also, the costume is probably my favourite of all the film/tv adaptations (no the armor one, though that is fine too, just the regular bat-costume)<br /> EDIT: yeah, well...</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman was the best thing about the movie. Wonder Woman wasn't too bad, but honestly, as little as they used her she shouldn't have been in this movie. Superman was just awful...Hell, the first time we see him this movie he straight up murders a guy(granted, he was a terrorist, but still). Plus, the story was a complete train wreck. The plot was all over the place with everyone having to little to no motivation for anything they did.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=856763#post856763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a good movie. I don't like the way they went with Batman but it isn't the animated series Batman, and I wasn't expecting it to be. Still, it wasn't as if he was the Terminator. Affleck was good, Wonder Woman was good, Superman was good, but they are going with the new 52 version, a man trying to find his place in the world. The movie was very much about fear and how it was keeping the heroes from being heroic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish they wouldn't have gone with anything New 52. Honestly, this movie made me wish they'd just done a live action version of The Dark Knight Returns...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T16:38:14-07:00","id":856771,"title":"","content":"I'd like to blame Geoff Johns, who didn't seem to be involved in writing it but was an executive producer. The basic plot seems to be following his Justice League idea, and I just can't stand his work. There were a lot of ways it could have been better.<br /> <br /> I have to admit, though, considering how little actual crime-fighting was done, they really made Batman have some presence. Being a cop or criminal in Gotham is bad enough, but I could really see this Batman putting the scare into people.<br /> <br /> I don't think Superman murdered the terrorist, though. The other terrorists were obviously killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T19:09:56-07:00","id":856849,"title":"","content":"What annoyed me about Batman was it felt like they had action scenes just for the sake of having action scenes, even if it went against Batman's character.<br /> <br /> Like where he puts the tracking beacon on the truck and then chases it through Gotham, machine guns blazing , shooting up bad guysand having this giant chase and firefight, only to sneak into the base later and quietly steal the McGuffin.<br /> <br /> Why didn't he just sneak in there to steal it to begin with? That's what Batman would do. Not get in a giant flashy car chase and shoot people with guns for no good reason. Is it just me, or was that out of character?<br /> <br /> Also, what was up with his gym? Did Bruce Wayne run out of money? &quot;So after all the money I spent on the Bat-jet, it looks like we only have 5 dollars left for workout equipment. I'll go check out the local landfill... oh sweet! An old tire. I can... oh, I can hit it with this old pipe I found. Yeah, this'll totally work.&quot;<br /> <br /> He should have had some kind of crazy NASA-type setup in his basement with the most state of the art bodybuilding equipment in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T19:43:40-07:00","id":856872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=856763#post856763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a good movie. I don't like the way they went with Batman but it isn't the animated series Batman, and I wasn't expecting it to be. Still, it wasn't as if he was the Terminator. Affleck was good, Wonder Woman was good, Superman was good, but they are going with the new 52 version, a man trying to find his place in the world. The movie was very much about fear and how it was keeping the heroes from being heroic.<br /> <br /> The other future Justice League member reveals was poorly placed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well thats the problem, unlike marvel they are going with the route of &quot;everyone already knows the backstory so we dont have to bother&quot; with batman, using the fact that it is a pop culture icon and everyone and their mom knows the basic of the character to avoid doing batman begins again. Which is fine DC, in theory, can pull that off. So we dont get any backstory for how this version of Batman was formed except the pop culture we as an audience know. Dead parents, batsuit, millonaire, no guns, no killing. So the complete disregard of this movie for human life feels off.<br /> <br /> I can forgive it more from superman because we had man of steel to show us how he was raise by papa Kent with his multiple personality disorder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=856849#post856849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why didn't he just sneak in there to steal it to begin with? That's what Batman would do. Not get in a giant flashy car chase and shoot people with guns for no good reason. Is it just me, or was that out of character?</div> </div> </div> </div>As side note, why is batman so bad at being a ninja in this movie? He either constantly blow his cover or get caught on the act.<br /> <br /> I think one of the worse part of the movie is that its full of scenes that could have work..... but they fail. Like the hotel scene. It could have a been a powerful moment in which those death show superman human side, maybe breaking down in front of louis.......but no, brooding and nolan-dialogue. Even the infamous martha scene could have work if they just were a little more subtle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T19:52:19-07:00","id":856877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=856849#post856849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What annoyed me about Batman was it felt like they had action scenes just for the sake of having action scenes, even if it went against Batman's character.<br /> <br /> Like where he puts the tracking beacon on the truck and then chases it through Gotham, machine guns blazing , shooting up bad guysand having this giant chase and firefight, only to sneak into the base later and quietly steal the McGuffin.<br /> <br /> Why didn't he just sneak in there to steal it to begin with? That's what Batman would do. Not get in a giant flashy car chase and shoot people with guns for no good reason. Is it just me, or was that out of character?</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">He didn't really sneak in and quietly steal it later, there's bullet shells all over the floor and unconscious security guards being taken out by the ambulance full. While the car machine guns were, to me, the worst part of the movie as it was real cold-blooded killing there, he wasn't just taking the kryptonite, he was also taking down human traffickers and folks who had committed a wide variety of crimes, including the murders in the beginning.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, what was up with his gym? Did Bruce Wayne run out of money? &quot;So after all the money I spent on the Bat-jet, it looks like we only have 5 dollars left for workout equipment. I'll go check out the local landfill... oh sweet! An old tire. I can... oh, I can hit it with this old pipe I found. Yeah, this'll totally work.&quot;<br /> <br /> He should have had some kind of crazy NASA-type setup in his basement with the most state of the art bodybuilding equipment in the world. </div> </div> </div>He usually just has simple gym equipment. I think he was getting ready for a battle that couldn't rely entirely on technology. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">As you saw, technology basically failed him and in the end it was mostly him, physics, a sharpened rock on a stick and a dash of kryptonite.<br /> <br /> But, really, I think it goes back to the movie being about fear. Batman is afraid of Superman in this movie, and he believes he is the weak point. He needed to toughen himself up psychologically just as much as physically.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T14:11:34-07:00","id":857279,"title":"","content":"Just watched a movie called 'he never died' with henry rollins. Not bad. If you're a WoD fan its worth a watch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T17:05:06-07:00","id":857348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=856771#post856771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Superman murdered the terrorist, though. The other terrorists were obviously killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>He flew at him at super speed, pushing him through at least one wall, possibly more. He was just a mortal man. I'm pretty sure that would kill him. If not, it'd at least cripple him for life. Not saying a terrorist leader doesn't deserve it...just saying that's not how Superman should act. Though I understand this is Zack Synders dark Superman, so I guess the rules don't apply...but still....<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T17:05:36-07:00","id":857349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfAsh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=857279#post857279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just watched a movie called 'he never died' with henry rollins. Not bad. If you're a WoD fan its worth a watch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I watched that the other weekend! pretty good, especially as a WoD fan! I was pretty surprised by it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T17:37:41-07:00","id":857362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=857348#post857348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He flew at him at super speed, pushing him through at least one wall, possibly more. He was just a mortal man. I'm pretty sure that would kill him. If not, it'd at least cripple him for life. Not saying a terrorist leader doesn't deserve it...just saying that's not how Superman should act. Though I understand this is Zack Synders dark Superman, so I guess the rules don't apply...but still....</div> </div> </div> </div>Odds are Superman was taking the brunt of the damage there, I really don't think he killed that guy, though he obviously hurt him. I don't think they'd balk at actually showing him do it if they were going to. Jack from Wayne Enterprises and guys engulfed in flames and metal are more clear than, basically, being thrown or pushed through a wall. If Superman had killed him and saw it as okay, he wouldn't have had an issue with Batman's taking down of criminals in Gotham.<br /> <br /> While it tries to cover some deeper material than a standard action movie, it is still a superhero movie. While in real life a person can die from a single punch or tripping down a pair of steps, there's a certain conceit that people are tougher than they are in real life. Except when the plot requires it, of course. Two people shot on a busy street in the early 80s would probably actually have a decent chance of surviving in a city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-01-2016, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T19:10:25-07:00","id":857398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=857362#post857362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Superman had killed him and saw it as okay, he wouldn't have had an issue with Batman's taking down of criminals in Gotham.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well this brings a good point, superman beef with Batman in the movie is his disregard for due process and law on crime fighting.....after he himself disregard due process and international law by taking down terrorist boss. That Batman generates fear in his crime fighting on gotham while national hearings are happening because people are shit scare of superman.<br /> <br /> Because Terrorist are worse than child molesters/human traffickers....i guess? Damm Papa kent other personality really mess up superman upbringing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:50:58-07:00","id":857449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=857362#post857362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odds are Superman was taking the brunt of the damage there, I really don't think he killed that guy, though he obviously hurt him. I don't think they'd balk at actually showing him do it if they were going to. Jack from Wayne Enterprises and guys engulfed in flames and metal are more clear than, basically, being thrown or pushed through a wall. If Superman had killed him and saw it as okay, he wouldn't have had an issue with Batman's taking down of criminals in Gotham.<br /> <br /> While it tries to cover some deeper material than a standard action movie, it is still a superhero movie. While in real life a person can die from a single punch or tripping down a pair of steps, there's a certain conceit that people are tougher than they are in real life. Except when the plot requires it, of course. Two people shot on a busy street in the early 80s would probably actually have a decent chance of surviving in a city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats a good point...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T08:41:06-07:00","id":857723,"title":"","content":"I saw BvS yesterday afternoon. I thought it was terrible. The plot, the editing, the action sequences, the soundtrack, etc. The only redeeming part of the movie was Gadot as Wonder Woman.<br /> <br /> My favorite scene from this train wreck was Batman doing Crossfit inside a high school gym. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T12:52:39-07:00","id":867001,"title":"","content":"Just came across a dvd of a move I saw in the cinema I saw last year - Solace starring anthony hopkins. It seems to have completely sank but its a good movie and worth checking out - certainly better than a lot of this shit that makes money these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T10:42:29-07:00","id":883892,"title":"","content":"Last night, I treated myself to a double feature of Batman vs. Superman and Civil War:<br /> <br /> BvS: Not as bad as I'd heard it was and, because I'd heard about specific complaints and was looking for them, I was able to see that some of them are actually explained in the movie, but the storytelling is pretty dense, so it's easy to miss a lot of them. But on the whole, Zack Snyder's take on the material is SOOO out of line with the source that I just can't get behind it. While this movie is FAR more technically accomplished than the recent Fantastic Four, I have the same issue with it: Even if it were narratively and technically *perfect*, I would still dislike it,<i> because that's not the FF! </i>I can forgive problems of plot, effects, and everything we fanboys love to wank about, but when the basic foundation of Tone/Mood is wrong, the very Essence of the work is just lost. <br /> <br /> Civil War: Now THIS is more like it, just the thing to wash the taste of Movie DC from my mouth! Interesting that both companies are headlining stories where the Superheroes fight each other, but CW feels much more earned and coherent. Without getting into details, the plot is almost entirely different from the comic CW, which is good, as that one relied on an established MU with decades of history and character interaction; it wouldn't have worked nearly as well in the MCU, so they wisely went with something different. I couldn't help but think of this as the next Avengers movie, since there were so many of them, including a few surprise guests (if you've been paying attention, you probably already know who they are, but I'd been avoiding spoilers and trailers, so it was all a surprise to me)! Be ready to be part of an entire theater fangasming at the showstopping airport scene! Finally, true comic book action up on the live big-screen! <br /> <br /> If I had any problem, it was with the real villain, and how well his plan comes together, when...just who IS this guy? Just some random guy can make the greatest superheroes in the world jump to his tune so easily?? At least he had a decent motivation...Also, where was SHIELD? I'm still a little confused as to the status of the organization, despite watching the tv show regularly? And shouldn't Nick Fury have been at the funeral, I'm pretty sure he's now known to be alive, right?<br /> <br /> Actually, I do have a larger issue, but it's with both films/companies/universes and this obsessive need to examine superhero fiction in a Real World context. The problem is simply that, if you deconstruct these stories so much, then you will BREAK them, and show why they don't really work. And it's fine that they aren't plausible, that's why they are *escapist fantasies*! If you can't get on-board with that, then maybe you are not the ones to be making these movies, guys...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Let's just have movies with superheroes fighting evil, *done really well*, and be happy with that, ok?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T11:40:57-07:00","id":883934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=781694#post781694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love all her movies. If you like buddy cop movies, definitely check out <i>The Heat</i>, whose sequel appears to have sadly been put on indefinite hiatus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've liked a rare FEW of her movies. For the most part though, i just can't stand Mccarthy..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=792752#post792752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that new Deadpool trailer...<br /> <br /> Wow. I can't believe I'm saying this, but it looks fantastic. Damn you, Fox. I want to hate everything Marvel you put out(because it usually sucks), but this looks like it could be one of the best Marvel films, ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>With all the language that film had, i was surprised it made it past the censors...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=812363#post812363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stepdad got a bunch of SAG screeners, going to watch The Big Short, Beasts of No Nation and Straight Out of Compton sometime this week. I really hope he gets a copy of The Force Awakens at some point, but I doubt that'll be on the mailing list.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mind step-dad, but it seems to follow a trend in hollywood of male parents = dumb as rocks/bad.. Smart ass kids who ridicule parents = good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfAsh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=813474#post813474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bridge of spies - really liked this one!</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely LOVED that film.. Great harkening back to the old 70's spy thriller films..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=832643#post832643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watching the Matrix hd for the first time in a while.<br /> <br /> Has anybody else encountered problems with the audio? Special effects really loud, dialogue too quiet?</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to get that a lot with quite a few movies on DVD, or even on the boobtube. Worst ones though imo, are ones where the chatting is low as heck, TILL they get to a crucial part then jacks up..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=17889#post17889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually disappointed by Mockingjay, but the screen adaptations have actually improved the first two books (I particularly like the expanded scenes in the Capital as a means of plot exposition). I'm more than a tad worried about the fact that they've split Mockingjay into two movies, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Add me to the list of those Disappointed with BOTH mockingjays, but LOVED catching fire.. Its the same with the Divergent series so far. 1 was good, 2 great, 3 so far looks pants..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=837316#post837316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just finished watching The Martian, with Matt Damon.<br /> <br /> Goodness gracious, this movie makes me want to work for NASA. An instant classic!</div> </div> </div> </div>+1000 from me. If that film doesn't win several major awards i will be sorely displeased.<br /> <br /> Con't next post!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T11:48:37-07:00","id":883941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=854048#post854048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone notice a rise in religious movies of late? My local theater (MJR) is showing two of them, and we're getting more of them in the video section at work (the latest is apparently about a father who's upset that his daughter is learning about *gasp* Evolution at college, and is <i>determined to do something about it!</i>)</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they are trying to make up for not having many for a long time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lilappleblossom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=854076#post854076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=847928#post847928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw '10 Cloverfield Lane' on Sunday. I thought it was great! I didn't know much going in...and it kept me guessing. Theres no real connection to Cloverfield, so if you go in expecting that you might be disappointed. Aside from that, I loved everything about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a giant monster in it at any point?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope its actually BETTER than the original cloverfield, cause of NOT having that massive beastie.. BUT i am gonna leave it till it hits redbox..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=856752#post856752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen it. I actually liked it, specially since that &quot;Superman&quot; deserved so much to be punched in the face. Serioulsy, is incredibly anoying and unbearable. I found Ben Afleck's Batman to be quite good, surprisingly. Also, the costume is probably my favourite of all the film/tv adaptations (no the armor one, though that is fine too, just the regular bat-costume)<br /> <br /> EDIT: yeah, well...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was surprised how well i liked Afleck's Batman.. Much better than a lot of people initially were giving him credit for. ALso Loved the way they did doomsday. <br /> <br /> Only gripe is how they seemed to make Lex into a crazy guy much like the Joker..<br /> <br /> <br /> As a linked question, has anyone seen either &quot;Midnight special&quot; or &quot;400 days&quot;??<br /> Were either of them any good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"",