Civil War was awesome! ~<br /> ~ I really liked it ~ a lot! ~","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 05-09-2016, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T22:48:53-07:00","id":889673,"title":"","content":"Only a couple of people here have seen Civil War yet? Or is The Awesome of it just too tongue-tieing to write about?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I finally bought Conan on blu-ray, because my store had it on sale and I feel I should own it already; it comes with a coupon for $8 off the Snow White and the Huntsman sequel out now, so I may as well go see that...<br /> <br /> Anyone seen the live Jungle Book yet? How do you feel about <a href=\"https://www.buzzfeed.com/adambvary/breaking-down-the-two-jungle-book-movies?utm_term=.ywKEprPgor#.arQGmbYgyb\" target=\"_blank\">Warner Bros doing their own live version of it next year?</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T06:35:05-07:00","id":889842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=889673#post889673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only a couple of people here have seen Civil War yet? Or is The Awesome of it just too tongue-tieing to write about?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It was good. Not <i>Winter Soldier</i> good, but definitely better than <i>Age of Ultron</i>. The plot and characterization made more sense than in the Civil War comic plotline. Every super and several of the supporting cast had good character <i>and</i> good action moments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T08:34:39-07:00","id":889928,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt4264426/?ref_=fn_al_tt_1\" target=\"_blank\">Bite</a> was abysmal. A couple good ideas strung together by the weakest characterization and plot possible. <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt4105970/\" target=\"_blank\">They Look Like People</a> was actually pretty good, but for some reason it's in the Horror category when it's more appropriately a Thriller with some Mystery and Drama, like IMDB points out. In case no one's read this thread and noticed, I like Horror movies. It's a solid story about fictional mental illness and the friendship of two guys in bad places in their lives. <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt3562786/\" target=\"_blank\">Uncaged </a>was surprisingly funny and good, though I wouldn't go so far as to say it was great. It's sort of sedate and a lot of things are underplayed, but still a decent movie. <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt3727982/\" target=\"_blank\">Ava's Possession</a> was a letdown, not nearly as bad as Bite but it seemed like they decided to abandon the horror side of things in favor of comedy but they didn't really do the comedy well either. It also seems like a lot of stuff was cut. <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt3698558/\" target=\"_blank\">Some Kind of Hate</a> was a solid flick, a sort of throwback to the old revenge rampages, very bloody but with some nicely thought out effects, might be inspiring to Geist the Sin-Eaters fans or ghost buffs. <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt4935334/\" target=\"_blank\">Southbound </a>is great, I'm surprised it hasn't been talked about more since it's release but I suppose the interest in horror anthologies is waning again, the stories within were fantastically gripping and one in particular left a lingering sense of unease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T12:37:05-07:00","id":890090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=889842#post889842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was good. Not <i>Winter Soldier</i> good, but definitely better than <i>Age of Ultron</i>. The plot and characterization made more sense than in the Civil War comic plotline. Every super and several of the supporting cast had good character <i>and</i> good action moments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually i felt it was Better than winter soldier.. And i also loved age of ultron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T17:54:50-07:00","id":890296,"title":"","content":"I saw Civil War last weekend and really enjoyed it!! Had a serious tone, but had some nice light hearted moments as well. The airport scene was pretty amazing! Spider-Man in this movie might be the best on film on to date!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T12:14:09-07:00","id":903705,"title":"","content":"Saw X-Men Apocalypse. Loved it. Fox is kicking ass right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T21:41:45-07:00","id":903951,"title":"","content":"I will be catching it tomorrow (well today since its now 12:40am)..<br /> <br /> Over the weekend i caught the Chris pine film Their Finest hour. man was that slow but GOOD..<br /> Also caught the Jeff Bridges sea flick, White Squall.. Man did i feel bad for those dead, but i loved how the students (just like in Dead Poet's society) stood up FOR their captain...<br /> <br /> On a different note, who here has ever seen the &quot;post WW1&quot; film In Pursuit of Honor with Don Johnson, where these cavalrymen take 'custody (well steal them technically) of hundreds of horses from the Dept of the Army, who is just gonna push them all into mass pits and shoot them, then rides them all north to Canada?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T13:36:25-07:00","id":907840,"title":"","content":"Not sure if its appropriate for this thread or should be in its own, but here goes..<br /> CNN had an article on it where several feminists are complaining about the X-men Apocalypse poster showing the strong lead female character (Mystique) being Choked by the bad evil man (Apocalypse..), and saying It seems to make &quot;battery can be fun&quot;..<br /> <br /> And the story is not just on CNN's site, but several others. But to me the wierder part of it is that Fox quickly jumped up and apologized for it??<br /> Why? Is having a female lead getting choked wrong, when that same female lead character has beaten up men like crazy through out all the films??<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.cnn.com/2016/06/03/entertainment/x-men-apocalypse-jennifer-lawrence-strangled-fox-apologizes/index.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://media.cnn.com/api/v1/images/stellar/prod/160603174513-jennifer-lawrence-strangeld-x-men.png?q=x_503,y_0,h_2114,w_3756,c_crop/w_800\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.cnn.com/2016/06/03/entertainment/x-men-apocalypse-jennifer-lawrence-strangled-fox-apologizes/index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Fox apologizes for &lsquo;X-Men: Apocalypse&rsquo; ads showing Jennifer Lawrence being strangled | CNN </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.cnn.com/2016/06/03/entertainment/x-men-apocalypse-jennifer-lawrence-strangled-fox-apologizes/index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.cnn.com/2016/06/03/entertainment/x-men-apocalypse-jennifer-lawrence-strangled-fox-apologizes/index.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> 20th Century Fox is apologizing for an &ldquo;X-Men: Apocalypse&rdquo; promotional image showing Jennifer Lawrence&rsquo;s character Mystique being strangled by villain Apocalypse. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-3626246/We-never-condone-violence-against-women-Fox-apologizes-X-men-poster-showed-Jennifer-Lawrence-s-character-strangled-man.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/arti...ngled-man.html</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.cbc.ca/news/arts/fox-apologies-xmen-billboard-1.3616804\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.cbc.ca/ais/1.3616862,1465079945000/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C58%2C600%2C337%29%3BResize%3D620\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.cbc.ca/news/arts/fox-apologies-xmen-billboard-1.3616804\" target=\"_blank\"> Did this X-Men: Apocalypse billboard go too far? Fox says sorry | CBC News </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.cbc.ca/news/arts/fox-apologies-xmen-billboard-1.3616804\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.cbc.ca/news/arts/fox-apologies-xmen-billboard-1.3616804 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Film studio 20th Century Fox has apologized for a billboard that features Jennifer Lawrence's X-Men: Apocalypse character, Mystique, being strangled. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T15:49:48-07:00","id":907936,"title":"","content":"Presumably because it's using an image of violence against women to sell the movie. And while Mystique does, or did at least, hurt men it didn't have her doing it on the poster.<br /> <br /> If anyone should be apologizing it should probably be the people behind this gem.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://greenappleent.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/02/Jokers-Poltergeist-Artwork.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> After a clown-masked assailant guns down Aurora's Place, the resident theater owner fights to re-open her business.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T16:42:37-07:00","id":907972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=907840#post907840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if its appropriate for this thread or should be in its own, but here goes..<br /> CNN had an article on it where several feminists are complaining about the X-men Apocalypse poster showing the strong lead female character (Mystique) being Choked by the bad evil man (Apocalypse..), and saying It seems to make &quot;battery can be fun&quot;..<br /> <br /> And the story is not just on CNN's site, but several others. But to me the wierder part of it is that Fox quickly jumped up and apologized for it??<br /> Why? Is having a female lead getting choked wrong, when that same female lead character has beaten up men like crazy through out all the films??<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.cnn.com/2016/06/03/entertainment/x-men-apocalypse-jennifer-lawrence-strangled-fox-apologizes/index.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://media.cnn.com/api/v1/images/stellar/prod/160603174513-jennifer-lawrence-strangeld-x-men.png?q=x_503,y_0,h_2114,w_3756,c_crop/w_800\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.cnn.com/2016/06/03/entertainment/x-men-apocalypse-jennifer-lawrence-strangled-fox-apologizes/index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Fox apologizes for &lsquo;X-Men: Apocalypse&rsquo; ads showing Jennifer Lawrence being strangled | CNN </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.cnn.com/2016/06/03/entertainment/x-men-apocalypse-jennifer-lawrence-strangled-fox-apologizes/index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.cnn.com/2016/06/03/entertainment/x-men-apocalypse-jennifer-lawrence-strangled-fox-apologizes/index.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> 20th Century Fox is apologizing for an &ldquo;X-Men: Apocalypse&rdquo; promotional image showing Jennifer Lawrence&rsquo;s character Mystique being strangled by villain Apocalypse. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-3626246/We-never-condone-violence-against-women-Fox-apologizes-X-men-poster-showed-Jennifer-Lawrence-s-character-strangled-man.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/arti...ngled-man.html</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.cbc.ca/news/arts/fox-apologies-xmen-billboard-1.3616804\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.cbc.ca/news/arts/fox-apol...oard-1.3616804</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> People were outraged that a super villain was acting like a super villain? I'm...sadly, not surprised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]}