/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T18:48:27-07:00","id":921283,"title":"","content":"Went to the drive-in last night and saw <i>Independence Day Resurgence</i> and <i>Central Intelligence</i>. iD4R was almost, but not quite terrible enough to be a good bad movie. Every 30 seconds they added some nonsense to keep the movie from making any sense. Highly recommend not watching this one sober. Central Intelligence, OTOH, was delightful. We were laughing almost the whole film through (well, we laughed a lot in iD4R, too). Special bonus points go to Dwayne Johnson because it's usually not clear whether his character is being weird <i>to throw others off</i> or if his character is being weird <i>because his character is weird</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T23:48:04-07:00","id":921380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=921247#post921247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=921166#post921166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They really dropped the ball on that. How in the hell was it not titled 'Now You Don't'? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts exactly!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I take it that was cause of the way the titles flow into one another if it was that way??<br /> <br /> Was it any good though??<br /> <br /> Anyhow, i did a pair of older movies for tonight's viewing pleasure.<br /> First up was an old Don Johnson film, In Pursuit of Honor.. For those who don't know it, its set in the late 1930s during the time of the Vets of WW1 riots and then later, when the US military was doing away with the Cavalry and going to tanks.. Don and his crew are part of the cavalry who are ordered to 'push their horses' into pits to get gunned down (so they can save money).. He and the rest rebel, steal the horses and drive them north, hoping to save them (though they did lose several in the trek) eventually making it to Canada.. <br /> <br /> Next up was an older Tom Cruise film, Far and Away..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T08:33:05-07:00","id":921503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=921283#post921283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Went to the drive-in last night and saw <i>Independence Day Resurgence</i> and <i>Central Intelligence</i>. iD4R was almost, but not quite terrible enough to be a good bad movie. Every 30 seconds they added some nonsense to keep the movie from making any sense. Highly recommend not watching this one sober.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! I'll keep that mind, should I see it. Probably be one I watch at home..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=921283#post921283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Central Intelligence, OTOH, was delightful. We were laughing almost the whole film through (well, we laughed a lot in iD4R, too). Special bonus points go to Dwayne Johnson because it's usually not clear whether his character is being weird <i>to throw others off</i> or if his character is being weird <i>because his character is weird</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno...the trailers looked so bad. That might be a watch at home as well...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by 