=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I just watched Deadpool.<br /> <br /> I was really surprised by this one - I stay away from superhero movies outside of the MCU, so this one was a bit of a risk for me. Grinning through most of the movie, with genuine laugh out moments and cool action - glad I gambled on this one.<br /> <br /> Not going anywhere <i>near</i> Man of Steel, BvS or the X-Men movies (except <i>maybe</i> First Class) though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amusingly I just finished watching it as well.<br /> <br /> It exceeded my expectations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T23:14:17-07:00","id":922478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=922429#post922429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I just watched Deadpool.<br /> <br /> I was really surprised by this one - I stay away from superhero movies outside of the MCU, so this one was a bit of a risk for me. Grinning through most of the movie, with genuine laugh out moments and cool action - glad I gambled on this one.<br /> <br /> Not going anywhere <i>near</i> Man of Steel, BvS or the X-Men movies (except <i>maybe</i> First Class) though.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me of the Xmen franchize films i would rank them..<br /> <br /> Xmen Apocalypse<br /> Xmen #1<br /> Xmen Days of future past<br /> Xmen 2<br /> Xmen origins Wolverine<br /> The wolverine (wolvie 2)<br /> Xmen 3...<br /> <br /> Man of steel i actually liked quite a bit and BvS was a good enough film for me to at least give others by DC another chance..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T16:23:27-07:00","id":935343,"title":"","content":"Guess we're not gonna talk about the new Ghostbusters?<br /> <br /> I saw it last weekend. It had it's moments...but overall, I didn't care for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T22:55:28-07:00","id":935455,"title":"","content":"I will be seeing it when it hits redbox (or my local library).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T06:23:55-07:00","id":935563,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen it yet: we're planning on watching it in the theatre, and I've heard it's &quot;Obviously not as good as the original, but better than the 2nd, and the first two acts are genuinely good which makes the weak 3rd act all the more tragic.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T20:22:35-07:00","id":935909,"title":"","content":"Was going to go see Ghostbusters on wed, but then saw that a local theater was showing a marathon of Star Trek, Star Trek Into Darkness, and Star Trek Beyond, all in IMAX, with the last in 3D...yeah, I'll spend a day doing that!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For the record, I loved both of Abram's takes on ST, and never really got what the hardcore fandom's problem with them were. STB, however, feels pretty *different*...it's clear others are behind the camera. I dunno, I feel like it was *good*, but not great, and I *liked* it, but did not love it...maybe it'll grow on me more with repeat viewings...<br /> <br /> I will say that it actually did feel more like the classic Trek series, probably because as they're well into the 5 year mission now, Chris Pine's Kirk has observably grown, matured and settled down some, to the point where he feels a LOT more like classic Kirk...he even has William Shatner's hairstyle from TOS, which I actually found a bit distracting at times!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The movie actually inspired me to watch some of the classic eps on Netflix afterwards, which none of the other movies have ever made me do...<br /> <br /> Word to the wise, btw, apparently some of the TV spots spoil a big plot reveal about Idris Elba's villain, so...consider yourselves warned (Simon Pegg is reportedly furious over this). <br /> <br /> One of my pet peeves with the Star Trek film series has been its need to target the Earth, no matter how far in space the story is set, as though audiences can't truly be invested unless our world was endangered (Generations was particularly clumsy with this), so I was really hoping this film would avoid that pitfall. It did, sort of, in a clever way that didn't directly threaten Earth, but still had a large target that we were invested in, in the form of one of THE most <i>amazing</i> space stations I've ever seen put on film! Seriously, this alone was almost worth the price of 3D (this is also where we meet Sulu's husband and child, giving us a personal stake to worry about)...<br /> <br /> There's also a really over-the-top action sequence at the climax that might have people wondering, &quot;Is this really Star Trek?? Should ST go there, and have this type of action in it?&quot; Personally, I loved it, and appreciate pushing the boundaries like that...although I might NOT like it if I saw something similar in a Star Wars movie. Hmm...<br /> <br /> Anyway, I recommend it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T22:20:29-07:00","id":935943,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen it. Ghostbusters or the Star Trek movie. The first I just haven't gotten around to and will probably wait for it to come out online, the latter I'm just not interested in.<br /> <br /> I'm seeing the Secret Lives of Pets tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Saw a horrible movie called On The Brain a couple days ago, awful acting and writing, it made me wonder if after the first filming the director redid half of it and told everyone to emote more. Then I saw another movie which had a nicely long title I can't remember. I only remember one line. 'My name's Dick Anus, but everybody round here calls me Stinkthumb.' Which is certainly up there in the ranks of memorable introductions.<br /> <br /> Looked it up. Blood Orgy at Beaver Lake. Amazon Prime has a lot of 'free' movies, but a huge amount of their selection is this kind of low budget stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-23-2016, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T00:29:25-07:00","id":935971,"title":"","content":"Caught 2 tonight, though i had to turn one off after 20 min it was that horrid..<br /> That was Identicals. Basically a film that had a decent concept, but the inception of it and the acting were sub par..<br /> Then came Tina Fey's Whiskey Tango Foxtrot. Man i was laughing like crazy.. LOVED Molina as the Afgan AG..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T22:43:09-07:00","id":936939,"title":"","content":"I saw the new Trek today. I thought it was OK. The actors all did a good job, I liked the new female alien character, liked the callback to &quot;Enterprise&quot; with some elements. About the only thing I didn't care for was the main antagonist, I found him to be pretty boring which is a big problem for me in a movie like this. Trek needs compelling bad guys, I liked Cumberbatch's Khan, didn't care for Bana's Nero and the new villain left me with a similar feeling to Nero. There was more &quot;right&quot; than &quot;wrong&quot; so overall it was a good movie, just not a great one. I'll probably check out Ghostbusters later this week, mainly because I like Kate McKinnon and have heard nothing but good things about her role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T03:34:27-07:00","id":938011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=935909#post935909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, I loved both of Abram's takes on ST, and never really got what the hardcore fandom's problem with them were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait 'till Werewolf's 'Shattered Dreams' time travels an creates a new time line, where everything is seemingly as it was before, but really isn't.<br /> <br /> But really, JJ Abrams is a storyteller, and that is okay. But one can have conflicting opinions about whether or not it is acceptable to allow beaming onto a vessel with warp speed to be a hand-waived element that leads to a silly 'one-liner' (Who knew it was Space that was moving) and a slap-stick-esque &quot;find Scotty in the tubing system&quot;-scene, with convenient transparent tubes and no grid to prevent objects to get caught in the turbine, but a even more convenient release module 3 meters above ground.<br /> <br /> Just like in Star Wars, where Kylo Renn is being able to stop a Laser Blaster bolt in mid air, without any apparent effort, have a conversation and then releasing the bolt it seems JJ Abrams aims for a &quot;story over setting&quot; approach. One has to be okay with that, if one wants to enjoy his movies, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T23:13:49-07:00","id":938630,"title":"","content":"I don't mind the Kelvin timeline, now that it's no longer being marketed as the replacement for the Prime universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T23:44:29-07:00","id":938649,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt4786282/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Lights Out</i></a> tapped directly into most of my deepest phobias.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T10:02:43-07:00","id":938916,"title":"","content":"Saw Ghostbusters last week and it got me thinking a lot about what movies we come to love. <br /> <br /> I have to admit a lot of these new sequels/reboots were based off classic movies I never watched before. I binged Terminator to watch the new one. Saw the Mad Max movies days before Fury Road, bought the three Jurassic Park movies and even finally watched all 6 star Treks. Ghostbusters was another one I'd never seen. It felt every time I watched these movies, I had the &quot;wrong&quot; opinion. The first terminator film, to me, was god awful as was the 4th one and the new one, but 2 was amazing and 3 was good. I hated Jurassic Park 1, liked 2 a bit better, and think the third one and fourth one are equally good but for different reasons. I didn't like any of the star wars movies except the new one (which admittedly is plotwise very similar to the first one but the plot never bothered me in the original) And I thought Ghostbuster 1 was bad, 2 was at least fun, and 3 was filled with way too many plotholes but like 2 was at least fun. Weirdly enough, I liked all the Mad Max films.<br /> <br /> I guess without any prior lead in or feelings, especially at the time, the movies didn't mean much to me. Not to say my opinions are in any way correct. It's very possible (and even likely) I have bad taste. It's stuff like knowing I would have loved Power Rangers, Dragon Ball Z, and Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles as a kid but because I never did, I doubt I could get into them as an adult.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? Does Nostalgia color a film's quality/enjoyablity, especially if it was good for that time? And can what is considered good change with time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T10:39:50-07:00","id":938935,"title":"","content":"I think nostalgia <i>can</i> color how somebody feels about a film, but with regards to, say, the original Ghostbusters, I didn't see it until I was 25 and I thought it was damn near a perfect movie. Same with Back to the Future. In some cases, I can actually enjoy a film even more: I watched Beetlejuice a lot as a kid because I thought it was great. I watched it again as an adult and like it even more, but hate the parts that I loved as a kid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T12:09:49-07:00","id":939006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=938935#post938935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think nostalgia <i>can</i> color how somebody feels about a film, but with regards to, say, the original Ghostbusters, I didn't see it until I was 25 and I thought it was damn near a perfect movie. Same with Back to the Future. In some cases, I can actually enjoy a film even more: I watched Beetlejuice a lot as a kid because I thought it was great. I watched it again as an adult and like it even more, but hate the parts that I loved as a kid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here. Took me iirc till my mid 20s (mid to late 1990s) before i saw princess bride (and some other early to mid '80s classics), Loved them then. And felt some i might NOT have loved had i watched them when they initially came out..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T20:51:16-07:00","id":941655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=935563#post935563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen it yet: we're planning on watching it in the theatre, and I've heard it's &quot;Obviously not as good as the original, but better than the 2nd, and the first two acts are genuinely good which makes the weak 3rd act all the more tragic.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say for me, the new Ghostbusters is not better than Ghostbusters 2, as I loved that one. The first one is the best obviously, but I still love 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=935909#post935909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was going to go see Ghostbusters on wed, but then saw that a local theater was showing a marathon of Star Trek, Star Trek Into Darkness, and Star Trek Beyond, all in IMAX, with the last in 3D...yeah, I'll spend a day doing that!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For the record, I loved both of Abram's takes on ST, and never really got what the hardcore fandom's problem with them were. STB, however, feels pretty *different*...it's clear others are behind the camera. I dunno, I feel like it was *good*, but not great, and I *liked* it, but did not love it...maybe it'll grow on me more with repeat viewings...<br /> <br /> I will say that it actually did feel more like the classic Trek series, probably because as they're well into the 5 year mission now, Chris Pine's Kirk has observably grown, matured and settled down some, to the point where he feels a LOT more like classic Kirk...he even has William Shatner's hairstyle from TOS, which I actually found a bit distracting at times!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The movie actually inspired me to watch some of the classic eps on Netflix afterwards, which none of the other movies have ever made me do...<br /> <br /> Word to the wise, btw, apparently some of the TV spots spoil a big plot reveal about Idris Elba's villain, so...consider yourselves warned (Simon Pegg is reportedly furious over this).<br /> <br /> One of my pet peeves with the Star Trek film series has been its need to target the Earth, no matter how far in space the story is set, as though audiences can't truly be invested unless our world was endangered (Generations was particularly clumsy with this), so I was really hoping this film would avoid that pitfall. It did, sort of, in a clever way that didn't directly threaten Earth, but still had a large target that we were invested in, in the form of one of THE most <i>amazing</i> space stations I've ever seen put on film! Seriously, this alone was almost worth the price of 3D (this is also where we meet Sulu's husband and child, giving us a personal stake to worry about)...<br /> <br /> There's also a really over-the-top action sequence at the climax that might have people wondering, &quot;Is this really Star Trek?? Should ST go there, and have this type of action in it?&quot; Personally, I loved it, and appreciate pushing the boundaries like that...although I might NOT like it if I saw something similar in a Star Wars movie. Hmm...<br /> <br /> Anyway, I recommend it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I saw the new Star Trek today and loved it. I didn't expect to, as the trailers made it look pretty bad. But, I was very surprised by it. I liked the 2009 Trek(I'm a sucker for time travel), though I didn;t feel Into Darkness was all that great. I wish they'd hadn't tried to anything related to Wrath of Khan. It was ok, but not as good as the other one. The new one was much better! I really liked what they did it with. And I agree, I felt more like the originals to me than the others were...<br /> <br /> Anyway, I loved it! And I loved that space station! That made for an awesome set piece!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=938630#post938630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind the Kelvin timeline, now that it's no longer being marketed as the replacement for the Prime universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I like that even though these movies are a reboot of sorts, there is still a direct tie-in with the original universe, even in this new one!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T09:10:28-07:00","id":941995,"title":"","content":"Has anyone seen the trailer for A Monster Calls? Saw it last night and it lookes beautiful. I had never heard of the book, I'll need to check it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T11:47:41-07:00","id":942127,"title":"","content":"Of the upcoming movies from NOW till the end of the year the ones i am looking forward to the most are..<br /> August: Pete's dragon, Ben Hur, War dogs, Mechanic Resurrection<br /> <br /> Sept: Magnificent 7 (remake), and miss pegrene's school for peculiar kids...<br /> <br /> Oct: Jack reacher 2, Keeping up with the Joneses, the Accountant<br /> <br /> Nov: Hacksaw ridge and Dr Strange<br /> <br /> Dec: Assassins creed and starwars rogue 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T16:49:29-07:00","id":943105,"title":"","content":"So, I just tried to watch Batman Begins again. Key word &quot;tried.&quot;<br /> <br /> This dialogue... was this dialogue written for human beings? At all? It's totally stiff, completely wooden, lacking <i>any</i> kind of life or poetry. Any more technical and matter-of-fact and it might as well be Blu-Ray player instructions.<br /> <br /> This is in contrast to Marvel movies, which feel like they have <i>vastly</i> more life and energy to them. Man. Why did I ever like the Nolan Batman movies in the first place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:50:49-07:00","id":943233,"title":"","content":"Many other sites say that the DC movies suck way much more than even the crappiest marvel one...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T19:41:25-07:00","id":945234,"title":"","content":"Blew off the game for the weekend and saw Suicide Squad, very good movie. Really liked the way they went with Joker and Harley, but they also helped show off origin stories in a way that added some depth to the movie and characters. Amanda Waller killed.<br /> <br /> Saw the Mind's Eye last night, too. I'd been looking forward to it for a while but was pretty disappointed. Good acting and all, it just told a very generic story in a very generic way.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar175_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"175\" data-vbnamecard=\"175\">Prometheus878</a> I though it was very dry, too. Nolan does that kind of stuff. I wasn't a fan of the Batman movies in the 80s and 90s and when Begins came out I didn't think I'd like the revamps. The sequels did much better, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-06-2016, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T11:48:18-07:00","id":945580,"title":"","content":"Watched Suicide Squad last night. Better than Batman vs. Superman, but that's really not saying much.<br /> <br /> The constant music playing every two minutes(I'm not kidding) was a HUGE distraction. It felt like they were trying to do their best Guardians of the Galaxy impression...except with shitty music.<br /> The acting was atrocious. Harley Quinn's Brooklyn accent kept disappearing and reappearing every other scene, Killer Croc was a giant stereotype, Will Smith played an excellent Will Smith. The Joker was horrible. Equally as bad as Luther in BvS. This Joker wasn't scary, frightening, or...well...I'm not sure what exactly he was supposed to be. The action scenes were too dark to tell what was happening, you'd think you were watching Batman Begins. The editing was also pretty bad. So bad, that I could easily point out all of the re-shoots.<br /> <br /> It just...it wasn't a good film. It wasn't the worst, but it wasn't good, either.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 08-07-2016, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T12:29:22-07:00","id":945598,"title":"","content":"Pretty much. I saw it on Thursday. It had it's moments. I liked Will Smith in it and HQ had a few moments I liked. The editing however was AWFUL. I am no editing expert but the film absolutely felt chopped together instead of flowing and from what little I've read about the post production well it's not far from the truth. I didn't mind the tatted up Joker as much as I thought it would annoy me. In fact I felt a little bad for Leto and I hope that when they do the solo Batman movie that, if it involves HQ and Mr. J that they get the chance for better performances. Beyond that the terrible racial stereotypes and throwaway characters(the villain, zip line guy,etc) weighed the film down for me. Oddly enough I also wanted to see more stuff with the Joker's main henchman. He didn't get many scenes and from something I saw at IGN he's a comic book character. I didn't hate the film, I thought it was okay. But mostly just...okay. While I am not a comic person and the vast majority of my interest in DC characters is Batman and his rogue's gallery, I am still a little sad to see DC's continued efforts to catch up to Marvel still stinking of desperation. I liked Man of Steel( a movie I know is contentious to man Superman fans, my sympathies) and that film so far still feels like the best of a sad bunch for the DCU.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T12:50:34-07:00","id":945603,"title":"","content":"It seems as if it's trendy to hate DC stuff, though the executive meddling doesn't help. Even before the movies, people have been praising Marvel for showcasing new characters that are shallowly executed or killed off. And complaining about DC reboots, which are comparatively rare considering Marvel's rebooted characters like Captain Marvel five times in five years. Or how if DC kills off a character there's an entire article about how 'seriously messed up' it is, while Marvel's showcased characters seem to drop like flies. WB should probably just sit back and wait until the inevitable tides turn, but the cape movie situation might be like pirate movies, just waiting for a final end that will taint the genre for years. As a company I can understand why it would strike while the iron's hot. However the critics feel the movies aren't exactly bringing in nickles and dimes.<br /> <br /> There are editing problems but they're not that bad. I'd definitely count it as a better team movie than Guardians of the Galaxy. Almost everyone got to be showcased, El Diablo and Deadshot brought the feels. Joker was excellent, and while they haven't turned completely away from his abusive relationship with her from the comics, I got much more of a Dracula vibe from their romance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-07-2016, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T13:54:01-07:00","id":945647,"title":"","content":"It's more than a little messed up seeing people dismiss any criticisms of something as a &quot;trend.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 08-07-2016, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T14:24:20-07:00","id":945662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=945647#post945647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more than a little messed up seeing people dismiss any criticisms of something as a &quot;tend.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>While I can see why you would think so, I wasn't attempting to dismiss your criticisms. Really, anyone's, though I think some of Fat Larry's problems were overstated. My first paragraph was more an indirect bitching.<br /> <br /> There is a trend, in general while not specifically here, that seems to be overly harsh to DC comics and overly obliging towards Marvel. It's more common on comic book forums or the types of sites that report 'news' related to comics. At conventions, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T14:37:27-07:00","id":945670,"title":"","content":"I disagree, I just think DC does worse live action movies. DC blows it out of the water with their animated films, though they're almost always awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T14:43:11-07:00","id":945673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=945603#post945603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are editing problems but they're not that bad. I'd definitely count it as a better team movie than Guardians of the Galaxy. Almost everyone got to be showcased, El Diablo and Deadshot brought the feels. Joker was excellent, and while they haven't turned completely away from his abusive relationship with her from the comics, I got much more of a Dracula vibe from their romance.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are massive editing problems with this movie. Massive. The fact that I can count the re-shoots speaks volumes. The movie feels like it was thrown together like a jigsaw puzzle, with pieces in randomized order. And the notion that you feel this movie is a better team movie than Guardians of the Galaxy is something I couldn't disagree with more.<br /> <br /> It's not trendy to dislike DC movies. It's trendy to dislike shitty movies. This(and BvS) is a shitty movie. If you look up DC's animated films on RT, they're mostly rated extremely high. I'm a huge DC fan, and still have the original run of Suicide Squad by Ostrander in one of my long boxes. <br /> <br /> This is simply a bad movie. Whether it's due to WB's meddling, or something else, I don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T14:45:43-07:00","id":945677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=945662#post945662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> though I think some of Fat Larry's problems were overstated.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can feel however way you'd like about the film. But I feel strongly that the movie has massive problems.<br /> <br /> Edit: I think by just looking at some of our own comic tastes, we're not going to agree regardless. I'm glad you enjoyed the film. I did not. I also don't mean offense, no father. I was simply heavily looking forward to SS, and it was a gigantic letdown.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 08-07-2016, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T15:54:01-07:00","id":945722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=945673#post945673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are massive editing problems with this movie. Massive. The fact that I can count the re-shoots speaks volumes. The movie feels like it was thrown together like a jigsaw puzzle, with pieces in randomized order. And the notion that you feel this movie is a better team movie than Guardians of the Galaxy is something I couldn't disagree with more.<br /> <br /> It's not trendy to dislike DC movies. It's trendy to dislike shitty movies. This(and BvS) is a shitty movie. If you look up DC's animated films on RT, they're mostly rated extremely high. I'm a huge DC fan, and still have the original run of Suicide Squad by Ostrander in one of my long boxes.<br /> <br /> This is simply a bad movie. Whether it's due to WB's meddling, or something else, I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I have yet to see BvS but even as someone who has had limited training in film , I can tell the film has little to no flow with few scenes of character development or real introduction. Can a director make a film that flash from scene to scene and maintains a fast space? Certainly, but one of the best example, arguably ever, came out recently in the form of Fury Road. From what seems to be coming out about the editing and reshoots, Leto's puzzlement at his scenes,etc it does seem that some degree of interference, second guessing,etc happened. For myself, I am not a comic reader. I've read maybe......5? comics in my entire life and all of them were read over 20 years ago. Every piece of media I've seen on comics has come from other sources. This isn't about a DC v Marvel thing or whatnot. It's on a wanting to see a good movie scene. Batman's villains are easily some of my favourite villains so I went into this hoping for a great movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T12:51:52-07:00","id":946388,"title":"","content":"I've seen the film succinctly described as &quot;a watchable mess&quot;.<br /> <br /> My own perspective is that it feels like a series of pieces that are strung along with no real overarching story to chain them together or narrative logic to drive them along.<br /> <br /> There are performances that I like, but that rather underlines the weakness. I'd say one of the biggest holes concerns Amanda Waller:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">A big deal is made out of how she's in possession of Enchantress' heart, which is supposed to be her big control and security measure, and yet Enchantress goes rogue at the earliest opportunity in the story, and we get no clear indication of why Waller does not or cannot trigger the heart to kill her. At one point Waller is stabbing it, which... is that intended to kill, or hurt? Why not just trigger its bomb? Incubus seems to do something that helps Enchantress, but we're not really privy to what or how; not even a reaction shot of Waller stabbing the heart to no effect. And getting the heart back seems to matter, so is it still her weakness?<br /> <br /> Plus how the whole mission turns out to be getting Waller out of the city... what exactly was her end game?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It doesn't seem to know what it's doing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T13:02:50-07:00","id":947181,"title":"","content":"I just saw it and found it to be much better than I expected it to be. I went in with low expectations and enjoyed it. Still not a fan of Leto's Joker, but other than that there was nothing that was really disappointing. If you were paying attention to the movie then you know the answers to Isator's questions. I'd answer them myself but don't want to give away spoilers, even in a spoiler tag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T00:13:57-07:00","id":947577,"title":"","content":"My problem with recent DC Movies is that they are draining. I mean emotionally, there are few breaks in between the drama, so even if I am Not invested the lack of a stylistic break is somewhat exhausting. Marvel movies mix it up. That said, I find movies like Antman and Guardians to have relatively little dramatic break and don't enjoy them much either. I used to be a DC fan most of my life (in terms of comics) but Marvel has just been doing better recently. I got a pile of comics right in front of me and maybe 1 is a DC book. The pendulum swings. There was a time that X-Men was the only well known marvel group outside the comics.<br /> <br /> I do think it is odd, since DC always used to seem more hopeful what with it's fake cities, less realism and more about huge figures. While Marvel was the gritty one that put it's characters in more real life situations. It's like they switched. But DC really took it too far.<br /> <br /> The problem is also partly with Batman. He's gotten so big he's hard to recognize sometimes? The Batman I knew growing up would have trouble fighting 5/6 no-name thugs at a time. I liked him because he was normal. Now Batman has super smarts in all but name and there is a legit question on whether he could win against superman. The playboy millionaire has become a bit misanthropic. I feel like what's wrong with Batman is what is wrong with DC comics/movies. So hard core they forgot their core. When Bruce Wayne says a lame joke because he thinks it's funny, embarrasses himself flirting, and get scuffed up by normal stuff people get scuffed up by, I'll feel DC is back on track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T15:16:16-07:00","id":948894,"title":"","content":"Hey guys...this seemed like a good thread to ask this question in. I have a bunch of dvds(and some blu-rays) I'm thinking about selling. Would anyone possibly be interested? I can put up a list soon if anyone might be inte