gue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> No responses about the new Star Wars movie, I mean, Story??</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually going to see that tomorrow, so I hope it's good.<br /> <br /> I did catch Dr. Strange a while back. It was a good movie, but I have a feeling the inevitable sequel would best be served by moving away from the action movie formula and going full psychedelic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T16:11:30-08:00","id":1019472,"title":"","content":"I saw RWD the other night. Interesting sci-fi horror movie. Found footage but done well, basically the ideal of found footage.<br /> <br /> Saw Morgan, too. Definitely a good movie, but I don't think Kate Mara pulled off the 'cold and distant' aspect of her character at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T18:25:14-08:00","id":1019537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1019325#post1019325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, did we all just stop going to the movies or something?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> No responses about the new Star Wars movie, I mean, Story??</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved it. Best Star Wars movie outside of the original trilogy so far, in my opinion. Maybe not a <i>tremendously</i> high bar, but it continues to inspire confidence in the brand outside of Lucas's hands. I've said before that Force Awakens was exactly what it needed to be to prove to the fans that they could return to form. Well, Rogue One was exactly what it needed to be to prove that they could make a good Star Wars movie without retreading the same plot. Can't wait to see where they go from here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T08:05:07-08:00","id":1019777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1019537#post1019537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I loved it. Best Star Wars movie outside of the original trilogy so far, in my opinion. Maybe not a <i>tremendously</i> high bar, but it continues to inspire confidence in the brand outside of Lucas's hands. I've said before that Force Awakens was exactly what it needed to be to prove to the fans that they could return to form. Well, Rogue One was exactly what it needed to be to prove that they could make a good Star Wars movie without retreading the same plot. Can't wait to see where they go from here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My only issue is:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> I want more movies about the Rogue One characters, but they killed them all! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I respect the writers for being ballsy enough to kill the characters, but I want to see them go on more adventures. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T08:26:16-08:00","id":1019783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1019777#post1019777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My only issue is:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> I want more movies about the Rogue One characters, but they killed them all! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I respect the writers for being ballsy enough to kill the characters, but I want to see them go on more adventures. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>You know what it reminds me of a lot, actually, is<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Halo Reach. Another brilliantly done prequel with a diverse cast of rag-tag heroes who give their lives to deliver an important message to the main series characters, without which the series couldn't have happened.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T09:06:57-08:00","id":1019807,"title":"","content":"Oh, I also love that it made the whole &quot;blow up the Death Star button&quot; make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T11:42:59-08:00","id":1019874,"title":"","content":"Just saw Rogue One a few minutes ago myself. Loved it! Right proper war movie, Star Wars style.<br /> <br /> I found the scene with Saw's Partisans attacking an Imperial patrol to be particularly intriguing: made them feel a whole lot like third-world insurgents, as opposed to the Alliance's more polished military.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T11:48:13-08:00","id":1019882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1019874#post1019874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just saw Rogue One a few minutes ago myself. Loved it! Right proper war movie, Star Wars style.<br /> <br /> I found the scene with Saw's Partisans attacking an Imperial patrol to be particularly intriguing: made them feel a whole lot like third-world insurgents, as opposed to the Alliance's more polished military.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was a really nice touch. Lest we forget, the Empire is a functioning (if tyrannical) government. The Rebels are terrorists. It's cool to see them presented in a less than glowing light. I also loved the argument about following orders. Dare I hope it could foreshadow a bit more complexity being revealed in the main series conflict beyond &quot;First Order Bad, Resistance Good&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T12:13:11-08:00","id":1019898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1019882#post1019882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that was a really nice touch. Lest we forget, the Empire is a functioning (if tyrannical) government. The Rebels are terrorists. It's cool to see them presented in a less than glowing light. I also loved the argument about following orders. Dare I hope it could foreshadow a bit more complexity being revealed in the main series conflict beyond &quot;First Order Bad, Resistance Good&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an entire galaxy full of moral grey to explore when you think about the implications of what it took to take down an interstellar empire.<br /> <br /> &quot;He's a ruthless, black-hearted crimelord with a rap sheet a mile wide... but we can't bring him to justice because the rebellion needed his assistance and we promised him amnesty after we won. Sorry.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, Bail Morgan and his Ironheart cell are heroes. Yes, they've taken down some of the worst war criminals in history, and were instrumental in liberating entire <i>sectors</i>. But he and his men have <i>no</i> right to claim that world for refugees from their home. That planet was promised to others. They've broken our laws, and so... we must do what is <i>necessary</i>. Bring them in, dead or alive.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;There's nothing we can do, do you hear me? Nothing! Etrium's support was critical for securing the Hydian Way hyperspace route, and they demanded concessions from the Alliance government for their support. As despicable as the idea of slavery is to you, it is a part of their culture and we must respect it! So <b>STAND</b>. <b>DOWN</b>.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T05:48:19-08:00","id":1020839,"title":"","content":"So, anything worthwhile this holiday season that isn't butchered romance masquerading as sci-fi (Passengers), or milking the nostalgia cow (Rouge One)? I'll obviously go see Silence the minute it comes out, but I found nothing else interesting listed in all of London.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T06:24:21-08:00","id":1020849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1020839#post1020839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, anything worthwhile this holiday season that isn't butchered romance masquerading as sci-fi (Passengers), or milking the nostalgia cow (Rouge One)? I'll obviously go see Silence the minute it comes out, but I found nothing else interesting listed in all of London.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Have you not yet seen Arrival or Moana? Also Sing looks good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T06:32:06-08:00","id":1020851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1020849#post1020849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Have you not yet seen Arrival or Moana? .</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly recommend Arrival. If you aren't too nitpicky about psuedoscience, it is a great Sci-Fi movie about language. <br /> <br /> I am planning on seeing Moana over the Holidays, so I can't get a personal recommendation. I hear it's good though. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T07:15:00-08:00","id":1020865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1020851#post1020851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am planning on seeing Moana over the Holidays, so I can't get a personal recommendation. I hear it's good though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's flippin' amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T07:19:56-08:00","id":1020868,"title":"","content":"Oh, I saw Arrival. It was quite funny, as it was me (a physicist), and my friend (a linguist) seeing it. I had some issues with it (the ending, and the end resolution of the language plot), but overall, it was very solid and well shot. It was an actual moving picture, not a radio play with visuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T09:36:55-08:00","id":1020925,"title":"","content":"The Autopsy of Jane Doe was great. Very well done, such a small cast too. I thought it was going to be a knock-off of the Corpse of Anna Fritz, another great movie, but no.<br /> <br /> Been looking forward to Moana. My kid likes CGI movies but he doesn't seem to like Dreamworks as much, and he hates people singing so he's never going to see Sing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T16:04:24-08:00","id":1021421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1019874#post1019874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just saw Rogue One a few minutes ago myself. Loved it! Right proper war movie, Star Wars style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saw it twice last weekend! Loved it!! I thought it was a great addition to the franchise! Can't wait to see it a few more times...and especially to watch episode 4 right after! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T21:11:52-08:00","id":1021468,"title":"","content":"Rogue One was fine to me. Other than that though, I felt that the film never really raised above just good through most of it and I think that's because the characters and plot are just satisfactory at best. The main characters are all archetypes; the reluctant rebel who realizes she can\u2019t run away from the galaxy\u2019s problems, the commander who has to do morally questionable things, the wise and spiritual monk, the cynical solider that learns that there is still hope, the comedy relief robot. All the actors do their job and none of these characters can be called bad or cringe-inducing, but beyond those archetypes they are paper-thin without much in the way of interesting interpersonal relationships or conflicts. Even the main female lead Jyn is ultimately just fine, with her relationship with her father, which I imagine is supposed to be the emotional heart of the film, being far too predictable. You probably already know everything that is going to happen with her character arc.<br /> <br /> In regard to the plot, well, just think about the film you expected to see after watching the trailers and think about basic war film plots that you\u2019ve seen hundred times before. Yeah, whatever you were imagining is exactly what you\u2019ve get in Rogue One. The hope speeches, the last-minute saves, the heroic sacrifices, and tear-jerking moments all come when you\u2019d expect them too. Even the supposed darker elements and atmosphere is average Hollywood fare. If you are a veteran of Walking Dead or Game of Thrones you\u2019re going to be very unimpressed by the \u201cdarker\u201d elements of this film. That all being said, the last third gives has an action set piece that is just mind-blowing. This is the best space battles we've have ever seen in a Star Wars film. Period. Seriously, the last action third is worth the price of admission alone. Episode 8 is going to have to go all out to beat it. Oh, there\u2019s also two CG lookalikes in this film. I\u2019ve heard people complain about them but I thought they looked fine.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, to sum it all up this is a good Star Wars film with great action and visual aesthetics but lackluster plot and characters. Go see it for the holidays but don\u2019t expect to see genius filmmaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T21:26:17-08:00","id":1021469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1019882#post1019882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that was a really nice touch. Lest we forget, the Empire is a functioning (if tyrannical) government. The Rebels are terrorists. It's cool to see them presented in a less than glowing light. I also loved the argument about following orders. Dare I hope it could foreshadow a bit more complexity being revealed in the main series conflict beyond &quot;First Order Bad, Resistance Good&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt that's going to happen with EP 8. I mean, how could it? A morally grey conflict, at least in my opinion, requires that both sides to be sympathetic. The First Order has already committed five counts of genocide in EP 7 and has been flat out compared by Abrams as a fusion of the Nazis that fled to Argentina and ISIL. Pretty hard to feel anything but loathing for such a group, but I guess anything is possible. Personally I was felt that Star Wars Good vs Evil nature was fine so as long as the good guys were interesting and the bad guys were threatening.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T22:16:33-08:00","id":1021476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1021469#post1021469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt that's going to happen with EP 8. I mean, how could it? A morally grey conflict, at least in my opinion, requires that both sides to be sympathetic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to have to disagree with you there. Just because one side of a conflict is unambiguously bad doesn't mean there can't be depth to the conflict - look at the Pentacle vs. the Seers in Awakening. In Rogue One we see the Rebel Alliance not as the paragon of goodness and hope they're made out to be in IV, V, and VI, but as the lesser of two evils. Heck, the empire is an obvious metaphor for the Nazi party (their soldiers are even called storm troopers) and we are fully aware that they are evil, but you can't deny that they are a force of stability in the galaxy, morally indefensible though they may be. The rebels are a disorganized band of terrorists who want to destroy the existing galactic government without agreeing on how they're going to replace it, and we see that their soldiers are just as much &quot;people following orders&quot; as the imperial soldiers are. You still want to side with them because again, lesser of two evils, but you get to see that it's not as simple as the good guys vs. the bad guys. And it would be cool to see more of that complexity in episodes VIII and IX.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T22:52:35-08:00","id":1021481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1021476#post1021476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rebels are a disorganized band of terrorists who want to destroy the existing galactic government without agreeing on how they're going to replace it, and we see that their soldiers are just as much &quot;people following orders&quot; as the imperial soldiers are. You still want to side with them because again, lesser of two evils, but you get to see that it's not as simple as the good guys vs. the bad guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that message is pretty clear. Saw's guys on Jedha are more than happy to inflict lots of collateral damage, for example. Captain Luna basically comes out and says 'we have all done a lot of bad stuff' when he rounds up the volunteers for the Scarif mission. These aren't choirboys, just desperate men and women fighting a very asymmetrical war. <br /> <br /> And you want to root for them because they are cool and heroic and fun (looking at you, K-2SO). But that doesn't mean they are necessarily <i>good. </i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T12:10:31-08:00","id":1021640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1021476#post1021476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rebels are a disorganized band of terrorists who want to destroy the existing galactic government without agreeing on <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>how they're going to replace it</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>With a Republic, like they had BEFORE the Empire? Palpatine created the Empire by starting a war that was basically one gigantic &quot;false flag&quot; operation. Nothing stable about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T12:46:06-08:00","id":1021649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1021476#post1021476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to have to disagree with you there. Just because one side of a conflict is unambiguously bad doesn't mean there can't be depth to the conflict - look at the Pentacle vs. the Seers in Awakening. In Rogue One we see the Rebel Alliance not as the paragon of goodness and hope they're made out to be in IV, V, and VI, but as the lesser of two evils. Heck, the empire is an obvious metaphor for the Nazi party (their soldiers are even called storm troopers) and we are fully aware that they are evil, but you can't deny that they are a force of stability in the galaxy, morally indefensible though they may be. The rebels are a disorganized band of terrorists who want to destroy the existing galactic government without agreeing on how they're going to replace it, and we see that their soldiers are just as much &quot;people following orders&quot; as the imperial soldiers are. You still want to side with them because again, lesser of two evils, but you get to see that it's not as simple as the good guys vs. the bad guys. And it would be cool to see more of that complexity in episodes VIII and IX.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose your right. It's just that even in Rogue One I couldn't help but think that sure the Rebel Alliance did bad things but at least their mildly apologetic about it and are not literally Space-Nazis. Even the idea of lesser of two evils lose is its punch to me when one side is Blackier than Black Evil. Plus, the Empire's stability and order seems pretty bankrupt when you consider that only old white British man seem to have any power and that its leader is pretty much pure evil. Order is worth nothing when freedom and social mobility is non-existent.<br /> <br /> Chances are the only real complexity were going to see in the sequel trilogy is Rey going to the dark side and/or finding out that Han and Leia really were crappy parents. We'll see in a year, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T12:47:14-08:00","id":1021650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1021640#post1021640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With a Republic, like they had BEFORE the Empire?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Some</i> of the rebels want a republic, and we see from VII that that's what they end up instituting. But you can tell from Rogue One that they are an extremely disorganized force who can't agree on anything, even whether or not to go after the Death Star plans or to disband after they learn that the Death Star is completed. Not to mention the fact that the Rebel Alliance are clearly not the only group of violent anti-imperialists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1021640#post1021640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Palpatine created the Empire by starting a war that was basically one gigantic &amp;quot;false flag&amp;quot; operation. Nothing stable about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>He had the near universal support of the senate in his movement to re-organize the republic into an empire. And as soon as the movement was successful, he <i>immediately</i> wiped out the entire separatist movement. Nevermind that he instigated and empowered them in the first place, his gambit still resulted in an empire that was stable as <i>fuck</i>. That doesn't mean they're <i>good</i>, it just means they're orderly in their evildoing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T13:38:18-08:00","id":1021670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1021650#post1021650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Some</i> of the rebels want a republic, and we see from VII that that's what they end up instituting. But you can tell from Rogue One that they are an extremely disorganized force who can't agree on anything, even whether or not to go after the Death Star plans or to disband after they learn that the Death Star is completed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's part of democracy; people disagreeing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He had the near universal support of the senate in his movement to re-organize the republic into an empire. And as soon as the movement was successful, he <i>immediately</i> wiped out the entire separatist movement. Nevermind that he instigated and empowered them in the first place, his gambit still resulted in an empire that was stable as <i>fuck</i>. That doesn't mean they're <i>good</i>, it just means they're orderly in their evildoing. </div> </div> </div>A cackling madman who would instigate a galaxy-wide conflict in his quest for power may be organized, but he is NOT stable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T13:54:33-08:00","id":1021677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1021670#post1021670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's part of democracy; people disagreeing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes it is... This doesn't change the fact that the rebel alliance is organized around the idea of &quot;down with the empire&quot; without agreeing on what to replace it with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1021670#post1021670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A cackling madman who would instigate a galaxy-wide conflict in his quest for power may be organized, but he is NOT stable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said Palpatine was mentally stable. I said the empire was a stable government. A horrible, tyrannical, fascist, but stable, dictatorship.<br /> <br /> Fuck, they built a space station the size of a goddamn moon. Twice. That kind of production doesn't come from an unstable civilization. Can you imagine how badly blowing it up fucked the galactic economy? How many trillions of credits of damage it did, how many jobs, how many lives were lost because of it? The empire is unambiguously evil, but stable. The rebels are unambiguously good, but unstable. And we have a morally complex conflict without needing both sides to be sympathetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-24-2016, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T14:26:36-08:00","id":1021689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1021677#post1021677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rebels are unambiguously good, but unstable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, trying to take down an oppressive force can be good, but leaving an entire galaxy in shambles and chaos isn't exactly unambiguously good. If they were going to be completely good, there would have to be some backup to that. And as we see from Force Awakens, just destroying the Empire doesn't seem to improve life in the galaxy, there's still people basically being slaves on desert planets, there doesn't seem to be any infrastructure or factories, there's space pirates and space poachers or whatever the groups hassling Han were about.<br /> <br /> Also it seems more like the Empire itself isn't unambiguously evil, though the leader and a lot of his top men were. They seem to be just doing a job and viewing the goals of the Empire more important than the goals of other groups.<br /> <br /> But to be fair I've not seen Rogue One yet. And people have vastly different perspectives on what they consider good or evil.<br /> <br /> Perhaps further Star Wars discussions could merit their own thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-24-2016, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T15:01:39-08:00","id":1021716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1021689#post1021689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also it seems more like the Empire itself isn't unambiguously evil, though the leader and a lot of his top men were. They seem to be just doing a job and viewing the goals of the Empire more important than the goals of other groups.<br /> <br /> But to be fair I've not seen Rogue One yet. And people have vastly different perspectives on what they consider good or evil.<br /> <br /> Perhaps further Star Wars discussions could merit their own thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, nofather. If just doing your job means destroying an entire civilization you're probably evil by apathy. Pretty sure most of the free world was decided that just following orders isn't a good excuse for genocide.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T15:08:49-08:00","id":1021720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1021677#post1021677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fuck, they built a space station the size of a goddamn moon. Twice. That kind of production doesn't come from an unstable civilization. Can you imagine how badly blowing it up fucked the galactic economy? How many trillions of credits of damage it did, how many jobs, how many lives were lost because of it? The empire is unambiguously evil, but stable. The rebels are unambiguously good, but unstable. And we have a morally complex conflict without needing both sides to be sympathetic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sort of thing wouldn't have been a problem if they didn't think that building superweapons was a great idea, which was a thing they were developing even before the Rebellion was formed. Also, I've read the new canon Star Wars Novel Bloodline (it was real good!) and it outright states that the Death Star was made by planet-wide slave labor. So you don't have to worry about jobs lost.<br /> <br /> Pretty shitty thing to do but at least the Empire was stable, right?<br /> <br /> Hope that this doesn't come across as to antagonist, but I just don't think the Empire's supposed stability makes it any less Evil, even it is only Lawful Evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T15:15:48-08:00","id":1021721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1021716#post1021716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, nofather. If just doing your job means destroying an entire civilization you're probably evil by apathy. Pretty sure most of the free world was decided that just following orders isn't a good excuse for genocide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure the free world has also decided that being a plucky group of rogues and outcasts isn't a good excuse for killing millions and destroying civilization either.<br /> <br /> And as I pointed out, the Empire is civilization. Yes, it's ugly at times and has nasty thorns. But without it, everyone's wearing robes stolen from the corpses of others and only the rich and merciless thrive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I've read the new canon Star Wars Novel Bloodline (it was real good!) and it outright states that the Death Star was made by planet-wide slave labor. So you don't have to worry about jobs lost. </div> </div> </div>Even if that were the case, though it sounds fantastic in the extreme, there's still jobs in preparing or transporting food for your planet worth of slaves, of transporting them, of making sure these slaves know how to build high-tech Death Star machinery and circuitry and you would have to have at least someone do checks of their work. And that just means that when the rebels blew up the second Death Star they weren't killing people employed by the Empire, they were killing a planet worth of slaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-24-2016, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T17:35:35-08:00","id":1021753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally 