-movies?p=1022150#post1022150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently a lot of the Republic senators were given heavy donations by the First Order, so that they would look the other way or denounce Leia's outcry over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder what they're going to do with Episode VIII now? What with Cassie Fisher's recent passing, are they going to write Leia out of it? Or will they do the same sort of thing they did with Tarkin in Rogue One?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T12:36:09-08:00","id":1022900,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine they'd CGI her in and write a reason for her not to appear much, like she's tending to administrative duties or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T14:22:08-08:00","id":1022949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1022858#post1022858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what they're going to do with Episode VIII now? What with Cassie Fisher's recent passing, are they going to write Leia out of it? Or will they do the same sort of thing they did with Tarkin in Rogue One?</div> </div> </div> </div>Episode 8 wrapped up filming back in July and is currently in the post-production phase, so no need to worry about Carrie Fisher's death affecting that movie at all. She had already finished filming all her scenes in the movie quite a while back. It will be interesting to see what they do for Episode 9 though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T20:49:42-08:00","id":1023092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1022949#post1022949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Episode 8 wrapped up filming back in July and is currently in the post-production phase, so no need to worry about Carrie Fisher's death affecting that movie at all. She had already finished filming all her scenes in the movie quite a while back. It will be interesting to see what they do for Episode 9 though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I heard she finished shooting all her material for Episode VIII. I was very sad to hear about her today. :'(","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T07:35:56-08:00","id":1028541,"title":"","content":"Underworld: Blood Wars was really good. I was very skeptical going in, because the last one was pretty &quot;meh,&quot; but this was one entertaining. Action was good, special effects were good, the acting was...what you'd expect.<br /> <br /> Just a fun, leave your brain at the door, entertaining vampire/werewolf flick.<br /> <br /> Few notes:<br /> <br /> 1. Selene is more of a Ventrue than a Toreador to me.<br /> 2. The Werewolves are all Bone Gnawers.<br /> 3. Lara Pulver(Semira) is hot as hell. Never heard of her before, but dammit if I'm not following her career now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T04:16:15-08:00","id":1028957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1028541#post1028541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Underworld: Blood Wars was really good. I was very skeptical going in, because the last one was pretty &quot;meh,&quot; but this was one entertaining. Action was good, special effects were good, the acting was...what you'd expect.<br /> <br /> Just a fun, leave your brain at the door, entertaining vampire/werewolf flick.<br /> <br /> Few notes:<br /> <br /> 1. Selene is more of a Ventrue than a Toreador to me.<br /> 2. The Werewolves are all Bone Gnawers.<br /> 3. Lara Pulver(Semira) is hot as hell. Never heard of her before, but dammit if I'm not following her career now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I saw it yesterday and thought it was ok. Fit in with the rest of the series...<br /> <br /> There were a few times I wondered where the budget went, just because it looked like they skimped on a few things, then they had the big effects with the sword(you know what I'm talking about) and then I went &quot;ohhh...thats where it went&quot;. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T06:39:34-08:00","id":1029016,"title":"","content":"Saw Hidden Figures yesterday. Great film. Fantastic period piece.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:15:36-08:00","id":1029040,"title":"","content":"Just watched the Girl King. It was a deliciously weird costume drama with lesbians. So it was definitely time well spent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:17:02-08:00","id":1029041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1022949#post1022949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Episode 8 wrapped up filming back in July and is currently in the post-production phase, so no need to worry about Carrie Fisher's death affecting that movie at all. She had already finished filming all her scenes in the movie quite a while back. It will be interesting to see what they do for Episode 9 though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Off-scene death, I imagine. Then again with CGI Tarkin in Rogue One anything is possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T20:28:56-08:00","id":1057423,"title":"","content":"Logan was so, SO good.<br /> <br /> It was everything I wanted in a Wolverine movie and then some. <br /> <br /> Fuck. I would kill for a television series starring some of the characters. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T22:47:01-08:00","id":1057471,"title":"","content":"I finally watched The Nice Guys after missing it in theaters and absolutely loved it. The whole thing basically felt like a brilliant Fiasco playset being played on screen, and it managed to make me hate Ryan Gosling a little bit less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T13:24:34-08:00","id":1058125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1057423#post1057423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Logan was so, SO good.<br /> <br /> It was everything I wanted in a Wolverine movie and then some.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally with you! Two words: Bezerker Rage!<br /> <br /> I thought it was a great send off for Hugh Jackmans version of the character. He's really done the character justice(X-Men Origins Wolverine aside). It was dark, brutal, and a little depressing...which is probably how it should be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1057471#post1057471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I finally watched The Nice Guys after missing it in theaters and absolutely loved it. The whole thing basically felt like a brilliant Fiasco playset being played on screen, and it managed to make me hate Ryan Gosling a little bit less.</div> </div> </div> </div>Watched it when it came out and highly enjoyed it!!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T07:07:33-08:00","id":1060501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1058125#post1058125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally with you!</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'm worried that D.C. will continue in its fantastical streak of failures to understand what makes a good movie good, and try to ride the coattails of <i>Logan</i>'s success. <br /> <br /> I predict a depressingly-grimdark <i>Lobo</i> movie set in the dystopian future.<br /> <br /> ___________<br /> <br /> In unrelated news, is anyone else annoyed at Disney's revelation that <b>LeFou</b> will be their first openly gay character in the upcoming <i>Beauty and the Beast</i>? Not because inclusivity is terrible or something - being inclusive is great! - but because <i>no, Disney, you are not in fact breaking new ground by having a gay villain or gay comic relief or gay comic relief villain</i>.<br /> <br /> Yes, Disney <i>is</i> due for an LGBT character to stand in the spotlight - in fact, it's <i>over</i>due. But deciding to have the representative for gays in the Disney universe be an obnoxious little troll (who plays the part of worshipful lackey to a pompous, illiterate misogynyst who doesn't know when to stop working out), a character whose name literally means &quot;The Fool,&quot; that's a fucking <i>mistake</i>.<br /> <br /> (Honestly, having him be attracted to Gaston <i>does</i> feel sensible, though - I suppose I'd be more down with it if LeFou wasn't the <i>only</i> such character mentioned. LGBT characters have been the villains or comic relief of movies for as long as they've been <i>in</i> movies.)<br /> <br /> Incidentally, Disney really missed their chance at having their first LGBT character in the part of Marlin in <i>Finding Nemo</i>. Clownfish naturally change sex based on the needs of their group, with the largest being the female, and the next largest becoming female should the worst happen. <i>Finding Nemo</i> <b>could</b> have been the story of a fish finding allies to support her in her transition while on a search for her son.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-10-2017, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T19:58:19-07:00","id":1063727,"title":"","content":"Well, saw <i>Beauty and the Beast</i>.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The supposed explicit gay moment for Josh Gadd's LeFou? It's about three seconds of <i>dancing with another man and smiling prior to the closing credits</i>. Scandalous!<br /> <br /> How does briefly having a male dance partner in a ballroom-type dance make you gay? Also, it wasn't like LeFou cut in so he could dance with this guy - it was the other way around.<br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> appreciate that he's rather less villainous than his cartoon counterpart, raising objections to Gaston when Gaston wants to throw Maurice to the wolves; in fact, he even switches sides after Gaston betrays him. <br /> <br /> And there <i>is</i> a lot of gay <i>subtext</i> in the movie, mind - LeFou spends a lot of time admiring Gaston and making excuses for why he's still a bachelor, and Josh Gadd does a good job bringing that across.<br /> <br /> But hey, enough about LeFou being gay; the director made a point of saying how tired he is of being badgered about it, and hey, aren't all these interracial couples worth mention? Well, okay, then - I can't help but notice, Mr. Director, that they all seem to be white men and black women, and not the other way around. But to be fair, I only just got out of the movie, my first time seeing it, and I wasn't particularly keeping my eyes peeled for interracial couples, so I might have missed one.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, it's a pretty good movie, and they fixed quite a few of the plot holes of the original. I just wish they'd handled the spoilered elements a little better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-17-2017, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T23:07:38-07:00","id":1063753,"title":"","content":"I saw John Wick 1 and 2 recently. I enjoyed them, not high art or feel-good summer blockbusters, but they had great action.<br /> <br /> Aaaannnnddd I'm watching Band of Brothers. Again. Seriously, Spielberg has me on lockdown.<br /> <br /> Possibly going to see Logan and Kong when(if) I recover from my latest illness*.<br /> <br /> *What even <i>is</i> this Winter? Jeez!*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T13:09:34-07:00","id":1064446,"title":"","content":"5 episodes into Iron Fist on Netflix and I'm loving it. I'm a pretty big Iron Fist fan, and I wasn't exactly enamored with the choice of Finn Jones(I wanted someone more athletic), but I think he's done a decent job. Fight choreography is hit or miss, but I'm enjoying it. More than Luke Cage, which I found to get boring after a few episodes, and Jessica Jones, who I watched and enjoyed only for the Purple Man who was a fantastic villain. <br /> <br /> Daredevil is still king to me, in the Netflix Marvel area. Especially the fantastic season 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T00:41:08-07:00","id":1064676,"title":"","content":"Ethan Embry out of nowhere!<br /> <br /> I just saw <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt4935372/\" target=\"_blank\">the Devil's Candy</a> on Amazon and man is it good. Chilling and brutal, found out it was written and directed by the same guy who made the Loved Ones, which doesn't surprise me a bit, that was also a great movie. There's some heavy religious undertones, that's partly what the movie is about, but it doesn't get preachy. Ethan Embry plays a Rob Zombie-esque painter who's a great husband and father, even if he struggles to support the family financially, and the close family moves to a house out in the country only somewhat recently evacuated by a mentally disturbed man who lost his parents, played excellently by Pruitt Taylor Vince. He's a 'that guy' and even if the name isn't familiar everyone's seen him, IMDB shows him with 100 acting credits and that's counting individual shows and movies not each appearance. Something seems to be influencing Vince's character, Ray, and it starts influencing Embry's character, Jesse. There's some definite Amityville vibes at first but it dovetails with, I suppose, some Exorcist 3 or something, I can't pin the other one down. It's pretty unique, and I was not expecting it to be as good as it was, or as thrilling. I think they really balanced the moods throughout the movie well, which served to keep the ending up in the air better.<br /> <br /> Also, I saw <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt3904278/\" target=\"_blank\">We Go On</a> a while ago and that was also very good, very memorable. Main character is a man who, gripped with fear of dying, offers a bounty in the newspaper for anyone who can show him some tangible evidence of life after death. He narrows the responses down to three possibilities and the first half of the movie is about him seeking them out. That part of the journey is pretty pat, though well handled. The rest is pleasantly surprising. I don't know who the main character was played by, but his mom features prominently in it, having raised him alone for most of his life and figuring he needs to be watched over so he doesn't get taken advantage of in his mission. She was played by the actress who played Martha Kent on Smallville, and one of the first people the protagonist goes to see was a professor, played by John Glover, who played Lex Luthor's father Lionel in Smallville. Was interesting seeing them together again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-19-2017, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T19:55:58-07:00","id":1067330,"title":"","content":"Just saw the new <i>Power Rangers</i>.<br /> <br /> Spoilers, for something that happens in the first five minutes.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Does TV Tropes have a page yet for &quot;a character tries to milk what he thinks is a cow, but it's actually a bull?&quot; I did like three searches just now and didn't find it. <br /> <br /> Truth be told, I'm getting fed up with this weird and overly specific animal-masturbation joke.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T20:26:33-07:00","id":1067346,"title":"","content":"Do they add Tropes anymore or is it just commenting on existing ones? I was looking for something representing the 'make a protagonist choose between letting villain go or letting someone die' trope and was surprised not to see it, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T05:25:00-07:00","id":1067511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1067346#post1067346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they add Tropes anymore or is it just commenting on existing ones? I was looking for something representing the 'make a protagonist choose between letting villain go or letting someone die' trope and was surprised not to see it, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>New tropes are added as they're approved, but I was just trying to make sure one way before the other before I suggested it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T08:29:04-07:00","id":1067608,"title":"","content":"So! I finally watched the new Ghostbusters movie on Monday.<br /> <br /> The pacing and style was of course *way* different from the first one.<br /> <br /> Generally I'd say it was a good/decent movie. Not great. Not something that's gonna have the staying power of the original, but good. Overall? I'd honestly rate it around about Ghostbusters 2 level, maybe slightly lower.<br /> <br /> On the negative side:<br /> <br /> With all the bloody cameos and endless original referencing it felt like the writers were trying to give the original a tongue bath while they hugged close their Original Ghostbusters body pillows, moaning sweet nothings to themselves.<br /> <br /> Some of the characters needed better rounding/background. The subway worker for example, she's filling in the Local Area Knowledge Expert role, but if it was mentioned WHY she had all that information it was a brief one-shot that I missed.<br /> <br /> On the positive side:<br /> <br /> I *much* prefer the presentation of tech progress in this one over the original. in the original it's just &quot;hey we scanned a ghost, now we can build all these weapons ideally suited to combat them!&quot;, but in this one you get a lot more &quot;yeah, this stuff is work in progress&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Engineer character/actor was spot on. 9/10, would want as a crazy engineer in any movie. Also several of us commented that if they remade Tank Girl she'd be perfect for the role.<br /> <br /> On the general side:<br /> <br /> The style is very different. With the exception of Venkman in the original, everything was &quot;straight&quot; humour... meaning they were playing the characters straight and the humour was part of that deadpan delivery, where as in this one it's MUCH more self-aware humour and jokes. If this is better or worse is purely a subjective and personal thing, and in my case at least can vary on mood at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T11:41:51-07:00","id":1067713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1067511#post1067511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New tropes are added as they're approved, but I was just trying to make sure one way before the other before I suggested it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/SadisticChoice\" target=\"_blank\">Sadistic Choice</a> trope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T08:11:47-07:00","id":1068012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1067608#post1067608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So! I finally watched the new Ghostbusters movie on Monday.<br /> <br /> The pacing and style was of course *way* different from the first one.<br /> <br /> Generally I'd say it was a good/decent movie. Not great. Not something that's gonna have the staying power of the original, but good. Overall? I'd honestly rate it around about Ghostbusters 2 level, maybe slightly lower.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd definitely rate it below Ghostbusters 2... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1067608#post1067608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the negative side:<br /> <br /> With all the bloody cameos and endless original referencing it felt like the writers were trying to give the original a tongue bath while they hugged close their Original Ghostbusters body pillows, moaning sweet nothings to themselves.<br /> <br /> Some of the characters needed better rounding/background. The subway worker for example, she's filling in the Local Area Knowledge Expert role, but if it was mentioned WHY she had all that information it was a brief one-shot that I missed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally with you. Plus, I hated Chris Hemsworth character. No one that stupid could live. He was very annoying...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1067608#post1067608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the positive side:<br /> <br /> I *much* prefer the presentation of tech progress in this one over the original. in the original it's just &quot;hey we scanned a ghost, now we can build all these weapons ideally suited to combat them!&quot;, but in this one you get a lot more &quot;yeah, this stuff is work in progress&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Engineer character/actor was spot on. 9/10, would want as a crazy engineer in any movie. Also several of us commented that if they remade Tank Girl she'd be perfect for the role.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally with you on this as well! The work-in-progress feel of the tech was great(even if some of the scenes of them testing it were dumb). And I really liked Kate McKinnon's character, she was great! And oh yea, if they remade Tank Girl I think she could pull it off!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T14:48:20-07:00","id":1069638,"title":"","content":"Just rewatched midnight Son for the first time in years - still a great movie","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1440,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","user":"LordOfAsh","date":". 03-29-2017, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T21:34:24-07:00","id":1071032,"title":"","content":"The New Ghost in the Shell is pretty good, it drifts away from the base material at points but over all its a solid flick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T15:51:11-07:00","id":1072226,"title":"","content":"Is it wrong that the new trailer for The Mummy gave me high hopes? Because I want so much for it to be a good movie that my judgment might be impaired, but I honestly liked that trailer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T17:01:52-07:00","id":1072250,"title":"","content":"Saw the new Ghost in the Shell. I liked it a lot!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T18:23:08-07:00","id":1072284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1072226#post1072226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it wrong that the new trailer for The Mummy gave me high hopes? Because I want so much for it to be a good movie that my judgment might be impaired, but I honestly liked that trailer</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I just saw the trailer, the movie looks like it'll be great for what it is. I don't have any particular investment in saying so, though I am a Tom Cruise fan. I wouldn't expect any soul-moving moments that will change your life but in terms of a supernatural action movie? Definitely going to be good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T06:13:04-07:00","id":1072479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1072284#post1072284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. I just saw the trailer, the movie looks like it'll be great for what it is. I don't have any particular investment in saying so, though I am a Tom Cruise fan. I wouldn't expect any soul-moving moments that will change your life but in terms of a supernatural action movie? Definitely going to be good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, this means I'm not alone on this. My friends strongly disagree with me as they would rather have a new Brendan Fraser's Mummy and are not giving this a chance. I sure will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T07:31:58-07:00","id":1072519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1072226#post1072226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it wrong that the new trailer for The Mummy gave me high hopes? Because I want so much for it to be a good movie that my judgment might be impaired, but I honestly liked that trailer</div> </div> </div> </div>I also liked the new trailer, especially because it makes it seem like more of a straight up horror movie than a generic action-adventure (the use of &quot;Paint it Black&quot; definitely helped). The Brendan Fraser Mummy movies were great for what they were, which is pulpy, witty action movies, and they didn't really pretend to be anything else. This is still ignoring that Imhotep was a charismatic villain with really great presence. Also, the actress they have playing Ahmanet was the best part of Star Trek Beyond, so I have no problem watching just to see more of her being awesome.<br /> <br /> Not sure if I'm sold on the &quot;Universal Monsters Universe&quot; concept, I'll probably pretend Russell Crowe isn't Dr. Henry Jeckyll and is instead a stand-in for the Museum Director in the first Brendan Fraser Mummy movie, but I'll probably watch it just for the atmosphere they seem to have going. It feels very <b>Mummy: The Curse</b> with a Deceived protagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T12:14:56-07:00","id":1072648,"title":"","content":"I'm a big dork when it comes to Universal Monsters, as they're a relevant part of my childhood. So while I'm not exactly sold with the concept of Marvel-style shared universe, I do hope they're gonna do it well. The mature, educated and jaded part of me is doubtful. The kid part just wants to see more movies about them. So it's a &quot;fingers crossed&quot; situation for me.<br /> <br /> Ahmanet looks great. I liked her actress both in Kingsman and Star Trek and I too will look forward for it to gather some <b>Mummy: The Curse</b>'s visuals and atmosphere. You know you're a fan when you start to look at all monsters in terms of CoD splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T17:35:48-07:00","id":1072810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1072648#post1072648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a big dork when it comes to Universal Monsters, as they're a relevant part of my childhood. So while I'm not exactly sold with the concept of Marvel-style shared universe, I do hope they're gonna do it well. The mature, educated and jaded part of me is doubtful. The kid part just wants to see more movies about them. So it's a &quot;fingers crossed&quot; situation for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can't be much worse than that Van Helsing movie with Hugh Jackman that recently came out.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* Recently. I just looked and it came out 13 years ago, back in 2004. Wow. Time flies, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T17:49:14-07:00","id":1072816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1072810#post1072810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It can't be much worse than that Van Helsing movie with Hugh Jackman that recently came out.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* Recently. I just looked and it came out 13 years ago, back in 2004. Wow. Time flies, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>13?!<br /> <br /> Excuse me as I have an epiphany about time and getting old.<br /> <br /> Ahem.<br /> <br /> No, I guess not. As far as attempts at a shared universe go, that one was not exactly without issues. It had its perks but boy, I sure can't look at it in the same way I did when I was thirteen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T23:14:42-07:00","id":1091834,"title":"","content":"Finally just saw Get Out, thank you, Amazon. Excellent horror flick, hit all the right beats, great writing and acting. I think making it about <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">mind control, at least in part</div></div> </div> </div> made a lot of sense and gave it a lot more impact than using some other plot device. Nice to see Daniel Kaluuya in something else, too, he was fun as Tealeaf in Psychoville, very sad what happened to his character. Pleasant surprise to see Stephen Root, too, he's in so much though.<br /> <br /> Think the whole 'meeting the parents' thing was a great choice, reminded me of You're Next and, obviously, the awkwardness is tilted for comedy in Meet the Parents. I still remember going to see my wife's parents in this small town in the country. We went out to the movies one day and I couldn't get the thought, 'The Innsmouth Look' out of my head. Everyone was pale, flabby-skinned, with small, thin heads and bulging eyes. Creepy as hell. Apparently one of the towns claims to fame was that the Siamese Twins lived there and, apparently, really got around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T19:23:24-07:00","id":1097665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1096800-lunar-the-sidekick-the-silvermedal-the-pet-companion-the-waifu?p=1097620#post1097620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes sense. Sorry, saw that goddamn King Arthur movie earlier, and it's probably left me a bit touchy.</div> </div> </div> </div>What didn't you like about it? I haven't seen it yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T07:58:07-07:00","id":1098431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1097665#post1097665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What didn't you like about it? I haven't seen it yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to my wife: Basically everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T17:38:56-07:00","id":1099696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1072648#post1072648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahmanet looks great. I liked her actress both in Kingsman and Star Trek and I too will look forward for it to gather some <b>Mummy: The Curse</b>'s visuals and atmosphere. You know you're a fan when you start to look at all monsters in terms of CoD splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my fantasy version of the film, Ahmanet would be the hero, while the villain would be someone else from Egypt (maybe even Imhotep). Now Ahmanet has to save this unfamiliar world she's woken up in, only this annoying pasty dude keeps complicating her life.<br /> <br /> <br /> In other news, Wonder Woman rocks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T20:05:03-07:00","id":1099732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1099696#post1099696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my fantasy version of the film, Ahmanet would be the hero, while the villain would be someone else from Egypt (maybe even Imhotep). Now Ahmanet has to save this unfamiliar world she's woken up in, only this annoying pasty dude keeps complicating her life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this plot. It sounds way better than the one it looks like we're going to get, with Tom Cruise gaining supernatural powers that are somehow greater than those of the being that gave them to him. The image of Tom Cruise as &quot;Heroic Mummy<sup>TM</sup>&quot; is just the opposite of appealing to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T12:45:39-07:00","id":1102074,"title":"","content":"So, I saw Wonder Woman today. Now, speaking as someone who stayed away from non-Disney non-Marvel superhero movies since Dark Knight Rises, my opinion is that this movie:<br /> <br /> Is okay. On a scale of 0 to 5, 0 being complete garbage and 5 being an instant classic, I'd rate this movie as a 3: enjoyable, had its moments, but wasn't really &quot;jaw-dropping.&quot;<br /> <br /> Aside from being the first major superhero movie headlined by a woman, which is cool.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'll add that it's pretty good inspiration for a Greco-Roman Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 06-27-2017, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T15:48:30-07:00","id":1102129,"title":"","content":"I liked the WW movie a little better, <i>maaaaybe </i>up to a 3.5, though keep in mind that, despite being a big superhero fan, I don't think any of the supers' movies could be called an instant classic. The good ones will range from 3 to 4 at most for me.<br /> <br /> Now, on a scale of 0 to 5 specifically for action blockbusters, I'd say it is worth a 4, though again I'm biased in favor of superhero movies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T16:14:17-07:00","id":1102139,"title":"","content":"Russel Crowe was fine and Sofia Boutella still is a really cool mummy but overall The Mummy was a huge disappointment not even worth the special effects and theatrics, plus a horrible start for a cinematic universe about something I love dearly.<br /> <br /> I'm back home watching the classic Universal Monster Movies right now while feeling both disappointed and sad. Those cannot be touched but I still think I was dumb for having hopes for this. Especially since I knew Alex Kurtzman was the director. Seriously, I don't get how that man still manages to get hired for this kind of high-profile movies after all the disasters he did.<br /> <br /> Silly me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T04:25:33-07:00","id":1108346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1098431#post1098431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to my wife: Basically everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's, ah, not very helpful. Is there more you or someone can say on the subject?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T04:23:59-07:00","id":1108694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1102139#post1102139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Russel Crowe was fine and Sofia Boutella still is a really cool mummy but overall The Mummy was a huge disappointment not even worth the special effects and theatrics, plus a horrible start for a cinematic universe about something I love dearly.<br /> <br /> I'm back home watching the classic Universal Monster Movies right now while feeling both disappointed and sad. Those cannot be touched but I still think I was dumb for having hopes for this. Especially since I knew Alex Kurtzman was the director. Seriously, I don't get how that man still manages to get hired for this kind of high-profile movies after all the disasters he did.<br /> <br /> Silly me</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea....I just decided not to go see it. The trailers looked real bad for it...so I figured it was best to just to skip it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T04:27:39-07:00","id":1108698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1102129#post1102129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the WW movie a little better, <i>maaaaybe </i>up to a 3.5, though keep in mind that, despite being a big superhero fan, I don't think any of the supers' movies could be called an instant classic. The good ones will range from 3 to 4 at most for me.<br /> <br /> Now, on a scale of 0 to 5 specifically for action blockbusters, I'd say it is worth a 4, though again I'm biased in favor of superhero movies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really enjoyed Wonder Woman, but that might be because I had super low expectations for it.<br /> <br /> So, just taken on it's own, on a scale of 1 to 5, yea, a 3.5 to 4 sounds about right. But, compared to the other DC Murderverse movies(Man of Steel and Batman v Superman) I'd say it's like a 6. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It was waaaaay better than those other DC movies for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _____________________