gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T18:11:43-08:00","id":1181541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1181512#post1181512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I wanted to see.<br /> But all Disney wants is comedies, since they're more marketable towards children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is they tried doing that with the first two Thor movies.<br /> <br /> It didn't work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T18:42:46-08:00","id":1181545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1181541#post1181541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is they tried doing that with the first two Thor movies.<br /> <br /> It didn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>The trouble is lazy writing, and dumbing it all down because it's easier.<br /> Most thought Captain America would be boring as hell. I mean after all how could Cap &quot;Whitebread&quot; be at all interesting? And yet he is written well and damned awesome. (Winter Soldier is probably the best of the MCU)<br /> Thor was on a par with Cap when it came to sheer righteousness. He doesn't need all that oratory and narration in the comic books. Just needs to show it.<br /> I'd love to see the Thor storyline involving the Eternals, and by extension, the Celestials.<br /> <br /> Maybe it wouldn't be so bad if everyone in the MCU didn't get hit with the nerf bat. (Iron Man vs Thor? That shouldn't have been close.)<br /> I mean Disney is planning to make Carol Danvers (Cap Marvel) the strongest character in the MCU. That's ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T19:18:02-08:00","id":1181549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1181541#post1181541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is they tried doing that with the first two Thor movies.<br /> <br /> It didn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It worked at the box office. It worked for lots of Thor fans.<br /> <br /> Not saying Ragnarok didn't work, by the way. But all three had their good parts, IMO. <br /> <br /> And each one managed to increase their profists by over 200 millions. From Thor 1, to Thor 3. And all three are considered successes. <br /> <br /> Sometimes, it's good to get a fresh pair of eyes behind a film.<br /> <br /> I did, however, find Thor 3 to be a BIT too comedic for my tastes. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 02-01-2018, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T20:48:14-08:00","id":1181557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally poste