ay Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T18:57:27-08:00","id":1272507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1272505#post1272505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd only be hurting yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) It's a pass time.<br /> 2) the correct answer, by the way, was &quot;I'll persuade you.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Quite. Rather wholesomely enjoyable. Might well be the strongest film to feature Spider people.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR][/LEFT] </div> </div> </div>I'm one of those folks burnt out on the superheroes, but if I get an itch, I shall check it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T20:39:23-08:00","id":1272524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1272507#post1272507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm one of those folks burnt out on the superheroes, but if I get an itch, I shall check it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen at least one person say that they were burnt out on Marvel movies, and then Spider-verse turned them around.<br /> <br /> It's quite unlike what has become typical fare over the last few years, and really it's own kind of beast.<br /> <br /> I feel as though it may be a meaningful distinction to say that it's less of a superhero movie than it is a Spider-Man one. If one just thinks about what it is that makes core Spider-Man stand out and endure.<br /> <br /> If I had one significant criticism for Spider-Man: Homecoming, it would be it labouring under the weight of being part of the wider MCU. Imagine a film with a similar tone, but instead of conversations with Tony Stark and something that Tony Stark has built, it's Spider-Man conversing with... other Spider-people.<br /> <br /> That and some other things that I won't give away, and the damn trailers have not given away, but plays into the whole thing being a loving celebration of Spider-Man.<br /> <br /> All packaged in some really fine animation, and clever stylistic quirks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T23:15:43-08:00","id":1272548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1272524#post1272524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've seen at least one person say that they were burnt out on Marvel movies, and then Spider-verse turned them around.<br /> <br /> It's quite unlike what has become typical fare over the last few years, and really it's own kind of beast.<br /> <br /> I feel as though it may be a meaningful distinction to say that it's less of a superhero movie than it is a Spider-Man one. If one just thinks about what it is that makes core Spider-Man stand out and endure.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be a little off-topic, but in my experience, Spiderman seems to be the favorite super hero of a lot of people who otherwise aren\u2019t all that into superheroes. I don\u2019t know if that holds true beyond my own social circles, but it is common enough within them to seem noteworthy. I\u2019ve always wondered if there\u2019s something to that. Some <i>je ne sais quoi</i> that Spider-Man has that appeals to non-super hero fans in a way other super heroes fail to capture.<br /> <br /> At any rate, the idea that this film feels like a spider-man movie more than a super hero movie suits my biases nicely, and is a strong selling point to me. Thank you for the recommendation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T00:18:41-08:00","id":1272555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1272548#post1272548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be a little off-topic, but in my experience, Spiderman seems to be the favorite super hero of a lot of people who otherwise aren\u2019t all that into superheroes. I don\u2019t know if that holds true beyond my own social circles, but it is common enough within them to seem noteworthy. I\u2019ve always wondered if there\u2019s something to that. Some <i>je ne sais quoi</i> that Spider-Man has that appeals to non-super hero fans in a way other super heroes fail to capture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that's easy:<br /> <br /> Spider-Man as a character being the every man.<br /> <br /> Someone who comes off as being relatable and down to earth, and not quite as larger then life as the other heroes. Spider-Man/Peter Parker as the guy that's trying to balance his superhero life and his normal life...you know, just like how IRL people need to balance their work life with their social/leisurely life. Compared to other heroes where their superhero life was all they did, and their civilian life was...just a break from their superheroics and nothing more.<br /> <br /> He's the gateway hero to all of the other superheroes, so to speak.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T04:03:03-08:00","id":1272571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1272548#post1272548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be a little off-topic, but in my experience, Spiderman seems to be the favorite super hero of a lot of people who otherwise aren\u2019t all that into superheroes. I don\u2019t know if that holds true beyond my own social circles, but it is common enough within them to seem noteworthy. I\u2019ve always wondered if there\u2019s something to that. Some <i>je ne sais quoi</i> that Spider-Man has that appeals to non-super hero fans in a way other super heroes fail to capture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that there are three major things that give Spider-Man a wide ranging appeal, even without an awareness of or investment in general superhero stuff.<br /> <br /> He's easy to market to kids: his costume is distinctly bright and colourful, recognisable and memorable, his persona is quippy and fun-loving, his capabilities make him look particularly dynamic whether he's travelling the city or getting into fights with his rogues gallery, who are often designed to be larger and stronger than he is to create a sharp contrast. His methods also lend themselves to memorable and endearing images, such as leaving a bunch of criminals bundled up in a tangle of webbing for police to take in.<br /> <br /> His central thesis as a superhero is endurance in the face of loss or suffering: it's arguably a well that has been gone back to a bit too frequently, but Spider-Man often has a bit of a hard knock life, or gets pounded down by the villains, and he gets back up and keeps going. He's super-powered, but not <i>so</i> much that he doesn't still often come across as a scrappy underdog, especially against the villains that he faces.<br /> <br /> He's a mainline Marvel hero that doesn't live in a mansion, sizable townhouse, or high-rise apartment.<br /> <br /> I'd say that good Spider-Man adaptations keep at least two of these, or at least very strongly emphasize one of them (generally the first). Bad adaptations are Spider-Man Unlimited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-04T07:25:19-08:00","id":1272838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1272555#post1272555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's the gateway hero to all of the other superheroes, so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, that was rather literal in the case of the animated series from the 90s, which served as my personal introduction to:<br /> <br /> Iron Man and War Machine<br /> Dr. Strange (as well as Baron Mordo and Dormammu)*<br /> Frank Castle<br /> Freaking Blade.<br /> Captain America (and the Red Skull)**<br /> <br /> Aaaaand those are about the ones I can remember off the top of my head, there might have been more.<br /> <br /> I think the X-Men and Fantastic Four showed up every now and then, but I was already familiar through their own shows.<br /> <br /> <br /> * All five of those characters were integral to the storyline that introduced Carnage, of all people.<br /> ** Who were tied into Black Cat's backstory by virtue of attributing her abilities to the super-soldier serum, whose formula her father had inadvertently almost stolen for the Nazis.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T13:46:38-08:00","id":1273624,"title":"","content":"A Quiet Place is really, really good","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T15:57:37-08:00","id":1273797,"title":"","content":"Bah, the day of Spider-verse's wide release so that more people can know its greatness and sing its praises can't come fast enough.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, Bumblebee is pretty damn good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T11:06:26-08:00","id":1274080,"title":"","content":"Anybody started seeing Spider-verse yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T11:11:03-08:00","id":1274083,"title":"","content":"In my personal opinion, Dawn of the Dead (1978) is the greatest zombie film ever made and one of the best horror movies period.<br /> <br /> It's a shame the 2004 remake was so terrible, but to be honest, I never liked Zack Snyder as a director. His recent superhero films have only confirmed my dislike even more.<br /> <br /> I recently re-watched the &quot;Extended Mall Hours&quot; fan cut of the original movie and it is awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T19:23:54-08:00","id":1274125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1274083#post1274083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my personal opinion, Dawn of the Dead (1978) is the greatest zombie film ever made and one of the best horror movies period.<br /> <br /> It's a shame the 2004 remake was so terrible, but to be honest, I never liked Zack Snyder as a director. His recent superhero films have only confirmed my dislike even more.<br /> <br /> I recently re-watched the &quot;Extended Mall Hours&quot; fan cut of the original movie and it is awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's a crime that the movie doesn't have a proper bluray(or DVD release in general) that's easy to obtain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T22:53:29-08:00","id":1274144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1274125#post1274125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> It's a crime that the movie doesn't have a proper bluray(or DVD release in general) that's easy to obtain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Agreed. I first saw Dawn of the Dead on VHS as a kid when I was about six or seven years old, so this would have been around 1999 or 2000 at the time.<br /> <br /> In fact, I first watched it with my mom (she was and still is a huge fan of horror movies) and I thought it was awesome. We also watched the first three Alien films together, if I remember correctly. That was a thing my mom and I did when I was a kid, watch horror movies together. My Dad was more of the Sci-Fi and Fantasy kind of guy, and he introduced me to awesome films like Highlander and Excalibur. Also, my Dad was my first Game Master when I started playing RPG's.<br /> <br /> I was the kind of kid who had really permissive parents when it came to media, they made sure to let me know it was all fake.<br /> <br /> I could watch R-rated movies, but as my mom would say, &quot;don't repeat them&quot;<br /> <br /> Hell, I remember in grade school that the other kids were shocked that I was allowed to watch The Simpsons (I grew up in a very conservative rural area)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T04:28:00-08:00","id":1274170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1274125#post1274125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a crime that the movie doesn't have a proper bluray(or DVD release in general) that's easy to obtain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got the dvd Ultimate Edition that came out several years ago. It's got the US theatrical version, the European version and an Extended Cut. It's pretty awesome. But yea, probably harder to get now...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T01:49:24-08:00","id":1274330,"title":"","content":"When I went to see Into the Spider-Verse for the second time a couple of days ago, it occurred to me that there was an element that I neglected in my prior endorsement of it.<br /> <br /> How it is not only a Spider-Man movie, but a comic book movie; a loving tribute to comic books, both in its themes, and its artistry. I'd say that if a person enjoys comic books, of any kind, they ought to see this movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T09:37:34-08:00","id":1274377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1274080#post1274080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anybody started seeing Spider-verse yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't get my tickets for it until tonight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T15:50:28-08:00","id":1275189,"title":"","content":"I am surprised at the lack of Spider-Man discussion going on in this thread, or any other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T20:02:53-08:00","id":1275225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1275189#post1275189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am surprised at the lack of Spider-Man discussion going on in this thread, or any other.</div> </div> </div> </div>My plans to see it the other day ended up being a wash, but I just got out of the theater, just now\u2026<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It's a seriously great movie. The cast was great, the dynamic visual style of the movie evoked the feel of comic books in all the right ways (compare Ang Lee's Hulk for a more jarring, less enjoyable attempt to evoke the same; I really feel that the choice to make it a cartoon instead of live-action makes a world of difference in terms of effectiveness), I really liked this take on Kingpin, and I am positively drooling at the prospects of some of the sequels/spinoffs suggested.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T23:32:26-08:00","id":1275733,"title":"","content":"Saw a few movies today and the past few days. Descent into Darkness: My European Nightmare was bad, and awful. Badly made film but awful in its grim depiction of a man taken advantage of, abused, and generally driven over the edge in a disappointingly bleak manner. Was a real bummer, but after that saw another movie, the Occupants. Not quite horror (my main interest) more of a supernatural thriller, the premise was more interesting than the plot, with a married couple documenting (via cameras set up all over the house) how they are during this fast they're trying. Then the videos start picking up different people. A couple, still, there are some vague physical similarities, they go by similar names and have jobs the main couple had thought about getting into. It's an alternate universe. Of course one can't just be a voyeur, especially when they feel they've seen one of their alternates wronged. Wasn't a great movie but I did like the premise. Think it musta been a SyFy movie, Robert Picardo was in it.<br /> <br /> Today I saw the new Halloween, which was surprisingly good. I was disappointed they erased all the movies in between but overall a nice movie, good actors, actresses. Then I watched some of this show called Deadwax, on Shudder. Blessedly brief, some of the episodes are like 15 minutes, and if horror serials can throw off the trend of having hour long slog-fests then I'm even more into them. Mysterious thief-woman with a penchant for finding rare records may have stumbled upon one of the rarest, but so far everyone who's heard it has died or gone insane. Haven't finished it up but I'm really enjoying it. Technically not a movie.<br /> <br /> Then I watched Terrified. Killer movie, very wild stuff, distorted timeline and such interesting things with horror. They're apparently already remaking it (it's an Argentinian movie so likely they'll redo it in America).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T04:42:59-08:00","id":1276214,"title":"","content":"Bumblebee was really, REALLY fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T11:21:20-08:00","id":1276669,"title":"","content":"Into The Spider-Verse was my Christmas present (it's the day 1 around here). Loved it SO much. I find it's the only movie that truly gets what makes comic Spidey special and pays it justice. The animation, the anti-Chosen One narrative, the heart...all stuff I love. I could go on. I was moved by it to the very end.<br /> <br /> And while an old Spidey fan like me was entertained and more teary-eyed that virility standards would allow me to admit, the kids in the theather were absolutely thrilled, which is all I could hope for.<br /> <br /> The MCU being triumphant, it's easy to forget that Iron Man, Cap, Starlord and all might be cool, but most of those like us were, are and will be Spider-Man more than any of them. Thanks to this movie for reminding me, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T02:54:52-08:00","id":1278274,"title":"","content":"Warning, the following post contains allegory.<br /> <br /> So, I've had a couple of bad experiences with this upscale restaurant; while some of their turnout has been good, or even great, the manager was a real turd-burger. Guy's pretentious, with this absolutely twisted sense of what his customers want, and a serious penchant for leering at his female employees. The grill guy for the first few visits clearly didn't care about job security; the last time I saw him there, he was sporting a moustache and no netting to stop his facial hair from ruining the diners' experience. <br /> <br /> But this time around, it's a bunch of new faces, everyone seems pleasant, and the slab of beef they're advertising looks positively mouth-watering. So I go in and order their $8 burger special and sit down to experience it.<br /> <br /> It's visually-interesting, one of the few things I've encountered where the actual thing looks exactly like it's been advertised. It's overstuffed and complex, but not to the extent that I couldn't handle it. I would even go so far as to say it's a fine burger.<br /> <br /> Right up until the last bite, where I realize I've encountered a hair under the cheese.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T03:09:24-08:00","id":1278277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1278274#post1278274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Warning, the following post contains allegory.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact I have two equally valid main suspects probably says a lot about the current state of the industry","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T05:59:12-08:00","id":1278295,"title":"","content":"The Predator was quite possibly the worst movie I've seen in the last decade. And I watch a lot of movies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T17:03:17-08:00","id":1279078,"title":"","content":"Oh, hey, they just added/re-added the Indiana Jones movies to Netflix!<br /> <br /> *gives them a watch, having not seen them in a while*<br /> <br /> What do y'all think of that fan theory about the spy in Cairo from <i>Raiders</i> being an alternate-universe Aladdin, one who never got his big break? Y'know, instead of a magic lamp, he got Nazis. <br /> <br /> Makes it really sad that he inadvertently poisoned his monkey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T22:36:41-08:00","id":1279129,"title":"","content":"So I saw Mary Poppins Returns, and can finally say...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.relatably.com/m/img/mad-max-memes/v1F1hk3.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> In my eyes, people have officially lost the right to complain about Star Wars: The Force Awakens being a carbon-copy of A New Hope. Because THIS movie, THIS does it WAAAAY worse then TFA. Beat for beat it's the first movie all over again:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>We open in our main family, which features and estranged relationship between the paternal figure and the children.</li> <li>Mary Poppins swoops in at the family's time of need.</li> <li>The cynical kids get introduced through a world of wonder via twisting a simple maintenance activity.</li> <li>An encounter with the scrappy, blue character side character that leads to a musical excursion into an animated world.</li> <li>Broken up by a much more melancholy song.</li> <li>Visiting a quirky family member that reside in a bizarre home with questionable physics.</li> <li>A visit to the bank on the behalf of the parental figure where things go from bad to worse, causing the kids to get lost in London.</li> <li>The blue collar side character returns, to lead the kids back home and to cheer them up with the help of his coworkers.</li> <li>The paternal has to face the music with the bank people...but things manage to work out in the end.</li> <li>Movie closes out with the family enjoying a day at the park, and Mary takes her leave.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> All of it rolls by, beat for beat, as if someone really did copy and pasted the original's script and changed the details to seem not exactly the same.<br /> <br /> And any additions made unique to Returns...makes things even worse.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">There's of course the much mentioned villain in the movie...one that the first movie didn't need. It adds an unnecessary conflict the movie didn't need. What is there to gain from making the Banks home getting deliberately taken away through malicious intent for the sake of it, when it could have easily been turned around to be an uncaring act of business bureaucracy?<br /> <br /> The romance between Jack and Jane...adds nothing to the plot at all and is just there for inexplicable reasons.<br /> <br /> And the climax of trying to &quot;turn back time&quot; for the sake of making things exciting and nothing else. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Songs are also completely forgettable and go out the ears as quickly as they go in.<br /> <br /> Only things of note in this movie are the visuals; the film is super pretty to look at. The bright and colorful animated worlds of animation are a delight, and even the darker and grimier world of London is still lavishly detailed. And all the performances are top notch; Emily Blunt in particular as Mary Poppins. I never got a sense that she was just copying what Julie Andrews did. That she really did embody the magical nanny; haughty, witty, confident, but still with a kind heart underneath all of it.<br /> <br /> The other exception being Lin-Manuel Miranda as Jack. His Cockney accent is somehow WORSE then Dick van Dyke's. Which is saying something since even as a kid I never minded his take as Bert. With Miranda, every time his character opens his mouth I'm trying to stifle laughter at how ridiculous he sounds.<br /> <br /> As for Angela Lansberry's mystery role...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yeah I get the sense her character was the one that was originally meant for Julie Andrews had accepted making a cameo appearance...and it does feel a little off that she's not here to be in it. Starting to wonder that they had already finalized the script when they asked Andrews...and I GUESS they were too far in to make any changes to accommodate the change. As amusing as it is to interpret this as a tie-in to Bedknobs and Broomsticks...it's not enough. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Overall...just watch the original movie. Don't waste your time with this one.<br /> <br /> <b>(And as a reminder, <i>THIS</i> was the movie Disney felt deserved the Holiday 2018 slot more then Solo did. And, amusingly enough, this movie is ALSO not doing so hot at the box office right now.)</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T08:19:33-08:00","id":1279471,"title":"","content":"Just saw into the Spiderverse. The plot was nothing unexpected, but everything else, the acting, visual style, music, jokes and the way the plot beats were handled were all amazing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T11:51:19-08:00","id":1279521,"title":"","content":"So a few week ago I had finally seen Ralph Breaks the Internet.<br /> <br /> (not going to bother with spoiler tags since it's been over a month since the movie came out)<br /> <br /> Needless to say I feel very...conflicted about this movie.<br /> <br /> One the one hand, the core story at the center (aka what was NOT shown in the trailers) about relationships is an excellent one. About how while you can make close relationships with your best friends, that you still need to respect their space as a person. That they will want to do Things outside of your interests, and that they will have friends that aren't you, that sometimes they'll want to hang out with instead of you. Not respecting that space will lead to toxic behavior, as seen in this movie. It's a beautiful message that should definitely be taught to more kids (and certain adults for that matter). The only issue with this story is the climax where they make the conflict a bit more...literal then it should be. A giant Ralph who tries to break the Internet, acting out his desire to not being able to let go forcing a confrontation.<br /> <br /> The problem with the movie is everything else and its setting.<br /> <br /> There's also knowing that, being constrained with a PG rating and being a Disney movie, that they can't get into any really deep commentary and critique on the internet.<br /> <br /> For instance, passing by the Twitter building, any adult using Twitter in 2018-19 knows full well that the thing the site is being most widely used for is NOT for sharing cat videos and pictures. Or the shocking lack of anything pornographic. Or the visit to eBay and not once was the idea of fake knock-off items were brought up. It all feels like a sanitized version of the actual Internet.<br /> <br /> The only thing that we get is Ralph looking at the comments for his BuzzzTube videos and a couple of mean comments...comments that never really go above and beyond &quot;Ralph SUCKS!&quot; Once again, if this is IRL Internet, the comments would be a lot more provocative then what was shown.<br /> <br /> So...what was the point of the Internet even being a thing in this movie?<br /> <br /> Considering the true core of Wreck-it-Ralph's story, I'll go as far as saying that you didn't need the Internet setting to begin with. The story could have easily been about new arcade machines coming to Litwack's, one of them being Slaughter Race, and the story going from there. I can understand not wanting to do this since it would have felt like repeating the premise of the first movie...but between that alternative and what we ended up getting, it only brings me back to the other answer of:<br /> <br /> &quot;Why was this movie made?&quot;<br /> <br /> If they really wanted to make a story revolving around toxic relationships, why not just make it a brand new, standalone movie instead of hijacking Wreck-it-Ralph?<br /> <br /> Overall I'd say it's a mixed bag. It's a wonderful story about relationships, but is surrounded by a lot of schlocky jokes and with a setting that can't be taken full advantage of because it's a PG-rated Disney movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T19:36:31-08:00","id":1281428,"title":"","content":"Just watched <i>Glass</i>. I skipped <i>Split</i>, even after hearing it takes place in the same universe as <i>Unbreakable</i>, but I'm a sucker for Samuel L. Jackson.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T20:16:21-08:00","id":1281437,"title":"","content":"Wow. Split's awesome, great acting in it, McAvoy is stellar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T20:12:27-08:00","id":1281613,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Aquaman</u></b><br /> It's as epic as they say.<br /> The level of detail, and just everything was fairly solid.<br /> They even touched on the actual culture of Atlanteans.<br /> ------------------<br /> ------------------<br /> <b><u>Bumblebee</u></b><br /> A Transformers' movie with heart and soul. But then Bumblebee has always been portrayed as closest to human. And even more so, proof of the saying that it isn't about the size of the dog in a fight, but the fight in the dog. Bee is like Bruce Lee and Jackie Chan when it comes to taking on bigger 'bots. He's unstoppable, unrelenting and typically hits first.<br /> That said he loses his memory for a lot of the movie...and gets his ass kicked as a result.<br /> He's matched up well with human &quot;Charley Watson&quot; (Hailee Steinfeld), a teenager who is kinda broken...and knows herself well enough to realize that she doesn't want to be the person she knows she's becoming. (likely a self-hating a-hole) Their bonding moments heal each other. (Lot of 'E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial' moments here, and Bee is quite the hugger. Speilberg revealing his own personal touch I should think)<br /> This movie is a prequel of a sort. I guess they're redoing the franchise. It's a good solid start. It opens up with the war on Cybertron going to hell. And I'm pretty sure that the &quot;watery gooey splash&quot; when the Decepticons kill humans...was a deliberate way to avoid the movie gaining an &quot;R&quot; rating.<br /> Some of the scenes of 'bot vs. 'bot are pretty vicious. So I won't be surprised if an R-rating is forthcoming. It's war and we should see it.<br /> <br /> Damn...I guess I liked this movie a lot more than I thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T17:27:45-08:00","id":1290146,"title":"","content":"<b>Alita: Battle Angel</b><br /> <br /> Overall I liked it.<br /> <br /> That said it's...nothing mind-blowingly special. To the outsider, it is a pretty typical Pinocchio-esque story: an artificial, sentient and naive construct learning about the world and people she's surrounded with and learning what it means to be human. Still, while it's a familiar kind of story, I do feel like it's well-executed that I don't mind. Rosa Salazar's performance as Alita can't be understated to maintain the innocence but earnest desire to do good and doing whatever it takes to do so.<br /> <br /> Also one of my favorite scenes (that was hinted at in the trailers)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Was the bit where Alita plucks out her own heart and offers it to Hugo. In context, Hugo is going on about how he doesn't have enough money to get to Zalem, and Alita declaring that she'll do anything for him...which includes selling her own heart. Which the way how it's described, is the equivalent of an Iron Man arc reactor.<br /> <br /> What's great about this scene to me is two-fold. One, it continues to reinforces Alita's own sense of selflessness, that she is more interested in maintaining the well-being and happiness of others except for herself. The second, is that it contrasts that with her own inhumanity. A few scenes before this, Hugo declared that Alita was more human then anyone else he ever knew. And yet here, we see her demonstrating that she...very much is not human. That no, no human can JUST open up their chest and pick out their heart, and then put it back in as if nothing happened. And no human is willing to be as selfless as Alita is here. So while she may look and act human she isn't one.<br /> <br /> A subtle, kinda creepy, but also oddly beautiful scene.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And as hinted by the reviews...yeah the action is great. All of it is genuinely exciting and thrilling to watch. It also allows me to revel in the sweet death of close-up shaky can, since all of the action is clean and legible, and you can tell what's going on at all times. My personal favorite being the second fight with Grewishka.<br /> <br /> As for Alita's eyes...again, I'm probably in the minority, but I thought in action they were fine. In motion and as you watch the movie you get used to them. I only found a few moments where I felt like the CG was getting stretched at the seams. Other then that? Not a big enough issue to take you out of the movie.<br /> <br /> At the very least, it's leagues ahead of blue-Smith-Genie's look.<br /> <br /> Still haven't made a whole lotta progress into the manga, but what I've read and seen on the screen has been pretty accurate.<br /> <br /> I'd say it's worth a look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T17:43:25-08:00","id":1290151,"title":"","content":"Alita was amazing. Loved every bit of it. Though, I'm not familiar with the manga, nor did I watch the anime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T01:11:10-08:00","id":1291451,"title":"","content":"<b>Ghost (1990)</b><br /> <br /> I was NOT prepared for that much beefcake.<br /> <br /> Now yes, looking back on it now the movie is a bit...melodramatic. The blinding light to indicate the Heavenly light, Demi Moore's &quot;beautiful tears&quot; being done almost on cue and to death (heh), the heavy-handed foreshadowing it's all...a bit much.<br /> <br /> Still, pretty good ghost story. Especially one where the ghost is the protagonist. And digging into what it would actually be like to be a ghost, where most stories would rather paint ghosts as the antagonists.<br /> <br /> ...and yeah I can see why this was probably a huge inspiration to Wraith: the Oblivion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T14:22:45-08:00","id":1291949,"title":"","content":"<b>Poltergeist (1982)</b><br /> <br /> That was...silly.<br /> <br /> The over-the-top antics of the ghosts, the not-subtle-at-all special effects, the bombastic music, it was all just...really dumb.<br /> <br /> Just...eh...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T17:45:31-08:00","id":1293198,"title":"","content":"<b>Lego Movie 2: The Second Part</b><br /> <br /> Hmm.<br /> <br /> Now don't get me wrong, it's definitely a good movie and its faults really isn't because of poor craftsmanship. And there were enough jokes I got a good laugh out of.<br /> <br /> It just...doesn't give me the fizz as the last one.<br /> <br /> The message at the heart, while well-intentioned, I could see coming from a thousand miles away...simply because I saw the ending of the first movie and could get where they were going with in this movie. While this movie does try to portray it as emotional and heart-warming it...the actual content of the message isn't said in any interesting way.<br /> <br /> Also, between this, Deadpool 2, and to some extent Wreck-it-Ralph 2...I think I really am starting to get tired of 4th wall breaking, self-referential meta humor. It doesn't really feel like anything different or innovative is done with it...there's just more added. And I'm starting to feel like it's only there to cater to adult nerd fans. Which, well, I don't know about you guys but for me I'm not so amused by it anymore.<br /> <br /> So yeah. Take that for what you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""