right?<br /> <br /> It's dialogue like this that reminds me why I tend to hate fandoms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear ya....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1305194#post1305194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: So Abrams gave a spoiler-free thematic explanation for the title, and<a href=\"https://movieweb.com/the-rise-of-skywalker-why-title-star-wars-jj-abrams/?fbclid=IwAR0ZZTc5ZlaLA3Xc5BCdwaPoJFve4eWoiKNDLTGIo_bsYkT_wF5ZpLpsdhk\" target=\"_blank\"> I'm using this link for you all</a>.<br /> <br /> You know what, that explanation actually lands fine for me. I'm not crazy about it, but I don't hate it either, and it <i>does</i> highlight how basically this movie is going to be a conflict between the two main sides of the Skywalker legacy. One of them is gonna win.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still not sure on the title either. I don't hate it, but it does seem a little odd. I have some theories on what it could mean, but I don't want to speculate too much. I'll just see it and hopefully be surprised by what it means.<br /> <br /> And yea, I do like in this movie that the main conflict seems to be between two sides of the Skywalker Legacy. That's awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T08:55:45-07:00","id":1305274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1305190#post1305190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shazam was decent. Not great, not terrible, but merely average.</div> </div> </div> </div>I respectfully disagree.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">\u2022 Our hero didn't kill his villain just because it was more convenient than subduing him non-lethally.<br /> \u2022 Our hero didn't kill extras or minions, either, for that matter.<br /> \u2022 Our hero never branded anyone, or even threatened to brand anyone.<br /> \u2022 He didn't follow a trail of clues in a plot to <i>stop a war</i>, only to unleash a giant CGI Julie Andrews monster on <i>both sides of the battle</i>, wiping out more in 20 minutes of CGI explosions than would have died if they'd just been left to slug it out.<br /> \u2022 Our hero never got tricked into committing genocide on behalf of a pitiless imperial machine.<br /> \u2022 Our hero never infringed on the civil liberties of tens of millions of Americans because it was easier on his conscience than understanding the bad guy's motivations.<br /> \u2022 Our hero never embezzled millions from his father's company to punch poor people and destroy their public transit.<br /> \u2022 Our hero never swore an oath not to kill, only to decide that it's still okay to kill through inaction or just plain pushing them off a high surface and letting the ground kill them.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm not saying he's <i>perfect</i> (he <i>did</i> charge people for selfies), but overall the movie kinda shined a spotlight on how dark we've let our colorful costumed cape guys get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-16-2019, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T10:45:32-07:00","id":1305299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1305190#post1305190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The special effects were pretty bad, however. Although with the budget they had, I'd say they did the best they could. Definitely a step back for DC after the fantastic Aquaman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I felt the exact opposite.<br /> <br /> While Aquaman was enjoyable, it went all-in on the CG eyesore, especially in the climax as modern DC movies are known for. Shazam's OTOH was practically reserved in its implementation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T13:36:04-07:00","id":1305329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1305299#post1305299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? I felt the exact opposite.<br /> <br /> While Aquaman was enjoyable, <b>it went all-in on the CG eyesore</b>, especially in the climax as modern DC movies are known for. Shazam's OTOH was practically reserved in its implementation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The special effects in Shazam were so bad, I had to TRY not to notice how bad they were. Especially the flying scenes and the entirety of the last act. They were awful. It was easy to distinguish between Zach Levy's bodysuit and when it was CGI. That shouldn't happen in 2019. But, as I said, there wasn't much they COULD do on a 20 million dollar budget. <br /> <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Aquaman, which primarily takes place in an underwater universe, was made more believable by it's stellar special effects. Not really a way to do Atlantis without going 'all-in on the CG'.<br /> <br /> But hey, to each his own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 04-16-2019, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T13:42:02-07:00","id":1305330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1305329#post1305329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, Aquaman, which primarily takes place in an underwater universe, was made more believable by it's stellar special effects. Not really a way to do Atlantis without going 'all-in on the CG'.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can't be helped...doesn't stop it from being noticeably bad.<br /> <br /> And incidentally, in the scenes you cited, those take up far less run-time versus Aquaman's, where the underwater scenes and Atlantis make a significant chunk. So for me, Aquaman's bad CG is more immediately noticeable because it has a larger presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T19:17:10-07:00","id":1305378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1305330#post1305330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It can't be helped...doesn't stop it from being noticeably bad.<br /> <br /> And incidentally, in the scenes you cited, those take up far less run-time versus Aquaman's, <b>where the underwater scenes and Atlantis make a significant chunk.</b> So for me, Aquaman's bad CG is more immediately noticeable because it has a larger presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>A movie about Aquaman is likely to have Atlantis as a focal point and a large chunk of the film. I only cited a few scenes from Shazam. The entire movie was riddled with poor effects--which makes sense considering the 20 million dollar budget.<br /> <br /> <br /> The group that I saw Aquaman with, consisting of hardcore comic fans, all agreed that the special effects were amazing; especially considering they were bringing an underwater world to life. <br /> <br /> To think that I'd ever bear witness to an actual Aquaman movie, is a a giant feat alone. The fact that Atlantis was done so well is the icing on the cake. Especially as someone who happens to be a big Aquaman fan. Peter David's run on the character still holds up incredibly well, even today.<br /> <br /> I'm happy you enjoyed Shazam, though. It was a decent film. Take care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T09:36:14-07:00","id":1305501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1305378#post1305378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A movie about Aquaman is likely to have Atlantis as a focal point and a large chunk of the film. I only cited a few scenes from Shazam. The entire movie was riddled with poor effects--which makes sense considering the 20 million dollar budget.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either way, if bad effects are more omnipresent they stay stuck in your head and you remember it more versus the previous scenes that were more effect-less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The group that I saw Aquaman with, consisting of hardcore comic fans, all agreed that the special effects were amazing; especially considering they were bringing an underwater world to life. </div> </div> </div>...why is that relevant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T17:30:58-07:00","id":1308178,"title":"","content":"Endgame was great. It had its flaws, sure. But overall, it was great ending to 10 years of a mostly fun and entertaining universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T18:08:53-07:00","id":1308187,"title":"","content":"Seeing Endgame tomorrow. Rewatching Infinity War tonight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T18:50:30-07:00","id":1308210,"title":"","content":"Considering the reaction I had to Infinity War was that it was one of most impressive bits of structural storytelling I've ever seen and all it got out of me was a &quot;meh&quot;, I'm curious how Endgame'll affect me.<br /> <br /> Love it, hate it, or meh, though, at long last I can at last be freed from this franchise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T11:38:23-07:00","id":1308349,"title":"","content":"FYI, I've made a spoiler thread for Endgame. If you've seen it (I'm in the theatre right now) come on over!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread\"> Avengers: Endgame Spoiler Thread - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> HERE BE SPOILERS! You have been warned. Anyhow, I'm sitting in the theatre earlier than I have ever been to any other movie. Ten years ago, if you had told me there would be five Avengers movies (Civil War is a Cap movie, but it still counts) and that they would end up being a cultural event, I would have thought you were nuts. Yet here we are. I am very much looking forward to this. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T17:39:46-07:00","id":1311101,"title":"","content":"Pok\u00e9mon Detective Pikachu is pretty good y'all. Go see it.<br /> <br /> I had the good fortune to catch a preview screening on Sunday. Do you want to know how good of a movie for kids it is? It's &quot;theatre packed to the gills with children who sit still without a peep throughout&quot; good. At the same time as it's got some characterisation, theming and humour that adults will get, or at least appreciate more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T18:11:50-07:00","id":1311108,"title":"","content":"Glad to hear it. I mean I figured but nice to have someone else saying so. Saw Shazam last weekend and definitely not a movie for 7 year olds. Great flick though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T18:36:43-07:00","id":1311113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1311108#post1311108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad to hear it. I mean I figured but nice to have someone else saying so.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, the trailers give one a sense of &quot;this looks pretty fun&quot;. My perspective on actually seeing it is &quot;this is actually a lot better than it needed to be&quot;. There's a genuine labour of love to it, and it's something that <i>gets</i> what makes Pok\u00e9mon so compelling and puts it at the heart of everything.<br /> <br /> And believe me, there are going to be things that will likely have an impact that one won't have gotten from the trailers; some of them expansions or recontextualizations, some of them completely unhinted and pretty well staged. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T21:42:52-07:00","id":1311146,"title":"","content":"<b>Pokemon: Detective Pikachu</b><br /> <br /> We're witnessing history being made people: a mainstream Hollywood movie, that's a video game adaptation, that's ACTUALLY good and not ironically good!<br /> <br /> I will say that the reviews were right in that the plot is kind of basic and predictable for the media-weary viewer...that honestly doesn't matter that much. Movie's just filled to the brim with fun and charm that you just don't care.<br /> <br /> -Yeah, the art direction chosen for the Pokemon themselves works...surprisingly well in action. You would think that mashing together game/anime-accurate designs with photorealistic textures would be a recipe for a disaster, yet it isn't. It all works really well.<br /> <br /> I'm starting to think that Legendary employs actual wizards at their studios.<br /> <br /> -I'm surprised I didn't take note of this right from the trailers but the other thing that this movie is for the 2/3rds:<br /> <br /> Kid-friendly neo-noir film.<br /> <br /> While obviously not in black and white, it does include the high-contrast lighting (here the bright neon signs of Ryme City), the more literal contrast of the clean and shiny daylight version of the city versus the dark, grimy, and sleazy night city, familiar archetypes like a cynical protagonist, detectives (of course), and with morally grey story elements, primarily &quot;ends justifies the means&quot;. Nice to have one of these kind of movies, we don't get them too often...<br /> <br /> ...goddamn has it really been over 30 years since Who Framed Roger Rabbit?<br /> <br /> -Although my biggest issue with the movie is not necessarily how basic the plot is, but...<br /> <br /> The mystery element not being quite as good...due to our heroes getting TOLD about the twists and revelations instead of finding it out themselves.<br /> <br /> Any good mystery story is about the characters unveiling and piecing together the mystery's answers themselves, and the audience being along for the ride with them. It's not super pervasive: there are a lot more instances where the characters deduce the next twist themselves and how they get to that point does make sense. But it is still there, and it is disappointing to have.<br /> <br /> -Now a question I'm sure some have been having: &quot;is this movie canon to the games or the anime in any way?&quot;<br /> <br /> Well...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yes...sort of. When talking about Mewtwo, it's revealed that it &quot;escaped from the Kanto region 20 years ago&quot;. Now, if we assume the usual that the movie takes place in the year it was released, than it would mean the movie takes place in 2019. 20 years ago would be 1999...which was indeed the year that Mewtwo Strikes Back's English dub was released in North America. Conversely, the year before in 1998 was when Red/Blue made their NA debut. Sadly, I didn't stick around for the credits to see what the gentleman as the red-capped Pokemon trainer near the beginning is credited as (although IMDB lists him as &quot;male Pokemon trainer&quot;...but since IMDB, no idea how reliable it is). So I can't confirm or deny if he is/isn't an adult Red or Ash.<br /> <br /> At the very least, it confirms that SOME version of the story depicted in the games and/or anime have happened in Detective Pikachu's universe. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> -Couple of cute references that I noticed:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">-Time's phone has a distinct phone cover that has a black middle but the top end is red and the bottom is blue...while it COULD be a Red/Blue reference, to me it looked more like an inverted Switch.<br /> <br /> -Lucy's cap, hoodie, yoga pants, and sneakers outfit of course resembling the default femTrainer outfit from Pokemon Go.<br /> <br /> -Presumably, Lucy having a Psyduck and being the main female side characters was PROBABLY trying to draw a connection to Misty.<br /> <br /> -I believe one of the designs on Tim's shirt was the &quot;O&quot; Unown.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> -Spoiler random stuff<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> -The twists for the movie...are not hard to figure out for any narrative-savvy geek. As soon as they revealed the master plan on integrating human souls into Pokemon I was like &quot;Oh...that's what happened to Tim's dad&quot;.<br /> <br /> -That said, I was super stoked for the reveal that Harry Goodman is in fact Ryan Reynolds.<br /> <br /> -I WAS NOT EXPECTING KAIJU TORTERRA TO BE A THING GODDAMN. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I've said this before about Legendary regarding their kaiju movies but: I always got a sense these guys are fucking nerds and it shows. That they love geeky shit as much as we do, and that while there is money to be made, I always get the sense there is a love and passion at play of them wanting to make genuinely entertaining movies that they'd enjoy as fans. It doesn't always work (hai <i>Warcraft 2016</i>, <i>Pacific Rim: Uprising</i>), but when it works like with Detective Pikachu, it does WONDERS.<br /> <br /> Go see, it's great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T09:23:55-07:00","id":1311234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1311146#post1311146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -Spoiler random stuff<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.di