c4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-03T11:30:34-07:00","id":1333860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1322852#post1322852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me neither, but there some people who continue to argue that the Sam Rami movies are vastly superior to Homecoming and Far From Home. Which I disagree with, largely because I think Holland is a much more believable Peter Parker and teenager. Not that the Rami movies were bad, mind you.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Rami films certainly have their flaws, but I think they succeed in a way that few superhero films do: being Sincere.<br /> <br /> They are films that aren't afraid to be very silly, very tropey, and very emotionally vulnerable. While other superhero films of that period did everything in their power to pretend to be &quot;serious movies&quot; (&quot;what, were you expecting yellow spandex?&quot;), the Sam Rami Spiderman films were exceedingly open and unashamed of their subject matter. While this was often goofy and melodramatic, it also freed it to be grand and resonant, like High Opera. Or campy theater.<br /> <br /> It's in that lens that I've come to appreciate the trilogy, now that I'm older.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, it's through a particular analysis of these films that I was introduced to a particularly fascinating philosopher, the late Robert Moore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/UD0cNRsJugg\" data-code=\"UD0cNRsJugg\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/UD0cNRsJugg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T15:57:46-07:00","id":1334725,"title":"","content":"<i>It: Chapter Two</i> might not have been as good as the previous installment, but it felt very necessary right now.<br /> <br /> Folks <i>need</i> to be reminded that even though the predatory monster masquerading as a buffoonish clown is making you question your sense of reality and dividing everyone with hatred and fear, that if you unite and stand against it, <b>you can win.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T07:21:36-07:00","id":1338270,"title":"","content":"Just had the opportunity to watch Once Upon a Time... in Hollywood. Brilliant movie! I must admit that I got a little bored at the first chapter but I loved it when things have started to get messy. A real Tarantino stuff. Also I think it's the funniest Tarantino movie so far, I laughed my head off during some scenes. Nevertheless I think still it's necessary to know the real story to enjoy the movie before watching it. I wish I could watch it even earlier however it's impossible since I managed to <a href=\"https://tranio.com/france/detached/\" target=\"_blank\">buy a cottage in France</a> in a small village and moved there recently. We can watch the foreign movies only after a month of the US release date. Darn European standarts.. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25632-tzuyu","name":"Tzuyu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T20:15:57-07:00","id":1338380,"title":"","content":"Soooo, Captain Marvel is supposed to be the face of the MCU going forward...<br /> <br /> New comics released, now depicting Captain Marvel as a <a href=\"https://youtu.be/zT6t-YUFY_A\" target=\"_blank\">fascist super villain!</a><br /> <br /> She also thinks it's acceptable to arrest / kill children for crimes that they might potentially commit in the future, without giving them any due process. Children like Miles Morales....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-28-2019, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T22:02:20-07:00","id":1338396,"title":"","content":"To be fair, superheroes have \u201c<i>seldom</i>\u201d been big on individual civil liberties or proper due process. It\u2019s a very fasc-y genre.<br /> <br /> I give this a 0/10 - there\u2019s more valid complaints to be had about cinematic Captain Marvel than the stuff from literally another universe entirely. One might as well shit on the Fantastic Four comics for <i>Fant4stic</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-29-2019, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-28T23:15:53-07:00","id":1338404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1338380#post1338380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooo, Captain Marvel is supposed to be the face of the MCU going forward...<br /> <br /> New comics released, now depicting Captain Marvel as a <a href=\"https://youtu.be/zT6t-YUFY_A\" target=\"_blank\">fascist super villain!</a><br /> <br /> She also thinks it's acceptable to arrest / kill children for crimes that they might potentially commit in the future, without giving them any due process. Children like Miles Morales....</div> </div> </div> </div>Civil War 1 was going on in the comics in the lead up to Iron Man 1, and Iron Man was literally taking villains and heroes and putting them into camps, and training the underage ones into be killers for the government. While I'm sure people are picking on Captain Marvel because of her spotlight in the MCU, in the comics this is nothing new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T00:45:26-07:00","id":1338410,"title":"","content":"No, the only thing that of note is that despite her initially being pushed as the face of the MCU going forward...Captain Marvel 2 isn't a part of the Phase 4 film slate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T07:09:10-07:00","id":1338457,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I\u2019m also going to wait for a take on this from someone like Thorgi rather than a video whose commenters are being assholes to Brie Larson. I ain\u2019t Watching anything that caters to that crowd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T15:28:32-07:00","id":1338516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1338396#post1338396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I give this a 0/10 - there\u2019s more valid complaints to be had about cinematic Captain Marvel than the stuff from literally another universe entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not exactly a good argument. People watching the MCU and enjoying Captain Marvel's role in it are going to think <i>&quot;yeah, she's a great role model for our generation!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Only to pick up the comics that she's featured in and think &quot;wait, what the hell is she doing!?&quot;<br /> <br /> Personally, I didn't watch the Captain Marvel movie, and after seeing End Game, I'm glad I didn't. The scant amount of screen time she did have in the recent film made her come across as insufferably pretentious and holier than thou. Her portrayal in the comic books does not surprise me in the least.<br /> <br /> And yes, I know this isn't Brie Larson's fault (entirely). She's just the actor who played the character, and the real problem stems from the writers who produced the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-29-2019, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T15:46:15-07:00","id":1338520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1338516#post1338516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not exactly a good argument. People watching the MCU and enjoying Captain Marvel's role in it are going to think <i>&quot;yeah, she's a great role model for our generation!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Only to pick up the comics that she's featured in and think &quot;wait, what the hell is she doing!?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">[img]<a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/qoZX0zp.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://i.imgur.com/qoZX0zp.jpg</a>[/img]<br /> <br /> [img]<a href=\"https://www.zonanegativa.com/imagenes/2017/05/Marvel-Saga-Spiderman-13-03.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.zonanegativa.com/imagene...rman-13-03.jpg</a>[/img]</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What's the problem with them doing it with Captain Marvel when they've been doing it with every other Avenger for years?<br /> <br /> Or just reading the news and seeing it play out in real life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T15:58:00-07:00","id":1338522,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> Yes, I'm aware of the whole Captain America thing, and everybody was justifiably outraged over it. Why? Because there was virtually no evidence to support this bait and switch leading up to it! The reveal came across as a ham fisted attempt at political satire. As soon as I heard about Captain America being a Hydra agent, my immediate thought to the news was <i>&quot;oh my god, they're comparing modern America to Nazi Germany.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> But in the case of Carol Danvers as Captain Marvel, she has apparently always been like her comic book portrayal. A self obsessed narcissist, who abused her powers to get what she wants, and damn the consequences. It's as if the MCU chose her as the face based completely off her namesake, and didn't do any actual investigation into her character.<br /> <br /> The MCU is not in any way comparable of a portrayal as the comics are. Why is that?<br /> <br /> Because movies come out slowly, and only feature one story involving the character's adventurers.<br /> <br /> Comic books are churned out on a regular basis, and continue to expand upon the character's surrounding mythos at a much faster rate than the movies.<br /> <br /> Captain Marvel has only been present in the MCU for less than a year. She's been present in the comics since the late 60's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-29-2019, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T16:06:13-07:00","id":1338524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1338522#post1338522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> Yes, I'm aware of the whole Captain America thing, and everybody was justifiably outraged over it. Why? Because there was virtually no evidence to support this bait and switch leading up to it!<br /> <br /> But in the case of Carol Danvers as Captain Marvel, she has apparently always been like her comic book portrayal. <b>A self obsessed narcissist, who abused her powers to get what she wants, and damn the consequences</b>. It's as if the MCU chose her as the face based completely off her namesake, and didn't do any actual investigation into her character.<br /> <br /> The MCU is not in any way comparable of a portrayal as the comics are. Why is that?<br /> <br /> Because movies come out slowly, and only feature one story involving the character's adventurers.<br /> <br /> Comic books are churned out on a regular basis, and continue to expand upon the character's surrounding mythos at a much faster rate than the movies.<br /> <br /> Captain Marvel has only been present in the MCU for less than a year. She's been present in the comics since the late 60's.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're basically describing Iron Man. And while they made it a switch after the fact, and in Ultimates he's about as bad, and even in the mainstream comics he's starting to share similar beliefs.<br /> <br /> Plus as sad as it is, they've shown time and again that movies don't seem to relevantly impact the amount of people reading comics (the exception is non-superhero based graphic novels). If an 'entire generation' is watching her movie and thinking she's a great role model, they're basing it off the movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T16:08:16-07:00","id":1338526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1338516#post1338516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only to pick up the comics that she's featured in and think &quot;wait, what the hell is she doing!?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Because superheroes being dicks in comics is completely novel and entirely absent of precedent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1338516#post1338516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The scant amount of screen time she did have in the recent film made her come across as insufferably pretentious and holier than thou.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Captain America wasn\u2019t, in \u201cFirst Avenger?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T16:33:42-07:00","id":1338530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1338526#post1338526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And Captain America wasn\u2019t, in \u201cFirst Avenger?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Did you watch First Avenger? Because I don't think you saw the same movie I did.<br /> <br /> Captain America was portrayed as a patriotic young man who wanted nothing more than to serve his country, even though he was deemed too weak to effectively do so. He wanted this so much, that he agreed to become a test subject for an experimental soldier program. And after the program turned out to be successful, he was disappointed that the military only used him as a PR stunt, instead of making proper use of his newly enhanced abilities. One of the most terrible wars in human history was taking place, and he was sitting around at home performing musical numbers.<br /> <br /> Captain America wanted to help people during a time of great crisis, and everyone around him kept trying to hinder that goal. Of course he would be upset with the situation, anybody would have!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T16:55:08-07:00","id":1338534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1338530#post1338530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you watch First Avenger?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1338530#post1338530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Captain America was portrayed as a patriotic young man who wanted nothing more than to serve his country, even though he was deemed too weak to effectively do so. He wanted this so much, that he agreed to become a test subject for an experimental soldier program.</div> </div> </div> </div>Captain America was portrayed as an underage boy who repeatedly falsified government documents and broke the law in the interest of doing things <i>his way</i>, even though the United States had plenty of soldiers and numerous options existed to help the war effort from home.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1338530#post1338530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And after the program turned out to be successful, he was disappointed that the military only used him as a PR stunt, instead of making proper use of his newly enhanced abilities. One of the most terrible wars in human history was taking place, and he was sitting around at home performing musical numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>So he went rogue because he thought his way was better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T19:22:24-07:00","id":1338553,"title":"","content":"Captain Marvel has been unlikable in the comics for years. As has Iron Man. But to be honest, I'm not entirely sure Marvel(or Disney) actually care how their characters are written or perceived as most of their current stuff might as well be cosplay fluff at 3.99 a pop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T19:49:28-07:00","id":1338556,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, what are you talking abo-<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://media1.giphy.com/media/fDO2Nk0ImzvvW/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T15:29:26-07:00","id":1338701,"title":"","content":"Loosely related to the conversation, so every once in a while you get the comments about how feminism or political correctness or what have you is ruining media these days, including our movies. Most of these arguments are done in such bad faith as to not warrant attention-so it's actually kind of satisfying that there is an arena where that misapplied &quot;wokeness&quot; does hurt movies and, and having people expose what the underlying flaw in that sort of paper-thin social justice fanservice really is, how lip service doesn't serve the needs of legitimate criticisms.<br /> <br /> Or in other words, have you checked out Lindsey Ellis's Woke Disney video?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xU1ffHa47YY&amp;t=0s\" data-code=\"xU1ffHa47YY\