":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T15:33:06-07:00","id":1344079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1344078#post1344078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good point...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks. Yea, just thought it'd be cool to try to talk about the new trailer. But, some people just have to be a buzzkill I guess.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, to be fair, it is a cool trailer! And I am cautiously optimistic for the new show, so if Nyr hadn't sucked, I would have liked to get into what seemed cool and what had me biting my lip.<br /> <br /> I don't think Rise will be as good as Last Jedi, but I imagine I'll have a lot of fun with it regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-31-2019, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T22:12:21-07:00","id":1344126,"title":"","content":"I saw a Cracked article speculating about the possibility of Disney introducing time travel into the latest Star Wars movie. I really hope that\u2019s not the case; two things that really turn me off of a series are introducing aliens or time-travel into the later installments. <br /> <br /> (It\u2019s different when it\u2019s planned in from the start but introduced later, because skillful writers planning this stuff out can have hints to it show up in the early installments, like the shape of the canyon in <i>Gravity Falls</i>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T16:38:08-07:00","id":1344296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1344079#post1344079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, to be fair, it is a cool trailer! And I am cautiously optimistic for the new show, so if Nyr hadn't sucked, I would have liked to get into what seemed cool and what had me biting my lip.<br /> <br /> I don't think Rise will be as good as Last Skywalker, but I imagine I'll have a lot of fun with it regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I thought it was great! I mean, I liked the other trailer with the Dark Rey vision or whatever at the end, but this had some really cool moments that had me going &quot;WHAAAT!?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Oh!! I saw something about the planet the Death Star wreckage is on is not Endor. Seems like an odd choice, but maybe it's a planet in the same system still, or another moon of Endor?<br /> <br /> I'm sure they decided to go with a different planet to try to stem off people yelling about how they're just remaking Return of the Jedi. :: sigh ::<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1344126#post1344126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw a Cracked article speculating about the possibility of Disney introducing time travel into the latest Star Wars movie. I really hope that\u2019s not the case; two things that really turn me off of a series are introducing aliens or time-travel into the later installments.<br /> <br /> (It\u2019s different when it\u2019s planned in from the start but introduced later, because skillful writers planning this stuff out can have hints to it show up in the early installments, like the shape of the canyon in <i>Gravity Falls</i>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, they kind of introduce the idea of time travel in an episode of Star Wars Rebels. But, I'm not sure it'd be a good fit for the main films. Although, I am a sucker for time travel, so depending on how it was done I could be ok with it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all you