beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T22:48:53-07:00","id":1345170,"title":"","content":"More of a show than a movie, but there's been this thing on Epix called Pennyworth, based on Alfred. But it's Alfred as a young veteran in a very surreal version of the 50s and 60s with blimps and anti-spy warnings everywhere. It mixes Guy Ritchie with, I'm not sure, the old Avengers show? The one with Emma Peel and John Steed from the 60s. It's a very weird show and so far there's no 'bat' stuff, but Thomas Wayne is a very intense and hyper doctor trying to help out the US government with some of the affairs there while Martha Kane (Bruce's mom) gets involved with Aleister Crowley's sex cult. The big plot this season has been a group of aristocrats who want their power back.<br /> <br /> It's a crazy show, but it's crazy in a fun way. I mention it because the first season has ended, and I just heard they announced a second one. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('