eat origin too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yea!! It'd be cool if they did a sequel.<br /> <br /> I saw 'Final Girls' too, and I thought it was a good riff on the genre as well, and set up it's potential sequel in an interesting way as well...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T13:54:07-08:00","id":1345875,"title":"","content":"Going back to the new SW trilogy for a sec,is it true that a subtantital amount of people think Kylo Ren is a interesting character because he i's pathethic and not the classic badass villiain? I mean,he stops a laser blast with the force! that's the coolest thing in the damn movie! And the fight scenes both against and together with Rey were amazing,he's clearly a skilled,dangerou terrifying warrior? Where is the pathetic side?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:11:58-08:00","id":1345883,"title":"","content":"Usually characters who aren\u2019t pathetic can hold in their rage enough to not destroy a wall out of impotent frustration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:23:15-08:00","id":1345893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1345883#post1345883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usually characters who aren\u2019t pathetic can hold in their rage enough to not destroy a wall out of impotent frustration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I.dont know,many cool villains have explosions of rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:24:18-08:00","id":1345894,"title":"","content":"Basically being a skilled warrior doesn't mean you're a good leader, or at anything. Especially when you constantly let yourself be so led by your emotions that someone who hasn't seen you in a decade can troll you from solar systems away. While there's probably more to their corruption in books and stuff, the manipulation used to bring folks like Anakin to the dark side has been pretty shallow, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T15:50:25-08:00","id":1345928,"title":"","content":"Well, if we're talking about Kylo Ren, I would be remiss if I didn't link to Folding Ideas's video &quot;<a href=\"https://youtu.be/gR1e4idmvWY\" target=\"_blank\">Kylo Ren as a Compelling Villain</a>&quot;, from 2015.<br /> <br /> (Seems like I'm just in the mood to cite sources directly to make my arguments today, rather than going to the effort of making them myself. Oh well.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T15:54:33-08:00","id":1345930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1345883#post1345883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usually characters who aren\u2019t pathetic can hold in their rage enough to not destroy a wall out of impotent frustration.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the whole concept behind Form Seven &quot;Juyo&quot; light saber combat.<br /> <br /> Harnessing the power of the Dark Side, without letting it dominate you. Practice of this form was restricted among the Jedi Order, because of how risky it was. Only very advanced masters (like Mace Windu) were permitted to study it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1345875#post1345875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean,he stops a laser blast with the force! that's the coolest thing in the damn movie! And the fight scenes both against and together with Rey were amazing,he's clearly a skilled,dangerou terrifying warrior? Where is the pathetic side?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yoda stopped a lightning blast with the force... something even Luke Skywalker wasn't able to do in the movies.<br /> <br /> As for his battle with Rey, let's take a moment to consider how little training she had before going to this fight. When Luke tried to run off and take on Vader to save his friends, he got his ass kicked, along with losing a hand. But Rey barely comes away from the fight with a scratch. THIS is the big, bad Sith Lord who managed to destroy Luke's new Jedi Order?<br /> <br /> Then again, I suppose the fact that she is Palpatine's granddaughter might have given her a boost in her natural aptitude?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-04-2019, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T16:42:26-08:00","id":1345948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1345875#post1345875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going back to the new SW trilogy for a sec,is it true that a subtantital amount of people think Kylo Ren is a interesting character because he i's pathethic and not the classic badass villiain? I mean,he stops a laser blast with the force! that's the coolest thing in the damn movie! And the fight scenes both against and together with Rey were amazing,he's clearly a skilled,dangerou terrifying warrior? Where is the pathetic side?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think he's pathetic.... he seems like a pretty interesting villain. In that he seems like he's trying really hard to be &quot;evil&quot;. Like he's been told because his grandfather was this great evil that he also needs to live up it. So he's trying really hard to be evil.... but he's not quite pulling it off. If that makes sense...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1345928#post1345928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if we're talking about Kylo Ren, I would be remiss if I didn't link to Folding Ideas's video &quot;<a href=\"https://youtu.be/gR1e4idmvWY\" target=\"_blank\">Kylo Ren as a Compelling Villain</a>&quot;, from 2015.<br /> <br /> (Seems like I'm just in the mood to cite sources directly to make my arguments today, rather than going to the effort of making them myself. Oh well.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Love that channel!! Good call on posting that video.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T18:21:15-08:00","id":1345976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1345930#post1345930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the whole concept behind Form Seven &amp;quot;Juyo&amp;quot; light saber combat.<br /> <br /> Harnessing the power of the Dark Side, without letting it dominate you. Practice of this form was restricted among the Jedi Order, because of how risky it was. Only very advanced masters (like Mace Windu) were permitted to study it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re thinking of Vapaad. Juyo is the base style, which while powerful, was incomplete. Vapaad was developed to address the flaws in Juyo, but doing so required one to tap into the dark side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1345930#post1345930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for his battle with Rey, let's take a moment to consider how little training she had before going to this fight. When Luke tried to run off and take on Vader to save his friends, he got his ass kicked, along with losing a hand. But Rey barely comes away from the fight with a scratch. THIS is the big, bad Sith Lord who managed to destroy Luke's new Jedi Order?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s pretty strongly implied in TFA that Kylo is inexperienced. He obviously has a great deal of raw power, but his training, both under Luke and later under Snoke, was incomplete. Heck, everything about the character, from his voice, his appearance, his movements, his fighting style, and if you are into non-film sources of canon, even his lightsaber design, scream \u201craw but unfocused power.\u201d Couple this lack of experience with his clear emotional instability, especially in that moment, having just killed his father, something he clearly was conflicted about, abs the fact that he was badly injured (by a shot from Chewy\u2019s bowcaster no less), and it\u2019s really not surprising that he struggled so much in that fight. Likewise, the implication throughout the film was that Rey had a similar degree of untapped potential, but where Kylo\u2019s power was wild and tumultuous, hers was elusive but focused. We also geot soft confirmation of this in TLJ with Snoke\u2019s line about darkness rising and light to meet it, though YMMV on if that is a satisfying explanation about the source of her power. At any rate, it\u2019s clear that both characters were armatures with a great deal of raw potential, but where Kylo relied on that unrefined talent, along with his rage to win through overwhelming force, which failed him when he was emotionally and physically compromised. Conversely, Rey largely relied primarily on discipline and skill, since she was previously unaware of the force (or, as the film implies, perhaps blocked out her connection to it). She won when she embraced the force and allowed it to act through her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1345930#post1345930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Then again, I suppose the fact that she is Palpatine's granddaughter might have given her a boost in her natural aptitude?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Get that eugenicist bullshit out of my Star Wars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T18:36:19-08:00","id":1345983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1345976#post1345976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You\u2019re thinking of Vapaad. Juyo is the base style, which while powerful, was incomplete. Vapaad was developed to address the flaws in Juyo, but doing so required one to tap into the dark side.<br /> <br /> <br /> Nope. Get that eugenicist bullshit out of my Star Wars.</div> </div> </div> </div>1 - I think Vapaad focuses on redirecting the Dark Side back upon your opponent in some kind of feedback loop. While <a href=\"https://youtu.be/9zKsQTAqPLQ\" target=\"_blank\">Juyo</a> involves immersing yourself in the thrill of combat, without losing your self control in the process. In a world setting where the Dark Side is revealed to have a literal will of its own, this would be incredibly difficult to perform without undergoing intense, rigorous training.<br /> <br /> 2 - hate to break it to you, but it's been in Star Wars ever since they introduced Midichlorians, and genetically engineered Force Jesus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T18:43:34-08:00","id":1345991,"title":"","content":"On record, I don't think feeding this conversation is helpful. I definitely don't think it goes anywhere healthy.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I mentioned a trepidation, and that trepidation is the idea that Palpatine is somehow coming back in. I mean, it's a thing, they have the actor, there's no denying it-but honestly, I feel like with where TLJ ended, the only real thing needed from there was something to help ramp up the stakes in the way the Second Death Star did in the original. I feel like as the main personal conflict goes, everything you need is there in Kylo and Rey, that where an infernal outside influence helped to pit Luke and Anakin's conflict to something outside of it, to mainly provide the immediate insight that Vader Came From Somewhere and This Asshole is It, Kylo's pretty much explained, and Rey's also pretty much explained, and the pair being so similar-but-disalike does all the work by itself. Kylo wants to be special because he is in the family of Luke and Anakin and has the burden of wanting to/feeling he has to match that and having betrayed by one where the other one never could. Rey wanted to be special and so desperately needed something, <i>anyone</i> to come along and <i>validate her</i> because she knew in her heart of hearts that her story wasn't just dismal, but utterly mundane, and now sits in that place of temptation-and-defiance where in Kylo can give her everything she wants, or she can try finding that validation in herself <i>only to</i> (possibly but not realistically)<i> fail and lose anything she ever had for it.</i><br /> <br /> I mean. Yeah. I know where they came from. I know why the Vader of this story is This Vader because of the Last Vader, and Luke's missteps. I know why the Luke of this story is This Luke because She's Legitimately This Nobody.<br /> <br /> I don't need Palpatine swinging his Sith-Dick around in that setup. I just need payoff. And I am worried that Palpatine's involvement is going to Fuck That Up.<br /> <br /> Everything else, I absolutely expect to just work out. And I really expected to at least get satisfaction from the Kylo-Rey arc. But Palpatine in the scene?<br /> <br /> I dunno man. I liked the idea of Rey being Palpatine's kid back before TLJ, but then the better way was shown to me and I <i>fucking loved it</i>, and I don't want to go back to that well now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T19:47:13-08:00","id":1346009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1345983#post1345983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 - hate to break it to you, but it's been in Star Wars ever since they introduced Midichlorians, and genetically engineered Force Jesus.</div> </div> </div> </div>And guess what? The Midichlorians/Force Jesus bit was also stupid eugenecist shit. Are we really dipping into the well of the SW prequels for justifications for this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T20:10:38-08:00","id":1346020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1346009#post1346009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And guess what? The Midichlorians/Force Jesus bit was also stupid eugenecist shit. Are we really dipping into the well of the SW prequels for justifications for this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I never claimed they were a good idea, but... well... they exist, now...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T21:55:40-08:00","id":1346046,"title":"","content":"I can't believe I finally like Jason Todd, all cuz of Titans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T22:08:33-08:00","id":1346050,"title":"","content":"Midichlorians are not an indication of force ability. They communicate the will of the force to force-sensitive people. Just sayin\u2019.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T22:17:19-08:00","id":1346054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1346050#post1346050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Midichlorians are not an indication of force ability. They communicate the will of the force to force-sensitive people. Just sayin\u2019.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would be inclined to believe that, if the Jedi did not specifically keep track of how many midichlorians the body contains... and the fact Anakin had the highest recorded count of any known Jedi, including Yoda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T22:30:21-08:00","id":1346061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1346054#post1346054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be inclined to believe that, if the Jedi did not specifically keep track of how many midichlorians the body contains... and the fact Anakin had the highest recorded count of any known Jedi, including Yoda.</div> </div> </div> </div>So? We track all manner of statistics in the real world, but their relevance to a person's skill level or affinity something isn't always concrete. The fact that he had a record number of Thetans in his bloodstream doesn't necessarily track with what the scouter says about his power level.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T22:45:56-08:00","id":1346065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1346061#post1346061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So? We track all manner of statistics in the real world, but their relevance to a person's skill level or affinity something isn't always concrete. The fact that he had a record number of Thetans in his bloodstream doesn't necessarily track with what the scouter says about his power level.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Again, I might have been inclined to believe that... if the story did not present the exact opposite. Such as Obi Wan being visibly surprised to find a count that high, and Qui Gon being convinced that he was the &quot;Chosen One&quot; of prophecy. And the fact that by Palpatine's own admission, Anakin would have become more powerful than either Yoda or himself, before his extensive cybernetic augmentations severely reduced his connection to the Force.<br /> <br /> And even then, he was still the deadliest Jedi hunter in galactic history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T22:58:54-08:00","id":1346068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1346065#post1346065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I might have been inclined to believe that... if the story did not present the exact opposite. Such as Obi Wan being visibly surprised to find a count that high, and Qui Gon being convinced that he was the &quot;Chosen One&quot; of prophecy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chosen One-ness does not equate to strength in the Force - it's about a prophecy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1346065#post1346065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the fact that by Palpatine's own admission, Anakin would have become more powerful than either Yoda or himself...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, let's trust the obviously manipulative chessmaster who engineered both sides of a conflict so as to advance himself politically, and take him at his word when he says something flattering to someone who he wants to join his side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-05-2019, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T00:12:12-08:00","id":1346090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1346054#post1346054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be inclined to believe that, if the Jedi did not specifically keep track of how many midichlorians the body contains... and the fact Anakin had the highest recorded count of any known Jedi, including Yoda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correlation is not causation. There is a correlation between high midichlorian count and aptitude with the force - a strong enough correlation that the Jedi Order developed a test for it and kept records on the matter. But that does not necessarily mean either phenomenon is caused by the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1346065#post1346065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I might have been inclined to believe that... if the story did not present the exact opposite. Such as Obi Wan being visibly surprised to find a count that high, and Qui Gon being convinced that he was the &amp;quot;Chosen One&amp;quot; of prophecy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anakin\u2019s midichlorian count was so high because he was conceived by midichlorians. Essentially, they took the place of the genetic material that would normally be provided by a father. Qui Gon recognized this fact, and believed Anakin was the chosen one because of it. Not because \u201coh, this kid has so many Midichlorians, he must be really powerful, therefore he must be the chosen one,\u201d but because he was immaculately conceived. It\u2019s a clumsy Jesus allegory,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1346065#post1346065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And the fact that by Palpatine's own admission, Anakin would have become more powerful than either Yoda or himself, before his extensive cybernetic augmentations severely reduced his connection to the Force.<br /> <br /> And even then, he was still the deadliest Jedi hunter in galactic history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, as you point out here yourself, arguably he did become more powerful than them. I\u2019d say that\u2019s actually very strong evidence that having a lot of midichlorians wasn\u2019t what made him powerful. He was powerful because it was the will of the force for it to be so - because he was the chosen one. His midichlorian count and his chosen status were correlated, but not caused by one another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T03:54:06-08:00","id":1346116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1346068#post1346068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, let's trust the obviously manipulative chessmaster who engineered both sides of a conflict so as to advance himself politically, and take him at his word when he says something flattering to someone who he wants to join his side.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He said it to Yoda during their battle at the senate. <i>&quot;Lord Vader will become more powerful than either of us!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I mean, as you point out here yourself, arguably he did become more powerful than them. I\u2019d say that\u2019s actually very strong evidence that having a lot of midichlorians wasn\u2019t what made him powerful. He was powerful because it was the will of the force for it to be so - because he was the chosen one. His midichlorian count and his chosen status were correlated, but not caused by one another.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Slept on this one for a bit, and I kind of see your point.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T06:00:56-08:00","id":1346140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1346116#post1346116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> He said it to Yoda during their battle at the senate. <i>&amp;quot;Lord Vader will become more powerful than either of us!&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Slept on this one for a bit, and I kind of see your point.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, let\u2019s also not take the chessmaster\u2019s word when he is in the heat of battle trying to knock his opponent off their game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" t