":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T16:15:22-08:00","id":1436310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1436306#post1436306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the flag smashers were created the mid eighties actually</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very aware that a character called Flag Smasher was around then, but I don't expect a nuanced understanding of anarchist principles from Disney.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-20-2021, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T16:27:03-08:00","id":1436314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/5750-movies?p=1436300#post1436300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, between the A-in-a-circle background used in the previews for <i>Cruella</i> and the &quot;Flag-Smashers&quot; (yes, <b>really</b>) antagonists for <i>Falcon &amp; Winter Soldier</i> series, it sure looks like Disney is building up something of a strawman to represent Anarchism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likely. As Nicolas Milioni points out the Flag-Smashers were created in the mid-80s, but they were meant to represent anti-nationalism. Though I get the feeling the &quot;media pushes a left wing agenda!&quot; crowd only pipes up when there's women or people of color or any non-hetero sex involved, and will probably shrug off suggestions that this was anything other than a random choice that happens to coincide with topical events.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-21T08:33:34-08:00","id":1436412,"title":"","content":"Y'know the sad thing is, in his early appearances, Flag Smasher was actually someone that Captain America respected the principles of, but didn't agree on him using violence to achieve his anti-nationalist ideals (and apparently they even teamed up once or twice to face greater threats); it'd be <i>nice</i> if the Flag Smashers got as much of a &quot;villain has a point&quot; moment, but I'm skeptical that that's going to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T09:12:03-08:00","id":1436691,"title":"","content":"Since it's relevant to the current topic, I will link to the &quot;The Politics of Legend of Korra&quot; series of videos by Kay And Skittles:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><a href=\"https://youtu.be/ModX151Ipgs\" target=\"_blank\">Book 1: Communism</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://youtu.be/6alQz2CEsz0\" target=\"_blank\">Book 2: Colonization</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://youtu.be/-DyKwTXPar4\" target=\"_blank\">Book 3: Anarchy</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://youtu.be/RGX2rRAlNME\" target=\"_blank\">Book 4: Nationalism</a></li> </ol>The one about Anarchism is the most immediately relevant, but the whole series of videos lays the foundations for why the creative decisions in that show were made (or assumed to be made).<br /> <br /> To sum up, creators that have no real understanding of political philosophy have a difficulty properly critiquing it. Hence why the villains who espouse them are made to be evil because they're either liars, or because they &quot;take it too far&quot;. Such works also tend to uncritically position the current, Real Life status quo (i.e. Neo-Liberal Capitalism) as the &quot;moderate&quot; or morally superior position. A result of unexamined beliefs so foundational to the creators' world view, viable alternatives to the status quo cannot even be imagined. Let alone portrayed in any nuanced or accurate fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","na